_Agostino et al.-2021-The contribution of online revie.txt,The Contribution of Online Reviews for Quality Evaluation of Cultural Tourism Offers: The Experience of Italian Museums,"Agostino, D.; Brambilla, M.; Pavanetto, S.; Riva, P.",,2021,journal article,Sustainability,MDPI,https://doi.org/10.3390/ su132313340,https://doi.org/10.3390/ su132313340,,,Cultural Heritage (2); cultural tourism (7),,Italian museums (6); museums (31); museum (14); Italian state museums (3); cultural institutions (2); cultural heritage sites (1),digital transformation (1); digital strategies (1); brand reputation (1); digital conversations (1); cultural heritage (2); heritage assets (2),,,,Italian state museums (2); Italy (3); Italian museums (1),Italy (3); Italian (7); Naples (1); Trieste (1); Rome (2),ancient times (1),COVID-19 pandemic (1),"Although automatic tools for text analytics have proven to be valuable in exploring quality dimensions in various applicative settings (e.g., [19,20]), to the best of our knowledge, there are still limited studies that analyse online reviews with the aim of automatically identifying quality dimensions of museums comparing the expectations of policy makers and the perceptions revealed by museum visitors through their own online voices.","To ﬁll these gaps, the current study compares two different approaches to automated textual analysis of Trip Advisor data, here called the ‘top-down’ and ‘bottom-up’ approaches, with the aim of evaluating which one is more adequate for assessing quality dimensions through user-generated content in an empirical setting of 100 Italian museums.",Trip Advisor (6); Facebook (1); Instagram (1); Twitter (1),textual data (2); comments (1); online reviews (17); user-generated content (4),,,seasonality (1); monthly (3); over time (1); daily (1),numerical ratings (2); ratings (4); review distribution (1),language (4),"47,993 online reviews",museum visitors (3),,,,,,2019 (4),100 Italian state museums (3),automated and scheduled da