_Albanese and Graziano-2021-The role of cultural heritage in.txt,Studies on the Value of Cultural Heritage,Valentina Erminia Albanese; Teresa Graziano,"Post-doc fellow of Economic and Political Geography, University of Pisa, Department of Civilizations and Forms of Knowledge, University of Pisa, via Paoli 15, 56126 Pisa; Assistant Professor of Economic and Political Geography, University of Catania, Department of Agricolture, Food and Environment, via Santa Sofia 100, 95123 Catania",,other,,,,,,,Cultural Heritage (11),tangible (2); intangible (3),,cultural heritage (23); World Heritage Convention (1); cultural capital (1),,"{'SOCIAL VALUES': 'The paper discusses the importance of cultural heritage in fostering a sense of place and belonging, which aligns with collective emotional values. It also touches on how heritage contributes to local identity reinforcement, suggesting a connection to cultural identity and pride.'}; {'ECONOMIC VALUES': 'The paper mentions cultural heritage as a driver of economic and social development, contributing to urban regeneration and competitiveness in global markets. This relates to the use value of heritage assets in attracting tourism and investment.'}; {'POLITICAL VALUES': 'The paper discusses how cultural heritage can be used in place branding strategies to make cities more competitive, indicating a management value. It also touches on how heritage contributes to local identity reinforcement, suggesting a symbolic value.'}; {'HISTORIC VALUES': 'The paper highlights the role of cultural heritage in fostering a strong sense of place and awareness of historical significance, which aligns with the educational value of heritage. It also mentions the importance of cultural heritage in contributing to local identity reinforcement.'}; {'AESTHETICAL VALUES': 'The paper mentions the aesthetic experience of heritage in reducing stress, which aligns with the artistic value of heritage. It also touches on how cultural heritage can contribute to local identity reinforcement.'}; {'ECOLOGICAL VALUES': 'The paper mentions the importance of cultural heritage in contributing to local sustainability, which aligns with the essential value of heritage. It also touches on how cultural heritage can foster a closer relationship with one’s local area.'}",,Milan; Vibo Valentia,Italian provinces (3); Italy (2); Salento (1); Lombardia (2); Calabria (1); United States (1),,pandemic (1),This article critically explores the role of cultural heritage in influencing the online narratives and perceptions of territorial wellbeing in two Italian provinces selected as case studies.,"The main goal is to compare narratives about the interplay between cultural heritage and wellbeing in areas included in official rankings of quality of life, based on a set of indicators, with those co-created in the Web in order to provide new theoretical/methodological insights on the challenges and potentialities deriving from the use of web-based sentiment analysis methodologies in territorial research.",Web (11); social Web (4); Internet (5); social media (13); Youtube (1); Instagram (2); Facebook (2); Twitter (6),data online (1); narrations digitali (1); online data (2); e-discourses (1); qua-liquantitative data (1); online texts (1); social media contents (1); online user-generated contents (1); semantic data (1); online opinions (1); online narrative (1); video sources (1); textual sources (1),,spatializing (1),temporal scales (1); temporal range (1),,,"58 online textual and video sources retrieved from the first ten pages of Google with reference to the macro-theme of urban wellbeing, while a corpus of 18 sources was selected for the macro-theme of cultural heritage",,,,,,,,,manual content-based opinion mining (1),App2check (3),,,,manual (4),researcher (2),"['positive (7)', 'neutral (7)', 'negative (10)']",,Sentiment Analysis (18); opinion mining (6); text mining (2); natural language processing (4),,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,"The analysis usually includes a first stage of manual “listening” of online “conversations”, namely a manual content-based opinion mining which evaluates the online exchange of opinions among users.",no,[],,,,,,,,,,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,,,territorial wellbeing (4); quality of life (10); urban wellbeing (3); bottom-up (2); e-WOM (1); electronic word of mouth (1); tag cloud (6); city users (3); city experiencers (1),,,
_Ali et al.-2021-Exploring destination's negative.txt,Exploring destination’s negative e-reputation using aspect based sentiment analysis approach: Case of Marrakech destination on Trip Advisor,Twil Ali; Bidan Marc; Bencharef Omar; Kaloun Soulaimane; Safaa Larbi,"School of Engineering (Polytech), The University of Nantes 44000, Nantes, France; Laboratory of Computer and Systems Engineering (L2IS), Faculty of Sciences and Techniques, Cadi Ayyad University, Marrakesh 40000, Morocco; Higher School of Technology, Cadi Ayyad University, Essaouira 44103, Morocco",2021,journal article,Tourism Management Perspectives,Elsevier Ltd,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tmp.2021.100892,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tmp.2021.100892,,,World Heritage Site (1); urban heritage (1); intangible heritage (1),cultural (1),Marrakech (10); medina (1); urban heritage (1); Jamˆa-El-Fna square (2); tourist destinations (2),cultural heritage (1); World Heritage Site (1); urban heritage (1); intangible heritage (1),,,,"Marrakech; Marrakech, Morocco; Marrakech’s destinations; Phuket; Chicago","Nantes, France; Marrakesh, Morocco; Essaouira; US; Europe; Florida; Phuket, Thailand; 16 countries; Paris; Africa; Morocco",11th century (2),,"The current research aims to provide a new technique by combining topic modeling and lexicon-based algorithms to gain insights about Marrakech’s e-reputation, enhancing the tourism experience in this city.","This study explores about 39,216 Trip Advisor reviews from different locations and attractions in Marrakech, Morocco. This approach is mainly based on Latent Dirichlet Allocation (LDA), to extract hidden aspects and dimensions from the feedbacks of tourists who visited Marra­ kech, search for some latent patterns inside the reviews and conduct Lexicon-based sentiment analysis to pinpoint the weaknesses directly and develop the touristic experience in this city.",Trip Advisor (13); social media (3); social networks (3); Expedia (1); Yelp (1); Virtualtourist.com (1),reviews (21); text (1); online reviews (11); feedbacks (1); opinions (3); comments (2),,spatial analysis (2),,ratings (5); scores (3); helpful votes (1),User name; User location; User information; Bubble rating; Review Title; Review date; Date of experience,"39,216",,,,,,,2008–September 2019,Marrakech,scraping,Python language with Scrapy package,All English reviews were collected starting from 2008,"punctuation elimination, stemming and lemmatization, removing N char characters, stop-words, and irrelevant words",English reviews,manually labeled,experts,"['positive', 'Negative', 'Neutral']",,topic modeling (6); sentiment analysis (10); classification (1),Topic Models,Latent Dirichlet Allocation (LDA) (10); Naîve Bayes (1); Naive Bayes (1),,word embedding space (1),,text (1),,train and test set,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,"This study follows a traditional natural language processing approach; Natural Language Processing is widely characterized as the automated manipulation of natural language, such as speech and text, by machines (Oumaima, Soulaimane, & Omar, 2020).",yes,['Co-occurrence network (1)'],word,indicates that these two words are found in the same review,,,centrality (1); betweenness (1),The co-occurrence network is often used to produce data-driven graphics to assess centrality and the relationship between frequent words from our reviews.,,,assess centrality and the relationship between frequent words from our reviews,Accuracy (4); Kullback Leiber Divergence (KLD) (1); Elbow method (1); R2 loss ratio (1); Human rating (1); face Validity (1); External validity (1); UCI measure (1); UMass measure (1); F1-score (1),[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['Using data from a single platform can sometimes lead to platform bias (Xiang et al., 2017) due to the difference of user base in several online platforms.', 'Future research should focus on other sets of languages since this research used an English-based reviews corpus.']","['Trip Advisor has prevented anonymous reviews, and every posted view is subject to a confirmation procedure that considers the IP address and the business email of the author to stop spam or fictitious reviews.']",[],[],[],[],"['animal ethics is one of the most critical issues, as animal exploitation for “touristic” purposes all over the world, unfor\xad\ntunately, remains a standardized and still widely tolerated practice']",[],[],The data used to conduct this research is available from the corre­ sponding author upon request.,available from the corre­ sponding author upon request,,,,nltk toolkit,,e-reputation (6); Tourism (15); touristic (11); tourist (25); travelers (4); Trip Advisor (13); sentiment analysis (10); topic modeling (6); LDA (10); reviews (21); feedbacks (1); opinions (3); comments (2); Marrakech (10); Morocco (4); Natural Language Processing (NLP) (4); Lexicon-based algorithms (3); User Generated Content (UGC) (3); machine learning (4); deep learning (2); Big Data (2); Cloud Computing (1); Data Scientist (1); Python (3); Scrapy package (2); Virtualtourist.com (1); VADER (3); Text Blob (3),,,
_Ali et al.-2022-Analyzing tourism reviews using.txt,Analyzing tourism reviews using topic-based sentiment analysis,,,,other,Science Direct,,,,,,,,,touristic experience (2),,,,Marrakech (3); Jamaâ-el-Fna (3),Indonesia,,COVID-19 pandemic,,This system aims to pinpoint hidden tourists’ concerned topics and extract corresponding sentiment polarity simultaneously using lexicon-based sentiment analysis algorithms. It is expected to facilitate designers to obtain feature-level visitors’ concerns from a large volume of textual review corpora.,Twitter (2); Trip Advisor (10),text (3); reviews (13),,,,ratings (2),review date; user location; rating; review text,"More than 39,200 reviews",,,,,,,2008 to 2020,Marrakech,web scraping,Python script based on the Selenium package,,Basic Natural Language Processing methods were used to pre-process the data,,"Ratings 1 and 2 on Trip Advisor were assigned as Negative, rating 3 was assigned as Neutral, and ratings 4 and 5 were assigned as positive",,[],,sentiment analysis (11); topic modelling (8); aspect classiﬁcation,Topic Models,LDA (5); JST model (3); VADER (2),,TF-IDF,,text,,,,,,,,,,{},Joint Topic Model approach for sentiment analysis,,,,,,,A topic modelling analysis was carried out using the LDA algorithm [18] to discover aspects and speciﬁc challenges concerning tourist experience and sentiment in the research.,no,[],,,,,,,,,,Average Accuracy,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,JST Sentiment,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['the sentiment analysis algorithms used in this analytical framework are primarily rule-based, and these models do not recognize irony, sarcasm, and connotations', 'data may be destination-speciﬁc; therefore, results, such as sentiments, ratings, and aspects results in distribution, should be interpreted with caution for other in-domain applications', 'the developed system focused only on English language reviews']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],I have shared the code and data at the Attach File step.,I have shared the code and data at the Attach File step.,,,,Python NLTK library,,User Generated Content (UGC) (2); online travel platforms,,,
"_Ali et al.-2022-Context-Aware Querying, Geolocal.txt","Context-Aware Querying, Geolocalization, and Rephotography of Historical Newspaper Images","Ali, D.; Blyau, T.; Van de Weghe, N.; Verstockt, S.","KBR, the Royal Library of Brussels",2022,journal article,Appl. Sci.,MDPI,https://doi.org/10.3390/app122111063,https://doi.org/10.3390/app122111063,,,cultural heritage (5),historical; architectural,historical buildings (2); historical urban scenes (2); historical images (14); historical collections (7); historical newspaper collections (3); historical materials (1); historical content (1),digitization of heritage materials (1); cultural heritage institutions (2); architectural heritage (1),,"{'SOCIAL': 'Emotional (collective): The study focuses on historical images and urban scenes, which contribute to cultural identity and a sense of place attachment by visualizing temporal evolution and changes in locations over time.'}; {'HISTORIC': 'Educational: The study aims to provide knowledge about the past by geolocalizing and rephotographing historical images, allowing users to explore and understand changes in locations over time.'}; {'AESTHETICAL': 'Artistic: The rephotography of historical images involves artistic techniques to blend and blur the images, creating a visually appealing representation of the transition from historical to current views.'}",preservation (1); digitization (4),,Belgium (2); Brussels (2); Chicago (1); Marseille (2); Versailles (2); Nieuport Bains (2); Prague (1); Paris (1),1938,COVID-19,"A number of challenges arise when dealing with digitized collections, such as those of KBR, the Royal Library of Brussels (used in this study), which contain only page-level metadata, making it difﬁcult to extract information from speciﬁc contexts.","This research study aims for the context-aware querying, geolocalization, and rephotography of historical buildings from the KBR digitized newspaper collections.",Flickr (1); Instagram (1); Google (4),images (21); text (10),,,timestamps (3); time travel (1); temporal evolution (1); time-based visualization (1),,,40,,,,,,,1938,Belgian,Google image search,,,filtered out by feature matching algorithms,,,,[],,image classification (2); named entity recognition (2); feature extraction (7); feature matching (6); article segmentation (4),convolutional neural networks (CNN) (3); deep learning (3),Res Net101 (1); Cirtorch (3); DELF (3),pretrained Cirtorch,,SIFT (3); SURF (2); ORB (2); PCA (1),image features (2); text (2),,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,F1 score (2),[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],['location-based service applications (1)'],[],[],[],[],"['The quality of OCR (text recognition) must be high enough to provide location information within the proposed workﬂow.', 'Moreover, if historical photographs contain excessive amounts of noise, geolocalization and rephotography algorithms will not be able to detect appropriate matches.']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,Not applicable.,,,,,,rephotography (13); geolocalization (11); context-aware (5); article segmentation (3); location information (10); caption detection (2); feature matching (5); k-NN (3); RANSAC (2); OCR (7); NER (1); ALTO/XML (1),,,
_Alsadik-2018-Practicing the geometric designa.txt,Practicing the geometric designa,Alsadik,,2018,other,J. Cultur. Heritage,El i M SAS,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.culher.2017.11.001,https://www.3dwarehouse. sketchup.com,,,cultural heritage (CH) (5),tangible (1),cultural heritage (CH) (5); archaeological sites (1); Haydarkhana mosque model (1); Georgia State Capitol model (2); mosque building (2),cultural heritage (CH) (5); restoration (1); conservation (1); documentation (1),,,restoration (1); conservation (1),Haydarkhana mosque; Georgia State Capitol,Russia; Switzerland; France; Saudi Arabia; Japan; USA,19th century (1),,"In contrary to what is presented in the literature to model real physical CH objects, we are presenting the concept of applying the reverse engineering or a simulation of the previously developed digital models of cultural heritage.","Accordingly, this approach will help non-professionals and students to practice and improve their skills in planning a camera network or a laser scanning network to ﬁnally re-create the similar real CH object of interest.",sketchfab (3); Sketchup (2),images (10); 3D point cloud (4),,,,,,,,,138 images are oriented with the addition of ten control points to ﬁnally create a point cloud of the 3D model of 1.6 million points,,,,,,simulation,Blender (10),,,,,,[],,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,RMSE (2); relative accuracy (2),[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],"['modelling of cultural heritage sites for restoration, conservation, documentation and other applications']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,Python,,3D pipeline; 3D Warehouse,,,
_Amato et al.-2016-Opinions Analysis in Social Netw.txt,Opinions Analysis in Social Networks,F. Amato; G. Cozzolino; S. Di Martino; A. Mazzeo; V. Moscato; A. Picariello; S. Romano; G. Sperlí,"DIETI - Department of Electrical Engineering and Information Technology, University of Naples “Federico II”, Naples, Italy; Ce RICT scrl - Centro Regionale Information Communication Technology, Complesso Universitario di Monte Sant’Angelo, Naples, Italy",2016,other,,Springer Singapore,,,,,cultural heritage (4),,cultural heritage events (4); historical center (2); historical district,Cultural Heritage (10); UNESCO World Heritage Site (1),,"{'SOCIAL VALUES': 'Emotional (collective) – The system aims to provide recommendations for cultural heritage events based on user preferences, which can contribute to a sense of cultural identity and pride.'}; {'HISTORIC VALUES': 'Educational – The system recommends cultural heritage events such as guided tours and exhibitions, which have the potential to provide knowledge about the past.'}; {'AESTHETICAL VALUES': 'Artistic – The system recommends events such as art exhibitions in museums or historical buildings, which are original products of creativity and imagination.'}",,Historic Centre of Naples,Naples; Italy; Naples Metropolitan area; Europe,Baroque genre,,"Nevertheless, the full exploitation of the knowledge in the Twitter messages is still an open and challenging issue. On one hand, event detection from Twitter is a problem due to the heterogeneity of messages, which can contain personal updates and re-tweets not related to any real-word event [12]. On the other hand, the limitation of 140 characters per Twitter message, and sometimes the low quality of the textual data makes diﬃcult to associate a tweet to the events.",In this work we present a system for topic detection and opinion analysis from tweets having the aim of suggesting upcoming cultural heritage events. The system aims at suggesting events occurring to user proximity according to the user preferences extracted automatically from the posted tweets.,Social Networks (2); Twitter (17),text (10); GPS (2),GPS (2),,timestamped actions,,tags (2),,,,,,,,,,collect users preferences analysing the Twitter stream,,,"Meta-Noise Filter module aims at rejecting, and thus removing, inaccurate or irrelevant words in the input text, called meta-noise words, because they have not attached useful meaning.",,,,[],,topic detection (5); sentiment analysis (7); classification (2),Recursive Neural Network (RNN) (2),LDA (1),,compositional vector representations,,text,,,cross entropy error,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,"In this model, we split the text of a tweet into sentences and for each one building a binary tree: each leaf, corresponding to a single word, is a dimension of the vector space model.","From one hand, the sentiment analysis phase allows to compute a sentiment score for each tweet using machine earning approaches [18]; in particular, we classify each tweet in one of the following ﬁve classes: very negative, negative, neutral, positive and very positive.",no,[],,,,,,,,,,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,"all the modules have been realized using JAVA technologies. In addition, the NLP Utilities are provided as web services and leverage the Stanford NLP libraries,1 while the Knowledge Base is built on the top of Mongo DB2 document database and Cassandra3 column-oriented repository.",,,tweets (17); topic detection (5); sentiment analysis (7); NLP (4); machine learning (2); Named Entity Filter module; Linguistic Normalization & Tagging module; Knowledge Base component; User Proﬁling module; Event Search Engine; Cultural Heritage Event Recommender; Tweet Analyzer component; Meta-Noise Filter module,,,
_Annad et al.-2017-Web information monitoring and c.txt,Web information monitoring and crowdsourcing: a tool for geoheritage enhancement,Oussama Annad,"Departement de Geologie, LGGIP-FSTGAT-USTHB, BP 32, El-Alia, Bab Ezzouar, Algiers, Algeria; Departement Sciences de l’Information et de la Communication, Centre de recherches sur les médiations-Universite de Lorraine, UFR Sciences Humaines et Sociales (Nancy), Campus Lettres et Sciences Humaines, 23 boulevard Albert 1er-BP 13397, 54015 Nancy, France",2016,other,Geoheritage,Springer International Publishing,,,,,geoheritage (17),natural (1); historical (1); cultural (2),Algerian geosites (3); geosites (13); geosite (11),geoheritage conservation (1); geotourism (3); geoconservation (2); geodiversity (1); geosites (1); geological heritage (1); geoheritage management (1); geoheritage value (1),,"{'value': 'Economic', 'reasoning': 'The paper discusses the promotion of geotouristic resources and the economic development of a region through popularization of its geotouristic resources. It also mentions the potential of geosites as a source of renewable energy.'}; {'value': 'Political', 'reasoning': 'The paper discusses the role of geoscientists in enhancing the geoheritage of Algeria and making decision makers aware of the interest of these geosites. It also mentions the importance of up-to-date information for the planning and strategic management of geotourism.'}; {'value': 'Scientific', 'reasoning': 'The paper discusses the scientific interest of geoheritage and the importance of documenting geoheritage features. It also mentions the use of scientific publications to gather information about geosites.'}; {'value': 'Aesthetical', 'reasoning': 'The paper mentions that Algeria contains a large number of geological sites which often combine scientific, aesthetic, and economic values. It also mentions Assekrem as one of the most beautiful natural sites in Algeria.'}; {'value': 'Social', 'reasoning': 'The paper mentions that geoheritage has a deep social dimension, which implies that its assessment and promotion should be grounded on multidisciplinary knowledge. It also discusses the use of crowdsourcing to involve people in sorting pictures of geosites.'}",geoheritage management (1); geoconservation (2); protection (2); preservation (1); planning (2),Hammam Meskhoutine (6); Hammam Debagh (1); Assekrem (Hoggar) (4); Assekrem Hoggar (2),Algeria (7); Africa (2); Middle East (2); North Africa (1); Saharan Desert (1),Roman times (1),,This raises the question of methods and tools that are needed to assist scientific and economic actors in collecting information that contributes to the promotion of geoheritage.,We address this question here by proposing the development of a web information monitoring system. The proposed system is designed as a tool for automating the search and the collect of documents on geosites from the web by using information retrieval methods and text mining to improve the result accuracy. It aims to support planners and different stakeholders in their activities by making the most objective knowledge on geoheritage more easily accessible.,Flickr (3),pictures (12); scientific publications (4); news articles (4); blog articles (2); web pages (2),Google Maps API (1),,,,,,,,,,,,,,automating the search and the collect of documents on geosites from the web by using information retrieval methods and text mining,"Bing Search API, Google Custom Search API, and Flickr API, Springer API and Elsevier API",,eliminate duplicates in the results,,GWAP,general public,[],output-agreement approach,information retrieval (2); text mining (2),,,,,Rapid Automatic Keyword Extraction (RAKE) algorithm (1),,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,precision (4),[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],"['support tool in their functions and activities (1)', 'enhance the geotourism (1)']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,HTML; PHP; JAVASCRIPT; My SQL,,games with a purpose (GWAP) (8); web information monitoring system (3); information monitoring (6); crowdsourcing (7); geoscience discipline (1); geotouristic resources (1); geoscientific community (1); decision makers (2); general public (3); knowledge management (3); information retrieval methods (1); text mining (1); stakeholders (1); aerial photo-interpretation (1); geographic information system (GIS) (3); web 2.0 (1); ESP game (3); output agreement (2); Galaxy zoo (1); Planet Four (1); Seafloor Explorer (1); Digi Talkoot (1); Zoom&Sort (3); Guess Year (5); Hammam Deabgh (1); tourisme thermal (1); Thalassothérapie (1); volcanism activity (1); Charles de foucauld (2); Sahara tourism (1); Peugeot (2); Yves Rocher (1); Ouedkniss (2); BImagerie et modélisation géologique et géophysique du Hoggar; Implications géodynamiques et métallogéniques (1),,,
_Antonio et al.-2020-Exploring User-Generated Content.txt,Article,,,2020,other,,MDPI,,http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/,,,UNESCO heritage (5); World Heritage (10),,UNESCO World Heritage Sites (2); heritage cities (2); historical urban spaces,UNESCO (10); UNESCO World Heritage (4); heritage (23); cultural (10); history (6); architecture (4); preservation (2); conservation (2); sustainable promotion; national identity; cultural identity; historic; heritage tourism; cultural tourism; cultural heritage; heritage sites (5); heritage site (3); World Heritage List (4); World Heritage Site (3),,"{'value': 'Educational', 'reasoning': 'The paper discusses the potential of heritage sites to provide knowledge about the past, aligning with the educational value of heritage assets. The authors mention the willingness of tourists to learn when visiting heritage sites.'}; {'value': 'Entertainment', 'reasoning': 'The paper mentions the tourists’ desire to be entertained when visiting a heritage site. The authors also discuss the role of heritage sites in providing recreational experiences.'}; {'value': 'Emotional (collective)', 'reasoning': 'The paper discusses the importance of heritage sites for enhancing cultural and national identity, which aligns with the emotional (collective) value of heritage. The authors mention the emotional involvement that visitors may feel at the visited site.'}; {'value': 'Economic (use)', 'reasoning': 'The paper discusses the potential of UNESCO World Heritage sites to increase visitor and tourism revenue, aligning with the use value of heritage assets. The authors mention the objective of increasing visitor and tourism revenue as a primary objective of UNESCO WHS applications.'}",preservation (2); maintenance; manage the sites; sustainable promotion,Salamanca; Coimbra,Spain (10); Portugal (7); Europe (4); Asia (2); America (2); China,13th century,,"there is an information gap between what visitors want and what they ﬁnd during their trips. Additionally, from the perspective of management and marketing, it is necessary to understand who the UNESCO World Heritage tourists are in order to oﬀer positive experiences without downplaying the much-needed support for place conservation","The general objective of this study is to emphasize the value of comprehensively exploring and understanding the main concerns and opinions the visitors’ reviews portray about the sites they visit, based on the collection and exploitation of data available on Trip Advisor social media, so that those responsible for heritage management can arrive at informed decisions.",Trip Advisor (8); Booking.com (2),text (10); reviews (20); Online Travel Review (OTR) (7),,,,ratings (3),user name; user’s place of residence; date in which the review was published; name of the site; language,"8,638",4695,,,,,,2017–2018 (2),Salamanca in Spain and Coimbra in Portugal,"extracted from Trip Advisor in April 2019 through a web robot, or simply bot, an application that performs tasks automatically","web robot, or simply bot, an application that performs tasks automatically",the ten most recommended places for tourists by tourist information sites or digital newspapers with sections dedicated to tourism,,,,,[],,sentiment analysis (7); text mining (7); keyword extraction (2),machine learning (2),,,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,yes,"['network analysis (2)', 'social media']",attraction,number of visitors who posted reviews in both connecting attractions,,,,,Apriori algorithm (2),,clearly depicts visitors’ preferences about which attractions to visit,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['First, it only focuses on two cities.', 'Second, UNESCO World Heritage tourists are male and female in equal numbers, are highly schooled, are employed, and travel in small groups (two to ﬁve people)']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,,,Smart Tourism Analytics; Text mining; Sentiment Analysis; Market Basket Analysis; online travel reviews (OTR); dest