_Arakawa-2014-Discovering popular point of int.txt,Discovering Popular Point of Interests for Tourism with,,,2014,other,"IWWISS ’14 September 01 - 02 2014, Saint Etienne, France",ACM,http://dx.doi.org/10.1145/2637064.2637100,,,,,,,,,,,New York; San Francisco; London; Paris; Berlin,London; New York; Paris; San Francisco,,,Another problem of a clustering-based social spatial data analysis is a name/meaning assignment against the obtained clusters. The results obtained after clustering are just numerical values such as a center coordinate value.,"In order to resolve these problems, ﬁrst, I conduct preliminary experiments. Especially, a proper bandwidth parameter for ﬁnding POIs in a city, and an adequate dataset size against the area size are determined. Furthermore, the problem of tag-based name assignment and the eﬀect of category setting are clariﬁed.",Flickr; Facebook,geo-tagged photos; location; date/time; tags,,,,,location; date/time; tags,more than 4 million,,,,,,,after 2004/01/01,"5 cities: New York, San Francisco, London, Paris, and Berlin",,,randomly selected according a given dataset size,"First, several photos taken by the same user in the close location within 10 minutes are omitted. Second, old photos are omitted because the accuracy of geo location information including them are not good.","I use only the photos taken after 2004/01/01, although the oldest photos in the collected data is taken in 2000.",,,[],,clustering,,Mean shift clustering (MS),,,,location; date/time; tags,,,,,,,,,,{'bandwidth': '0.001'},,Macbook Pro,,,RAM:16G,,,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,,[],[],[],,I conﬁrmed that the proposed system obtain more appropriate names than the conventional system in every cities.,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],['generate a tourist map automatically based on social data analysis'],[],['a novel name estimation method that utilizes several reverse geocoding APIs has been proposed'],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,python script,,,Point of Interests; reverse