_Ardizzone et al.-2012-Extracting Touristic Information.txt,Extracting Touristic Information from Online Image Collections,Ardizzone; Giuseppe; La Cascia; Marco; Pirrone; Renato,,2012,other,,,,,,,,,touristic attractions (1),,,"{'value': 'Entertainment', 'reasoning': 'The paper discusses extracting touristic information from online image collections to determine interesting places and reconstruct touristic routes, which aligns with the entertainment value of heritage assets in the contemporary tourism market.'}; {'value': 'Educational', 'reasoning': ""The paper aims to derive information about major touristic attractions of a city, which can be used for educational purposes to learn about the city's history and culture.""}",,Palermo,Italian city; Palermo,,Palermo Marathon,The main problem faced during our work was the lack of accurate and reliable annotations by the Flickr users.,The goal is twofold: finding places of interest in a city and reconstructing touristic routes of Flickr users that visited that city.,Flickr,photos; tags; annotations; descriptions; geo-referencing,GPS coordinates,,timestamps,,photo.exif; photo.note; photo; photo.comment; photoset; photoset.comment; place; photo.tag; user; group; contact; context,"3,010 different titles",,,,,,,,city of Palermo,"collect from Flickr all the photos, and related information, that are associated to a specific city, by using the Flickr API",Flickr API,,"discarded all the “social” information, which are not useful for our purposes. We discard also tags, which are very noisy, and do not add much useful information to our system. Furthermore we discarded also “place” information as, on Flickr, it does not refer to a specific location but to an area too large for our purposes.",,,,[],,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,,[],,,,,,,,,,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],"['suggest new touristic paths to the users, depending on their constraints (visiting time, starting place, specific interests, etc.)']",[],[],['