_Borrajo-Millán et al.-2021-Sentiment Analysis to Measure Qu.txt,Sentiment Analysis to Measure Quality and Build Sustainability in Tourism Destinations,F. Borrajo-Millán; M.-d.-M. Alonso-Almeida; M. Escat-Cortes; L. Yi,,2021,journal article,Sustainability,MDPI,https://doi.org/10.3390/su13116015,https://doi.org/10.3390/su13116015,,,,,historical–cultural tourist attractions (1); ancient architecture (1),cultural heritage (1); historical authenticity (1),,"{'Aesthetical': 'The paper mentions the aesthetic value of churches, indicating an appreciation for their artistic qualities.'}; {'Historic-Artistic': 'The paper discusses the historical changes in Baroque and Gothic architecture, highlighting the artistic movements associated with these styles.'}; {'Entertainment': 'The paper mentions sports events (La Liga Football League) and bullfighting as tourist products, indicating their role in the contemporary market, especially tourism.'}; {'Educational': 'The paper mentions academic travel and study tours as new tourism products, indicating the educational role of heritage assets.'}; {'Emotional (collective)': 'The paper mentions that Chinese tourists travel to Europe and Spain for cultural, gastronomic, and shopping tourism, indicating a cultural identity and pride.'}",,Spain; Madrid; Barcelona; Seville,Spain; China; Europe; North Africa; Morocco; western Europe; northern Europe; eastern Europe; Britain; France; Germany; Austria,,COVID-19,"Thus, it is necessary to look for new methods for analyzing the tourist management and attractiveness of tourist spots.","This study analyzed the quality of tourism in Spain, a major tourist destination that is considered to be the country with the greatest tourist competitiveness according to the World Economic Forum, and in China, the country with the greatest level of development and potential.",social networks (5); Baidu Travel; Ctrip; Mafengwo; Qunar; Sina Weibo,text (1); images (2),,heat map (2),,,,"38,337 reviews",,,,,,,2019,"18