_Capodieci et al.-2015-Visualizing cultural digital res.txt,Visualizing Cultural Digital Resources using Social Network Analysis,,,,other,,,,,,,Cultural Heritage (5),,cultural digital resources (6); cultural resource (1); cultural heritage objects (CHOs) (6); cultural objects (2); cultural heritage (4); cultural items (1); digital representations of cultural heritage objects (1); digital cultural resources (3),Cultural Heritage (5); cultural digital resources (6); digital resources (10); cultural resource (1); cultural heritage objects (CHOs) (6); cultural objects (2); cultural heritage (4); digital objects (2); cultural items (1); digital representations of cultural heritage objects (1); digital cultural resources (3); metadata (8); conservation (1); preservation (1),,"{'value': 'Educational', 'reasoning': 'The paper discusses the potential of cultural heritage objects to provide knowledge and insights into the past, which aligns with the educational value of heritage.'}; {'value': 'Economic', 'reasoning': 'The paper mentions the potential for regional development through a systemic approach, which implies an economic value associated with cultural heritage.'}; {'value': 'Social', 'reasoning': 'The paper highlights the role of social media and online communities in sharing and interacting with cultural heritage, suggesting a collective emotional value and cultural identity.'}",conservation (1); preservation (1),,Italy (2); Sicily (Italy) (1); Europe (3); European (3),prehistory to modern era (1),,"Despite the recent interest in capturing data on the creation of cultural digital resources, there seem to be still issues concerning the quality and quantity of the information found in the descriptive metadata associated with the digital representations of cultural heritage objects (Beaudoin, 2012). This information is often considered inadequate to make sure users understand the nature of the cultural object and its digital representation (Tsirliganis et al., 2004).","