_Cardia-2018-Routes and Itineraries as a Mean.txt,Routes and Itineraries as a Means,,,,other,,,,,,,Cultural Heritage (3); Natural Heritage (2),,cultural routes (10); historical routes (2); thematic routes (2),cultural values (4); heritage (6); sustainable tourism (11); cultural diversity (3); cultural heritage (2); traditions (2); conservation (1); European values (2),,"{'value': 'Social Values', 'reasoning': 'The paper discusses the importance of tourism in promoting cultural diversity, reviving traditional activities and customs, and empowering communities, which aligns with the emotional (collective) value of cultural identity, motivation, and pride.'}; {'value': 'Economic Values', 'reasoning': 'The paper highlights the economic benefits of tourism, including job creation, contribution to world GDP, and export revenue, which aligns with the use and entertainment values of heritage assets.'}; {'value': 'Political Values', 'reasoning': 'The paper mentions the educational role of heritage assets in promoting cultural awareness and the use of tourism in strategies for disseminating cultural awareness for political purposes, aligning with the educational and entertainment values.'}; {'value': 'Aesthetical Values', 'reasoning': 'The paper implicitly discusses the artistic and conceptual values of cultural routes by mentioning architecture and prehistoric art as themes for cultural routes.'}",,"Santiago of Compostela; Canterbury Cathedral; Historic centre of San Gimignano; Siena; Rome; Landscape of Val D’Orcia; Vatican City; Vilnius historic centre; Bialowieza Forest; Wieliczka Salt Mine; Centennial Hall in Wroclaw; Classical Weimar in Belvedere Castle; Cathedral of Notre-Dame; Former Abbey of Saint Remi and Palace of Tau, in Reims; the banks of the Seine in Paris; the Port of the Moon in Bordeaux; the Roman Walls of Lugo; Las Médulas; Mallorca; Aragón; Vía de Plata Route; Transromanica network; European itineraries of Jewish Heritage; the European route of thermal heritage and thermal cities; Balearic Archaeosites; Cinque Terre, Liguria; Way of Gods; Valle d’Aosta; Piedmont; Lombardy; Emilia Romagna; Tuscany; Latium; Quebrada de Humahuaca; Ollantaytambo; Sacred Valley; Machu Picchu; Bhutan; India; Nepal; Pakistan; China; Argentina; Bolivia; Chile; Colombia; Ecuador; Peru; Central Asia; West Asia; Africa; Yemen; Oman; Arabian Peninsula; Mediterranean; Huixian; Xinxiang; Yukon",Spain (8); Europe (10); European (10); France (2); Italy (5); South Asia; Mexico; Slovenia; Lithuania; Germany; Switzerland; Netherlands; Belgium; Northern Europe; Southern France; Central Europe; Israel; Paraguay; Nepal (2); Humla; Dolpo; Gorkha; Manaslu; Solukhumbu; Taplejung; Western Hills; China (3); Kazakhstan; Kyrgyzstan; North Africa,past centuries,International Year of Sustainable Tourism for Development (UNWTO 2016),,"The main objective of this research is focused on the exploration of opportunities that sustainable tourism could bring to local destinations and communities, as a catalyst for positive change of policies, business practices and consumer behavior in in the context of the universal 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development and the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). Moreover, this research is directed to the analysis of the potential of routes and itineraries for building a tourism sector that is more responsible and committed to global development goals.",social network pages,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,[],,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,,[],,,,,,,,,,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,,,,,"The paper discusses routes and itineraries in the context of sustainable tourism and development goals. It explores the potential of cultural and natural routes to contribute to economic growth, social inclusion, environmental protection, and cultural heritage. The methodology involves a literature review and classification of routes based on geographical, historical, thematic, and motivational criteria.",
