_Castiglione et al.-2018-CHIS A big data infrastructure.txt,CHIS: A big data infrastructure to manage digital cultural items,Aniello Castiglione; Francesco Colace; Vincenzo Moscato; Francesco Palmieri,"University of Salerno, Dipartimento di Informatica, Via Giovanni Paolo II, 132 - 84084 Fisciano (SA), Italy; University of Salerno, Dipartimento di Ingegneria Industriale, Via Giovanni Paolo II, 132 - 84084 Fisciano (SA), Italy; University of Naples, Dip. di Ingegneria Elettrica e delle Tecnologie dell’Informazione, Via Claudio 21, - 80125 Napoli, Italy",2017,journal article,Future Generation Computer Systems,Elsevier B.V.,,,,12,cultural heritage (7); Cultural Heritage (11),,digital cultural items (2); cultural items (13); cultural Points of Interest (2); cultural environment (7); archeological site (4); old town centers (2); historical building (2); famous squares (2); digital cultural contents (2); cultural digital contents (1); cultural objects (1); ancient buildings (3),digital libraries (5); digital archives (4); multimedia collections (4); Web Data Services (4); digital cultural heritage (3); digital libraries (2); museums (1); digitization (1); cultural heritage preservation (1); cultural heritage security (1),,"{'value': 'Social: Emotional (collective)', 'reasoning': 'The paper discusses promoting cultural heritage through web portals and multimedia guides, which can foster cultural identity and a sense of place attachment.'}; {'value': 'Economic: Entertainment', 'reasoning': 'The paper mentions mobile multimedia guides and web portals to promote cultural heritage, indicating a focus on tourism and the role of heritage in the contemporary market.'}; {'value': 'Political: Educational', 'reasoning': 'The paper refers to the educational role of heritage assets, particularly in the context of smart cities, suggesting that cultural heritage can be used for political purposes such as nation-building myths or glorification of leaders.'}; {'value': 'Historic: Educational', 'reasoning': 'The paper discusses the potential of heritage assets to provide knowledge about the past, which aligns with the educational value of historical sites and artifacts.'}; {'value': 'Aesthetical: Artistic', 'reasoning': 'The paper mentions sculptures, pictures, and other art pieces exhibited within a museum, indicating the artistic value of cultural heritage.'}",cultural heritage (2); cultural heritage identification (1); monitoring (1); restoration (2),Paestum (5); Paestum archeological site (2); Campania (1),Italy (3); Lazio (1); Calabria region (1); European (4); European countries (2); Southern Italy (1),Graeco-Roman (2),,"Summarizing, the main research problems that can be correlated to the management of Cultural Heritage digital contents in the Smart Cities context are: • the adoption of architectural models and standards in the context of Future Internet and Big Data [12,13]; • the interfacing and communication with the sensors of a site [14–17]; • the access, retrieval, integration and analysis of information from all data sources and the correlation with spatial data [18,19]; • the transformation of ‘‘captured’’ data in the form of knowledge and its management [20,21]; • the localization and tracking of users on a site [22,23]; • the access to the knowledge based on the user profile, the context and the use of applications [24–26]; • the analysis of users’ opinions from social networks [27].","In this paper, we describe CHIS (Cultural Heritage Information System), a system to query, browse and analyze cultural digital contents from a set of distributed and heterogeneous repositories.",Social Media (2); Social Media Networks (6); Facebook (2); Twitter (2); Panoramio (2); Picasa (2); You Tube (2); Flickr (2),multimedia (10); video (4); text (5); image (5); audio (3); sensor data (3); spatial data (1); user data (3); JSON (6),GPS technology (1),,temporal instant (1),ratings (2),metadata (16); user profiles (2); user preferences (4); user needs 