_Cehan et al.-2016-USING GIS TECHNIQUES AND GEOTAGG.txt,"USING GIS TECHNIQUES AND GEOTAGGING TO ASSESS TOURISM DENSITY AND ATTRACTIVENESS IN THE CITY OF IASI, ROMANIA",Alexandra Cehan; Mihai Bulai; Lucian Rosu,Alexandru Ioan Cuza University; Alexandru Ioan Cuza University; Alexandru Ioan Cuza University,2016,conference paper,"Proceedings of SOCIOINT 2016 3rd International Conference on Education, Social Sciences and Humanities",,,https://www.researchgate.net/publication/331564727,,,,,urban space (5); urban environment,tourism heritage,,,tourism planning (6),"Iași Municipality, Romania; Iași city",Romania; Eastern region of European Union,,,This paper uses GIS techniques to spatially define tourism areas in a post-socialist city and consequently identify the different levels of tourism density.,"Therefore, this paper aims to explore the spatial distribution of tourism attractiveness in a post-socialist city (Iași Municipality, Romania) through a GIS-based approach, taking into consideration the main components of the tourism supply: tourist attractions, accommodation units and catering services.",Social Media (6); Facebook,geo-tags,,spatial distribution,,ratings,,,,,,,,,,Iasi,,,,,,,,[],,classification,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,,[],,,,,,,,,,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,,,tourism density (3); tourism attractiveness (7); tourism areas (3); urban tourism (10); GIS tools; geo-tags,,,
_Chai-allah et al.-2023-Mining crowdsourced text to capt.txt,Mining crowdsourced text to capture hikers' perceptions associated with landscape features and outdoor physical activities,Abdesslam Chai-allah; Nathan Fox; Fritz Günther; Fadila Bentayeb; Gilles Brunschwig; Sandro Bimonte; Fr´ed´eric Joly,"University of Clermont Auvergne, INRAE, Vet Agro Sup, UMR Herbivores, 63122 Saint-Gen`es-Champanelle, France; University of Michigan, School for Environment and Sustainability, Ann Arbor, MI 48109, USA; Department of Psychology, Humboldt Universit¨at zu Berlin, 10099 Berlin, Germany; University of Lyon, Lyon2, ERIC, EA 3083, 5 avenue Pierre Mendes France, F69676 Bron Cedex, France; University of Clermont Auvergne, INRAE, TSCF, 63178 Aubi`ere, France",2023,journal article,Ecological Informatics,Elsevier B V,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ecoinf.2023.102332,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ecoinf.2023.102332,,,,,archaeological sites (1); historical sites (1),UNESCO heritage site (1),,,,,France (3); Auvergne region (2); Auvergne (7),,,"Despite the increased number of studies using crowdsourced online data to assess how people interact with the landscape during recreational activities, the focus remains largely on mapping the spatial distribution of visitors or analyzing the content of shared images and little work has been done to quantify the perceptions and emotions people assign to the landscape.",What are the landscape features and outdoor physical activities preferred and mentioned by hikers? 2) What are the perceptions mentioned by hikers? 3) What perceptions do hikers associate with landscape features and outdoor physical activities?,Wikiloc (13); GPSies (1),text (10); photographs (3); images (4); GPS trails (3); videos (1),latitude and longitude (2),spatial distribution (2),,,,978 hiking trails (2),388 users (1),1128 trails (1),,,,,2017–2020 (1),Auvergne (1),,,"keeping only the trails that were assigned by users as hiking trails, 2) removing those without associated text data, and 3) applying the “Trail-User-Days” (TUD) measure (i.e., a single trail per user per day)","translated all text descriptions into English using Deep L (https://www.deepl.com). Second, data preprocessing consists of using natural language processing (NLP) methods to perform automated text mining in R, primarily using the packages tidytext (Silge and Robinson, 2017) and tm (Feinerer and Hornik, 2018) for tokenization, lemmatization and English stop words removal based on a predefined list of common English words (e.g., and, the). An additional set of words such as the name of the country, towns, places, and those related to transportation (e.g., car, parking, and train) were also removed for the lack of relevance to the purpose of the study.",,manual (2),,"['positive (3)', 'negative (3)']",,clustering (4); classification (2); topic modeling (1),word embedding methods (2),Word2vec (6); Glo Ve (1); BERT (2),pre-trained (3),word embeddings (2),,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,,[],[],[],chi-square test (1); p < 0.001 (1),,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],['data sets were anonymized (1)'],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],script available at this link: https://github.com/achaiallah-hub/Wiki4CES (1),,,,Python environment (1),R (3),,,,,
_Chai-allah et al.-2025-Assessing recreationists' prefer.txt,Assessing recreationists’ preferences of the landscape and species using crowdsourced images and machine learning,Abdesslam Chai-allah; Johannes Hermes; Anne De La Foye; Zander S. Venter; Fr´ed´eric Joly; Gilles Brunschwig; Sandro Bimonte; Nathan Fox,"University of Clermont Auvergne, INRAE, Vet Agro Sup, UMR Herbivores, 63122 Saint-Gen`es-Champanelle, France; Leibniz Universit¨at Hannover, Institute of Environmental Planning, Herrenh¨auser Str. 2, 30419 Hannover, Germany; Norwegian Institute for Nature Research – NINA, Sognsveien 68, 0855 Oslo, Norway; University of Clermont Auvergne, INRAE, TSCF, 63178 Aubi`ere, France; University of Michigan, School for Environment and Sustainability, Ann Arbor, MI 48109, USA; Michigan Institute for Data Science, University of Michigan, Ann Arbor, MI, USA",2025,journal article,Landscape and Urban Planning,Elsevier B V,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.landurbplan.2025.105315,www.elsevier.com/locate/landurbplan,,,,,,,,,,Auvergne; Chaîne des Puys – Faille de Limagne,France; Europe; Great Britain,,,"In rural areas, understanding which land covers people prefer to recreate in, and how these land covers provide different CES, is necessary to support sustainable use.","This study aims to assess recreationists’ revealed preferences of landscape aesthetics and species observation as CES at the landscape scale, considering multiple land cover types. To do this, we applied a machine learning algorithm (Google Cloud Vision) to images extracted from a social media (Flickr) and outdoor sports app (Wikiloc) in a rural area in France (Auvergne).",Flickr; Wikiloc; Instagram; Facebook; Panoramio; Strava; All Trails,images; photographs; text,georeferenced images; geotagged photos; spatial location; coordinates,spatial distribution,monthly distribution,,,"8,357","613 users were available on Flickr, and 447 users on Wikiloc",,"9,563 georeferenced photographs uploaded by 613 users were available on Flickr, and 6,527 photographs associated with 1,218 trails were uploaded by 447 users on Wikiloc.",,,"1,902 geotagged photos uploaded by 117 users on Flickr, and 6, 455 geotagged photos uploaded by 440 users on Wikiloc.","January 1, 2017, to December 31, 2020",Auvergne,downloaded images,Flickr API,We filtered the remaining data to represent day trips using the “Trail User Days (TUD)” approach,"We excluded data points that had no photo image available at the time of the analysis, and those localized in urban areas",excluding data points localized in urban areas,manual,one author,[],"The mean agreement for CES was 95 % with good scores for sensitivity and specificity, as well as for fungi, invertebrates and livestock, demonstrating both the ability of the algorithm and the pro­posed tag classification framework for these categories.",classification; image recognition,,Google Cloud Vision,pre-trained,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,sensitivity; specificity; percentage agreement,[],[],[],one-sample Wilcoxon signed rank test; Wilcoxon signed-rank test; Wilcoxon rank-sum test; Benjamini − Yekutieli correction,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],available,The data used in this study are open-source and publicly available.,,https://github.com/achaiallah-hub/Wiki4CES and https://github.com/achaiallah-hub/image-analysis-paper,"R, version 4.1.0",,,,,,
"_Chaney and Brassier-2024-Destruction of heritage, communi.txt","Destruction of heritage, community effects: The case of Notre-Dame",Damien Chaney; Pascal Brassier,"EM Normandie Business School; IAE Clermont Auvergne, France",2024,journal article,Annals of Tourism Research,Elsevier,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.annals.2024.103839,https://www.globe-trotting.com/post/les-lieux-et-monuments-les-plus-visites-en-france,,16,Cultural Heritage (2),cultural,heritage sites (7); historic resources; archaeological heritage sites; heritage attractions (3); heritage objects; heritage site; heritage monument,heritage management (2); authenticity; cultural identity (2); heritage tourism (10); heritage attributes (2); cultural heritage (3); heritage attractions (3); heritage activities; heritage management efforts; heritage preservation (2); heritage objects; heritage sites (7); heritage site; heritage monument; heritage anthropomorphism (7); heritage education; heritage listing; shared heritage (2); historic resources,,"Social (collective) – Cultural identity, motivation and pride, sense of “place attachment,” and communal value. The heritage sites connect people with one another and reinforce their sense of common belonging, fostering a sense of unity.; Historic-Artistic – Being a rare or unique example of historical, stylistic, or artistic movements now considered historical. Notre-Dame Cathedral, commonly referred to as ‘Notre-Dame’, holds international renown and serves as a symbol of French cultural heritage.; Aesthetical – Artistic – Original product of creativity and imagination. Notre-Dame Cathedral, commonly referred to as ‘Notre-Dame’, holds international renown and serves as a symbol of French cultural heritage.; Political – Symbolic – Emblematic expressions of power, authority, or prosperity deriving from the asset. Heritage sites also function as symbols of a community's cultural identity, embodying traditions, values, and practices passed down through generations, thereby fostering a sense of unity.",heritage management (2); heritage preservation (2); heritage protection; heritage management efforts,Notre-Dame Cathedral (4); Notre Dame de Paris Cathedral (2); Notre-Dame de Paris,France (6); Iraq; Southern Spain; North American; Middle Eastern; Paris (4),Middle Ages,the Notre Dame de Paris Cathedral ﬁre,This raises the pivotal question of how communities respond to such loss.,What are the community effects of the destruction of heritage sites?,Twitter/X (7); Facebook; Instagram (2),text; links; videos; emoticons,,,,likes,followers; tweet counts; likes,6394 tweets,"21,216 Twitter users",,,,,,"April 16, 2019",,"Data from Twitter/X was gathered on April 16, 2019, using Node XL Pro software",Node XL Pro software,"The selection criteria focused on tweets containing “Notre-Dame”, “Notre Dame”, “Notre_Dame”, or “Notre Dame” keywords or hashtags, or those engaged in related conversations.","Raw data was cleaned, removing irrelevant elements (HTML code elements, symbols, etc.).",,manual,linguistic researchers,"['positive', 'negative', 'neutral']",84 % coding agreement,sentiment analysis,natural language processing techniques,,,,,text,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,yes,['social network'],Twitter users,"tweets, likes, replies, referrals, and network connections","21,216","20,085","Network Modularity (NM); geodesic distance metric; Mean Geodesic Distance, MGD; Max GD",,Clauset-Newman-Moore (CNM) algorithm; Harel Koren Fast Multiscale layout algorithm,,examine social structures through network analysis,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['ensuring proper consent, data protection, and anonymity measures to comply with privacy regulations and user expectations']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,"The collected data encompassed user tweets, likes, replies, referrals, and network connections.",,,"Node XL software version 1.01.508 (Hansen et al., 2010) facilitated SNA, collecting users’ social networks and message content from Twitter."