_Chen et al.-2019-Geo-tagged photo metadata proces.txt,Article ABSTRACT:,Wen Chen; Zhiyun Xu; Yonglong Luo,,2019,journal article,,MDPI,,http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/,,,,,historical cities (1); historical sites (1),,,,,Beijing City; Melbourne,China; Hong Kong; Hainan; Beijing; Spain; Australia; Austria,,,"However, an in-depth study of the data processing methods designed to conduct tourist ﬂow prediction based on geo-tagged photo metadata has not yet been conducted.","In order to acquire accurate substitutive data regarding inbound ﬂows in cities, this paper introduces and designs several methods, including data screening, text data similarity calculation, geographical location clustering, and time series data modelling, in order to realize a data preprocessing model for inbound tourist ﬂows in cities based on geo-tagged photo metadata.",Flickr; Panoramio; Pinterest; Trip Advisor; Twitter; Weibo,geo-tagged photo metadata; text tags; geotags; image contents; time of image capture,geotags; geographic coordinates; latitude; longitude,,shooting time; time series data,,User ID; Latitude; Longitude; Location; Date & Time; Tags,"349,665 pieces of photo data from 2007 until 2016",,,,,,,2007 until 2016,Beijing,crawler code was edited with Python based on the Flickr API,Flickr API,,deleting emoji,,,,[],,time series prediction,neural network (NN),NN; SVR; ELM; word2vec,,word2vec,TF–IDF,time series of inbound tourist ﬂows; statistical yearbook tourism data,,,,,,,,,,"{'sigma': '0.1', 'C': '10', 'nhid': '12'}",,"Intel i5 2.5 Ghz processor, 8 GB memory, Win10 system",,,8 GB,,,,,[],,,,,,,,,,mean absolute error (MAE); root-mean-square error (RMSE); mean absolute percentage error (MAPE); correlation coeﬃcient (R),[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],cross-validation approach,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],"['tourism recommendation', 'tourism behavior analysis', 'tourism prediction']",[],[],[],[],"['the sample distribution of geo-tagged photo metadata is unbalanced, meaning that not all regions have suﬃcient samples available']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,Python sklearn,Python sklearn; Beautiful Soup,,geo-tagged photo metadata; inbound tourism ﬂow; big data analytics; machine learning algorithm; data correlation analysis; EXIF; UGC data; POI; word2vec; TF–IDF; DBSCAN; P-DBSCAN; N-Gram,,,
_Chen et al.-2023-A Cross-Scale Representation of.txt,A Cross-Scale Representation of Tourist Activity Space,Xinyue Chen; Yang Xu; Sangwon Park; Yimin Chen; Xintao Liu; Chengxiang Zhuge,"Department of Land Surveying and Geo-Informatics, The Hong Kong Polytechnic University, China; College of Hotel and Tourism Management, Kyung Hee University, Republic of Korea; School of Geography and Planning, and Guangdong Key Laboratory for Urbanization and Geo-Simulation, Sun Yat-sen University, China",2023,journal article,Annals of the American Association of Geographers,"Taylor & Francis Group, LLC.",10.1080/24694452.2023.2231533,https://doi.org/10.1080/24694452.2023.2231533,,2333-2358,,,,,,,,,South Korea (6),,,"Existing studies usually focused on investigating tourists’ activities and movements either at the intradestination (e.g., within a city) or interdestination scale. Although useful in numerous research contexts, these models based on fixed spatial scales are incapable of portraying the complex spatial structure of tourist activity spaces, which sometimes exhibit hierarchical structures, and could span across different spatial scales.","In this study, we introduce a new representation of tourist activity space to bridge the research gaps discussed earlier. The activity space representation aims to portray the spatial organization of tourists’ activities and the hidden hierarchies of their movements.",Twitter (1),mobile phone data (7); mobile phone trajectory data set (2); GPS data (1); digital footprints (1),GPS data (1),spatial distribution (2); spatial dispersion (1),timestamps (3); time series (1),,,,"192,302 international travelers (1)",,,,,,during a period of fifteen days (1–15 August 2018) (1),South Korea (1),anonymized mobile phone positioning data set collected by one of the major cellular operators in South Korea (1),,,conduct data cleaning to ensure reliability and generality (1),Users with a very short time span (the duration between the first and the last record is less than twelve hours) or same-day visitors (the first and the last record are within the same day). (2) Users without any records for a long time.,,,[],,clustering (2),,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,yes,['time-varying graph (2)'],locations (nodes) (1),tourist movements (paths) (1),,,,,,,,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],"['reference information for tourism bureaus on location selection of new attractions or hotels (1)', 'hotel stakeholders on targeting potential customers (1)', 'travel agencies or individuals on travel planning or itinerary design (1)']",[],['The proposed activity space representation also contributes to the study of tourism geography methodologically. (1)'],[],[],"['The study is subject to some limitations that guide the directions for future work. (1)', 'The detection of activity location involves clustering, which is based on a fixed threshold distance. (1)', 'Subject to the two-week data set, some longer journeys might be recorded incompletely. (1)', 'Given the nature of positioning data, it is hard to consider contextual determinants of behavior (Spielman and Singleton 2022), for instance, implying the reasons behind travelers’ change of accommodation. (1)']",['This study uses an anonymized mobile phone positioning data set (1)'],"['This might lead to a slight overestimation of the proportion of short-time visitors (e.g., single-NAP travelers), which is the systematic bias of the empirical results. (1)']",[],[],[],[],[],"['The study is subject to some limitations that guide the directions for future work. (1)', 'The detection of activity location involves clustering, which is based on a fixed threshold distance. (1)', 'Subject to the two-week data set, some longer journeys might be recorded incompletely. (1)', 'Given the nature of positioning data, it is hard to consider contextual determinants of behavior (Spielman and Singleton 2022), for instance, implying the reasons behind travelers’ change of accommodation. (1)']",