_Cheng et al.-2024-Effects of cultural landscape se.txt,Effects of cultural landscape service features in national forest parks on visitors’ sentiments: A nationwide social media-based analysis in China,Yingyi Cheng; Bing Zhao; Siqi Peng; Kai Li; Yue Yin; Jinguang Zhang,"College of Landscape Architecture, Nanjing Forestry University, Nanjing, China; College of Landscape Architecture, Sichuan Agricultural University, Chengdu, China",2024,journal article,Ecosystem Services,Elsevier B V,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ecoser.2024.101614,www.elsevier.com/locate/ecoser,,,Cultural Landscape (1),cultural (1),National Forest Parks (NFPs) (10),cultural heritage (3); cultural dimension of landscape services (CLSs) (5); nature-based (2),,"{'SOCIAL VALUES': 'The study mentions the importance of NFPs in nurturing positive experiences among visitors, enhancing their sentiments, and augmenting visitor well-being through recreational and social engagement. This suggests a focus on emotional (collective) values related to cultural identity and sense of place attachment.'}; {'ECONOMIC VALUES': 'The study discusses the role of NFPs in promoting nature-based tourism and providing recreational infrastructure. This indicates a consideration of entertainment values, as the assets play a role in the contemporary market, especially tourism.'}; {'POLITICAL VALUES': 'The study highlights the educational opportunities within NFPs that foster a deeper appreciation of the links between nature and biodiversity. This suggests a focus on educational values, as the heritage assets play an educational role.'}; {'AESTHETICAL VALUES': 'The study emphasizes the aesthetic and spiritual experiences offered by NFPs, ranging from the visual beauty of natural landscapes to an inspiring sense of connection with nature. This indicates a consideration of artistic values, as the assets are original products of creativity and imagination.'}",NFP management (3); NFP planning (3),267 NFPs across 31 provinces in China,Chi