_Cho et al.-2022-Classifying Tourists' Photos and.txt,Classifying Tourists' Photos and Analyzing Tourism Destination Image Using a Deep Learning Model,Nayeon Cho; Youngok Kang,"Department of Social Studies, Colledge of Education, Ewha Womans University, 52 Ewhayeodae-gil, Seodaemun-gu, Seoul 03760, South Korea",2021,journal article,,,https://doi.org/10.1080/1528008X.2021.1995567,www.tandfonline.com/journals/wqah20,,,,,traditional palaces (2),,,,,Seoul (6); Korea (5); Beijing; Hong Kong; London,Korea (5); Seoul (6); Beijing; Hong Kong; London; United States; Ottawa; Canada; Asia; America; Europe; Africa; Latin America; West Asia,,,"However, the pre-trained models have limitations of properly classifying the photos with the unique landscape or specific elements of the tourism destination.","(1) develop tourists’ photo classification by analyzing the characteristics of photos posted by tourists, (2) construct a deep learning model to accurately classify photos according to the photo classification developed, (3) analyze the TDI for Korea by combining visual contents with location and user information of photos.",SNS (3); Flickr (15); Twitter; Panoramio; Instagram,text (3); photo (20); location; time information; metadata (3); visual contents (5); image (11); video data,location (2); latitude; longitude,spatial analysis (2),time information,,,"168,216 (3)","5,609 (2)",,,,,,"January 1, 2013 to December 31, 2018",Korea,crawled,public API (Application Programming Interface) provided by Flickr,,"removing the post deleted by the user or data with latitude, longitude and temporal errors",,manually labeled,,[],,classification (13); image recognition (2); object detection,deep learning model (6); CNN (Convolutional Neural Network) (5); deep CNN,Alex Net (4); Goog Le Net; Res Net (7); VGGNet; Dense Net; Mobile Net; Inception-v3 (7); Places365_Res Net,pre-trained models (10),,,photo image data,,"60% training data, 20% validation data, and 20% test data",,Adam,0.0001,128,"25,000 for step",,panning; zooming; rotating; brightness adjustment; horizontal flip; vertical flip; shearing,{},,p3.16xlarge specification provided by Amazon Web Service,NVIDIA Tesla V100,8ea,RAM 488GB,,the original network architecture of Inception-v3 is maintained and the pre-trained weights by Image Net are used to initialize the network,"Initially, 20% of photos were manually labeled and then a deep learning model was created using the labeled data. The model developed was run repetitively to classify the remaining data. Then the results had been checked one by one as “true” or “false.” If it was determined to be “false,” a “true” label was manually assigned.",yes,[],,,,,,,k-means clustering algorithm (4); DBSCAN (density-based spatial clustering of applications with noise) (2),,,top1 accuracy (3); top5 accuracy (3); F1-socre (2); Precision (2); Recall (2); confusion matrix,"['top 1\naccuracy of 85.77%, top 5 accuracy of 95.69%, and F1 score of 0.8455', 'the classification accuracy of the model was 91.9%']",[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],matrix heatmap (3),[],[],[],[],[],[],[],['the analysis of TDI\ncan provide an idea of what images DMO shall offer to tourists and how to promote the tourism destination by understanding microscopic characteristics of regions'],"['develops a tourist photo classification suitable for local characteristics', 'shows the process of retraining a deep learning model to effectively classify tourism photos', 'shows how to analyze TDI in detail by\nROA, tourism category, and tourists’ continent by using DBSCAN, metrics heatmap, and k-means clustering methods']",[],[],"['photo classification was based on assigning one label per photo', 'it is needed to develop a hybrid deep learning model which includes text information such as tags and titles in addition to location and photo image data in Flickr metadata', 'it is necessary to incorporate other SNS data such as Instagram or video data with\nFlickr, which will make the analysis results more comprehensive and powerful']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,"python 3.6.5, anaconda 3.5.2 and Tensor Flow 1.13.0",,,,,,
_Chu and Yang-2025-Exploring Tourists' Points of I.txt,Introduction SECTION: Conclusion,Xu Chu; Byungsun Yang,,2025,journal article,J. People Plants Environ.,"the Society for People, Plants, and Environment",10.11628/ksppe.2025.28.1.63,https://doi.org/10.11628/ksppe.2025.28.1.63,,63-79,,,historical buildings (1),preservation (2); restoration (1); historical (3),,,preservation (1); restoration (1),Datang Furong Park,China,Tang Dynasty (2),,This study fills a gap in existing studies and presents the following research conclusions and specific recommendations for park management policies.,"This study combines social media reviews with text analysis to collect and analyze tourists' opinions. It comprehensively compares differences in tourists' interests across multiple dimensions (e.g., emotional categories and temporal trends), predicts future trends in tourists' interests, and examines the differences in interests and emotional experiences between local and non-local tourists.",Ctrip,"text (posts, captions, comments, reviews, hashtags)",,,temporal trends (1),,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,[],,sentiment analysis,,,,,,text tokens,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['this study has certain limitations, including the potential bias associated with using data collected solely from the ""Ctrip"" platform.', 'this study focuses on only one representative urban park, which imposes regional constraints on the findings.']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,,,,,,
_Chu et al.-2022-Language interpretation in trave.txt,Language interpretation in travel guidance platform: Text mining and sentiment analysis of Trip Advisor reviews,Miao Chu; Yi Chen; Lin Yang; Junfang Wang,"Department of Marxism, Xi’an Jiaotong University, Xi’an, China; Department of Electronic Information, Hangzhou Dianzi University, Hangzhou, China; Department of Journalism and New Media, Xi’an Jiaotong University, Xi’an, China",2022,journal article,Frontiers in Psychology,,10.3389/fpsyg.2022.1029945,,,,,,,,,,,,China; Iran; US,,,"Traditional sentiment analysis is mostly based on statistics, which can analyze the sentiment of a large number of texts. However, it is diﬃcult to classify the overall sentiment of a text, and the context-independent nature limits their representative power in a rich context, hurting performance in Natural Language Processing (NLP) tasks.",The primary objective of this study is to answer the research questions of “what travel elements greatly aﬀect tourists’ emotions? What elements of travel motivate travelers to leave emotionally charged reviews on travel platforms?”,Trip Advisor,text,,,,,,"4,000",,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,[],,sentiment analysis; classification,Transformer models,BERT,pre-trained,,TF-IDF,,,,cross entropy,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,"The structure is shown in Figure 2C. Bidirectional Encoder Representation from Transformers is based on the transformer structure, but it only uses the encoder part of the transformer. Its overall framework is made up of multiple layers of transformer’s encoder stacking.","For the sentiment classiﬁcation problem, this paper uses pretrained models trained based on Book Corpus (Zhu et al., 2015) and English Wikipedia. Based on the original network, two linear layers are used in the last layer to output the category probabilities with cross entropy as the loss, and after training on the dataset we built, the sentiment classiﬁcation of travel reviews can be ﬁnished.",no,[],,,,,,,,,,precision; recall; accuracy,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['DMO managers should focus on improving services in destinations, with particular emphasis on key elements that may contribute to negative WOM.', 'Through this study, DMOs managers can ﬁnd the deﬁciencies of destinations more accurately to improve their competitiveness more eﬀectively.']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,"The raw data supporting the conclusions of this article will be made available by the authors, without undue reservation.",,,,,,travel-related UGC; electronic word of mouth; online reviews; tourist attractions; tourism facilities; travel destination; sentiment analysis; BERT; online reviews; electronic word of mouth; travel-related UGC; Trip Advisor; Term Frequency-Inverse Document Frequency; TF-IDF; Bidirectional Encoder Representation from Transformers,,,
_Chua et al.-2016-Mapping Cilento Using geotagged.txt,Mapping Cilento: Using Geotagged Social Media Data to Characterize Tourist Flows in Southern Italy,Alvin Chua; Loris Servillo; Ernesto Marcheggiani; Andrew Vande Moere,"Department of Architecture, KU Leuven, Belgium; Department of Earth and Environmental Sciences, KU Leuven, Belgium; Department D3A, University of Marche, Italy",,other,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Cilento,Southern Italy; Tuscany; Campania; Naples; Sarleno; Sorrento; Padula; Capaccio; Agropoli; Ascea; Palinuro; Camerota; Castellabate; IT; DE; NL; Vallo di Diano,,,"As it stands, the quality of existing data is insufficient for our analysis since 153 measurements made at different spatial-temporal granularities or demographic 154 segmentations cannot be jointly analyzed without loss of precision.","This paper describes an approach to 7 analyze geotagged social media data from Twitter to characterize spatial, temporal 8 and demographic features of tourist flows in Cilento - a regional tourist attraction in 9 southern Italy.",Twitter,geotagged data; text,geotagged tweets,spatial variations; spatial diffusion,time series; temporal features,,user profiles; user Ids; time-zone; location field,"72,031","3,135",,,,,,29 May 2014 and 31 December 2014,Cilento,"gathering geotagged tweets posted within the boundaries of Cilento between 29 May 2014 and 31 December 2014 through Twitter’s stream API (Twitter, 2014b).","Twitter’s stream API (Twitter, 2014b), Twitter’s REST API (Twitter, 2014a)",,,,,,[],,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,yes,['directed graph'],vertices vi 314 ∈V are cells in the grid that corresponds to physical locations in the region,edges 315 ei∈E indicate movement pathways between cells,,,centrality,Aggregation,,,,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,,,,,,
_Ciesielski and Sterenczak-2021-Using Flickr data and selected e.txt,Using Flickr data and selected environmental characteristics to analyse the temporal and spatial distribution of activities in forest areas,Mariusz Ciesielski; Krzysztof Stere´nczak,"Department of Geomatics, Forest Research Institute, Sękocin Stary, ul. Braci Le´snej 3, 05-090 Raszyn, Poland",2021,journal article,Forest Policy and Economics,Elsevier B V,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.forpol.2021.102509,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.forpol.2021.102509,,,Cultural Ecosystem Services (CES) (2),,forest areas (20); forest spaces (3); green spaces (2); forest ecosystem (2); forest Promotional Complexes (FPC) (7),recreation (11); recreational (14); recreational activities (2); recreational function (5); recreation management (2); tourism (6); tourist (10); tourism purposes (1); cultural (4); cultural diversity (1); spiritual (1); religious values (1); knowledge sys (1); educational values (1); inspiration (1); aesthetic values (2); social relation (1); sense of place (1); cultural heritage values (1); ecotourism (1); forest management (5); forest environment (1); forest management plan (3); forest Silviculture Rules (1); forest district (2); forest use (2); forest ecosystem stability (1); forest coverage (2); nature protection (1),,"{'SOCIAL': 'Emotional (collective): The study highlights the importance of forests for recreation and improving the well-being of users, indicating a sense of place attachment and communal value associated with forest areas.'}; {'ECONOMIC': 'Entertainment: The study discusses the spatial and temporal distribution of recreational activities in forest areas, suggesting the role of forests in providing entertainment and recreational opportunities for society.'}; {'POLITICAL': 'Management: The study emphasizes the need for data and tools to minimize negative impacts on forest ecosystems, indicating the incorporation of forest management into political strategies and policies.'}; {'HISTORIC': 'Educational: The study mentions the educational values of ecosystems and the potential of forests to provide knowledge about the past, indicating an educational role of heritage assets.'}; {'AESTHETICAL': 'Notable: The study discusses the attractiveness of forest areas and the influence of landscape heterogeneity, suggesting that forests can be considered notable for their aesthetic qualities.'}; {'ECOLOGICAL': 'Spiritual: The study mentions the importance of contact with nature and the role of forests in providing recreational opportunities, suggesting a harmony between the built environment and the natural environment.'}",forest management (5); forest management plan (3),,Poland (11); Europe (3); Russia (1); Sudety (1); Karpaty Mountains (1); Warsaw (2); Krak´ow (2); Gda´nsk (2); Ł´od´z (2); Wrocław (1); Grodzisk County (1); Tuscan forest (Italy) (1); Germany (1),,pandemic COVID-19 (1),"Taking the above into account, the objective of this work was to study whether social media data may be used as a reliable data source for studies related to the recreational function of the forest.","In particular, the following goals have been defined: i) Determining the spatial and temporal distribution of recreational activities in forest areas. ii) Determining variables influencing the attractiveness of forest areas and their actual use. This work pays special attention to the tree stand characteristics, the location and topography, and socioeconomic variables. iii) Proposing groups of variables that should be taken into account when modelling the recreational potential of forest areas.",Flickr (16); Twitter (4); Instagram (4); Facebook (1),photographs (11); geolocation (6); metadata (2); spatially-oriented Big Data information (1); Volunteered Geographic Information data (1),"geolocation (6); GPS (3); X,Y coordinates (1)",spatial distribution (4); spatial variability (2),temporal distribution (4); time distribution (1); temporal variability (1),,"author (nick, owner id) (1); date and time the photo was taken (1); camera type (1); title (1); description (2); tags (1)","1,035,539 photos with geolocation were retrieved for Poland from 1/1/2010–31/12/2018","Due to privacy re­ strictions, these data only allow a small part of the user to be identified.",,"1,035,539 photos",,,,1/1/2010–31/12/2018,Poland,Photographs with geolocation were retrieved from Flickr servers using Flickr API and an appropriate query created in the R software (version 3.6),Flickr API (2),"According to methodological recommendations accepted in the literature, the photo set was filtered, leaving only one photograph taken by a single user on the given day and at the same time (Tenkanen et al., 2017).",Data were stored in a comma-separated values (csv) file and converted to a shapefile in Arc GIS 10.6.,only photographs taken in PGL LP managed areas were selected,,,[],,,Boosted Regression Trees (BRT) (7),,,,,,,The data were divided into training and verification sets in a ratio of 70 to 30,Bernoulli distribution loss function,,0.05,,,,,"{'tree complexity': '5 (the number of nodes)', 'fractions': '0.75 (ratio of data selected during every stage)'}",,,,,,,,"BRT's general idea includes generating individual trees based on a random sub-sample from the entire data set. In other words, individual trees are generated to predict the remaining items (out of all previous items) independently and randomly selected samples.",no,[],,,,,,,,,,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],10-fold cross-validation of the executed procedure,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],['tool for decision-makers who manage forest areas when making decisions regarding such places in the context of forest use for recreation and forest management (1)'],['ensure forest management is tailored to recreation and leisure needs (1)'],['The presented use of social media data in conjunction with geographic information is a novel approach in studies of forest recreation function that significantly expands the scope of knowledge in this field.'],"['Using BRT statistical models, it was possible to find factors with the most significant influence on forest area use.', ""This work uses several variables that have not been previously included in modelling forested areas' recreational potential."", 'Analysis of the Flickr data distribution made it possible to identify areas with the highest intensity of recreational use (conurbation, Forest Promotional Complexes, mountain areas) and identify times of day, week and year with the highest intensity.']",[],"['Most of the portals largely or entirely prevent the identification of motivations from spending time in forest areas.', 'It should be emphasised that despite the lack of representativeness of Flickr data populations, and the lack of information about users, the effects of using Flickr data confirm previous results obtained using traditional methods.']","['Due to privacy re\xad strictions, these data only allow a small part of the user to be identified.', 'Data access, taking into ac\xad count the privacy policy of the websites, as well as the rules of data use, usually takes place via Application Programming Interfaces (APIs), which enable large datasets to be retrieved using appropriate queries (Di Minin et al., 2015; Heikinheimo et al., 2017).', ""Their limitations are dictated by the websites' privacy policies, lack of repre\xad sentative nature of the sample, or data registration variations resulting, e.g. from population density or terrain availability (Balmford et al., 2015; Ciesielski et al., 2019).""]","['Due to these limitations and the fact that the data only comes from Flickr users, mostly young people, the data sample is not representative.']",[],[],[],[],[],"['It should be emphasised that despite the lack of representativeness of Flickr data populations, and the lack of information about users, the effects of using Flickr data confirm previous results obtained using traditional methods.']",,,,,"The calculations use the BRT model implemented in the R software, version 3.0.3 with the gbm package.",gbm package,,Big Data (3); Application Programming Interfaces (APIs) (1); State Forests National Forest Holding (PGL LP) (3); Local Administrative Unit (LAU) (2); Forest Promotional Complexes (FPC) (7); State Forest IT System (1); Numerical Forest Map (1); General Environmental Protection Directorate (1); Local Data Bank of Statistics Poland (1); CORINE Land Cover (1); Open Street Map (1); Shuttle Radar Topography Mission (1),,,
