_Collini et al.-2023-Reputation assessment and visito.txt,Reputation assessment and visitor prediction in cultural heritage sites by exploiting social media and data analysis,Enrico Collini; Paolo Nesi; Gianni Pantaleo,,2023,journal article,Online Social Networks and Media,Elsevier,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.osnem.2023.100274,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.osnem.2023.100274,,,cultural heritage sites (2),,attractions (4); cultural heritage sites (1); tourism destinations (1); touristic attractions (4); Uffizi Gallery (6); Florence (4); Pont du Gard (5); Pont-Du-Gard cultural attraction (1); Uffizi Museum (1),reputation (31); online reputation (8); tourism (17); touristic (4); cultural heritage sites (1); cultural attraction (1); tourism management (2); tourism demand (5); tourist (11); tourists (10); attractions (4); touristic attractions (4); tourism services (2); tourism business (1); touristic attractions (2); tourism industries (1); tourism sentiment classification (1); tourism opinions (1); tourism metrics forecasting (1); tourism management (1); tourism data (1); tourism attractions (3); cultural attraction (1),,"{'SOCIAL': 'Emotional (collective) – The study aims to improve tourist experience and market strategies, which implies understanding the cause-effect phenomena from promotion on social media to the number of presences. This relates to cultural identity and pride.'}; {'ECONOMIC': 'Entertainment – The study focuses on tourism services and attractions, aiming to provide decision-makers with predictive tools related to online reputation and number of presences in touristic attractions. This directly relates to the role the asset plays in the contemporary market, especially tourism.'}; {'POLITICAL': 'Management – The study aims to provide decision-makers with predictive tools related to tourism services, which can be used for political strategies and policies related to tourism management.'}; {'HISTORIC': 'Educational – The study uses data-driven approaches, such as machine learning and data analytics, to empower decision-makers with the ability to anticipate changes in online reputation and number of presences in touristic attractions. This relates to the potential of the asset to provide knowledge about the past in the future.'}",tourism management (2); Online Reputation Management (3),Florence; Pont du Gard; Uffizi Gallery; Firenze; Mount Siguniang; Jiuzhaigou; Republic of Macedonia; Taiwan; Bangkok,"Italy (2); France (3); Spain (1); Bosnia and Herzegovina (1); Croatia (1); Greece (1); Manhattan, New York City (1); Finland (1); Moroccan (1); China (3); Taiwan (1)",,,"Decision makers seek frameworks capable of assessing the online reputation of attractions, forecasting the indicators, and predicting the number of presences in advance.","The main objectives of this research are related to presenting an integrated framework mainly focused on reputation and related effects, which allows to perform the: • Estimation and prediction of reputation as to touristic attractions. • Long term prediction of presences attending touristic attractions. • Causality analysis allowed to understand drivers and motivations to attract tourists in specific locations.",social media (12); Trip Advisor (18); Twitter (24); TW (3),social media data (6); comments (3); reviews (11); scores (8); tweets (13); retweets (7); text (5); images (2); geolocations (1); weather data (2); historical data (2); data from sensors (2); tickets (2); presences (2),,,time-series data (2); time-series prediction (1); time-series forecasting (2); temporal features (3); temporal shifts (2); temporal window (4); temporal targets (1); temporal resolution (1),stars (6); scores (4),,"About 2 M of tweets/retweets in the period since January 2018 up to December 2019, related to Firenze and Uffizi Gallery keywords, hashtags, citations, etc., acquired and processed in real-time through the Twitter Vigilance platform [11].",,"About 7300 regarding the Uffizi Gallery reputation. Trip Advisor scores are reported in a scale from 1 to 5 stars, where 3 is considered neutral, 4 and 5 positive and 1 and 2 negative.",,,,,January 2018 up to December 2019,Florence and Pont du Gard,collected from official reports,Twitter Vigilance platform [11],,,,"annotation tool for multilingual SA, enabling mother tongue experts to annotate the text relevant to the tourism with a SA",mother tongue experts,"['negative', 'neutral', 'positive', 'skip']",,prediction (12); sentiment analysis (10); regression (4); classification (3); forecasting (10),machine learning (6); deep learning (8); ensemble learning (4); random forest (RF) (3); gradient boosting machines (XGBoost) (2); recurrent neural networks (RNNs) (2); temporal convolutional networks (TCN) (5); temporal fusion transformers (TFT) (9); Artificial Neural Network (ANN (1); Support Vector Regressor (SVR (3); Gated Recurrent Unit (GRU (2); Long Short-Term Memory networks (LSTM (4); ARIMAX (1); SVM (2); RF (1),BERT (3),fine-tuning of a multilingual Bert Transformer model [51],,,,,"80% for training, 10% for validation and 10% as a test set",,Adam optimizer,0.00005,16,15,,,{},,,,,,,,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,MAE (7); MAPE (7); R-squared (R2) (4); RMSE (4); F1score (1); Precision (2); Recall (2); Accuracy (2),[],[],[],p-value (6),,[],[],,[],[],[],"cross validation has been used to fit this model, particularly in the configuration leave-on-out",,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['The proposed framework combines BERT sentiment analysis, forecasting AI architectures, and XAI techniques.']",[],[],[],[],['This unbalanced distribution is not ideal and could create biases in the SA model.'],[],[],[],[],[],[],,The authors do not have permission to share data.,,,,,,word of mouth; web reputation; Destination Branding; Online Reputation Management; big data; data analytics; sentiment classification; human-centered artificial intelligence (HCAI); Big Data; artificial intelligence; eXplainable AI (XAI); Natural Language processing (NLP); Sentiment Analysis (SA); Progressive Mean of Reputation (PMR); Daily Mean Reputation (DMR); local interpretable model-agnostic explanations (LIME); Snap4City; Granger causality analysis,,,
_Comalada et al.-2025-Using georeferenced text from so.txt,Full Length Article SECTION: Body Using georeferenced text from social media to map the cultural ecosystem services of freshwater ecosystems,F. Comalada; O. Llorente; V. Acu˜na; J. Sal´o; X. Garcia,"Catalan Institute for Water Research (ICRA - CERCA). Carrer Emili Grahit 101 17003 Girona, Spain",2025,journal article,Ecosystem Services,Elsevier,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ecoser.2025.101702,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ecoser.2025.101702,,,,,river ecosystems (4); freshwater ecosystems (7); river landscape,Cultural ecosystem services (CES) (20); ecosystem services (3); conservation (2); restoration; river restoration; river conservation; sustainable ecosystem management; environmental planning; policy,,,conservation; restoration; planning,Ter River; Fluvi`a basin; Forth basin; Scarce basin; Ter River (Catalonia); Fluvi`a (Catalonia); Forth (Scot­land); Scarce (France and Belgium),Spain; Catalonia (3); Scotland (2); France; Belgium; Europe; China,,,"Despite the value of social media data containing text for mapping CES, its practical application beyond academic research to facilitate decision-making has rarely been realized. A major barrier is the scarcity of integrated tools that non-expert users can employ to effectively obtain, treat, process, and present this data, transforming it into useful information for decision-makers","To address this challenge, our aim was to develop a methodological framework capable of using georeferenced text from social media to map different CES of specific ecosystems. This framework aims to automate the various steps of CES mapping (extraction, treatment, analysis, and mapping), ensuring user-friendliness and accessibility.",social media (11); Twitter/X (10); Flickr (4); Strava; Wikiloc; Google Earth; Instagram (4); Trip Advisor; Google Maps; Bluesky,text (10); geotagged photos; image-based approaches; text-based information; images; georeferenced text; georeferenced text-based data,"georeferenced text; geotagged; geographic parameters; X, Y coordinates; bounding box; locations of these points (X, Y coordinates); radius parameter; georeferenced posts",spatial distribution; spatial heterogeneity; spatial scales; spatial patterns,over time (2); temporal; date of creation of the tweet; annual evolution; temporal trends; annual variations; daily database; temporal variations,n_retweets; n_likes,tweet_id; tweet_text; author_id; n_retweets; n_likes; created_at; id; coord_x; coord_y,"764,226 tweets were extracted",,,,,,,since Twitter’s inception in 2006,"Ter River, Fluvi`a, Forth, and Scarce",Twitter/X API,Twitter/X API V2,points spaced 250 m apart. A radius of 500 m was set as the extraction area around each point,"removing emojis, removing hashtags (while preserving the meaning and context of the text), removing links, and removing both the “@” symbol and the attached text (such as usernames)","keyword-based filter was applied using the words: channel, dam, ditch, fall, pond, reservoir, river, riverbank, stream, waterfall, weir, and wetland","manually extracted, filtered, and classified a set of tweets from a river based on expert knowledge",two co-authors who are experts in the field,"['seven CES categories, based on the content of the tweets and derived from the CES categorization of (Cheng et al., 2019)', 'Aesthetic values', 'Recreation and ecotourism', 'Cultural heritage', 'Educational values', 'Stewardship', 'Nature fascination', 'Information']",This collaborative approach ensured a high level of consistency and accuracy in the classification process,classification (10); Natural Language Pro­cessing (NLP) (3); text classification,,Multinomial Naive Bayes (MNB) algorithm (3); BERT (2),,,,text,,"70 % of the classified tweets from the Ter case are used for training the AI algorithm, with the remaining 30 % reserved for vali­ dation purposes",,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,"The text within the training dataset of tweets had to be processed before the AI training. Specifically, this involved two steps: “tokeniza­ tion” and “lemmatization.” Both processes were conducted using the NLTK Python library. In the Tokenization the text is separated into in­ dividual words that the model will later evaluate. For example, if the text was “They are playing in the park,” the result after tokenization would be: “They,” “are,” “playing” “in,” “the,” “park.” In the Lemmati­ zation the text is normalized by transforming each word to its base or root form. Continuing the previous example, the result after lemmati­ zation would be: “They,” “be,” “play,” “in,” “the,” “park.”.",no,[],,,,,,,,,,Bayesian Average Model (BAM),[],[],[],Generalized Linear Mixed Model (GLMM) (3); Negative Binomial GLMM model,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],density plot,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['methodological framework for CES mapping', 'Tweet My River QGIS plug-in']",[],[],"['the representativeness of Twitter/X users poses another limitation, as social media data does not fully reflect real-world demographics or behaviors, hindering broader generalizations', 'Issues such as gender bias (Ghermandi et al., 2023) and non-neutrality in usergenerated content (Kubota et al., 2024) are well-documented and not unique to this platform.', 'These biases, along with limitations in data accessibility and ethical concerns related to privacy and consent, constrain the practical application of social media-based research\n(Ghermandi et al., 2023).']",[],"['Issues such as gender bias (Ghermandi et al., 2023) and non-neutrality in usergenerated content (Kubota et al., 2024) are well-documented and not unique to this platform.']",[],[],[],[],[],"['the representativeness of Twitter/X users poses another limitation, as social media data does not fully reflect real-world demographics or behaviors, hindering broader generalizations']",Data will be made available on request.,Data will be made available on request.,,,,NLTK Python library; Python library sklearn; deep_translate,,Tweet My River (4); QGIS (4); river vector layer; API key; keyword file; a priori filter (5); a posteriori filter (7); TUD filtering; Photo-User Day criterion; Tweet-User Day; deep-translate; Google Translate API (3); Python (4); Excel (4); Git Hub; sklearn; BAM; VGI; PPGIS,,,"The tool’s code was updated in June 2024 to comply with the current Twitter/X API, but its functionality remains limited due to the high cost of the required licenses."
_Constantinou et al.-2022-EnterCY A Virtual and Augmented.txt,Enter CY: A Virtual and Augmented Reality,,,2022,conference paper,23rd IEEE International Conference on Mobile Data Management (MDM),IEEE,10.1109/MDM55031.2022.00069,https://www.mdpi.com/2071-1050/12/16/6592,,314,Cultural Heritage (2),,archaeological sites (3),,,"{'SOCIAL VALUES': ""Cultural identity, motivation and pride, sense of “place attachment,” and communal value. The platform aims to enhance tourists' experiences and promote cultural dissemination, fostering a sense of connection to the heritage of Cyprus.""}; {'HISTORIC VALUES': 'Potential of the asset to provide knowledge about the past in the future. The platform includes virtual reconstructions of archaeological sites as they stood at different points in time, providing users with a historical perspective.'}; {'AESTHETICAL VALUES': 'Original product of creativity and imagination. The digital collection of tourist attractions and cultural heritage items is captured in high resolution 3D, focusing on shapes, textures, and colors.'}",,Cyprus (5),Cyprus (5); Republic Of Cyprus,,COVID-19 pandemic outbreak,"These challenges primarily relate to the industry’s long-standing pursuit of novel and effective ways for: (i) increasing tourism satisfaction, which affects destination loyalty intention [1] in the form of repeat visits and a keen willingness to recommend destinations to others; and (ii) effectively promoting destinations to attract travelers, who currently lack the means for discovering and exploring the hidden gems of different tourism destinations.","Enter CY is an integrated platform that leverages and gracefully combines the state-of-the-art technologies to enhance tourists’ experiences before, during and after their visit to Cyprus",You Tube; social media platforms (2),images (3); videos (4); audios; 3D content; structured text; unstructured or semi-structured text,GPS geo-location; coordinates,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,[],,recommendation,machin