_Corinna et al.-2015-Digital Social Media to Enhance.txt,Digital Social Media to Enhance Public Spaces of Historic City Centers,Corinna Morandi; Rocco Palmieri; Bojan Stojanovic; Luca Tomarchio,,2015,other,,Springer International Publishing Switzerland,,,,,Cultural Heritage (1),historic (6),historic city center (7); ancient municipalities (1); historic public realm (2); historic city (1),UNESCO (3); integral conservation (1); architectural and historical heritage (1); UNESCO site (1),,"{'SOCIAL VALUES': 'Cultural identity, motivation and pride, sense of “place attachment,” and communal value. The study aims to strengthen community ties and reinforce common attachment toward venues, suggesting a focus on collective emotional values.'}; {'HISTORIC VALUES': 'Potential of the asset to provide knowledge about the past in the future. The paper discusses the historic city center of Urbino, listed under UNESCO patronage since 1983, thanks to its prominent historic heritage dated back to the Renaissance.'}; {'AESTHETICAL VALUES': 'Original product of creativity and imagination. The paper mentions the high quality spaces of the historic city center, suggesting an appreciation for artistic and aesthetic values.'}",preservation (1),Urbino (17); Marche region (1),Italian peninsula (2); Italy (2),Renaissance (1),,"Potentialities and limitations, created by the use of digital social media for urban analysis and planning, are spotted regarding the specific conditions of an historic city center with the goal of creating a more livable public realm.","The research aims at drafting a general methodology both in data mining both in public places promotion and enhancement, through in- formation and digital connection, referring to the specific case of historic city centers.",social media (15); digital social media (DSM) (6); Foursquare (2); Flickr (1); Instagram (5); Facebook (1),data (14); media contents (3); pictures (2); geo-location (1),geo-location (1),,real time (3),,age (1); gend