_Corrado et al.-2024-Tourism Asset and Spatial Comple.txt,Tourism Asset and Spatial Complexity Analyzed,S. Corrado; R.V. Gatto; F. Scorza,,2023,other,18th International Forum on Knowledge Asset Dynamics (IFKAD) - Managing Knowledge For Sustainability,,,https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-39646-5_42,,,cultural heritage (5),cultural (2); natural (1); recreational heritage (1),minor cultural places (1); local cultural heritage (2); tourist attraction (3); tourism-related services (3); local historical and identitary assets (1); cultural activities (1); Italy’s cultural heritage (1),sustainable tourism (2); sustainable development (1); heritage fruition (1); Green Deal (1),,"{'SOCIAL': 'Emotional (collective): The study aims to revitalize communities and enhance the relationship between travelers and local historical assets, indicating a focus on cultural identity and a sense of place attachment.'}; {'ECONOMIC': 'Use: The paper discusses the function and utility of tourism assets in revitalizing communities and enhancing the relationship between travelers and local historical assets.'}; {'POLITICAL': 'Management: The study discusses the incorporation of tourism assets into political strategies and policies, particularly in the context of EU cohesion policy and the promotion of sustainable tourism.'}; {'HISTORIC': 'Educational: The paper aims to revitalize communities and enhance the relationship between travelers and local historical assets, indicating a focus on the potential of these assets to provide knowledge about the past.'}; {'AESTHETICAL': 'Notable: The paper aims to revitalize communities and enhance the relationship between travelers and local historical assets, indicating a focus on the artistic and cultural value of these assets.'}; {'SCIENTIFIC': 'Technological: The paper discusses the use of digital technologies and spatially explicit models to facilitate context-aware socio-economic growth, indicating a focus on the technological aspects of heritage managem