_Dai et al.-2019-Perceptions of Cultural Ecosyste.txt,Article ABSTRACT:,P.D.; S.Z.; Z.C.; H.H.; Y.G.,,2019,journal article,Sustainability,"MDPI, Basel, Switzerland",,https://population.un.org/ wup/,,14,,,city parks (2); urban parks (10); urban ecosystem,cultural ecosystem service (11); cultural heritage (10); biodiversity conservation; National Forest City; National Ecological Garden City; Habitat Scroll of Honor Award; cultural relics (2); tombs (2); antiques; monuments,,"{'SOCIAL': ""Emotional (collective): The study explores how urban parks contribute to residents' sense of place and cultural identity by providing spaces for recreation, aesthetics, and spiritual experiences.""}; {'ECONOMIC': 'Entertainment: The study analyzes online comments from social media to understand how tourists perceive and value urban parks for leisure and recreation activities.'}; {'POLITICAL': 'Educational: The study highlights the educational role of urban parks by examining how visitors gain knowledge about history, culture, and nature through park visits and exhibitions.'}; {'HISTORIC': 'Symbolic: The study acknowledges the symbolic association of urban parks with historical events and cultural heritage, particularly in cities like Xuzhou with a rich history.'}; {'AESTHETICAL': 'Artistic: The study emphasizes the aesthetic value of urban parks by analyzing how visitors appreciate the beautiful natural landscapes and artistic elements within the parks.'}; {'SCIENTIFIC': 'Workmanship: The study implicitly discusses the value of workmanship by recognizing the human effort and craftsmanship involved in creating and maintaining urban parks.'}; {'AGE': 'Existential: The study touches on the existential value of urban parks by acknowledging their role in preserving memory and connecting people to past generations through historical sites and cultural heritage.'}; {'ECOLOGICAL': 'Spiritual: The study implicitly discusses the spiritual value of urban parks by recognizing their role in fostering harmony between the built environment and nature, providing spaces for relaxation and spiritual experiences.'}",,Xuzhou City; Yunlong Lake Park; Kuaizai Ting Park; Chuwang Tomb in Han Culture Park; Han Tomb in Guishan Park; Aquarium Exhibition Hall in Yunlong Lake Park; zoo in Pengzu Park; Jiulong Lake; Kuishan; Wuming Shan; Quanshan Forest Park; Dalong Lake Park; Jinlong Lake; Hubu Shan Park; Ancient Yellow River Park; Yunlong Park; Zhushan relics Park; Xima tai Park; Huai Hai Campaign Memorial Tower Park; Xuzhou Botanical Park,Xuzhou; Jiangsu Province; Eastern China; China; Paraguay; Upper Parana Atlantic Forest Rainforest,Han Dynasty,,"With the advent of the era of network big data, social media provides a new data source for the study of cultural ecosystem service perception, so that the study of these services is expected to make new breakthroughs.","This study addressed three questions. First, how does online comment data match the various categories of cultural ecosystem services? Second, can the types of cultural ecosystem services provided by each park be determined based on online comments? Third, how can diﬀerences in the perception of the cultural ecosystem services provided by each park be quantiﬁed based on comment data?",Ctrip Travel; Baidu Travel; Tuniu Travel; Trip Advisor; Travelocity; Booking.com; Hotels.com,online comments; photographs,,,comment publication date,scoring evaluation,username; comment publication date; comment content; scoring evaluation; picture sharing functions,7257,135 million users,"323,189 words",,,,,from 17 April 2012 to 28 September 2018,19 parks in Xuzhou,"Using Gooseeker search crawler software, the comment data (in Chinese) provided by users of 19 parks in Xuzhou from 17 April 2012 to 28 September 2018 were collected from the above three tourist social networking sites, including 7257 comments (Figure 2) and 323,189 words.",Gooseeker search crawler software,,"Then, all these data were imported into a database, the comment content was sorted alphabetically, and 135 duplicate reviews and invalid comments were deleted",135 duplicate reviews and invalid comments were deleted,Delphi expert method,ten experts in the ﬁeld of ecology and land resource management,"['aesthetics', 'recreation', 'sports', 'inspiration', 'education', 'cultural heritage', 'spiritual satisfaction']",,semantic analysis,,,,,,comment sentences,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,Pearson correlation coeﬃcient,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],Arc GIS,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['Information about individual commentators is diﬃcult to collect.', 'The classiﬁcation of keywords.', 'Comprehensiveness of comment data issues.']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,,,search crawler software; Rost Content mining semantic analysis software; Delphi expert method; Arc GIS software; social network data; online shopping review data; tourism website online comment data; Gooseeker search crawler software; ROST Content Mining software; Word Art,,,
