_Date and Allweil-2022-Towards a new image archive for.txt,Towards a new image archive for architectural and urban history: A method using machine learning,Kartikeya Date; Yael Allweil,"Faculty of Architecture & Town Planning, Technion, Israel Institute of Technology; Faculty of Architecture and Town Planning at the Technion, Israel Institute of Technology, Haifa, Israel",2022,journal article,,,,https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0226-9527,,519–534,world heritage site (1); urban heritage (2),,built environment (4); Historic Urban Landscapes (HUL) (5); historic center (1); urban landscape (2); modernist buildings (2); urban heritage (1); period architecture (1); building facades (2); urban blocks (2); building by-laws (1),HUL (5); UNESCO (2); preservation (1),,"{'value': 'Emotional (collective)', 'reasoning': ""The study focuses on the urban history and modernist legacy of Tel Aviv, which is identified as a UNESCO world heritage site, suggesting a sense of cultural identity and pride associated with the city's heritage.""}; {'value': 'Educational', 'reasoning': 'The study aims to augment the existing capacity to develop case studies and enrich the study of architectural history, indicating an educational role of heritage assets in providing knowledge about the past.'}; {'value': 'Aesthetical', 'reasoning': 'The study focuses on the aesthetic changes and density requirements in the building by-laws of Tel Aviv during the 1980s, indicating an artistic and conceptual value related to the built environment.'}",preservation (1),Tel Aviv (12),Israel (2); Mumbai India (1); Haifa (2),1920s–1930s (1),,"The ever-growing online corpus of images of the built environment, on social media and mapping platforms, offers a new kind of archive of the built environment.","In this paper, we propose a new method by which historians of the built envi- ronment can use these vast image corpuses in their study, enabling new research questions.",Google Street View (3),images (7),geotagged (2),,,,,,,,"12,500 (1)",,,,,Tel Aviv (2),web-based interface (1),Google Street View API (1),"select the identified urban blocks to demonstrate one of various semantic features modeled in each swatch, which are later applied to other urban blocks (1)",labeling and verifying the training data (1),,expert-tagged images (1),PI and post-doc experts in Tel Aviv’s architectural and urban history (1),['semantic swatches (6)'],,,convolutional neural networks (CNN) (2),,,,,image pixels (1),,,,,,,,standard data augmentation technique (1),"different field-of-view, pitch and heading (1)",{},,,,,,,,"The architectural historians involved are specialists in architectural history of the 20th century, specifically of the city of Tel Aviv (Allweil, 2016a, 2016b; Allweil and Zemer, 2019). These experts designed the swatches.",no,[],,,,,,,,,,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,Keras (1),,semantic swatches (6); building facades (2); urban blocks (2); building by-laws (1),,,
_de Los Ríos Pérez et al.-2014-Using augmented reality and soci.txt,Using Augmented Reality and Social Media in Mobile,de Los Ríos Pérez et al.,,2014,other,,,,,,,cultural heritage (13),,cultural artefacts (3); cultural items (1); historical palace (1); fortress complex (1); Monumental Complex of Alhambra and Generalife (4); Palace of Charles V (3); Nasrid Palaces (2); Alcazaba (1); Generalife Palace and Gardens (1); Court of the Lions (2),lifelong engagement (2); curated content (2); cultural sector (1); cultural institutions (3); cultural resources (1); cultural experience (2); cultural events (1); cultural site (5); cultural heritage sites (1); heritage sites (1); heritage institution (2); digital technologies (1); digital artefact (1); digital objects (1); social tagging (2); social virtual spaces (1); social networks (4); archaeological sites (1); museums (2); archives (1); scholarly collections (1); exhibitions (2); virtual guardian (1),,"{'SOCIAL': 'Emotional (collective): The paper discusses how augmented reality and social media can enhance visitor experiences and create personalized interactions with cultural heritage, fostering a sense of connection and cultural identity.'}; {'ECONOMIC': 'Entertainment: The paper explores how gamification and serious games can educate and entertain visitors, enhancing the appeal of cultural heritage sites and potentially increasing tourism.'}; {'HISTORIC': ""Educational: The paper highlights the potential of augmented reality to provide additional information about cultural artifacts and sites, enriching the visitor's understanding of history and culture.""}; {'AESTHETICAL': 'Artistic: The paper mentions the beauty of the Court of the Lions, suggesting that the aesthetic qualities of heritage sites contribute to visitor engagement and appreciation.'}",,"Monumental Complex of Alhambra and Generalife; Granada, Spain; London; St Etienne Cathedral in Metz",Europeans; European; Granada city; Spain; London,,,"heritage sector fac