_de Santana et al.-2025-Investigating cultural ecosystem.txt,Investigating cultural ecosystem services of the Caatinga,TITLE:; ABSTRACT:,,2025,journal article,Ethnobiol Conserv,,,,,,,,,Cultural ecosystem services (CES) (4); ecosystem services (3); Cultural Services (1),,"Aesthetical: The study mentions the aesthetic value of animals, indicating an appreciation for their beauty and visual appeal. The authors highlight that the interest in animal life may be attributed to aesthetic value.; Recreational: The study discusses social activities such as hiking, fishing, and cycling, which are recreational activities that contribute to cultural ecosystem services. The authors mention that CES provide recreational opportunities.; Spiritual: The study mentions religious activities as part of social activities, indicating a spiritual connection to nature. The authors highlight the importance of human-nature interaction in development, including religious initiatives.",,Caatinga (8); Catimbau National Park; Serra da Capivara,Brazil (3); northeast Brazil; Pernambuco; Piauí; NE Brazil,,,These issues highlight an urgent need for innovative conservation strategies.,This study aimed to identify the cultural ecosystem services (CES) that generate the most interest among social media users and evaluate the feasibility of utilizing social media and deep learning to gather data on public interest in the Caatinga region.,Flickr (10),photographs (12); videos (2),geotagged photographs,,,,tags (3),1500,,,1500,,,,between 2012 and 2022,Brazil,downloaded,Flickr application programming interface (API),,removal of photographs that did not conform to the selected criteria for each category and duplicated images,,"manual classification based on visual analysis of photographs, and DL classification",,"['Nature Appreciation - Animals', 'Nature Appreciation - Plants', 'Landscape Appreciation', 'Social Activities', 'Artistic and Cultural Expression']",,image classification (4),convolutional neural network (CNN) (3),,,,,pixels in photographs,,,,,,,,data augmentation; abandonment functions,,{},,,,,,,"The main point of the model is formed by a CNN, which has layers that simulate groups of neurons, detect the attributes of the presented image, and organize them hierarchically and in an abstract manner to generate information","The image classification model consists of data preprocessing and standardization, convolutional neural network (CNN), training, and validation.",no,[],,,,,,,,,,accuracy (3),"['The DL model achieved an accuracy of 100% using the training data and 59% using the validation data', 'After the data increase and abandonment functions, the model achieved 100% accuracy in training and 63% accuracy in validation']",[],[],"chi-square test (χ2 = 84.535, p < 0.0001)",,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['Flickr may not be the most appropriate platform for collecting data for this biome, as evidenced by the insufficient photographs gathered and analyzed in our investigation.']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],https://colab.research.google.com,The data are available upon reasonable request.,,,,Tensor Flow; Matplotlib; Numpy; PIL; Keras,,,,,
