_Derdouri and Osaragi-2021-A machine learning-based approac.txt,A machine learning-based approach for classifying tourists and locals from geotagged photos,Ahmed Derdouri; Toshikazu Osaragi,,2021,other,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Tokyo,Japan; Tokyo; Germany; Florida; USA; Beijing; China; Manhattan Island of New York City; Paris; France; London; UK; San Francisco; New York City,,COVID-19 crisis,distinguishing between tourists and locals from this data is problematic since residence information is often not provided.,"this paper proposes a method for classifying tourists and residents based on machine learning (ML) algorithms and considering parameters that could explain the variability between the two (e.g., weather, mobility, and photo content).",Flickr; Instagram; Twitter,photos; geotagged photos; metadata; GPS,spatial coordinates; latitude; longitude; geographical bounding box,spatial distribution; spatial patterns; spatial extent; spatial dispersal; spatial density,temporal distribution; hourly patterns; monthly patterns; time spent at certain locations; posting time,,photo id; URLs; taken datetime; uploaded datetime; latitude; longitude; title; description; tags; user ID; country; city; hometown,"150,688",3063,,,,,,"July 1, 2008, to December 31, 2019",Tokyo,collect photo records with spatial coordinates,Flickr API,"study area was divided into small grids of 27.5 ­km2, and the authors searched for photos during a short period of time, ranging from one hour to 1 month, depending on the volume of records found in each of these grids.","applied the following rules: •	 Users with at least two photos were chosen. Then, we checked to see whether at least two of their photos were taken for 1 day. If not, they were excluded from the analysis. This condition was added to permit the calculation of mobility indicators (see Sect. 3.2.2). •	 For each user, a single photo record was kept when multiple photos were taken continuously at the same latitude and longitude. •	 “Snapshot effect” was defined as the bias that might be introduced by “active users”—that is, uploaders who contribute large numbers of photographs (Hollenstein and Purves 2010). This bias might lead to a study area dominated by the behaviors of active users (Hu et al. 2015). To minimize this effect, only one record was retained if several images were taken within the same minute. •	 If a user’s account indicated that the user had taken photos at the same time (i.e., within the same minute) at different geographical locations separated by at least 13 m (Merry and Bettinger 2019), those records were removed.",users with at least two photos,multi-labeling photos via DL techniques,,"['Nature', 'Culture', 'Business', 'Amusement', 'Infrastructure', 'Residence', 'Crowd', 'Other']",,classification; multi-labeling,stacked ensemble; gradient boosting machine; generalized linear model; distributed random forest; deep learning; extremely randomized trees; convolutional neural network,Mobile Net V2,"Mobile Net V2 model had already been trained using the Image Net dataset (Russakovsky et al. 2015), we left the trained parameters unchanged and only fine-tuned the whole network during training.",,,weather conditions; distances to different POIs; population density; human mobility measures; TEN; SEN; period of stay; photo count; average probabilities of the most visited locations; the number of photos taken for each category,,70:30,,,,,the number of epochs,,,"{'activation function': '', 'optimizer': '', 'the number of epochs': ''}",,,,,,,"The model was based on the transfer-learning approach, using the Mobile Net V2 architecture (Sandler et al. 2018).","The model was trained and validated on threefold splits of a 70:30 ratio.2 The splits were generated to obtain a balanced mix of samples across the eight categories. Therefore, the authors applied the stratification method proposed by Sechidis et al. (2011) and improved by Szymański and Kajdanowicz (2017).",no,[],,,,,,,,,,accuracy; Logarithmic loss; F1 score; AUC; AUPRC; Gini coefficient,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],tenfold cross-validation,TEN-based approach,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],The Python code used to produce the paper’s results is available from the authors upon request.,,,,,H2O,,,,,
_Derdouri and Osaragi-2021-Exploring the Differences Betwee.txt,Exploring the Differences Between Tourists and Locals in,,,,other,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Tokyo (2),Japan (2); Tokyo Metropolitan Area,,,Understanding how tourists and locals behave in urban settings is crucial to tourism and urban planning.,"(1) to multi-label geotagged and time-stamped photos taken by both groups and, eventually, (2) compare the spatial and temporal distributions based on their popular activities and/or most frequented places.",Flickr (6); Open Street Map,geotagged photos (5); spatial coordinates,spatial coordinates (2); geographic coordinates,spatial distribution (2); density analysis; hexagonal grid,time-stamped photos; temporal variations; monthly variations; hourly variations,,photo ID; URLs; date and time information; latitude and longitude; title; tags; user ID; country; city,"150,688","3,063",,,,,,"July 1, 2008, to December 31, 2019",Tokyo,API,application programming interface (API) (2),,"Users with less than two records were excluded. • When photos were taken continuously at the same spot, only one record was kept. • Similarly, one record was retained when a user took several photos within the same minute. • In the case of two records of the same user, we filtered out those records that were taken within the same minute in two distinct geographical locations distant from each other by more than 13 meters.",records with spatial coordinates located within the boundary box covering the extent of Tokyo,manually,authors,"['amusement', 'business', 'culture', 'crowd', 'nature', 'infrastructure', 'residence', 'other']",,multi-label classification (4); image labeling (2); single-label image classification (4),convolutional neural network (CNN) (3),Mobile Net V2 (4); Res Net (3); Res Net-101; Inception v3,Mobile Net V2 model had already been trained using the Image Net dataset. We kept the trained parameters unchanged and only fine-tuned the entire network during testing,,,,,70:30,,,,,,,,{},,10-Intel-core i9-10900X,,,120 GB RAM,,,"We then developed a model using the transferlearning approach based on the Mobile Net V2 architecture, which was selected because of its capacity to (i) avoid issues related to overfitting due to the relatively small training dataset as well as (ii) minimize the execution time and memory consumption while minimizing prediction errors.",,[],,,,,,,,,,mean accuracy; microaveraged area under the curve; microaveraged area under the precision-recall curve,"['mean accuracy of 83.46%', 'microaveraged area under the curve of 0.87', 'microaveraged area under the precision-recall curve of 0.78']",[],[],Chi-squared test (2); ordinary least squares (OLS) (4),,[],[],,[],[],[],threefold splits of a 70:30 ratio,,[],heatmaps (3),[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['the limited number of categories considered to reflect the nature of activities or locations both group populations tend to carry out or go to.', 'Flickr does not account for the actions of the general public, given that not all Internet users take pictures, much less post them on social media.']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,Arc Map,,,,,
_Derungs and Purves-2016-Characterising landscape variati.txt,Characterising landscape variation through spatial folksonomies,C. Derungs; R.S. Purves,,2016,journal article,Applied Geography,Elsevier,,,,60e70,,,,natural features (11); landscape (20); toponyms (2); spatial folksonomies (14); cultural ecosystem services (2),,,,Switzerland (10); Swiss Alps (2); Bernese Oberland (1); Valais (1); Jura mountains (1); Mittelland (2); Matterhorn (2); Salbit (1); Finster- aarhorn (3); Bernina regions (1); Thun (4); Uetliberg (3); Lenzerheide (1); Toggenburg (1); Pre-Alps (2),Switzerland (10); Swiss Alps (2),20th century (1),climate change through deglaciation (1),"current land use, land cover and landscape classiﬁcations typically reﬂected a top-down pro- cess, especially with respect to the involvement of non-experts.","explore how these term vectors could be used to form spatial folksonomies, and in particular the related reproducibility (RQ1), comparability (RQ2) and utility (RQ3) of such data structures",,text (10),,,,,,"Text þ Berg: 10,000 articles, HIKR: 25,000 articles",,,,,,,post-1950,Switzerland,digitized and preprocessed Text þ Berg corpus,,,,,manual,inter-annotator agreement,['natural landscape features'],,,,,,tf-idf values (4),,natural feature terms,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,Kolmogorov-Smirnov test (1); p-value (1),[],[],[],statistically signiﬁcant differences (Kolmo- gorov-Smirnov test with p-value<0.05) (1); About 25% of all pairwise correlations are statistically signiﬁcant (Table 2). (1),,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],"['generating spatial queries using folk landscape terms (such as ridge, summit or forest) and ranking documents according to the prevalence of such terms in a particular region']","['providing ways of exploring the appropriateness of current land cover and land use classiﬁcations at a local level, and in providing ways of linking rich text descriptions to existing ways of classifying land cover and land use.']","['Using diverse, rich tex- tual corpora we captured, at a relatively coarse granularity, varia- tion in descriptions of (mountain) landscapes through natural features in Switzerland.']",[],"['Our approach is a novel one, using full text corpora as a starting point to generate rich, spatially referenced, landscape descriptions.']","['lack of availability of homogenous, ﬁne granularity gazetteers (the popular Geonames does not meet this requirement) remain a challenge.', 'our approach to identifying natural features was manual, and based on inter-annotator agreement.', 'we were rapidly confronted with a problem of data scarcity despite the initially large and rich corpora.', 'we do not differentiate between being in and seeing a landscape from afar.']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,,,natural landscape features; spatial folksonomy; term vectors; land cover; land use; grid cell; mountain landscapes; natural feature terms; landscape descriptions; textual corpora,,,
_Ding et al.-2023-A Comparative Study of Perceptio.txt,A Comparative Study of Perceptions of Destination Image Based on Content Mining: Fengjing Ancient Town and Zhaojialou Ancient Town as Examples,J. Ding; Z. Tao; M. Hou; D. Chen; L. Wang,,2023,journal article,Land,"MDPI, Basel, Switzerland",https://doi.org/10.3390/ land12101954,https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/ 4.0/,,,ancient town (14),,ancient towns (14); Fengjing Ancient Town (7); Zhaojialou Ancient Town (8),historic and cultural villages (3); historic sites (1); preservation (1),,,,Fengjing Ancient Town; Zhaojialou Ancient Town; Zhouzhuang,Shanghai (6); Jiangnan region (2); England; China (4); Zhejiang; Jinshan District; Minhang District; Suzhou City,Ming and Qing Dynasties (1),,"Each ancient town merits a more profound examination, as they may not be entirely similar to one another.","(1) What is the level of alignment between tourists’ perceptions of the ancient town destination image and the ofﬁcial promotional image? (2) Regarding different ancient towns, does the alignment between UGC and DMO destination images exhibit similarities?",Sina Weibo (2); Facebook (1); Instagram (2); Twitter (1); Flickr (1); Red (1); tourism websites (1),text (3); photographs (2),,,,,,,,"Fengjing ancient town, the original textual data (FJ-UGC) consisted of 10,619 comments, while Zhaojialou ancient town (ZJL-UGC) had 11,485.",,,,,2010 to 2020,"Fengjing Ancient Town, Zhaojialou Ancient Town",keyword searches,,,"Blank comments and irrelevant content such as items only containing phrases like “share pictures”, “I am at” in UGC data were removed. Additionally, duplicate comments were eliminated.",,,,[],,clustering (4),machine learning (7),Word2Vec (4); K-means clustering (5),a pre-trained Word2Vec model released by Tencent AI Lab [36] was utilized to embed keywords and acquire their respective word vectors.,word embedding (2); word vectors (4),,keywords (15),,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,silhouette coefﬁcient (2),[],[],[