_Gabrielli et al.-2014-From Tweets to Semantic Trajecto.txt,From Tweets to Semantic Trajectories: Mining,,,2012,conference paper,"Citi Sens 2012. LNCS (LNAI), vol. 7685","Springer, Heidelberg",,http://penggalian.org/semantic Trajectories/,,pp. 43–56,,,,,,,,Barcelona (5),Catalonia Region,,Mobile World Congress 2012 (MWC2012) (7),"In this paper, we address the problem of reconstructing collective mobility patterns by the retrieval and analysis of publically available opportunistic data sources: in particular, we investigate approaches to sense the mobility of people by mining the collection of geo-located tweets crawled from a speciﬁc geographic area","Our analyses are tailored to the automated identiﬁcation and characterization of variations of ﬂows and urban activities in order to point out relevant mobility patterns, identify outliers and link them to events.",Twitter (8); Facebook; Foursquare (5),text (tweets) (7); GPS coordinates; geo-located tweets (10); geographic data,GPS position (2),,timestamps,,username; account,183 k,11 k,,,,,,three weeks,metropolitan area of Barcelona,Geo-located tweets concerning these three weeks have been gathered by means of bounding-box ﬁltered Twitter Streaming API,Twitter Streaming API,,,bounding-box ﬁltered,manual (2),,"['Local', 'Tourist']",,classification,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,classifier able to point out if a Twitter user is Catalan or not (thus a tourist) by analyzing the information contained in his Twitter user proﬁle,,yes,['social network analysis (2)'],regions of the geographic tessellation,ﬂows between the two corresponding nodes,,,edge betweenness (4),OD matrices,,,identiﬁcation of relevant zones associated with urban anomalies like large events is performed by means of the analysis of variations in regular patterns of movement,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],chord diagram,[],[],[],[],['locals versus tourists (2)'],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,An interactive Web visualization of the Semantic OD matrix