_Galiano-Coronil et al.-2023-Social media impact of tourism m.txt,Social media impact of tourism,Araceli Galiano-Coronil; Sofia Blanco-Moreno; Luis Bayardo Tobar-Pesantez; Guillermo Antonio Gutierrez-Montoya,,2023,journal article,Journal of Management Development,Emerald Publishing Limited,10.1108/JMD-04-2023-0131,http://creativecommons.org/licences/by/4.0/legalcode,,pp. 436-457,,,,,,entertainment; social; emotional,,,Spain,,COVID-19 situation,"however, although it has been shown that the content promoted by official destination profiles has a direct influence on the behaviour of tourists (Ballester et al., 2021), there is a clear gap in the analysis of the content published by tourism managers, which can be seen by tourists or future destination consumers and can therefore be key to their decision to visit that destination.","This study aims to analyze communication from the perspective of social marketing, positive emotions, and the topics chosen by Spanish tourist destinations to show their destination image. Additionally, this research shows a message classification model, based on the aforementioned characteristics, that has generated a greater impact, offering clarity to tourism managers on the type of content they should publish to achieve greater visibility.",Facebook; Twitter; Instagram,text; photographs,,,,likes; retweets,,"9,458",17,,,,,,"January 1st and December 31st, 2022",Spain,,,"the official Twitter accounts of the 17 autonomous communities of Spain have been analyzed from social marketing, happiness, and sustainability perspective.",,messages reflecting positive emotions related to happiness were selected,two experts have coded a sample of messages,two experts,"['Gastronomy', 'nature', 'plans', 'rural', 'sport', 'culture', 'city', 'weekend trip/day', 'special dates']",0.7,classification,classification tree,CHAID,,,,emotions; social marketing; topic variables,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[]