_Gao et al.-2024-Mining tourist preferences and d.txt,Mining tourist preferences and decision support via tourism-oriented knowledge graph,Jialiang Gao; Peng Peng; Feng Lu; Christophe Claramunt; Peiyuan Qiu; Yang Xu,"State Key Laboratory of Resources and Environmental Information System, Institute of Geographic Sciences and Natural Resources Research, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Beijing 100101, China; University of Chinese Academy of Sciences, Beijing 100049, China; The Academy of Digital China, Fuzhou University, Fuzhou 350002, China; Jiangsu Center for Collaborative Innovation in Geographical Information Resource Development and Application, Nanjing 210023, China; Naval Academy Research Institute, Brest Naval, France; School of Surveying and Geo-Informatics, Shandong Jianzhu University, Jinan 250101, China",2023,journal article,Information Processing and Management,Elsevier Ltd.,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ipm.2023.103523,www.elsevier.com/locate/infoproman,,,,,,,,,,,China (mentions: 10); Chinese (mentions: 6); Taiwan (mentions: 1); Spain (mentions: 1); Croatia (mentions: 1); Australian (mentions: 1); Central plain (mentions: 1); northeast (mentions: 2); eastern coastal regions (mentions: 1); west (mentions: 2); mideastern (mentions: 1); Pearl River Delta (mentions: 2); Sichuan (mentions: 1); Chongqing (mentions: 1); Haerbin (mentions: 1); southern cities (mentions: 1); Changsha (mentions: 1); Chengdu (mentions: 1); Sanya (mentions: 1); Shenzhen (mentions: 1); northern (mentions: 2); temperate (mentions: 1); subtropical (mentions: 1); Midwest regions in China (mentions: 1); Beijing (mentions: 3); Shanghai (mentions: 3); Guilin (mentions: 3),,COVID-19 pandemic (mentions: 1),"To overcome these limitations, the study proposes a novel knowledgegraph-driven framework, involving the systematic construction as well as the thorough investi­ gation and inference of a tourism-oriented knowledge graph (TKG).","This study is to address the following three research questions (RQs): 1. In order to comprehensively model the complicated correlations between various objects within tourism scenes and further realize a complete decision-support system for tourist preference mining and tourism development planning, what kind of data organi­ zation mode and knowledge representation ontology can be applied to integrate the large-scale multi-source heterogeneous tourism data into a unified architecture? 2. Compared to the conventional text mining methods commonly-used in tourism management, what significant enhancements would the TKG methodology bring to accurately extracting tourist preference knowledge and meticulously depicting tourism scenes? 3. What novel regularity characteristics of tourist preferences will be unveiled through the constructed TKG, and how can we advance towards their causal interpretation and potential effects? Moreover, what downstream decision-support tasks can TKG facilitate, and what specific enhancements can TKG offer?",Trip Advisor (mentions: 2); Yelp (mentions: 1); Instagram (mentions: 1); Ctrip (mentions: 1); Ma Feng Wo (mentions: 5),text (mentions: 11); online reviews (mentions: 15),,spatial distribution (mentions: 3); geographic regularities (mentions: 2); spatial correlations (mentions: 2),time series (mentions: 1); seasonal trend (mentions: 2); monthly seasonal concentration index (mentions: 1),likes (mentions: 2),,"11,049,090 reviews (mentions: 2)","1,174,034 tourists (mentions: 1)",,,,,,from 2014 to 2019 (mentions: 3),all 340 city-level destinations across China (mentions: 3),web crawler (mentions: 2),Python 3.7 (mentions: 1),,,After eliminating inactive users (history <5) and un wanted attractions (access <100),manual annotation (mentions: 2),28 independent volunteers (mentions: 1),[],,topic modelling (mentions: 7); knowledge extraction (mentions: 7); multi-label classification (mentions: 1); demand prediction (mentions: 4); competitive intelligence (mentions: 6); link-prediction (mentions: 1); KG completion ta