_Garzia et al.-2020-Emotional reactions to the perce.txt,Emotional Reactions to the Perception of Risk in the Pompeii Archaeological Park,TITLE:; ABSTRACT:,,2019,other,Journal homepage: http://iieta.org/journals/ijsse,WIT Press,https://doi.org/10.1109/CCST.2018.8585519,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.asej.2014.04.011,,,Cultural Heritage (1),,Pompeii Archaeological Park (PAP) (7); Pompeii (14); archaeological evidence (1); World Heritage site (1); ancient city (3); archaeological Park (2); ancient inhabitants (1); ancient Pompeii (2); Public Forum (1); Public Lari (1),cultural heritage security (1); heritage preservation (1); heritage protection (1); World Heritage site (1),,"{'value': 'Emotional (collective)', 'reasoning': 'The study focuses on the emotional components of risk perception within the Pompeii Archaeological Park, suggesting an interest in the collective emotional experience of visitors and how it shapes their perception of the site.'}; {'value': 'Entertainment', 'reasoning': ""The paper mentions the tourist influx and the role of the site in attracting visitors, indicating a discussion of the site's value in the contemporary market, especially in tourism.""}; {'value': 'Educational', 'reasoning': ""The paper discusses the historical and artistic importance of the archaeological evidence, suggesting a discussion of the site's potential to provide knowledge about the past.""}; {'value': 'Artistic', 'reasoning': ""The paper mentions mosaics, paintings, houses, and temples, indicating a discussion of the site's original product of creativity and imagination.""}; {'value': 'Existential', 'reasoning': ""The paper discusses the tragic history of Pompeii and the casts of the victims of the eruption, suggesting a discussion of the site's representation of memory and the lives of past generations.""}",heritage preservation (1); heritage protection (1),"Pompeii Archaeological Park; Pompeii; Colosseum in Rome; Vatican City State; Senate of the Italian Republic; Quintili