_Garzia et al.-2021-Emotional reactions to risk perc.txt,Emotional reactions to risk perception in the,,,,conference paper,2021 International Carnahan Conference on Security Technology (ICCST),IEEE,10.1109/ICCST49569.2021.9717406,,,,cultural sites (1),,Herculaneum Archaeological Park (4); archaeological sites (2); historic city’s (1); ancient walls (1); ancient city (1),world heritage site (1); cultural heritage (1),,"{'value': 'Emotional (collective)', 'reasoning': 'The study analyzes emotional responses from social media data related to a heritage site, indicating a focus on cultural identity, motivation, pride, and a sense of place attachment.'}; {'value': 'Entertainment', 'reasoning': 'The paper mentions the role of tourism and visitor experience at the Herculaneum Archaeological Park, suggesting the entertainment value of the site.'}; {'value': 'Educational', 'reasoning': 'The paper discusses the historical significance of the Herculaneum Archaeological Park and its potential to provide knowledge about the past.'}; {'value': 'Historic-Artistic', 'reasoning': 'The paper mentions the historic and artistic values of the archaeological sites, indicating their significance as examples of historical and artistic movements.'}; {'value': 'Archaeological', 'reasoning': 'The paper focuses on the Herculaneum Archaeological Park, which is connected to an ancient civilization.'}; {'value': 'Existential', 'reasoning': 'The paper refers to the terrible past of Herculaneum and the devastation by the Vesuvius volcano, which represents memory and the lives of past generations.'}",preserve (1); protect (1),Herculaneum Archaeological Park; Pompeii; Pompeii Archaeological Park,Italy (4),79 A.D. (1),catastrophic Vesuvius volcanic eruption in 79 A.D. (1),important to evaluate the extent of perceived risk by tourists of heritage and cultural sites.,Our aim is to assess the emotions of people and estimate their risk perception.,Twitter (5),text (2),,,Timeline analysis (1),,,"Due to the