_Ghermandi et al.-2022-In the AI of the beholder A com.txt,In the AI of the beholder: A comparative analysis of computer vision-assisted characterizations of human-nature interactions in urban green spaces,Andrea Ghermandi; Yaella Depietri; Michael Sinclair,"Department of Natural Resources and Environmental Management, University of Haifa, 199 Aba Khushy, Haifa 3498838, Israel; Natural Resources and Environmental Research Center, University of Haifa, 199 Aba Khoushy Ave, Mount Carmel Haifa 3498838, Israel; Faculty of Architecture and Town Planning, Technion – Israel Institute of Technology, Haifa 3200003, Israel; Urban Big Data Centre, School of Social and Political Sciences, University of Glasgow, Glasgow, UK",2021,journal article,Landscape and Urban Planning,Elsevier B V,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.landurbplan.2021.104261,http://flickr.com,,,,,,,,,landscape planning (3); planning (2); management (2),Haifa; Bah´aí Gardens; Carmel beaches; Shikmona beach,Haifa; Israel; Mediterranean Sea; Great Britain,,,"Here, we analyze ~ 10,000 outdoor photographs retrieved from three social media platforms and geolocated within green and blue spaces in Haifa (Israel) by means of machine tags from three popular cloud-based services.","This study investigates the application of three cloud computer vision services (Clarifai, Google Cloud Vision and Microsoft Azure Computer Vision) on almost ten thousand geotagged, outdoor social media photographs reflecting direct human-nature interactions in the entire network of green and blue spaces in the city of Haifa in Israel.",Flickr; Instagram; VKontakte; Panoramio,photographs; text,GPS,,time; temporal resolution; temporal scales,,metadata,"~ 10,000",,,"9,454",,,,2005–2018,Haifa (Israel),retrieved,Application Programming Interfaces (APIs),,"manually scrutinized to identify indoor photographs, lead­ ing to the removal of 30% of the sample",indoor photographs,automated image content analysis,,[],,clustering; image content analysis; image recognition,pre-trained models; Convolutional Neural Network models,Places CNN; Res Net50,pre-trained,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,average silhouette width; Adjusted Rand Index (ARI),[],[],[],chi-square test; Bonferroni correction; Kendall’s rank correlation (tau-b),,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],"['planning and governance of urban green infrastructure', 'valuation of the benefits of urban green and blue areas', 'analysis of green gentrification in urban areas', 'characterization of perceptions of landscape aesthetics']",[],[],[],[],"['the majority of photographs in the final sample were obtained from VKontakte, which suggest a bias towards overrepresenting the landscape experience of Russian-speaking locals and visitors.', 'Tags with a low confidence retrieved, for instance, from Clarifai or Azure (as opposed to Google, which only returns tags associated with an estimated confidence of 0.5 or higher) might have lower relevance and should be treated with caution.', 'the results presented are derived from the analysis of a single case-study (the city of Haifa in Israel) and may not be straightforwardly transferable to other contexts.']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,"R, version 4.0.3",,,,,,
_Ghosh et al.-2025-From Restoration to Reaction A.txt,From Restoration to Reaction:,S. Ghosh; J. Masih; J. Noone; S. R. Chandra; P. Khanna,"School of Management, BML Munjal University, Gurugram, Haryana, India",2025,other,"M. Alaali et al. (eds.), The Paradigm Shift from a Linear Economy to a Smart Circular",Springer Nature Switzerland AG,,https://www.deccanherald. com/india/ancient-kashi-vishwanath-temple-gets-a-new-look-1060275.html,,,cultural heritage (3),cultural (1),Kashi Vishwanath Temple (10); historical sites (1); ancient city (1); religious sites (2); historical temples (1),historical (2); renovation (13); cultural (5); preservation (1); promotion (2); revered (1); sacred (1); shrines (1); spiritual (5); ancient (2); temple (25); heritage (2); management (4); modernized (1); pilgrims (4); tourists (5); devotees (1); Ganga ghats (2); Jyotirlingas (1); redevelopment (1); conservation (0),,"Spiritual: The Kashi Vishwanath Temple is described as a revered Hindu temple dedicated to Lord Shiva, holding immense spiritual significance for Hindus worldwide. This indicates a spiritual value associated with beliefs and religious practices.; Emotional (collective): The temple's renovation and its impact on visitor experiences and sentiments suggest a connection to cultural identity and a sense of place attachment for the community and visitors.; Economic (entertainment): The increase in tourism and development in the area, leading to job creation and improved living standards, indicates an entertainment value related to the temple's role in the contemporary market, especially tourism.; Educational: The temple's historical significance and the potential to provide knowledge about the past in the future suggest an educational value related to its role in disseminating cultural awareness and historical information.; Aesthetic (artistic): The enhancement of the temple complex with new lighting, landscaping, and architectural elements indicates an artistic value related to the original product of creativity and imagination.",renovation (13),Kashi Vishwanath Temple; Varanasi,Varanasi; Uttar Pradesh; India; Northern India; Southern India; Western India; Eastern India; Union Territory; Europe; North America; Asia; Australia; Africa; South America,,Kashi Vishwanath Temple renovation,"While the renovation has undoubtedly been a transformative project, there is still room for further research and development. One area that has not been extensively explored is the sentiments of the people towards the project. While evidence suggests widespread approval, rigorous studies based on empirical data are needed to understand the nuanced perspectives of the local community, pilgrims, and tourists.",To evaluate the impact of the recent Kashi Vishwanath Temple renovation on the perceptions and experiences of Hindu pilgrims and tourists visiting the site.,Tripadvisor; Google Reviews,"text (posts, captions, comments, reviews, hashtags); ratings",,,timeline; temporal analysis,ratings,month of the visit; date of their visit; company they had while visiting; states; countries; years,"1475 datapoints (Tripadvisor), 360 datapoints (Google Reviews)",,comments,,,,,2008 to 2024,"65 countries, 22 Indian state",sourced from website reviews,,,"Duplicate records were removed, and standardization was applied to columns like states and countries. To facilitate analysis, months and years were extracted into separate columns. Comments were preprocessed to prepare them for sentiment analysis",,manual and computational methods,,"['positive', 'negative', 'neutral']",,sentiment analysis; clustering; classification,,BERT,BERT-enhanced models,,,comments,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],pie chart; density plot; line chart; word clouds,[],[],[],"['The analysis revealed key insights into visitor perceptions, identifying aspects of the renovation that were particularly well-received and those that attracted criticism. The results indicated a signiﬁcant increase in positive sentiments, particularly regarding the temple’s aesthetics and visitor facilities, while concerns about crowd management and accessibility were also noted.']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,IEEE,,EDA; Exploratory Data Analysis; sentiment analysis; visitor sentiments; visitor experience; visitor perceptions; visitor satisfaction; visitor emotions; pilgrims; tourists; Hindu; Ganges River; Shiva; lingam; Shravan; pujas; abhishekas; Aarti; darshan; Rajghat; Shree Shivay Thali,,,
