_Gugulica and Burghardt-2023-Mapping indicators of cultural e.txt,Mapping indicators of cultural ecosystem services use in urban green spaces based on text classification of geosocial media data,Madalina Gugulica; Dirk Burghardt,"Institute of Cartography, Technische Universit¨at Dresden, 01069 Dresden, Germany",2023,journal article,Ecosystem Services,Elsevier B V,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ecoser.2022.101508,www.elsevier.com/locate/ecoser,,,,cultural,Urban green spaces (UGSs) (7); urban nature (4); cultural landscape (2),Cultural ecosystem services (CES) (14); cultural values (4); ecosystem management (3); nature-based recreation (6); landscape values (2); cultural benefits (5); nature conservation (1),,"{'value': 'Aesthetical Values', 'reasoning': 'The paper discusses aesthetic appreciation of urban green spaces, which aligns with the definition of aesthetic values as original products of creativity and imagination.'}; {'value': 'Social Values', 'reasoning': 'The paper mentions the role of urban green spaces in diminishing mental, physical, and social pressures by providing citizens with diverse opportunities to recreate and experience nature in their cities, which aligns with the definition of social values.'}; {'value': 'Economic Values', 'reasoning': 'The paper mentions the economic benefits of urban green spaces, especially tourism.'}",ecosystem management (2); urban planning (5); nature conservation policies (1),city of Dresden; Dresden Elbe Valley; K¨onigsufer; Waldschl¨osschenwiesen; Blaues Wunder bridge; Schmuckplatz; Great Garten; Zschonergrund; Lingnerpark; Dresdner Heide; Pieschen; Alaunplatz; Blüherpark; Lingnerallee skatepark; Kaitzbachtal bei Mockritz; Pillnitzer Elbinsel,Germany; Saxony; Europe,,current pandemic,This study was motivated by the need to develop efficient tools for extracting spatially explicit information from geosocial media data to quantify CES use.,We introduce a novel methodology that relies on the text classification of large volumes of Flickr and Instagram data to quantify and map indicators of CES flow in UGSs.,Instagram; Flickr; Netlytic,textual metadata; geotagged posts; geographic coordinates; timestamps,geographic coordinates,spatial patterns; spatial distribution,timestamps; temporal patterns,,user IDs; post IDs; post description; post title; tags; captions; hashtags,"827,776","30,182",,,,,,"January 1, 2015, and December 31, 2018",city of Dresden,API calls,"API endpoint flickr.photos.search (Flickr, 2022)",,the contributions of single users with identical locations and textual annotations were removed from the datasets,"social media posts published on Flickr and Instagram between January 1, 2015, and December 31, 2018",manual,,"['aesthetic, nature, and landscape photography', 'flora, fauna, and wildlife photography']",,text classification; natural language processing (NLP),deep learning; machine learning,word2vec,,word2vec word embeddings,term frequency-inverse document frequency (TF-IDF),textual annotations,,30 % of the sample dataset,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,"The methodology relies on an unsupervised approach to text classification that we developed to identify and select Flickr and Insta­gram textual annotations, in which social media users document and share aesthetic appreciation of urban landscapes or their observations of flora and fauna in UGSs.",no,[],,,,,,,,,,accuracy; precision; recall; F1-score,"['aesthetic appreciation (94.19 %)', 'wildlife recreation (98.10 %)', 'aesthetic appreciation (81.07 %)', 'wildlife recreation (76.61 %)']",[],[],,,[],[],"The slightly decreased precision rate (72.9 %) was caused by the number of posts that were falsely classified as being related to aesthetic appreciation (168 out of 620 positively classified posts), as a consequence of wordsense ambiguities.","The majority of the misclassified posts were related to topics such as architecture, fashion, or beauty, which on a semantic level are related to aesthetics but are irrelevant for our analysis because they are not specifically related to the natural elements of the environ­ment.",word-sense ambiguity issues caused by the polysemy of words and course semantic granularity,[],,,[],,"['intense flows of aesthetic appreciation and wildlife recreation concentrated within landscape and nature protection areas', 'The perceived aesthetic value of water bodies is also corroborated by the concentration of hotspots along the river Elbe', 'social media users associate certain cyclic events, such as Sonnenuntergang “sunset”, weather phenomena and atmospheric conditions (e.g., sunny weather, clouds), the presence of some plants and animals (e.g., flowers, trees, swans), or certain seasons (mostly spring and summer) with the aesthetic values of UGSs.']","['Flickr users tend to be nature enthusiasts and enjoy photographing nature and biodiversity, whereas Instagram users share more content about people and their daily activities']",[],[],['significant differences between the two user groups regarding the use of UGSs for aesthetic appreciation and wildlife recreation'],[],"['urban planning', 'ecosystem management', 'conservation planning']",['identifying the underappreciated UGSs for aesthetic and wildlife recreation services can represent the inception of collaborative work between urban planners and designers toward improving their attractiveness by introducing a number of flowering plants and trees species into the local flora'],['proposing a methodology for quantifying and mapping CES flow based on the spatial and semantic analysis of geosocial media data'],[],[],"['geosocial media are not universally representative owing to a series of biases', 'demographic and sample biases', 'restrictions on content', 'geotagging inaccuracies']",[],"['demographic and sample biases', 'omission of minority language communities']",[],[],[],[],[],"['geosocial media are not universally representative owing to a series of biases', 'demographic and sample biases', 'restrictions on content', 'geotagging inaccuracies']",yes,Data will be made available on request.,,,Python (version 3.9.7),,,photo-user days (PUD); chi expectation surface; tagmaps,,,
_Guo et al.-2018-CrowdTravel scenic spot profili.txt,ORIGINAL RESEARCH,Tong Guo,"School of Computer Science, Northwestern Polytechnical University, Xi’an 710129, People’s Republic of China; Department of Electrical and Electronic Engineering, The University of Hong Kong, Hong Kong, People’s Republic of China",,other,,,,,,,,,scenic spots (12); natural scenes; cultural scenes,,,,,Beijing; Xi’an; The Summer Palace; The Forbidden City; Tang Paradise; Beijing Wtown; Great Wild Goose Pagoda; Fragrant Hills Park; Huaqing Palace; The Xi’an Circumvallation; Xi’an Bell Tower; Badaling Great Wall,China,,,"To address these issues, this paper proposes Crowd Travel, a multi- source social media data fusion approach for multi-aspect tourism information perception, which can provide travel- ling assistance for tourists by crowd intelligence mining.","We first study the problem of discovering popular scenic spots over crowd contributed data. Second, we propose a cross-media multi-aspect correlation method to connect fragmented travel information. Then we mine popular travel routes from travelogues based on Sequential Pattern Min- ing Algorithm. Finally, we achieve cross-media informa- tion relevance based on the similarity between the reviews",Flickr; Dazhongdianping; Mafengwo,text; images; travelogues; reviews; multimedia,,,,,,,,,"After pre-processing, the dataset for each scenic spot contains around 1800 reviews and 2000 images with the surrounding contexts.",,,,,The targeted tourist cities in this experimental applica- tion of the framework are Beijing and Xi’an in China.,crawling,,,"A pre-filtering process is performed on the dataset to remove duplicate reviews, images and trav- elogues which are not related to the scenic spot.",We only included images that have completely associated textual contexts.,,,[],,clustering,,,,,color moment; edge histogram; wavelet texture fea- ture; LBP feature; GIST feature,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,,[],,,,,,,,,,accuracy rate,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['For the travel route recommendation algorithm, we do not consider incorpo- rating costs (e.g., the prices and time cost) and personal- ized objectives (e.g., preferences and interests) into our current implementation.', 'We would like to explore these issues further as a part of our future research.', 'Besides, we plan to incorporate prior knowledge of locations to improve unsupervised knowledge mining and take vari- ous granularity levels of locations into consideration, so as to better meet more practical travel information needs.']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,,,travel-related websites; mobile social net- works; travel experience; social media; travel plans; Textual reviews; travelogues; social travel sharing; travel knowledge; tourism information; tourists; crowd intelligence mining; scenic spots; travel routes; Sequential Pattern Min- ing Algorithm; cross-media informa- tion relevance; multi-document summa- rization (MDS); frequency-based meth- ods; semantic-based methods; probabilistic latent semantic analysis (PLSA); latent Dirichlet allocation (LDA); text mining; tourism social information; multiple media types; image; tourist; natural scenes; cultural scenes; scene-feature’ characteri- zation; user-generated reviews; travelogues; Flickr tags; travel routes; multi-source social media data fusion approach; travel route recommendation; crowd intelligence; event discovery; business intel- ligence; activity recommendation; tourism knowledge mining; travel recommendation; graph-ranking algorithm; structural SVM; travel plan assistant system; tourists sight extraction; images retrieval; personalized tourism summary; trip planning system; tag-based place similarity; user-contributed photo collections; landmark; geo-tagged photos; feature mining; noun phrases; Cyberguide project; mobile context-aware tour guide; contextual information; intelligent system; personalized recommenda- tions; Bayesian network techniques; Analytic Hierarchy Process (AHP) method; travel behaviors; Collaborative Filtering (CF) method; location recommendation; user-generated data; geo-tagged photos; probabilistic topic models; topics; travel recommendation; scene words; average growth rate (AGR); average monthly growth rate (AMGR); Fudan NLP package; stop words; information entropy; incremental learning method; feature words; fuzzy matching algorithm; spectral clustering; affinity propagation method,,,
_Guo et al.-2025-Multi-Modal Social Media Analysi.txt,Multi-Modal Social Media Analysis via SHAP-Based Explanation: Decoding Public Art Perception Across China’s Urban Hierarchy,Tianhao Guo; Zhengyang Lu; Feng Wang,"School of Design, Jiangnan University",2025,other,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,China; Jiangsu Province,,,"Social media platforms have fundamentally transformed public engagement with urban cultural spaces, generating extensive multi-modal data that documents residents’ interac- tions with public art installations.",Our research framework combines Large Language Mod- els for image captioning and sentiment analysis with random forest modeling to examine public art perception across urban environments.,Weibo,text; visual materials; metadata (geolocation and timestamp); images,geolocation; GPS coordinates,GIS mapping; spatial distribution,timestamp,,geolocation; timestamp,"103,427",,,,,,,December 2022 to December 2023,Jiangsu Province,systematic keyword-based sampling framework,,"search parameters encompassing terminol- ogy specific to public art installations, interactive exhibitions, digital artistic interventions, and regional cultural program- ming.","removal of special characters, standardization of punctuation, and conversion of traditional to simplified Chinese characters for consistency. Emoticons and hashtags were preserved to maintain contextual information.","non-art related visuals (e.g., user selfies) filtered out using a pre-trained convolutional neural network classifier",manually curated and annotated by art experts,art experts,[],Cohen’s κ = 0.87,topic classification; sentiment analysis; emotion classification,Large Language Models; CNNs; Random Forest model,Res Net-152; Qwen-7B-Chat,fine-tuned on public art installations,,,visual features; post text,,5-fold cross-validation,,,2e-4,16,3,,,"{'Lo RA rank': '8', 'Lo RA alpha': '16', 'Gradient accumulation steps': '4', 'weight decay': '0.01'}",,,NVIDIA A100,4,,,,"The LLM-based image captioning system begins with feature extraction with pre-trained CNNs, specifically a Res Net-152 architecture [32]. These visual features are then encoded into a format compatible with the input requirements of our LLM, which is a fine-tuned version of Qwen-7B-Chat [33]. The LLM processes the encoded visual features as input to generate descriptive captions through an autoregressive decoding process.",,[],,,,,,,,,,BLEU-4; METEOR; CIDEr; SPICE; Mean Squared Error (MSE); coefficient of determination (R2),[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],5-fold cross-validation,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],['development of an innovative methodological frame- work for analyzing multi-modal social media data in cultural research'],['empirical documentation of emergent forms of cultural capital combining traditional and digital competencies'],['evidence-based recommendations for cultural pol- icy development that recognize the complex inter- play between technological innovation and cultural preservation across diverse urban contexts.'],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,"To request access to this dataset, please contact corresponding author with reasonable purposes due to the Terms of Service on Weibo platform.",,,,,,,,,
_Gurlahosur et al.-2022-Comparative Analysis of Neural A.txt,Comparative Analysis of Neural,S. V. Gurlahosur; S. M. Meena; U. Kulkarni; W. Dcosta; V. Lokur; R. V. Sirigeri; S. Porwal; S. P. Sammed; U. Mudenagudi,"KLE Technological University, Hubballi, India e-mail: svgurlahosur@kletech.ac.in; KLE Technological University, Hubballi, India e-mail: msm@kletech.ac.in; KLE Technological University, Hubballi, India e-mail: uday_kulkarni@kletech.ac.in; KLE Technological University, Hubballi, India e-mail: uma@kletech.ac.in",2022,other,Proceedings of the Satellite Workshops of ICVGIP 2021,Springer Nature Singapore Pte Ltd,,https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/ azure/machine-learning/concept-automated-ml,,25,Cultural Heritages (2); Cultural Heritage (4),,Indian Heritage sites (2); heritage sites (7),heritage sites (7),,,,,India (1); Indian (2),,,"NAS method efﬁciency should be uniform across datasets; thus, a custom image data set based on Indian Heritage sites using crowdsource framework is proposed to study whether the NAS methods are generalizable across tasks rather than dataset-speciﬁc (standard datasets).",1. Custom image data set comprising of Cultural Heritages sites in India. 2. Comparative performance analysis of the NAS methods on the custom dataset. 3. Propose a neural architecture model for the classiﬁcation of Cultural Heritage sites with 88.625% accuracy.,,images (12),,,,,,"4,68,651",,,"20,000",,,,,India,web-based crowdsourced framework,,,removed the remaining portrait images and redundant images with a similarity score of 85%. Quantitative analysis is performed on the data set to remove the blur and occluded images.,,,users,['heritage sites'],,image classiﬁcation (5),CNN architecture (1); Neural Architecture (2); convolutional neural network (2),ENAS (8); DARTS (8); NSGA-Net (7),,,,images,,"16,000 training images and 4000 test images",cross-entropy loss,Adam optimizer,0.00035,64 (6),150 (7),,,{},,"NVIDIA DGX-1, Tesla V100 GPUs",Tesla V100 GPUs,two GPUs,,48 GPU h