_Hu et al.-2024-Examination of experience attrib.txt,Examination of experience attributes in urban tourist destinations: a topic modelling analysis of user-generated content,Zongwei Hu; Jian Ming Luo; Christina Geng-Qing Chi; Dogan Gursoy,"Faculty of Hospitality and Tourism Management, Macau University of Science and Technology; School of Liberal Arts, Macau University of Science and Technology; School of Hospitality Business Management in the Carson College of Business, Washington State University; School of Hospitality Business Management, Carson College of Business, Washington State University",2024,journal article,LEISURE STUDIES,,https://doi.org/10.1080/02614367.2024.2392583,https://doi.org/10.1080/02614367.2024.2392583,,,,,urban parks (22),culture (3); heritage (3); historical (3); cultural (10),,,,Central Park in New York; Central Park,"New York; Manhattan; Hong Kong; China; Tokyo; Estonia; Phuket, Thailand; Luton; Darlington; Spanish",,,"Therefore, significant research gaps remain regarding the dimensions of urban park experiences, particularly concerning the currently neglected cultural heritage experiences.",RQ1: What are the prominent attributes of urban park experience? RQ2: What attributes of urban park experience correlate with visitor satisfaction? RQ3: Are there differences in park experience across different seasons?,Trip Advisor (4),text (2); online reviews (5),,,seasonal,satisfaction ratings (3),,"70,922",,,,,,,between 8 June 2003 and 9 February 2023,Central Park in New York,python crawler,,,"(1) Lower case all texts and remove non-English characters, including punctuation and numbers; (2) Remove line breaks and convert to spaces. (3) Filter stop words (unimportant words) and certain proper nouns (such as ‘Central Park’). (4) Perform semantic markup, keeping only verbs and nouns.",Comments not written in English were excluded to maintain consistency of analysis methods,,,[],,topic modelling (6); sentiment analysis,,Latent Dirichlet Allocation (LDA) (5),,,,,,,,,,,,,,"{'α': '0.5', 'topic numbers': '25'}",,,,,,,,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,topic coherence (2); topic exclusivity (2); topic interpretability (2),[],[],[],Kruskal–Wallis H-test (2),,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['This study will identify the experiential attributes of urban parks that are associated with visitor the relative popularity of attributes across seasons and implement different strategies in different seasons.', 'In addition, this study utilised UGC and natural language processing (NLP) techniques to overcome limitations of traditional methods in examining visitor data']",[],[],"['Firstly, we only tested the seasonal variations of experiential attributes. However, factors such as weather conditions, cultural differences and travel modes could also influence the variations in these attributes.', 'Secondly, we did not investigate the relationship between experiential attributes and visitor emotions.', 'Thirdly, we only considered user generated textual content in this study.']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,Natural Language Toolkit (NLTK),,urban destinations; park experience; user-generated content (UGC) (6); latent Dirichlet allocation (LDA) (5); seasonal; natural language processing (NLP) (2),,,
