ive computing and large language models.",Dianping (2); Instagram,text (4); image (7); multimodal data (5); user-generated content (UGC) (11),,,,likes (2); comments (2); followers,,9207,,9207,"29,742",,,,,Qianmen Street,scraped,,,"The textual data were processed using Jieba word segmentation, with stop words removed",,,,[],,sentiment analysis (5); named entity recognition; classification; topic modeling; clustering,Transformer models; large language models (LLMs) (7),GPT-4 (2); Qwen LM (6); Ro BERTa (5); Chat GPT; ELECTRA,pre-trained,deep-learningbased text embeddings,,text; image,cross-modal matching,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,"This approach enabled a systematic workflow encompassing the data collection, feature extraction, multimodal semantic fusion, and information presentation",yes,['knowledge graph'],,,,,,,Graph Attention Neural Network,,,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],heatmaps,[],[],[],[],[],[],['smart tourism systems'],[],['This study offers a more data-driven and personalized information optimization strategy.'],[],[],"['VR experiments cannot fully replicate their immersed perceptions of real-world settings.', 'the eye-tracking data do not fully capture all of the emotional dimensions encompassed in the UGC data, limiting their ability to represent the depth of user sentiment.']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,The data that support the findings of this study are available from the corresponding author upon reasonable request.,,,,,,affective computing (7); multimodal information fusion (3); user-generated content (UGC) (11); information presentation (6); emotional engagement (3); emotional resonance (2); emotional tendencies (3); emotional feedback (2); emotional involvement (2); emotional experiences (2); emotional connection (2); emotional potential; emotional needs; emotional arousal (2); emotional responses (2); emotional expression; emotional dimensions (2); emotional states; emotional signals; emotional bias; emotional layers; emotional impact (2); emotional intensi