_Huai et al.-2022-Using social media photos and co.txt,Using social media photos and computer vision to assess cultural ecosystem services and landscape features in urban parks,Songyao Huai; Fen Chen; Song Liu; Frank Canters; Tim Van de Voorde,"Department of Geography, Ghent University, Ghent 9000, Belgium; School of Resources and Environment, University of Electronic Science and Technology of China, 2006 Xiyuan Avenue, West Hi-Tech Zone, Chengdu 611731, Sichuan, China; Center for Information Geoscience, University of Electronic Science and Technology of China, 2006 Xiyuan Avenue, West Hi-Tech Zone, Chengdu 611731, Sichuan, China; College of Architecture and Urban Planning, Tongji University, Shanghai 200092, China; Key Laboratory of Ecology and Energy-saving Study of Dense Habitat (Tongji University), Ministry of Education, Shanghai 200092, China; Cartography and GIS Research Group, Department of Geography, Vrije Universiteit Brussel, 1050 Brussels, Belgium",2022,journal article,Ecosystem Services,Elsevier B V,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ecoser.2022.101475,www.elsevier.com/locate/ecoser,,,,urban,urban parks (14),,,,urban park planning (2); tourism management (3); green space management (2),Brussels’ urban parks,Belgium; China; Europe,,,"In recent years, social media data have become a promising data source for the assessment of cultural ecosystem services (CES) and landscape features in urban parks. However, it is a challenging task to identify and classify the CES and landscape features from social media photos by manual content analysis.","The research goal is to use social media photos and computer vision methods such as scene recognition, image clustering, and image labeling to identify the CES preferences and landscape feature preferences of tourists and locals in the urban parks of Brussels.",Flickr,geotagged social media photos; metadata,geotagged photos; latitude; longitude,spatial preferences; spatial distribution; spatial intensity,,,photo ID; user ID; photo date; latitude; longitude; photo title; tags; photo URLs,"12,568",1380 tourists and 1459 locals,,4996 outdoor images,,,,"January 1st, 2004 to September 30th, 2021",79 urban parks in Brussels,collected the metadata of publicly geotagged photos,"Flickr API (flickr.photos.search, https://www.flickr.com/services/api/flickr.photos.search.html)",,applied a scene recognition model (the Places365-Res Net18 model: https://github.com/CSAILVision/places365) to filter the outdoor images,outdoor images,manual classification,authors,"['plants', 'flowers', 'water bodies', 'insects', 'birds', 'animals', 'sculptures', 'buildings', 'recreational elements', 'landscape views']",,scene recognition; image clustering; image labeling,convolutional neural networks (CNN),Places365-Res Net18 model; Inception Res Net V2,pre-trained CNN model,image feature vectors,,photos’ visual contents,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,This 164-layer network is founded on a bi ti f th I ti t t d th R id l ti d,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,average silhouette score; True Positive (TP); True Negative (TN); False Positive (FP); False Negative (FN); precision; recall; F1-score,"['average F1-score of the image clustering was 0.942', 'average silhouette coefficient: 0.472']",[],[],"Chi-square test (X-squared = 7128.8, df = 63, p-value < 2.2e-16)",,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],"['tourists and locals have distinct spatial preferences for urban parks', 'tourists prefer well-known urban parks located in the city center, while locals have a broad spatial preference for urban parks throughout the city.', 'landscape features associated with place identity were perceived more frequently by tourists, whereas local species of fauna and flora were perceived more frequently by locals in the urban parks.']",[],"['environmental planning', 'tourism management']",['Analyzing the differences in spatial preferences and landscape preferences of tourists and locals could help to identify the hotspots and coldspots of green space use and prioritize the management focus for specific users.'],['use of computer vision methods to improve photo content analysis in the CES assessment'],[],[],"['inherent biases and representativeness of social media data', 'measurement uncertainties']",['users’ privacy and sensitive information'],['social media data have an inherent bias in which certain groups of people are underrepresented'],[],[],[],[],[],"['inherent biases and representativeness of social media data', 'measurement uncertainties']",Data will be made available on request.,Data will be made available on request.,,,,,,cultural ecosystem services (CES); landscape features; urban parks; social media photos; computer vision methods; scene recognition; image clustering; image labeling; convolutional neural networks (CNN); Google Cloud Vision platform; spatial preferences; landscape preferences; tourists; locals,,,
