_Jeribi et al.-2023-Developing an MQ-LSTM-Based Cult.txt,Developing an MQ- LSTM-Based Cultural Tourism Accelerator with Database Security,"Jeribi, F.; Ahamed, S.R.; Perumal, U.; Alhameed, M.H.; Chari Kamsali, M.",,2023,journal article,Sustainability,MDPI,https://doi.org/10.3390/su152316276,https://doi.org/10.3390/su152316276,,,Cultural Heritage (1),,historical sites (6); historical destinations (1); cultural events (5); historical site (10); tourist places (1),heritage culture (1); historical information content (1); monuments (1); cultural sources (1); traditional value (1); historical signiﬁcance (3); cultural symbol (1),,"{'SOCIAL VALUES': 'Cultural identity: The paper discusses reinforcing identities and enhancing cross-cultural understanding, which aligns with the concept of cultural identity as a collective emotional value.'}; {'ECONOMIC VALUES': 'Entertainment: The paper focuses on improving cultural tourism and attracting tourists, which directly relates to the entertainment value of heritage assets in the contemporary market.'}; {'POLITICAL VALUES': 'Educational: The paper aims to assist tourists in understanding points of interest and making them aware of the significance of nature and monuments, indicating an educational role for political purposes.'}; {'HISTORIC VALUES': 'Educational: The paper emphasizes the importance of historical sites and their cultural significance, suggesting the potential of these assets to provide knowledge about the past.'}",preserving (1),Riyadh (5); Riyadh City (4),Saudi Arabia (2); Spain (1); Italy (1); Malaysia (1); China (2); Hong Kong (1),,,"Even though some research like [16–19], are available for the tourism recommendation model, they exhibit several limitations, which are given as • During the busy hours in historical sites, the recommendation model for analyzing the culture of the place by recommending the most nearby cultural events is scarcely developed. • In conventional works, when the recommendation is created only grounded on the reviews, the historical importance was neglected, which affects the recommendation of CT. • When a tourism-centric database is created, there is no guarantee that the database is used by legal users only. This would cause a security threat to the historical sites, which are the cultural symbol of a country. • Most of the existing research works did not concentrate on analyzing the historical sites or tourist places of Riyadh city based on the restaurant details that tourists accommodate. This greatly impacts the RS.","By analyzing the aforementioned issues, the proposed framework’s objective is to develop a smart CT model in a secure database, and its contributions are • To develop KIC and Cramer’s’ V Correlated-Minimal Spanning Tree (CVC-MST) schemes for analyzing the possible nearest cultural events to the historical sites and suggested to tourism planners. • To develop an MQ-LSTM recommendation model considering the location, time, and review, along with historical signiﬁcance. • To establish an LSH hashing for providing the security of the tourism recommendation database using the user attributes.",social network sites (SNS) (2); social media platforms (2); Trip Advisor (2); Google (2),map data (1); reviews (4); news (4); ratings (3),,,,likes (1); ratings (2),latitude (1); longitude locations (1); prices (1); photos (1); tips (1); addresses (1),20K,,,,,,,,Riyadh,web scraping (1),external application programming interface (API) (2),,preprocessing was carried out to remove the missing columns (1),,,,[],,recommendation (19); clustering (7); sentiment analysis (2); data mining (1); prediction (2); classiﬁcation (3),deep learning (DL) (3); machine learning (ML) (4); neural networks (2); convolutional neural network (CNN) (1); support vector machine (SVM) (2); BERT (6); LSTM (10); RNN (3); DNN (2); ANN (2),MQ-LSTM (10),pre-trained (1),word embedding (4),Rapid Automatic Keyword Extraction (RAKE) (3); term frequency-inverse document frequency (TF-IDF) (2),location (3); time (2); review (2); user attributes (1); edge weight (1); number of vertices (1); end-node (1); starting nodes (1); name (1); month (2); date (2); latitude (1); longitude locations (1); prices (1); photos (1); tips (1); ratings (2); addresses (1),,"80% of the data was used for training, and the remaining 20% of the data was used for testing purposes (1)",,,,,,,,{},LSTM (6); RNN (3); DNN (2); ANN (2),PYTHON (1),,,,,MQ-LSTM (10),"The proposed work underwent various steps like spectral grouping, attribute extraction, tree construction, word embedding, keyword extraction, score value estimation, and ﬁnally a recommendation grounded on the collected details. (1)",yes,['social network (2)'],locations (1),"KNN-based graph generation, a node (Lhs) is connected with its κ closest neighbor (Lce) by an edge that is given weight equal to the inversion of their distance (1)",,,,KNN (1),,,This process is to arrange the historical site location and its nearest events in order. (1),precision (4); recall (4); F-measure (2); sensitivity (1); training time (1); FDR (2); NPV (2); recommendation rate (RR) (5); speciﬁcity (1); misclassiﬁcation rate (MR) (1); Mathews correlation coefﬁcient (MCC) (1); false negative rate (FNR) (1); mean absolute error (MAE) (3),"['the proposed recommendation model achieved a recommendation rate (RR) of 97.22%, precision of 97.7%, recall of 98.27%, and mean absolute error (MAE) of 0.0521 (1)']",[],[],,"From the analysis, it is clear that by obtaining a high RR of 97.22%, the proposed model exhibited superior performance. (1)",[],[],,[],[],[],,LSTM (6); RNN (3); DNN (2); ANN (2),[],ROC curve (2),[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['However, the usage of BERT embedding in this framework makes the system more expensive and it requires more computation. This affects the overall computation complexity of the proposed RS. (1)']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,The data presented in this study are available upon request from the corresponding author. 