"_Ji et al.-2025-Visual Quantification, Spatial D.txt","Visual Quantification, Spatial Distribution and Combination Association of Tourist Attractions in Qingdao Based on Social Media Images",X. Ji; S. Zhang; J. Liu,,2025,journal article,Land,MDPI,https://doi.org/10.3390/,https://doi.org/10.3390/land14091900,,,,,tourist attractions (27),tourism (24); tourism activities; tourism market; tourism demands (7); tourism development (3); tourism industry (2); tourism resources (4); tourist destinations; coastal tourism; coastal leisure cities; coastal city; urban tourism development; urban style; historical buildings; historical urban style; natural landscapes (2); humanistic customs; European-style buildings; characteristic streets; Urban landmarks; leisure formats; tourism scenarios,,"{'SOCIAL': ""Emotional (collective): The study mentions Qingdao's popularity as a coastal leisure city, suggesting a sense of place attachment and communal value associated with its tourism image.""}; {'ECONOMIC': ""Entertainment: The paper discusses Qingdao's tourism market and its attractiveness to tourists, indicating the role of the city in the contemporary tourism market.""}; {'HISTORIC': ""Historic-Artistic: The paper mentions modern Western-style building clusters and characteristic former residences of celebrities in Qingdao, suggesting the city's value as a rare or unique example of historical, stylistic, or artistic movements.""}; {'AESTHETICAL': ""Artistic: The paper refers to Qingdao’s tourism image of coordinated narrative integrating mountains, sea, and city, suggesting the city's value as an original product of creativity and imagination.""}",tourism spatial planning (3); tourism spatial layout planning; resource integration; development; management optimization,Qingdao (14); Jiaozhou Bay; Fushan Bay; Taiping Bay; Laoshan Mountain Range; Guzhenkou–Dongjiakou Bay Area; West Coast Qianhai Bay Area; Jiaozhou Bay Area; East Coast Qianhai Bay Area; Laoshan Bay Area; Dingziwan–Tianheng Bay Area; Shinan District (6); Shibei District (3); Laoshan District (5); Huangdao District (3); Chengyang District; Licang District (2); Jimo District (2); Jiaozhou City (2); Pingdu City (2); Laixi City (2); Badaguan Building Complex; Kang Youwei’s Former Residence; Lao She’s Former Residence; Qingdao Bay; Huiquan Bay; Maidao Bay; Tangdao Bay; Lingshan Bay; Fushan Mountain; Taiping Mountain; Qingdao Mountain; Signal Mountain; Laoshan Mountain; Huangdao Golden Beach; Laoshan Yangkou Beach,China (2); Shandong Peninsula; Yellow Sea; Shandong Province (2),,,"Focusing on the deficiencies of traditional tourism attraction survey methods in terms of accuracy, efficiency, and large-scale visual representation, this study selects Qingdao as the research case, collects tourism image data from the Weibo platform, applies a deep learning model to identify the visual elements of tourism images, and employs kernel density analysis and Apriori association analysis to clarify further the distribution characteristics and associated features of tourist attractions.","Its core objective is to systematically reveal the visual composition, spatial distribution patterns, and related features of tourist attractions in the case study area by identifying and extracting tourist attraction elements from images, thereby providing a decision-making basis for effectively identifying tourism demands and their spatial distribution characteristics, as well as for tourism spatial planning.",Weibo (5),tourism image data (3); photos (3); geographic coordinates (2); users’ attribute information,geographic coordinates (2); geographic information,spatial distribution (7); spatial distribution characteristics (4); spatial agglomeration (3); spatial pattern (3); spatial visualization analysis; spatial dimension exploration,,,users’ IP locations; age; gender; credit status,"59,175 images (3)","10,032 users (2)",,"59,175",,,,from 1 January 2020 to 3 November 2023,Qingdao,web data crawling,Python 3.10.12,,"data is processed and cleaned, and core inclusion criteria for data are established: Weibo content must contain at least one picture and be generated content with precise geographic coordinates. The user account status for publishing Weibo must be normally available.",users with official Weibo credit ratings marked as “poor” or “very poor” are excluded; user data with abnormal ages (under 18 or over 100 years old) are removed; and duplicate publications of the same pictures are deduplicated.,image semantic segmentation,,['visual element types'],,image semantic segmentation (3); image segmentation,deep learning model,Deep Labv3+; Res Ne ST-269,based on the pre-trained weights of the ADE20K dataset,,,original photos,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,"encoder–decoder structure. Its core atrous spatial pyramid pooling module uses multi-scale atrous convolution to capture targets of different sizes accurately, and the decoder fuses shallow boundary features to optimize segmentation accuracy, ultimately outputting pixel-level classification labels.","After inputting the original photos, based on the pre-trained weights of the ADE20K dataset2. The model identifies element categories through pixel-by-pixel classification using an encoder–decoder structure.",,[],,,,,,,Apriori association algorithm,,,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,"['buildings and sea are the core visual elements of tourist attractions in Qingdao', 'tourist attractions in Qingdao take the sea and buildings as the main elements, and are divided into four combination types (building-core, sea-core, cityscape-core, and sign-core) according to the core nature of the dominant elements in the frequent itemsets and the theme characteristics of the scenes.']",[],[],[],[],"['tourist attractions in Qingdao exhibit the spatial distribution characteristic of “distribution around bays and agglomeration towards the sea”, with a certain circular structure and multi-level core distribution pattern.', 'natural tourist attractions in Qingdao generally exhibit the spatial distribution characteristic of “small-scale agglomeration and large-scale dispersion”, with agglomeration centers formed along the coastal zone and distributed in a point-like divergent spatial pattern.', 'the spatial distribution of humanistic tourist attractions in Qingdao is mainly agglomerated at the western end of the Eastern Coast Qianhai Bay Area, with secondary cores scattered in a point-like manner from the coast to inland areas across various counties and districts.']",['provide practical guidance for tourism development'],[],"['providing an extensible technical path for quantitatively representing tourist attractions', 'provides a standardized analysis framework for tourist attraction research and deepens the attraction mechanism of “co-creation by hosts and guests” in tourism.']",[],[],"['over-reliance on visual proportion may ignore symbolic meanings.', 'There are still shortcomings in the research on the value orientation and functional demands of tourist attractions: first, in the identification of tourist attractions, this study uses image segmentation technology to identify tourist attractions, mainly through image proportion and occurrence frequency for analysis, but has not discussed the impact of visual attention;\nin addition, this study only discusses fixed tourist attractions through image segmentation, while lacking discussion on non-material tourist attractions.', 'this study has not further analyzed seasonal variations, and empirical analyses such as comparative studies on differences between multiple case destinations, data sources, and temporal continuity need further verification.']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],The raw data supporting the conclusions of this article will be made available by the authors on request.,The raw data supporting the conclusions of this article will be made available by the authors on request.,,"http://groups.csail.mit.edu/vision/datasets/ADE20K/, accessed on 22 March 2023.",Python environment,SPSS Modeler,,image semantic segmentation; Apriori association analysis; kernel density analysis; Deep Labv3+ model architecture; Res Ne ST-269 backbone network; ADE20K dataset; atrous spatial pyramid pooling module; multi-scale atrous convolution; tourist gaze; host-guest relationship; co-creation by hosts and guests; embodied gaze,,,
_Jia et al.-2024-Research on image style transfer.txt,Research on image style transfer algorithm based on semantic,,,,conference paper,"Third International Conference on Electronic Information Engineering, Big Data, and Computer Technology",,,,,,cultural heritage (1),,,intangible cultural heritage (1),,,,,Yunnan (1),,,"However, the stylized images generated by the existing algorithm are prone to fuzzy texture and inconsistent color distribution with semantic information.","To solve these problems, a framework for semantic perceptual style transfer based on identity loss is proposed.",social media (1); Tiktok (3),images (1); Short video (1),,,,,,,700 million (1),,,,,,,,,,,,,,,[],,style transfer (16); image rendering (2); texture synthesis (2),deep learning (4); convolutional neural networks (2); feedforward network (1); cyclic consistency generation adversarial network (1); autoencoder (2),VGG19 (2); SANet (5); Ada Att N (5); Adal N (3); WCT (2),pre-trained VGG19 network (1),,,content image (10); style image (15),,,identity loss (5); global style loss (2); local feature loss (2),Adam (1),0.0002 (1),8 (1),,,data enhancement (1),{},WCT (2); Adal N (3); SANet (5); Ada Att N (5),,,,,,The algorithm architecture is composed of autoencoder structure.,"The algorithm architecture is composed of autoencoder structure. By introducing the same image as content input and style input at the same time to measure the difference in pixel space and feature space, richer style features and more accurate content structure can be obtained.",,[],,,,,,,,,,,[],[],[],,"Experiments show that the proposed method can realize the style transfer based on semantic information, and the resulting style transfer results are better than other advanced style transfer algorithms.",[],[],,[],[],[],,WCT (2); Adal N (3); SANet (5); Ada Att N (5),[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['The shallow and deep information of content features and style features are considered comprehensively, and the style feature statistics based on attention mechanism are matched with the normalized content features.']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,,,semantic perception (2); attention weighting (2); Measure loss (2); beauty software (1); filters (2); animation manuscript coloring (1); geometric graphic style painting (1); non-photorealistic imagery (1); face attribute editing (1); face photo (1); pixel space (2); feature space (2); feature modeling (1); landscape painting (1); MS-COCO data set (1); Wikiartl46 data set (1),,,"This work was supported by ""Research on Image Style Transfer Algorithm Based on Artificial Intelligence in the Gene Bank of Sports Intangible Cultural Heritage"", funded by the Science Research Fund of Yunnan Provincial Department of Education for Teachers."
_Jiang et al.-2022-Research on the Perception of Cu.txt,Research on the Perception of Cultural Ecosystem Services,JIANG Qianzi; WANG Guangxing; LIANG Xueyuan; LIU Na,"School of Architecture and Urban Planning, Shandong Jianzhu University, Jinan 250101; Ruison Lean Constrction Co., Ltd., Jinan 250101",2022,journal article,,,,,,,Cultural Heritage (3),,urban parks (11); historic buildings (1); historical sites (1); cultural facilities (2); regional culture (1),Cultural Significance (1); historic buildings (1); historical sites (1); cultural facilities (2); regional culture (1),,"{'Social': 'The study mentions spiritual/religious value, sense of place, and social relations, indicating a discussion of social values related to beliefs, cultural identity, and community value.'}; {'Aesthetical': 'The paper highlights aesthetics as the most easily perceived CES category, discussing the delightful visual experience of the beautiful scenery in the park.'}; {'Economic': 'The paper discusses leisure/ecotourism services, which relates to the entertainment value of the asset, especially in the context of tourism.'}; {'Political': 'The paper mentions the educational role of parks, which can be used for political purposes such as disseminating cultural awareness.'}",,Baotu Spring Park; Huancheng Park; Quancheng Park; Daming Lake Park; Zhongshan Park; Baihua Park; Huashan Lake Park; Jinan Forest Park; Wulongtan Park; Jinan Zoo; Jinan City,China; Shandong Province; Jinan City; Licheng District; Lixia District; Shizhong District; Huaiyin district; Tianqiao District,,,"Addressing the above gaps, this research demonstrates a case study on 10 typical urban parks in the central districts of Jinan City, Shandong Province, China by obtaining high-frequency CES perception words and their occurrence frequency via content analysis method of the public comment data from tourism websites; the paper then analyzes the differences of the perceived CES categories in different urban parks, and applies association rules f",the following questions. 1) Which CES categories are most easily perceived by the public in urban parks? 2) What are the differences of CES perception among different urban parks? And 3) can different CES categories be perceived simultaneously in a given site?,Ctrip; Mafengwo; Tripadvisor; Meituan; tourism websites (4),text; photos; geographic; semantic; emotional information,,,,,user names; comments; release dates; ratings,"46,181",,,,,,,"February 9, 2009 to June 23, 2021","study area enclosed by the bypass expressway in Jinan City, covering five administrative districts",crawl comments from tourism websites,,,"clean, segment, vectorize, and structure the textual data",,Delphi method,expert team of 5 professionals,"['spiritual/religious value', 'aesthetics', 'leisure/ecotourism', 'artistic inspiration', 'sense of place', 'cultural heritage', 'education/knowledge', 'social relation', 'cultural ecosystem disservice']",the team reached consensus on all the coding results,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,yes,[],frequent item,,,,,"Excel VBA to replace each codable high-frequency CES perception word in online comments as a “frequent item,” then count the support (i.e. number of occurrence) of each frequent item.",FP-Growth algorithm,,analyze the correlations among the perceived CES categories,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],word cloud,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,Python,,Urban Parks; Landscape Perception; Online Comment Data; FP-Association Rule; Jinan; Urban Green Space; Park City,,,
_Jiang et al.-2025-A Human-machine Collaborative An.txt,A Human-machine Collaborative Annotation Model for Cultural Heritage Images:,Yunzhe Jiang; Xu Tan; Xiaoguang Wang,,2024,conference paper,Joint Conference on Digital Libraries (JCDL’24),ACM,https://doi.org/10.1145/3677389.3702572,https://doi.org/10.1145/3677389.3702572,,2,Cultural Heritage (4),cultural (4),cultural heritage images (6); Dunhuang mural (2); cultural heritage objects,Cultural Significance; cultural heritage (10); domain semantic framework; domain knowledge; cultural background; knowledge graph,,,,Dunhuang murals,Hong Kong; China (2),,,"Cultural heritage images are imbued with profound historical and cultural significance. However, the prevailing image annotation methods for this domain are often plagued by an inverse relationship between the semantic depth of the annotations and the efficiency.",This study proposes a human-machine image collaborative annotation model for cultural heritage that integrates the advantages of deep learning and crowdsourcing.,,images (12),,,,,image length; image width,,,,"1,958",,,,,,,,,,,semi-automated,experts and crowdsourcers,"['simple', 'medium', 'complex']",,object detection; image annotation,deep learning,YOLOv5; Faster R-CNN; YOLOv5-SE; SAM; Clip; DALLE-3,,,,image pixels,,7:2:1,box loss function,,,,10,,,{},Faster R-CNN; initial YOLOv5,,,,,,YOLOv5 enhances the backbone network structure by incorporating CSP (Cross-Stage Partial) connections and PANet (Path Aggregation Network).,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,mean average precision (m AP_0.5); Precision,[],[],[],,The results of crowdsourcing annotation are generally satisfactory.,[],[],,[],[],[],,Faster R-CNN; initial YOLOv5,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],['human-machine collaborative annotation model that adopts a hybrid strategy of crowdsourcing and deep learning'],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,,,entity objects; entity-relation semantics; emotion and cultural background of entities; Buddha's face,,,
