_Kaldeli et al.-2021-CrowdHeritage Crowdsourcing for.txt,Crowd Heritage: Crowdsourcing for Improving the Quality of Cultural Heritage Metadata †,E. Kaldeli; S. Bekiaris; O. Menis-Mastromichalakis; M. Ralli; V. Tzouvaras; G. Stamou,,2021,journal article,Information,MDPI,https://doi.org/10.3390/ info12020064,https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/,,12,cultural heritage (7); digital cultural heritage (2),digital heritage,cultural heritage metadata (3); digital cultural content (1); cultural heritage assets (2); cultural heritage collections (3); cultural heritage records (4); cultural material (1); digital resources (1); digital heritage object (1),metadata enrichment (4); semantic technologies (1); aggregation mechanisms (1); crowdsourcing platform (4); annotation model (1); digital cultural heritage domain (1); CH Institutions (1); digital cultural heritage collections (1); CH portals (1); semantic tagging (2); image tagging (1); geotagging (2); CH repositories (1); CH-speciﬁc training data (1); CH sector (2); digital heritage collections (1); digital heritage (2); Linked Data vocabularies (2); Linked Data vocabularies and datasets (1); EDM-consistent representation (1); CH presentation platforms (1); cultural items (1); European Collections (1); Chinese Heritage (1),,"{'value': 'Social (Emotional (collective))', 'reasoning': 'The paper discusses engaging users and raising awareness about cultural heritage assets, which aligns with fostering cultural identity, motivation, and pride, contributing to a sense of place attachment and communal value.'}; {'value': 'Political (Educational)', 'reasoning': 'The paper mentions engaging pupils and students in meaningful tasks, which aligns with the educational role of heritage assets, often used for political purposes such as nation-building myths or glorification of leaders.'}; {'value': 'Aesthetical (Artistic)', 'reasoning': 'The paper discusses art style recognition and the importance of art studying and artwork or artist categorization, which aligns with the artistic value of heritage assets as original products of creativity and imagination.'}; {'value': 'Historic (Educational)', 'reasoning': 'The paper mentions that through the art style of a painting, one can deduce valid historical facts and extract useful information about artworks, artists, art movements and in general cultural movements and periods, which aligns with the potential of the asset to provide knowledge about the past in the future.'}",metadata quality improvement (3); metadata enrichment (7); validation (6); annotation (13); curation (1); collections creation (1); enrichment (10); moderation (3); tagging (4); publishing (3); improve the quality (5); improve the search (1); improve the presentation (1),,Europe (3); European (7); Irish (1); Italy (1); France (2); China (3); Chinese (2); Gwynedd (1),1950s (1),,"However, due to the complex, heterogeneous and multi-channel aggregation workﬂow and shortcomings in the data providing process, many of the digital resources served through the numerous web platforms suffer from poor metadata descriptions. The lack and insufﬁcient quality of structured and rich descriptive metadata highly affects the accessibility, visibility and dissemination range of the available digital content, and limits the potential of added-value services and applications that reuse the available cultural material in innovative ways, consequently limiting the user experience provided by CH platforms.","To address this need, we propose the Crowd Heritage open end-to-end enrichment and crowdsourcing ecosystem, which supports an end-to-end workﬂow for the improvement of cultural heritage metadata by employing crowdsourcing and by combining machine and human intelligence to serve the particular requirements of the cultural heritage domain.",,audiovisual content (1); textual data (1); images (7); videos (2); metadata (23),geotagging (3),,,upvoting (2); downvoting (2); leaderboards (2); rewards (1); karma points (4),title (3); description (4); creator (2),"more than 12,000 CH records",more than 350 contributors,,,,,,Each campaign lasted three months,trans-European,"collect CH-related data from various sources and take advantage of the federated and faceted search services that allow for the simultaneous search of multiple searchable CH repositories such as Europeana, DPLA, Digital NZ (www.digitalnz.org), the Rijksmuseum (www.rijksmuseum.nl), and others, giving access to a huge set of heterogeneous items (images, videos, different metadata schemata etc.).",Europeana Search and Record API (1),,,,manual (6),human annotator (2),[],,Named Entity Recognition (2); Disambiguation (2); object detection (2); landmark recognition (1); visual recognition tasks (1); art style recognition (3),machine learning (1); deep learning (1); Convolutional Neural Networks (CNN) (1),,trained and tuned on corpora outside the CH sector (1),,,text (2); images (3); metadata (3),,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,The main part of the system consists of a deep ensemble network that uses Convolutional Neural Networks to process images of paintings and recognize their art style.,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],"['making content make readily available for browsing, search, study, and reuse (1)', 'improve the search and presentation services of these platforms (1)', 'curation and collections creation (1)', 'mediating participation in collaborative and interactive projects in CH and humanities (1)', 'mobilizing crowd-taskers with different backgrounds and motivations-domain experts, culture lovers, students, the general public to contribute their knowledge to research and social causes (1)', 'engage with new audiences (1)', 'recruit willing collaborators (1)', 'engaging pupils and students in meaningful tasks (1)', 'citizens at large who expand their knowledge and exercise responsible citizenship in a fun way (1)']",['streamlining and simplifying the work of aggregators and data providers (1)'],"['an easy to use platform, designed to take into account the particularities and requirements set forth by the CH domain without being bound to speciﬁc types of heritage (1)', 'offers a rich variety of features and customization possibilities that make it applicable in a large variety of application use cases and enable any interested party to organize a campaign in the way they wish and (1)', 'can be seamlessly integrated into existing workﬂows at a place in the CH community, through the mapping to common standards regarding the representation of descriptive metadata for collection objects, the interconnection with established CH aggregation and presentation platforms such as Europeana, the modular presentation of different types and formats of CH objects, and the support of a rich set of relevant vocabularies (1)', 'The platform’s interconnection with automatic enrichment tools is also a characteristic that further improves the overall annotation workﬂow as well as the quality of the achieved annotations and opens a large number of future possibilities (1)']",[],[],"['the accuracy of results is negatively affected by the fact that the automatic enrichment tools have been trained and tuned on corpora outside the CH sector (1)', 'the acquisition of appropriate labeled data is a costly process (1)', 'parties interested in exploiting state-of-the-art AI tools for enriching their datasets, lack a streamlined and scalable process for evaluating the automating enrichments and for deciding which are acceptable for being published and presented on their platforms (1)', 'Manual validation of all automatic enrichments is costly and evidently does not scale up, with existing tools lacking the necessary functionalities to support this process (1)']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"The source code is available on Git Hub (https://github.com/ails-lab/crowdheritage), licensed under the Apache 2 license.",Not applicable.,,,"For the backend, the Play Framework (https://www.playframework.com) is used, following the model–view–controller architectural pattern, and the code has been written in Java and Scala. The frontend uses the Aurelia (https://aurelia.io) Java Script client framework, along with Node.js (https://nodejs.org) as a runtime environment. The languages and technologies used for the development are Java Script, Less.js, and HTML5.",,,nichesourcing (2); crowd-taskers (2); AI-driven tools (2); digital cultural objects (1); cultural sector (1); Educational community (1); digital transformation of heritage (1); citizen science project (1); museum collections (1); audiovisual collections (1); museums (1); folksonomy (1); Semantic Web (1); Metadata Interoperability Platform (1); Human-Computer Collaboration (1); art experts (2); art movements (1); cultural movements (1); trans-European crowdsourcing campaigns (1); fashionistas (1); fashion scholars (1); music professionals (1); music teachers (1); music scholars (1); musical instruments (2); medieval depictions (1); famous composers (1); sport-relevant content (1); trafﬁc infrastructure (1); photographic qualities (1); active learning cycle (1); human-in-the-loop (2); active learning (1),,,
_Kamel et al.-2023-A Crowdsourcing Recommendation M.txt,A Crowdsourcing Recommendation Model for Image Annotations in Cultural Heritage Platforms,M.M. Kamel; A. Gil-Solla; L.F. Guerrero-Vásquez; Y. Blanco-Fernández; J.J. Pazos-Arias; M. López-Nores,,2023,journal article,Appl. Sci.,"MDPI, Basel, Switzerland",doi.org/10.3390/app131910623,https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/ 4.0/,,,Cultural heritage (CH) (14); Egyptian heritage (2),tangible (2); intangible (4); digital (3),artwork (1); legacy artefacts (1); monuments (2); museums (2); groups of buildings (1); archaeological sites (1); music (1); values (1); traditions (2); oral history (1); religious ceremonies (1); storytelling (1); cuisine (1); clothing (1); paintings (1); statues (1); buildings (2); historic artifacts (1); drawings inside ancient documents (1),values (2); digital transformation (2); digital cultural content (1); digital heritage (2); digital material (1); digital collection (2); digital collection assets (1); digital collection items (1); digital cultural heritage (1); heritage originals (1); heritage damage (1); preservation (4); conservation (1); metadata (7); annotations (8); open data (2); digitalization (2); digitalisation (1); digitalized newspapers (1),,"{'SOCIAL VALUES': 'Emotional (collective) – The paper discusses cultural heritage as a key element in the identity formation of citizens, highlighting its role in shaping thinking and identity as members of a homogeneous local neighborhood or a universal nation.'}; {'HISTORIC VALUES': 'Educational – The paper mentions that cultural heritage encompasses a wide range of different aspects related to the study and preservation of previously conducted human activities and various societal attributes from previous generations.'}; {'AESTHETICAL VALUES': 'Artistic – The paper refers to tangible elements such as artwork, legacy artefacts, monuments, museums, groups of buildings, or archaeological sites, with a broad range of values from a symbolic, historic, and artistic points of view.'}",heritage preservation (2); heritage study (1); heritage damage (1),Luxor (2); Aswan (2); Upper Egypt (2),UK (1); US (1); Switzerland (1); Europe (1); European Union (2); Egypt (5); Egyptian (5); Australian (1); Campania (1); Italian (1); Galician (1),ancient (2),,"This paper focuses on a very important challenge faced by cultural heritage crowdsourcing platforms, which is how to attract users and make such activities enjoyable for them in order to achieve higher-quality annotations.","Thus, we present an image annotation recommendation system for users of cultural heritage platforms. The recommendation system design incorporates various technologies intending to help users in selecting the best matching images for annotations based on their interests and characteristics.",Facebook (5); Pinterest (1),text (12); images (17); videos (1),,,,,,,approximately 3100 user data elements (1),,6000 images (1),,,,,,crawled (1),,randomly scraped (1),"Arabic text, this was ﬁltered in the data preprocessing, as well as some non-text symbols, such as numbers or emojis.","If some user posts pictures with description, they become ignored as well as they are not useful for our processing.",automatic (2),users (11),[],,classification (12),machine learning (ML) (6); neural networks (NNs) (6); word embeddings (3),Word2Vec (7),trained on the Google News corpus (1),word embeddings (3),,text data (2),,"splits of 60% for training and 40% for testing, 70–30%, and 80–20%. (1)",log-loss function (1),SGD (2),,,,,,{},,,,,,,the model of the NN classiﬁer has been created with only one hidden layer (1),"historic records of accepted/rejected tasks according to the user and image features are fed to the classiﬁer. In the testing phase, the trained model is used to predict some randomly selected images across the user’s features to see if the prediction is correct or not (1)",no,[],,,,,,,,,,classification accuracy (7); average precision (6); F-score (Macro) (3); F-score (Micro) (3); F-score (Weighted) (3),[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],random subsampling (1),,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],['recommendation system (6)'],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,The datasets generated during and/or analyzed during the current study are available from the corresponding author on reasonable request.,,,Python (2),Scikit-learn (1); Gensim (1),,crowdsourcing (16); Semantic Web (3); ontologies (3); machine learning (ML) (6); DBpedia (11); SPARQL (3); RDF (2); SKOS (1); OWL (1); DB-SL (4); Bo W (3); TF-IDF (3); Word2Vec (7); SVMs (2); RFs (2); ANNs (1); GLAMs (2); ICT (3); OCR (1); API (1),,,
