_Karasov et al.-2020-On How Crowdsourced Data and Lan.txt,Communication,Oleksandr Karasov; Marko Kohv; Ivari Chervanyov; Andres Dvorjaninov; Siim Himma,,2020,journal article,Sustainability,MDPI,,http://www.mdpi.com/2073-445X/9/5/158/s1,,,,,,cultural ecosystem service (CES) (7); landscape sustainability (1); landscape values (2); nature conservation (2),,,nature protection (1),Estonia (8); Tallinn (1); Tartu (1); Narva (1),Estonia (6); Russia (1); Belgium (1); Ghent (1); Delaware (1); US (1); Sacramento (1); Switzerland (1),1970s (1),,"However, CESs have proven diﬃcult to quantify, and consequently they are diﬃcult to manage.","In our study, the objectives are to (a) identify and map CES use in Estonia by using a combination of automated content image recognition and topic modelling on photos from selected social media platforms, and (b) quantify the association between two types of landscape attributes reﬂecting subjective landscape organisation, i.e., the landscape coherence and colour harmony of land cover, and CES ﬂow.",Flickr (3); Panoramio (2); Instagram (2); Strava (1); VK.com (4); Twitter (1),photographs (11); images (4); metadata (3); geographic coordinates (2),geographic coordinates (2),,,,user ID (1); photo ID (1); date of taking (1); web-links to photographs (1),"21,242 (1)",,,9983 (1),,,,2015 to 2018 (1),Estonia (1),retrieving metadata by means of application programming interface (API) calls (1),application programming interface (API) (1),,remove the metadata for indoor photographs (1),,manual (2),,[],,topic modelling (6); machine learning classiﬁcation (1); image recognition (3),machine learning models (2),Latent Dirichlet Allocation (LDA) (4),,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,,,,,,
_Karatas et al.-2025-Sustainable Heritage Planning fo.txt,Sustainable Heritage Planning for Urban Mass Tourism and Rural Abandonment: An Integrated Approach to the Safranbolu–Amasra Eco-Cultural Route,E. Karata¸s; A. Özköse; M.A. Heyik,,2025,journal article,Sustainability,"MDPI, Basel, Switzerland",https://doi.org/ 10.3390/su17073157,https://www.mdpi.com/article/10.3390/su17073157/s1,,,Cultural Heritage (10); World Heritage (5); Natural Heritage (7),cultural (12); natural (11); tangible (6); intangible (8); urban (6); rural (7),cultural heritage sites (4); heritage sites (5); historical towns (1); Ottoman architecture (1); archaeological sites (4); civil architectural heritage (1); historic city centers (1); vernacular landscapes (1); ancient cities (1),heritage (30); UNESCO (6); conservation (12); sustainable (16); preservation (10); site management (3); cultural heritage (10); natural heritage (7); World Heritage Site (2); Tentative List (2); archaeological (4); historic (6); urban (6); rural (7); tangible (6); intangible (8); protection (2); planning (12); restoration (4); cultural routes (4); cultural diversity (1); cultural significance (1),,"{'value': 'Social: Emotional (collective)', 'reasoning': 'The study emphasizes the importance of preserving local identity and supporting local production, which aligns with the concept of cultural identity and pride, contributing to a sense of place attachment and communal value.'}; {'value': 'Historic: Educational', 'reasoning': 'The study focuses on historical towns and the preservation of Ottoman architecture, highlighting the potential of these assets to provide knowledge about the past.'}; {'value': 'Aesthetical: Artistic', 'reasoning': 'The study mentions the architectural enrichment of the region and the picturesque appearance of the area, suggesting an appreciation for the artistic and aesthetic qualities of the heritage sites.'}; {'value': 'Economic: Use', 'reasoning': 'The study discusses the function and utility of heritage assets in the context of tourism, indicating a recognition of their economic value through their use as tourist attractions.'}",heritage conservation (6); heritage preservation (3); heritage planning (2); heritage listing (1); heritage protection (1),Safranbolu (14); Amasra (16); Yörük (Üçevler) (2); Hadrianoupolis (4); Küre Mountains National Park (1),Türkiye (10); USA (1); Western Europe (1); southern France (1); Mediterranean region (1); Asia Minor (1); Anatolia (3); Black Sea (4); Karabük Province (3); Bartın Province (2); Germany (1); Spain (1); Poland (1); Lithuania (1); Croatia (1); Romania (1); Portugal (1),Middle Ages (1),COVID-19 pandemic (1),The unplanned development of mass tourism and the increasing abandonment of heritage sites highlight the urgent need for comprehensive planning to control tourism levels and mitigate their impacts.,This study introduces an eco-cultural route aimed at guiding tourism planning in the region to foster sustainable conservation and development.,,GIS (5),,,,,,,,,,,,,,,crowdsourcing field studies (2),Fulcrum mobile and web application (2),,,,,,[],,clustering (5),neural network (2),Self-organizing Map (SOM) (5),,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,,[],,,,,,,,,,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['This study seeks to bridge this gap by proposing an eco-cultural tourism route based on a replicable model that harnesses collective intelligence, historical narratives, and extensive site analysis.']",[],[],[],[],[],['Declaration of Helsinki (1)'],[],[],[],[],[],,Original data will be provided in dialogue with the authors to ensure the safety and anonymity of the people present in the recordings and transcriptions.,,"https://web.fulcrumapp.com/shares/15956227ecc9e0c9?&popup_properties=status, label,administrative_units,type,detection_date,information,photo&title",,,,eco-cultural tourism (6); mass tourism (7); rural abandonment (5); participatory approach (8); stakeholder (11); GIS (5); AHP (6); SWOT analysis