_Kim and Kang-2022-Automatic Classification of Phot.txt,Article ABSTRACT:,Jiyeon Kim; Youngok Kang,,2022,journal article,ISPRS Int. J. Geo-Inf.,MDPI,https://doi.org/10.3390/ ijgi11040245,www.tripadvisor.com,,,,,tourist attractions (8); Gyeongbokgung Palace (6); Insadong (6); palace (2),,,,,Gyeongbokgung Palace; Insadong; Seoul,Korea,Joseon Dynasty,COVID-19,The research methods that analyze tourism photos using recent deep learning technology have a limitation in that they cannot properly classify unique photos appearing in speciﬁc tourist attractions with predetermined photo categories such as Places365 or Image Net dataset or it takes a lot of time and effort to build a separate training dataset to train the model and to generate a tourism photo classiﬁcation category according to a speciﬁc tourist destination.,The purpose of this study is to propose a method of automatically classifying tourist photos by tourist attractions by applying the methods of the image feature vector clustering and the deep learning model.,Trip Advisor; SNS (2),texts; photos (22); videos,,spatial clustering,,,user nickname; region of origin; the number of posts; star rating; review title; date of visit; type of visit; textual body; attached photos; date of creation; nationality data of the publisher,"10,655 reviews",more than 260 million monthly users,,9940 photos,,,,all data before 2020,‘Gyeongbokgung Palace’ and ‘Insadong’ in Seoul,collected reviews of ‘Gyeongbokgung Palace’ and ‘Insadong’ using Python,Python,only selected the photos posted by foreign tourists using language ﬁltering and the visitors’ origin information,excluding Koreans using the publisher’s country of origin and the language used in writing the review,language ﬁltering and the visitors’ origin information,,,[],,clustering (7); image classiﬁcation (4),deep learning model (7); convolutional neural network (CNN) (4); Siamese network (12),VGG16 (7); Face Net (2),pre-trained with Places365 (8),image feature vector (2),scale-invariant feature transform (SIFT); speeded up robust feature (SURF); binary robust independent elementary features (BRIEF),photos,,,triplet loss (2),,,,18,,,{},,,,,,,two convolutional layers were added to the basic structure of the VGG16 network,trained a Siamese network based on the VGG16 network using Gyeongbokgung Palace’s photo dataset,,[],,,,,,,,,,accuracy (4); ROC curve (5); True Positive Rate (TPR) (3); False Positive Rate (FPR) (3),[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],histogram (6),[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['make categories based on clustering results', 'features that make tourism destinations attractive can be identiﬁed more speciﬁcally and ﬂexibly in a data-driven manner', 'set the results of clustering analysis as categories, it is not necessary to manually build the training dataset', 'employ a Siamese network that can improve classiﬁcation performance with a rather small volume dataset']",[],[],"['possibility that various photos may be less mixed because the categories are divided into tourist destinations, tourist attractions, and activities']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,Not applicable,,,,,,tourist destination images (TDI) (4); user-generated contents (UGC) (2); deep learning technology (3); image feature vector clustering (2); automatic classiﬁcation of tourist photos; deep learning model; clustering (7); image classiﬁcation (4); Siamese network (12); convolutional neural network (CNN) (4); VGG16 (7); Places365 (8); t-SNE (4); HDBSCAN (7); DMO (3); scale-invariant feature transform (SIFT); speeded up robust feature (SURF); binary robust independent elementary features (BRIEF); Face Net (2); triplet loss (2); semi-hard triplets (2),,,
_Kim and Son-2021-Assessing and mapping cultural e.txt,Assessing and mapping cultural ecosystem services of an urban forest based on narratives from blog posts,Jeeyoung Kim; Yonghoon Son,"Interdisciplinary Program in Landscape Architecture, Seoul National University, Seoul, Republic of Korea; Graduate School of Environmental Studies, Seoul National University, Seoul, Republic of Korea",2021,journal article,Ecological Indicators,Elsevier Ltd,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ecolind.2021.107983,www.elsevier.com/locate/ecolind,,,,,urban forest (2),,,,,Bukhansan (11); Bukhansan National Park (4); Dobongsan (2); Seoul (2); Gyeonggi-do (2); Baegundae (3); Uiryeong Pass,Korea (4); Seoul; Republic of Korea (2); Gyeonggi-do,Silla,COVID-19 pandemic,"Although extensive research has been conducted to quantify and map the cultural values of nature and wildlife, there are still many challenges that need to be solved.","assessment and mapping of cultural ecosystem services were performed using blog posts on Bukhansan, which is a forest national park and an urban forest in Korea.",Naver (3); Flickr; Panoramio,text (2); geotagged images (2),geotagged images,spatial patterns,,,post title; upload date; summary paragraph; username; post URL,"4,000",28 million,2.1 billion,,,,,"September 2018 to November 2018 (Autumn), December 2018 to February 2019 (Winter), March 2019 to May 2019 (Spring), and June 2019 to August 2019 (Summer)",Bukhansan National Park in Seoul and Gyeonggi-do,web crawler in Python,"Urllib and Beautiful Soup, Requests libraries",One random post was selected among multiple posts by different bloggers to avoid bias.,information related to user identification was excluded.,contents that were open to the public,coded and classified according to the ten categories established in the Millennium Ecosystem Assessment. (MA) (2005),two authors,[],"Almost all author classifications were consistent; however, discussions and cross-checks on disagreements were conducted until a complete consensus was reached.",document classification,embedding model; deep learning,Word2Vec (7),,word embedding,,words; sentences,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,"Word2Vec learning was performed using the Gensim Python module (v3.7.3). To implement Word2Vec, we tokenized the entire corpus of blog posting data using KKMA, a Korean morphological analyzer provided by the Python",no,[],,,,,,,,,,cosine similarity (6),[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['the user rate for Naver Blog was high among those in their 20 s to 30 s (more than 60 percent), and the gender ratio of users is 62 percent female and 38 percent male.', 'social media blind spots caused by differences in age, gender, education, and social level can overlook the opinion of CESs that minority groups have and find ways to supplement their opinions', 'social media can overestimate specific viewpoints, interests, or values']","['To protect user privacy, we only collected the user accounts and contents that were open to the public.']",['This implies the possibility of sample bias in previous studies due to gaps in access to social media and gender participation'],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,Gensim Python module (v3.7.3),Python,,cultural ecosystem services (CESs) (15); indirect use values (5); urban forest (4); blog posts (11); place keywords (7); narrative-based social media (2); Millennium Ecosystem Assessment (MA) (6); word-embedding model (2); distributional semantics; Bukhansan Dulegil (3); Korea national park Research Institute (KNPRI) (2); Naver Map; Kakao Map; location-based service (LBS); POI (point of interest) (2); Arc GIS 10; KKMA,,,
_Kim et al.-2020-Understanding tourists' urban im.txt,Understanding tourists’ urban images with geotagged photos,Nayeon Kim; Youngok Kang,"Department of Social Studies, Ewha Womans University, Seoul, South Korea",2020,other,,,,,,,,cultural,old palaces; historical monuments; cultural assets,cultural properties; historical monuments,,,,Seoul,Seoul; South Korea,Joseon Dynasty,,There have been no studies to analyze the image of tourists in the area by classifying the whole photos posted by the tourists who visit the speciﬁc area.,The purpose of this study is to analyze representative images and elements of sightseeing attractions by analyzing the photos uploaded on Flickr by Seoul tourists.,Flickr; Social Network Services (SNS); Tweeter; Instagram,texts; images; videos; geo-tagged photos; photo metadata,,spatial density,,,owner location,"86,304",1974,,"86,304",,,,"January 1, 2015 to December 31, 2017",Seoul,crawled,open API,,downloaded them into BMP format and then converted them into size of 299 * 299 RGB,,manual labeling,,[],,classiﬁcation,convolutional neural networks (CNN),Inception V3 model; Google Net; Le Net-5; Alex Net; Res Net,"pre-trained model trained by 14,197,122 photographs in Image Net",,Speeded-Up Robust Features (SURF) technique,photo images,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,"CNN is basically composed of three layers such as a convolutional layer, a pooling layer, and a fully connected layer.",,no,[],,,,,,,,,,accuracy ratio,['overall accuracy ratio was about 27.93%'],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,"['tourists have a strong image of palaces, historical monuments, traditional food, and restaurants']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['it analyzes urban image with the photos posted on the SNS by tourists.', 'it uses deep learning technique to analyze the photos.', 'it classiﬁes and analyzes the whole photos posted by Seoul tourists while most researches focus on only speciﬁc objects.']",[],[],"['the Inception v3 model that we applied in this study had a limitation because it is a pre