_Kulkarni et al.-2019-Classification of Cultural Herit.txt,Classiﬁcation of Cultural Heritage Sites Using,,,,other,,,,,,,Cultural Heritage (3); UNESCO listed heritage sites (2),,renowned architectural sites (2); historical sites (1); heritage sites (5); Indian Digital Heritage Space (IHDS) monuments data (1); Indian Heritage Digital Sites (IHDS) (1); heritage monuments (1),heritage (10); cultural assets (2); 3D reconstruction (1); digitalization (1); heritage information (1),,"{'value': 'Emotional (collective)', 'reasoning': 'The paper mentions that cultural heritage connects generations over time and needs to be preserved, indicating a sense of cultural identity, motivation, and pride associated with these sites.'}; {'value': 'Economic', 'reasoning': 'The paper mentions that heritage sites are a source of interest for tourists, suggesting an entertainment value related to tourism.'}; {'value': 'Educational', 'reasoning': 'The paper mentions that heritage sites are a source of interest for historians and architects, suggesting an educational role in providing knowledge about the past.'}; {'value': 'Historic-Artistic', 'reasoning': 'The paper mentions renowned architectural sites, suggesting that these sites are rare or unique examples of historical, stylistic, or artistic movements.'}",preserve (1); archiving (2); documenting (2); sharing the knowledge (2); conserve (1); maintain (1); rehabilitate (1); digital preservation (1),,India (3); New Delhi (1); Mexican (1),,,"The task of archiving, documenting and sharing the knowledge of these cultural assets is challenging due to the scale and reliability of the information.","An accurate prediction of the images to its correct label (heritage site) allows more proﬁcient searches through speciﬁc terms, thus helping in the studying and understanding the heritage assets.",,images (13),,,,,,108080,,,108080,,,,,,crowd source platform,,,images are resized to standard resolution [192X192] and labelled respectively,,manual,,[],,