_Kumar et al.-2020-Detection of Disaster-Affected C.txt,Detection of Disaster-Affected Cultural Heritage Sites from Social,Pakhee Kumar; F. Ofli; M. Imran; C. Castillo,"IMT School for Advanced Studies Lucca; Qatar Computing Research Institute, HBKU Research Complex; Universitat Pompeu Fabra",2020,journal article,"ACM Journal on Computing and Cultural Heritage, Vol. 13, No. 3, Article 23",ACM,10.1145/3383314,https://doi.org/10.1145/3383314,,23:2–23:31,Cultural heritage (10),intangible (2),cultural heritage sites (4); heritage sites (10); archaeological sites (1); monuments (1); cultural landscapes (1); museums (1); galleries (1); libraries (1); artifacts in urban space (2); heritage building (1); heritage city (1); heritage property (1); historic town (1); historic city (1); historic site (1); historic architecture (1); historic center (1); historic settlement (2); historic settings (1); historic civilization (1); historic ensemble (1); historic built (1); historic environment (1); old city (1); old town (1); old buildings (1); sacred building (1); ancient architecture (1); ancient building (1); ancient settlement (1); ceremonial architecture (1); ceremonial buildings (1); landmark building (1); iconic site (1); iconic building (1),protection (1); conservation (1); heritage preservation (1); legally protected (1); Venice Charter (1); damage (20),,"{'value': 'Social (Collective Emotional)', 'reasoning': 'The paper mentions that cultural heritage represents our collective memory and shapes our identity, indicating a sense of cultural identity and communal value.'}; {'value': 'Economic (Use)', 'reasoning': 'The paper states that cultural heritage drives the economy, suggesting a functional and utility value of the assets.'}; {'value': 'Political (Educational)', 'reasoning': 'The paper implicitly discusses the educational role of heritage assets by highlighting the need for protection and conservation, which can be used for political purposes such as nation-building myths or glorification of leaders.'}; {'value': 'Historic (Educational)', 'reasoning': 'The paper refers to cultural heritage as representing our collective memory, indicating its potential to provide knowledge about the past in the future.'}; {'value': 'Aesthetic (Artistic)', 'reasoning': 'The paper mentions artifacts and artworks as part of cultural heritage, suggesting an original product of creativity and imagination.'}; {'value': 'Age (Existential)', 'reasoning': 'The paper refers to cultural heritage as representing our collective memory, which represents memory and the lives of past generations.'}",protection (1); conservation (1); heritage management (2),Nepal,Italy; Qatar; Spain; London; Turkey; India; UK; Denmark; Bhutan; France; Australia; China; Indonesia; USA; Vietnam; Myanmar; Afghanistan; Syria; Yemen; Netherlands; Brazil; Malta; Canada; Peru; Pakistan; Mexico; Jordan; Greece,,2015 Nepal earthquake,"Most works have focused on extracting urgent needs from the affected populations, while in comparison applications for detecting and evaluating damage to cultural heritage using social media data have not been studied.","This article aims to bridge this gap by describing a method to automatically detect images of cultural heritage sites, particularly images depicting damage.",Social networking sites; Twitter (5); Flickr (3); Instagram (2); Facebook (1),images (23); text (2); multimodal data (1),,spatial and temporal pattern analysis (1),,retweeted images (1),,1.8 billion images are shared daily on social media platforms,,,"6,529 images",,,,2015,Nepal,Google Image Search was used to construct two datasets of images.,,,"images that are significantly edited, images where a heritage site is merely a backdrop and not the main subject (e.g., selfies), images that are covered almost entirely with text, 3D reconstruction or 3D models of sites, paintings of heritage sites, memes, architectural plans and sections of heritage sites, sketches, maps, images in which contextual information is missing (e.g., a close-up photograph of a stone in a building), and images of replicas unless it has a protected status.",,manual (2),lead author of this article (a domain expert),"['heritage vs. not-heritage', 'damaged heritage vs. not-heritage', 'SEVERE damage', 'MILD damage', 'NO damage']",,classification (11); damage assessment (5),deep neural networks (2); convolutional neural networks (CNNs) (5); deep learning models (2),VGG16 (4); Res Net50 (4); Dense Net121 (6); Inception Res Net V2 (4); Xception (4); NASNet Large (4),pretrained on the Image Net dataset,,Scale Invariant Feature Transform (SIFT) (1); Histogram of Oriented Gradients (HOG) (1),raw data (1),,80:20,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,The Dense Net121 network consists of 121 layers and around 8 million weight parameters,Our heritage classification system is composed of two stages: (i) deep feature extraction and (ii) training a heritage/not-heritage classification model,no,[],,,,,,,,,,Precision (positive predictive value) (2); Recall (or sensitivity) (2); F1-score (5); accuracy (1); confusion matrix (6),[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],site-based data split,lexicon-based model (6),[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],['rapid damage assessment (2)'],['post-disaster heritage management practices (1)'],[],[],[],"['The quality of our classifier can be improved by a larger, more diverse training set.']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,https://crisisnlp.qcri.org/heritage,,,,,,,
_Kumi et al.-2024-Uncovering Concerns of Citizens.txt,Uncovering Concerns of Citizens Through Machine Learning,Sandra Kumi; Charles Snow; Richard K. Lomotey; Ralph Deters,"University of Saskatchewan, Canada; The Pennsylvania State University, University Park, PA, USA; The Pennsylvania State University, USA; Penn State Beaver Campus; University of Saskatchewan",2024,journal article,,,,,,,,,,,,,,city of Saskatoon,Canada; Saskatoon; Saskatchewan; North America,,COVID-19 pandemic,The challenge however is that there is no straightforward way to analyze societal issues from data.,"In this work, our goal is to analyze the concerns of the citizens of Saskatoon, Canada based on their social media engagements.",Reddit; Twitter,text,,,,,,"2,562",,"114,390 comments",,,,,"January 1, 2019, to September 20, 2023","Saskatoon, Canada",We leveraged the Python Reddit API Wrapper (PRAW),Python Reddit API Wrapper (PRAW),"to collect the hot, top, contro- versial, and rising posts from the Saskatoon subreddits.","Removal of bots and Auto Moderator accounts, Removal of [deleted] or [removed], Removal of Links, Removal of non-English comments, Expand contractions, Check duplicate comments",We eliminated comment rows with such contents as they are irrelevant.,manually annotated,,"['negative comments', 'positive comments', 'neutral comments']",,topic modeling; sentiment analysis; classification; clustering,Topic Models; Transformer models; supervised ML models,Latent Dirichlet Allocation (LDA); Non-negative Matrix Factorization (NMF); BERTopic; Si EBERT; Ro BERTa-large,Si EBERT (a pre-trained transformer model),BERT embeddings; SBERT; TF-IDF,Bag-of-Words (Bo W); Term Frequency-Inverse Document Frequency (TF-IDF),text,,stratified 10-fold cross-validation,,,,,,,,{},VADER; Logistic Regression; Decision Tree; Random Forest; Extreme Gradient Boosting (XGBoost),"Mac operating system with an Intel Core i7 3.8 GHz 8-Core Processor with 32GB of memory, Google Colab notebooks with GPU runtime",,,32GB,,,"We used three topic modeling algorithms namely, Latent Dirichlet Alloca- tion (LDA), Non-negative Matrix Factorization (NMF), and BERTopic to discover the hidden topics in the collected com- ments. We categorized similar topics into themes, and then leveraged sentiment analysis tools to explore the sentiments of each text in the discovered themes.",,[],,,,,,,,,,Accuracy; Precision; Recall; F1-Score; CV; UMass,"['The BERTopic with the K-means clustering algorithm achieved the highest coherence score of approximately 0.64 in the extraction of 25 topics from the dataset.', 'The Si EBERT model outperformed the other sentiment classifiers with an accuracy of 89% in the prediction of sentiments.']",[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],We used a stratified 10-fold cross-validation to train and evaluate the ML models.,LDA; NMF; BERTopic_UMAP_HDBSCAN; VADER; Logistic Regression; Decision Tree; Random Forest; Extreme Gradient Boosting (XGBoost),[],intertopic distance map; similarity matrix,[],[],[],[],[],[],['smart city design'],[],"['Employed AI/ML, and social media data from the Red- dit community to highlight the societal issues affecting the citizens of Saskatoon, Canada.', 'Explored multiple AI/ML topic models such as LDA, NMF, and BERTopic to determine the best-performing model as applied to the Reddit data.', 'The work further evaluated the performance of the BERTopic model (a) when no preprocessing is done, and (b) when data is pre-processed.']","['The research discovered factors for smart city engagement such as Housing and Facilities, Education, Downtown Devel- opment, Tourism and Entertainment, Policing, Healthcare, Online Community, Cost, and Animal Control.']",[],['Topic Models used in this study perform better on short texts than long texts.'],[],"['We used a stratified 10-fold cross-validation to train and evaluate the ML models.', 'The Synthetic Minority Over-Sampling Technique (SMOTE) is applied to handle our imbalance annotated dataset.']",[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,Gensim; bertopic; scikit-learn; NLTK; Hugging Face,,smart city; social good; citizens’ engagement; governance; smart city deployment; value chain; governance structure; societal issues; social media data/posts; users’ sentiments; views; needs; demands; public discourse; international trade; developmental projects; social approach; text vectorization; bag-of-words (Bo W); semantic similarity; Bidirectional Encoder Representations from Transform- ers (BERT) embeddings; contextual word and sentence vector representations; coherent and accu- rate topic representations; lexical sentiment analysis classifier; social science; social computing; Natural Language Processing (NLP); opinion analysis; self-driving cars; Markov models; neg- ativity (toxicity); deep learning-based classifier; word embedding; bidirectional Recurrent Neural Networks (RNN); Dilated Convolutional Neural Network (DCNN); Sentic Net; public emotions; BERT sentence clustering; public sentiments; COVID-19 vaccination; agriculture stake- holders; support vector machines (SMV); rule-based classification; emotionally dis- tressed individuals; fusion sentiment analysis model; Artificial Neural Networks (ANN); geospatial data; big data analytics; urban planning; livability in cities; transit experience; road crashes; event detection; Social Media Analysis (SMA); Multiple Regression Analysis (MRA); semantic-based risk classification; supervised NLP techniques; criminal networks; Long Short Term Memory (LSTM); military sentiment dictionary; hate and aggressive speech; Logistic Regression; CNN; political microtargeting (PMT); attitudinal and behavioral changes; electioneering season; fake news; misinformation; K-Nearest Neighbors; Linear Regression; Multinomial Naïve Bayes; Decision Trees; SVM; Random Forest; Gradient Boosting; Multilayer Perception; false or misleading COVID-19 information; Hybrid Heterogeneous SVM; misinformation; cost-effectively monitoring; urban infrastructure; computer vision; semi-supervised lear