_Kádár and Gede-2013-Where do tourists go Visualizin.txt,Where Do Tourists Go? Visualizing and Analysing the Spatial Distribution of Geotagged Photography,Bálint Kádár; Mátyás Gede,Budapest University of Technology and Economics; Eötvös Loránd University,2013,journal article,Cartographica The International Journal for Geographic Information and Geovisualization,,10.3138/carto.48.2.1839,https://www.researchgate.net/publication/262972685,,,,,,,,,,Budapest,Estonia; Florence; Italy; Hong Kong; Germany; Go¨rlitz,,,"Ashworth and Page (2011), reviewing the most recent progress in urban tourism research, noted, ‘‘Given the quantitative importance of urban tourism, it is curious that very little attention has been given to questions about how tourists actually use cities.’’","Our primary aim is to provide an easy-to-use tool for urban planners and urban tourism scholars showing the spatial and temporal distribution of people spending time in a city, with a focus on the different behaviours of visitors staying only one day, visitors staying for longer periods, and locals.",Flickr.com; Facebook,photographs; images; geographical coordinates (latitudes/longitudes),geotags; geographical coordinates (latitudes/longitudes),spatial distribution,time-stamps,,ID number of the photo; ID number of its owner; the time-stamp of its creation; the coordinates of the geotag,"more than 100,000 photos that are geographically positioned in Budapest",4546,,"more than 100,000",,,,one year,Budapest,downloading,application programming interface (API),,,download only photos with the highest accuracy value (16),,,[],,clustering,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,yes,['tourist graph'],photo locations,paths of photographers between these nodes,,,,automated clustering of photo locations,,,Analysing this graph could lead to new conclusions in regard to the structure of the city.,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],['urban planning'],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,the downloaded database i