_Lee and Son-2023-Mapping of user-perceived landsc.txt,Mapping of user-perceived landscape types and spatial distribution using crowdsourced photo data and machine learning: Focusing on Taeanhaean National Park,Sunghee Lee; Yonghoon Son,"Interdisciplinary Program in Landscape Architecture, Seoul National University, Seoul, Republic of Korea; Graduate School of Environmental Studies, Seoul National University, Seoul, Republic of Korea",2023,journal article,Journal of Outdoor Recreation and Tourism,Elsevier Ltd,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jort.2023.100616,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jort.2023.100616,,,Cultural Heritage (1),natural (1),coastal landscapes (2); forest landscapes (3); sand dunes (2); horizontal land landscapes (2); urban landscapes (3); Taeanhaean National Park (20); Sinduri Coastal Sand Dune (2),cultural ecosystem services (CES) (4); national parks (7); protected areas (PAs) (10); Natural Monument (1),,"{'SOCIAL VALUES': 'Emotional (collective) – The study identifies landscape types that users perceive and experience in Taeanhaean National Park, reflecting cultural identity and a sense of place attachment.'}; {'AESTHETICAL VALUES': 'Artistic – The study analyzes social media images to understand user perceptions of landscapes, indicating an appreciation for the artistic and scenic qualities of the natural environment.'}; {'ECOLOGICAL VALUES': 'Spiritual – The study explores the relationship between humans and the environment in Taeanhaean National Park, suggesting a harmony between the natural setting and human experiences.'}",management (3); monitoring (4); management plan (3); conservation (1),Taeanhaean National Park; Taean Peninsula; Garorim Bay; Anmyeondo Island; Seoul; Hakampo; Yeongmok; Sinduri Coastal Sand Dune; Hakampo Beach; Mallipo Beach; Mongsanpo Beach; Cheongpodae Beach; Kkotji Beach; Sobunjeomdo Island,Republic of Korea (2); Korea (1); South Korea (1); Seoul (2); Chungcheongnam-do (1); Korean Peninsula (1); Germany (1); Netherlands (1),,,User 