"_Li et al.-2023-Scene clusters, causes, spatial.txt","Scene clusters, causes, spatial",Jiayan Li; TX; PY; MS; XG; Jingyuan Lin; ML; PT; XD,"Department of Landscape Architecture, Beijing Forestry University, 35 Qinghua East Road, Haidian District, Beijing, China; Department of Landscape Architecture, Zhejiang A & F University, 88 Huancheng North Road, Lin’ an District, Hangzhou, Zhejiang, China",2023,journal article,Heritage Science,Springer Nature,https:// doi.org/ 10. 1186/ s40494- 023- 01051-x,https:// doi.org/ 10. 1186/ s40494- 023- 01051-x,,29,Cultural Heritage (2); cultural heritage value (1),cultural (4); natural (4),Tang Poetry Road (10); classical Chinese poetry landscapes (1); landscape heritage corridors (1); natural and cultural heritage landscapes (1); Tang poetry landscape features (1); historical poetry texts (1); scenic spots (2); literary landscape characteristics (1); poetic works (1); natural and cultural heritage value (1); scenic elements (1); historical allusions (1); scenic elements (1); historical landmarks (2); ancient prefectural city (1); historical sites (1); ancient relics (1); ancient cities (1); cultural sites (1); poetic heritage (1),heritage (1); cultural (4); natural (4); cultural heritage (2); cultural heritage value (1); preservation (1); heritage corridors (2); heritage value (1); heritage landscapes (1); heritage secrets (1); heritage corridor (1); heritage sites (1); heritage corridor experience (1); heritage and provides guidance (1),,"{'value': 'Social: Emotional (collective)', 'reasoning': 'The study explores the cultural and natural landscapes depicted in Tang poems, aiming to promote visual transmission of poetic aesthetic heritage and guide the development of differentiated landscapes, thus fostering a sense of cultural identity and communal value.'}; {'value': 'Historic: Educational', 'reasoning': 'The research seeks to uncover elements of natural and cultural landscapes within Tang poetry texts, construct a database of Tang poetry landscape elements, and extract aesthetic imagery, contributing to the potential of the asset to provide knowledge about the past.'}; {'value': 'Aesthetical: Artistic', 'reasoning': 'The study focuses on extracting the aesthetic imagery of Tang poetry landscapes and promoting the visual transmission of poetic aesthetic heritage, highlighting the original product of creativity and imagination in the poetic works.'}",preservation (1); conservation (2); planning (3); development (4),Tang Poetry Road in eastern Zhejiang (4); Mount Lu (1); Eastern Zhejiang (4); Shaoxing (7); Taizhou (7); Ningbo (7); Hangzhou (2); Zhoushan (1); Kuaiji ancient prefecture in Yuezhong (1); Tiantai County (1); Yuyao (1); Jinghu lake (2); Shanxi (1); Dayu Cave (2); Xishi Mountain (1); Yunmen Mountain (1); Wuzhou Mountain (2); Ruoye Creek (2); Wanwei Mountain (2); Jian Lake (1); Siming Mountain (1); Chicheng Mountain (2); Xuedou Temple (2); Chenxin Temple (1); Longxing Temple (1); capital of Yuezhou (1); ancient city of Linhai (1); Shanzhong (1); Yanxi River (1); Tongbai Mountain (1); Shiqiao Temple (1); Cao’e River basin (1),Eastern Zhejiang (5); China (4); Zhejiang Province (5); Beijing (3); Jiangnan (3); Hangzhou Bay (1); Yangtze River (1); Sichuan (1),Tang Dynasty (12),,"Undertaking digital humanities research using Chinese classical poetry as the material holds crucial significance in uncovering the value of world cultural heritage. However, compared to Indo-European literary traditions, Chinese ancient poetry, which belongs to the Sino-Tibetan language family, often relies on word order and function words as the primary means of expressing grammatical meaning [12]. This characteristic consequently brings about complex variations in word meanings, posing substantial challenges to the quantitative mining of knowledge and information in classical poetry texts.","(1) to uncover the elements of natural and cultural landscapes within the Tang poetry texts and construct a database of Tang poetry landscape elements specific to eastern Zhejiang, (2) to extract the aesthetic imagery of Tang poetry landscapes in Shaoxing, Taizhou, and Ningbo cities, thereby promoting the visual transmission of poetic aesthetic heritage, and (3) to identify key regions constituting distinctive characteristics of landscape imagery and conduct causal analyses, thereby guiding the development of differentiated landscapes in different regions.",,text (15); spatial maps (1),location information (1),spatial differentiation features (2); spatial distribution (2),,,geographic information (1); location information (1); biographical information (1),"1,589 (1)",376 (1),"1,589 (1)",,,,,,eastern Zhejiang (1),crawled (1),"Python Requests module (1), Baidu API (1)",semantic comparative sampling (1),"character-level segmentation (1), frequency analysis (1), part-of-speech tagging (1), low-frequency characters appeared less than twice and meaningless characters were removed (1)",Two hundred and eighty-three (283) poems with no clear geographic information were excluded as well as 11 poems written in Zhoushan and Hangzhou with strong text contingency (1),manual (2),,"['skyscape (3)', 'landscape (7)', 'waterscape (6)', 'animals (4)', 'plants (4)', 'people (5)', 'construction (5)', 'allusions (6)']",,text mining (8); named entity recognition (1); text clustering (4); sentiment analysis (1); semantic analysis (2); clustering (10),semantic networks (4),,,,,text (15); spatial information (2); location information (1); geographic information (1); biographical information (1),,5–5 proportionate split (1),,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,"The Python Jieba module was utilized for named entity recognition, followed by the implementation of code using functions such as Replace, Collections, and Posseg. These functions facilitated character-level segmentation, frequency analysis, and part-of-speech tagging.",yes,"['co-occurrence semantic networks (2)', 'social network (4)', 'hyper-network (1)']",natural and cul