_Li et al.-2025-Spatial distribution and influen.txt,Spatial distribution and influencing,Congzhi Li; Ying Pan; Weilun Yin; Siren Lan,,2025,journal article,Acta Ecol. Sin.,Springer Nature,,,,,,,village (7); rural environments (1); rural areas (3); ancient houses (1); ancient roads (1); Confucian temple (2); ancestral hall (1); Fujian’s villages (1); villages (2),heritage characteristics (1); culture (10); cultural (10); traditional customs (1); cultural resources (1),,"{'SOCIAL VALUES': 'Cultural identity: The study discusses the unique connotations of villages as geographical and social entities, reflecting a sense of place and cultural identity. The presence of features like ancient houses and roads contributes to this collective emotional value.'}; {'AESTHETICAL VALUES': 'Artistic: The study mentions the visual appeal of villages, encompassing words such as most beautiful grassland and cherry blossoms, reflecting the artistic value of the landscape.'}; {'HISTORIC VALUES': 'Educational: The study discusses the process of the village transmitting knowledge to the audience, with representative words including tour guide, wisdom, and interpretation, reflecting the educational role of heritage assets.'}; {'SOCIAL VALUES': 'Spiritual: The study mentions words like ancestral hall, feeling, and peacefulness, reflecting the spiritual contentment in individuals.'}; {'ECONOMIC VALUES': 'Entertainment: The study mentions activities in the village, such as entertainment, leisure, and sightseeing, with representative words including attractions, transportation, and tickets, reflecting the role the asset plays in the contemporary market, especially tourism.'}",,Fujian Province; Pingtan County; Fuzhou City; Nanping City; Sanming City; Quanzhou City; Xiamen City; Zhangzhou City; Longyan City; Shanghang; Xiapu counties; Gutian; Cangshan District of Fuzhou City,Fujian Province; China; English countryside; Lower Rhine area; Switzerland; Baltic Sea; Finland; Brazilian coastline; Europe; Beijing; Colorado; Wyoming; Nanjing; Patagonia; Portugal; Shenzhen; Dalian; Kona; Hawai ‘i; Shaanxi Province,,,"Faced with the current limited resources, how to scientifically and rationally allocate resources to promote the high-quality development of rural cultural services has become a key issue that needs to be addressed.",The exploration of methods to precisely quantify the spatial distribution of rural cultural ecosystem services (CES) and a deep analysis of the influencing factors behind them is both a long and challenging research path.,Dianping.com,review texts; online textual data,,spatial distribution map,,,,,,,,,,,,Fujian Province,,,,implement appropriate data cleaning and preprocessing steps to ensure the robustness and validity of the research results.,,,"Two experts, three Ph D students, and five Master’s students were invited to classify the 28 topics into CES categories, considering the meaning of rural CES and the characteristics of the comment data, while referring to relevant literature.","['aesthetic', 'spiritual', 'recreational', 'knowledge', 'culture', 'popular science']",,topic modeling; classification,Topic Models,BTM,,word vector,,word pair,,,,,,,2000,,,"{'K': '28', 'α': '50/K', 'β': '0.01'}",,,,,,,,The modeling process of the BTM comprises four steps (Fig. 3): (1) Constructing a word-pair corpus using the target text as the foundational data; (2) Training the model with the word pair corpus; (3) Adjusting model calculation parameters; (4) Generating the topic distribution.,no,[],,,,,,,,,,Perplexity; Coherence; topic validity (TV),[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],word cloud,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['the governments of the coastal regions increase their investment in transport infrastructure construction in remote regions, improve transport accessibility in remote regions, and make people aware of the different cultural characteristics of the coastal regions in order to increase the perceived value of the region’s cultural type services.', 'Inland areas, such as Sanming, Longyan, and Nanping, should address infrastructure deficiencies, enhance service quality, leverage cultural diversity advantages, and emphasize cultural depth experiences.', 'Both coastal and inland areas should enhance rural scientific capabilities, refine rural interpretation systems, and innovate rural research and learning approaches.', 'villages should be prioritized for holistic development to create a unified rural ambiance and to prevent waste of resources due to micro-renewal.']",[],[],[],"['the generation of the CES distribution map in this study was based on interpolation methods, which are highly dependent on the spatial location of rural samples.', 'When using online review texts for CES assessment, the data are collected from internet platforms, meaning they reflect certain user characteristics.', 'Although nine indicators in the areas of Natural ecology, Community economy and Attractive potentiality were selected to explore the influencing factors of CES in this study, these indicators can only shed light on some of the causes.']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,,,rural CES; rural ecosystem cultural services; Maritime Silk Road; mountainous areas; coastal city; coastal regions; inland areas; night economy; night scenery; night experience activities; rural ambiance; micro-renewal; interpolation methods; online review texts; internet platforms; Natural ecology; Community economy; Attractive potentiality; ecological resource endowment; community cultural characteristics; economic drivers,,,
