_Liao et al.-2023-Quantifying and mapping landscap.txt,Quantifying and mapping landscape value using online texts: A deep learning approach,Jingpeng Liao; Qiulin Liao; Weiwei Wang; Shouyun Shen; Yao Sun; Peng Xiao; Yuci Cao; Jiaao Chen,"College of Landscape Architecture, Central South University of Forestry Technology, Changsha, 410004, Hunan, China; Hunan Provincial Big Data Engineering Technology Research Center of Natural Reserve and Landscape Resource, China; Institute of Human Settlements and Green Infrastructure of Central South University of Forestry and Technology, China",2023,journal article,Applied Geography,Elsevier,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.apgeog.2023.102950,www.elsevier.com/locate/apgeog,,,Historic urban landscape (5),,Orange Islands (2); Orange Island (20); historic buildings (3); historical landscape (2); cultural landscape (3),recommendation on the historic urban landscape (HUL) (7); heritage value (2); historical attributes; cultural values (3); natural values (2); historical value (10); heritage conservation (2); historic buildings (4); cultural heritage; historic urban landscape (2),,"{'Social': 'The study discusses the importance of public perception, emotional tendency, and intensity in evaluating landscape value, indicating a focus on collective emotional and cultural identity.'}; {'Aesthetical': 'The paper mentions the aesthetic value of landscapes and how urban development can lead to its disappearance, suggesting a discussion of artistic and notable qualities.'}; {'Economic': 'The paper mentions economic value and the role of tourism, indicating a discussion of the entertainment value of heritage assets.'}; {'Political': 'The paper discusses the educational role of heritage assets and the importance of public participation in historical landscape conservation, suggesting a discussion of educational and management values.'}; {'Historic': 'The paper discusses the historical attributes of landscapes and the importance of examining urban history, indicating a discussion of the potential of the asset to provide knowledge about the past.'}",heritage conservation (2),Orange Island; Xiangjiang River; Changsha city; Hunan Province,China (4); Hunan Province (3); Changsha city (3); New Zealand,early 20th century,,"Current studies have quantified landscape value based on the quantity of social media, ignoring public preference, emotional tendency and intensity.",Our objective is to quantify and map landscape value by developing a novel intelligent landscape value evaluation method based on online texts.,Twitter; Google Places; Flickr; Instagram; Airbnb; Panoramio; Ctrip (5); Go Where (5); Dianping (5),images; text; audiovisual elements,,spatial distribution,,,,"more than 14,000 (2)",,"14,394",,,,,from 2010 to 2020 (2),Orange Islands in Changsha city,crawled,Scrapy data crawler,,"Python and Excel functions such as ‘find’, ‘sort’ and ‘filter’",eliminate invalid comments,,,[],,sentiment analysis,deep convolutional neural networks (CNNs); long short-term memory (LSTM),Clarifai; Google Cloud Vision; latent Dirichlet allocation (LDA),,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,bidirectional single-layer LSTM model,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,perception frequency; perception heat; perception preference; value index,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],perception heatmaps; preference maps; value maps,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],['novel intelligent landscape value evaluation method based on online texts'],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,,,,,,
_Lin and van Ameijde-2024-LEVERAGING SOCIAL MEDIA AND NATU.txt,LEVERAGING SOCIAL MEDIA AND NATURAL LANGUAGE,S. LIN; J. VAN AMEIJDE,,2024,conference paper,"ACCELERATED DESIGN, Proceedings of the 29th International Conference of the Association for ComputerAided Architectural Design Research in Asia (CAADRIA)","the Association for Computer-Aided Architectural Design Research in Asia (CAADRIA), Hong Kong",,,,109-118,cultural heritage (4),cultural (7); historic (3),historic urban places (1); historic districts (3); historical and cultural heritage site (1); historic urban areas (2); ancient city (1),cultural significance (1); cultural values (3); cultural heritage (5); historic (3); cultural perception (11); cultural preservation (3); historic districts (3); historic urban areas (2); cultural interventions (1); cultural events (4); historical values (2); cultural meanings (1); cultural activities (2); cultural heritage protection (1),,"{'SOCIAL': 'Emotional (collective) – The study analyzes public discussions on Weibo to understand cognitive and emotional responses to the cultural values of Nantou Walled City, indicating a focus on cultural identity and sense of place attachment.'}; {'HISTORIC': 'Educational – The study uses NLP to analyze public perceptions of Nantou Walled City, aiming to provide knowledge about its past and cultural significance through social media data.'}; {'AESTHETICAL': ""Artistic – The study identifies themes related to art and creative products in Nantou Walled City, reflecting the public's interest in the artistic aspects of the area.""}",cultural heritage preservation (2); cultural preservation (1); cultural heritage management (1); urban renewal (5); land redevelopment (1); urban regeneration (1); conservationists (1); intervention strategies (1),Nantou Walled City (9); Shenzhen (3),China (1); Chinese region (1),,Bi-City Biennale of Urbanism/Architecture (UABB) in 2017 (2),"The preservation of cultural heritage during urban renewal processes is an issue that is often subservient to economic urban development goals. While physical structures of historic importance might be preserved or adapted, the social and cultural significance of historic urban places is often lost during the comprehensive redevelopment of historic neighbourhoods. The absence of adequate measurements and procedures to assess the cultural and social values of historic districts remains a key concern in urban renewal practice.","This research presents a novel workflow to analyse text data from social media platforms. Referencing recently developed methods for multidimensional text mining and sentiment analysis, it obtains online text data by identifying the keywords on the Weibo platform and applies BERTopic to construct a quantitative assessment of cultural perceptions by identifying the topics and sentiments about a historic district.",Weibo (4),text (6),,,time series (1),retweet volume (1); comment volume (1); likes volume (1),comment time (1),"5,702 comments (1)",,"3,037 valid text data (1)",,,,,1 January 2023 to 1 December 2023 (1),Chinese region (1),web crawler technology (1),,"setting the keywords ""Nantou Walled City"" and ""culture"" on the Weibo platform (1)","screening measures were taken to exclude comments with obvious advertising colours, comments that only mentioned Nantou Walled City, but the actual description of the content or object of the evaluation was not related to culture and duplicated content (1)","comments with obvious advertising colours, comments that only mentioned Nantou Walled City, but the actual description of the content or object of the evaluation was not related to culture and duplicated content (1)",,,[],,topic modelling (6); sentiment analysis (5); classification (2),deep learning (4); Transformer models (1),BERTopic (8); BERT (5); LDA (3); NMF (2); SVM (2),,BERT text embedding (2),,text (2),,,,,,,,,,{},LDA topic models (1); NMF data feature extraction (1); SVM classification algorithms (1),,,,,,"The model combines the techniques of BERT text embedding, UMAP dimensionality reduction, and HDBSCAN clustering to effectively extract text topics and their keywords.",,no,[],,,,,,,,,,similarity ranking (1),[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],['This study provides a new perspective for urban planners and conservationists in the assessment of cultural values and the development of intervention strategies in historic urban areas.'],[],[],"['the research methodology still needs to be improved in the face of challenges specific to Chinese social media data, such as information filtering and the accuracy of sentiment analysis.']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,,,Natural Language Processing (NLP) (3); Big Data (1); Machine Learning (1); sentiment polarity (3); social media data analysis (1); urban micro-regeneration (1); thematic quantitative analysis (1); fine-grained sentiment analysis (2); affective polarity (2),,,
