_Liu et al.-2019-Isolated or integrated Planning.txt,"Isolated or integrated? Planning and management of urban renewal for historic areas in Old Beijing city, based on the association network system",Zhao Liu; Shunyi Wang; Fang Wang,"NSFC-DFG Sino-German Cooperation Group on Urbanization and Locality (UAL), College of Architecture and Landscape Architecture, Peking University, Beijing, 100871, PR China",2019,journal article,Habitat International,Elsevier,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.habitatint.2019.102049,,,,,cultural; historic,historic areas (14); Old Beijing city (10); historic architecture (1); cultural landscapes (1); historic buildings (1),heritage protection (2); heritage conservation (3); historic heritage conservation (1); heritage nodes (3); heritage trails (1); heritage routes (2); heritage environment (1); cultural heritage (2); heritage (10); Integral conservation (1); cultural resources (1); historic features (1); urban fabric (2); historic areas (14); historic buildings (1); cultural landscapes (1); historic construction (1); cultural value (1); historic old cities (1); national historic and cultural conservatory areas (1),,"{'SOCIAL': 'Emotional (collective) – The study emphasizes the importance of tourism in enhancing the sense of belonging and identification within the community, which aligns with the emotional (collective) value related to cultural identity and pride.'}; {'HISTORIC': 'Educational – The study focuses on the potential of historic areas to provide knowledge about the past, which aligns with the educational value of heritage assets.'}; {'ECONOMIC': 'Use – The study discusses the function and utility of historic areas in terms of tourism and economic development, which aligns with the use value of heritage assets.'}",heritage protection (2); heritage conservation (3); heritage trails (1); heritage routes (2),Old Beijing city (10); Xihua Gate Street historic and cultural conservatory area (1); Xisi Area (No. 1) (3); Fuchengmen Street (No. 2) (3); Shichahai Area (No. 3) (5); Nanluogu Lane (No. 4) (7); Guozijian (No. 5) (3); Beichizi Street (No. 6) (4); Nanchizi Street (No. 7) (5); Dongsi Area (No. 8) (6); Dongjiaominxiang (No. 9) (1); Dashilar Area (No. 10) (8); East Liulichang Street (No. 11) (1); West Liulichang Street (No. 12) (1); Xianyukou (No. 13) (2); Jingshan Area (No. 14) (7); Beiluogu Lane (No. 15) (1); Xintaicang Areas (No. 18) (1); South Naoshikou Area (No. 20) (3); Fayuan Temple Area (No. 21) (3),China (2); UK (1); Germany (1); France (1); Beijing (6),Ming and Qing dynasties (1),Beijing's Urban Master Plan (2016–2035) (1),"Against the backdrop of urban renewal and owing to functional segmentation, land resources in old cities are often trapped in an isolated management mode, causing ratcheting tensions in the human–land relationship.","This study provides an urban renewal planning and management model to improve land-use eﬃciency and revitalize the old city via integrated development. Further, it seeks to strengthen system connectivity and network coordination of natural, social, and cultural resources in the old city and to propose a resource-sustainable development strategy of regionalization, cooperation, and diﬀerentiation for historic-area development.",,GPS tracking data (3),geographical location data (1),,,,,,,,,,,,2019 (2),22 historic areas in old Beijing city (1),GPS tracking data (3),outdoor route website www.foooooot.com (1),,After data cleaning (1),,,,[],,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,yes,"['urban network (11)', 'social network (5)', 'tourism network (10)', 'spatial network (4)', 'association network (7)', 'street network (4)', 'transport network system (1)']",Cities and regions are nodes (1),"when tourists move between tourism nodes, a spatial network is generated (1)",22 (1),,network density (3); centrality (10); betweenness centrality (6); closeness centrality (3); degree centrality (3); constraint degree (1); eﬃciency (2); integration (1),matrix analysis method (1),,,This can 