_Luong and Manthiou-2026-Video game-inspired tourism A s.txt,Video game-inspired tourism: A synergistic framework,Van Ha Luong; Aikaterini Manthiou,"Paris School of Business, Marketing and Communication Department, 59 Rue Nationale, 75013 Paris, France; NEOMA Business School, Marketing Department, 1 Rue Du Mar´echal Juin, 76825 Mont-Saint-Aignan, France",2025,journal article,Tourism Management,Elsevier Ltd,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tourman.2025.105282,www.elsevier.com/locate/tourman,,,Cultural Heritage (2),,Shanxi province (3); Yungang Grottoes (3); Yingxian Wooden Pagoda (2); Wutai Mountain (3); Hengshan (1); Datong Ancient City (1); Huaguo Mountain Scenic Area (2); Lingyan Temple (2); Minor Western Heaven (2),cultural pride (2); cultural narratives (2); cultural heritage (3); cultural authenticity (2); cultural reconnection (1); UNESCO World Heritage Sites (1),,"{'SOCIAL VALUES': 'Emotional (collective) - The game and associated tourism surge foster cultural identity and pride in Shanxi province, creating a sense of place attachment and communal value among locals and visitors alike.'}; {'HISTORIC VALUES': ""Educational - The game and related tourism provide knowledge about the past, specifically the Journey to the West narrative and Shanxi's historical sites, offering educational opportunities for both gamers and non-gamers.""}; {'AESTHETICAL VALUES': ""Artistic - The game's visual artistry and craftsmanship, as well as the scenic beauty of Shanxi's landscapes, contribute to aesthetic appreciation and artistic value, attracting visitors seeking visually pleasing experiences.""}",heritage promotions (1),Shanxi province; Yungang Grottoes; Yingxian Wooden Pagoda; Xiaoxitian Scenic Area; Wutai Mountain; Hengshan; Datong Ancient City; Huaguo Mountain Scenic Area; Lingyan Temple,France (2); China (3); Shanxi (18); Italy (1); Beijing (1); Sichuan (1); Chongqing (1),,release of Black Myth: Wukong,"Existing literature has made strides in exploring isolated elements of game-induced tourism, such as the formation of destination image (Carvalho et al., 2019), the impact of social media on tourist behavior (Zhang & Liu, 2024), and the role of gamification in enhancing visitor engagement (Xu et al., 2017).","This study therefore aims to propose a synergistic pathway to investigate how culturally themed video games, amplified by social media, inspire and translate into real-world tourism, particularly for culturally rich but under-promoted destinations. Its objectives are threefold. First, it aims to examine how immersive game experiences, especially those rich in cultural heritage, shape tourism-related in­ tentions. Second, it investigates how social media narratives act as mediators and amplifiers of gaming experiences, especially for nongamer audiences. Third, it explores how destination gamification helps translate digital interest into real-world visitor engagement.",Douyin (7); Weibo (2); Xiaohongshu (5); Bilibili (5); Steam (3); Meituan (2); Fliggy (2); Tik Tok (1); YouTube (1); Instagram (1),user-generated content (UGC) (3); short video descriptions (1); user comments (2); transcripts (1); videos (7); posts (3); reviews (7); livestreams (6); influencer narratives (2),,,,views (3); likes (3); recommended (1),,"10,000 reviews",610 million by 2030,"10,000 reviews in Chinese",,20 videos,,,August and November 2024,Shanxi,keyword-based crawling and platform-specific APIs,Python steamreviews package,Guided by hot search keywords suggested by the platform,,,mixed human–AI collaborative approach,two researchers,"['thematic content', 'emotional tone', 'culturally specific markers']",over 85 % agreement,content analysis (3); coding (2),Large language model (LLM) (5),Chat GPT-4o (4),,,,textual datasets (1),,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,"['cultural authenticity (1)', 'aesthetic richness (1)', 'emotional power (1)', 'cultural pride (4)', 'cultural identity (1)', 'spiritual journey (2)', 'symbolic pilgrimage (2)']",[],[],"['admiration (2)', 'awe (3)', 'excitement (1)', 'curiosity (1)', 'nostalgia (2)', 'joy (1)']",[],[],"['tourism marketing (3)', 'digital consumer behavior (1)', 'cross-sector collaboration (1)']",['sustainable planning (1)'],[],[],[],"['over-tourism (2)', 'environmental stress (1)', 'loss of authenticity (1)']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,,,gamer experience (2); social media dynamics (1); destination marketing initiatives (1); gamer community (1); non-gamers (7); influencer narratives (3); short-form videos (2); digital tourism discourse (1); social media storytelling (2); gamified destination design (1); digital amplification (2); algorithmic visibility (1); parasocial bonds (2); emotional contagion (4); narrative transportation (6); presence theories (2); media psychology (1); experiential marketing (1); open-world (1); themed quests (1); symbolic passes (1); collectible in-game artifacts (1); AAA1 titles (1); storyworld (1); user-generated content (UGC) (3); Games Live Streaming (1); algorithmic recommendation systems (1); pre-experiential familiarity (1); intrinsic motivators (1); experience economy (2); symbolic artifacts (1); character motifs (1); thematic trails (2); cosplay zones (2); AR-enhanced exhibits (1); symbolic passports (1); collectible badges (1); myth-themed challenges (1); role-play zones (1); AR-enhanced scavenger hunts (1); cosplay installations (1); culturally themed exhibits (1); DOMs (1); hot search keywords (1); Python steamreviews package (1); Simplified Chinese (4); intercoder reliability (1); grounded theory (1); bilingual codebook (1); cross-cultural comparison (2); digital content creators (1); digital-to-physical rewards (1); policy-makers (1); destination managers (1); community-based tourism models (1); casual tourists (1); virtual and augmented reality (1); behavioral analytics (1); media-induced tourism (2); opinion leadership (1); digital co-creation (1); stakeholder ecosystem thinking (1); de-marketing strategie