_Matrone et al.-2020-A BENCHMARK for LARGE-SCALE HERI.txt,A BENCHMARK FOR LARGE-SCALE HERITAGE POINT CLOUD SEMANTIC,TITLE:,,,other,,,,,,,Cultural Heritage (CH) (6),,architectural heritage (2); immovable cultural assets; architectural elements (5); heritage scenarios (2); heritage scenes (1),HBIM (Historical Building Information Modeling) (2); UNESCO World Heritage List (WHL) (1); heritage field (3); heritage point cloud (2); Sacri Monti of Piedmont and Lombardy (1),,,restoration (1); conservation (1),"Strasbourg Cathedral; Grande Île; Valentino’s Castle; Sacro Monte of Varallo; Ghiffa; St. Pierre church; Neustadt; porticoes of Bologna; Candia (Italy); Sacro Monte of Varallo (Italy); Trompone, cloister (Italy); Trompone, church (Italy); Kasepuhan (Indonesia); Sacro Monte of Varallo (Italy); Sacro Monte of Varallo (Italy); Santo Stefano street, Bologna (Italy); Ottmarsheim (France); Piazza Duomo, Trento (Italy)",Italy; France; Indonesia,,,The lack of benchmarking data for the semantic segmentation of digital heritage scenarios is hampering the development of automatic classification solutions in this field. Heritage 3D data feature complex structures and uncommon classes that prevent the simple deployment of available methods developed in other fields and for other types of data.,This paper aims to present a new 3D point cloud classification benchmark dataset (named Ar CH dataset1 - Architectural Cultural Heritage) with millions of manually labelled points belonging to heritage scenarios.,,3D data (4); point clouds (18); 2D images (3),,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,manual annotation (2),experts,"['Floor', 'Roof', 'Wall', 'Window', 'Door', 'Column', 'Stair', 'Vaults', 'Arches', 'Moldings', 'Other']",,semantic segmentation (4); classification (10); object recognition (2),Deep Learning (DL) (5); Deep Neural Networks (DNNs) (3); Convolutional Neural Networks (CNN) (2),"Point Net (Qi et al., 2017a); Point Net++ (Qi et al., 2017b); PCNN (Atzmon et al., 2018); DGCNN (Wang et al., 2019)"