_Morelli et al.-2024-The Legacy of Sycamore Gap The.txt,The Legacy of Sycamore Gap:,,,,other,,,,,,,Cultural Heritage (2); Natural Heritage (2); UNESCO World Heritage Site (2),natural (1); cultural (1); lost (2),Sycamore Gap tree (6); Hadrian's Wall (2); Housesteads Fort (1); Roman heritage sites (1),digital preservation (1); UNESCO (2); 3D digitization (1); heritage objects (1); heritage sites (1); heritage (1); documentation (2); preservation (1),,"{'SOCIAL VALUES': ""The study focuses on preserving the memory of the Sycamore Gap tree, which holds emotional and communal value for local communities and visitors. The tree is described as a symbol of Hadrian's Wall and a recognizable landmark, indicating its cultural identity and sense of place attachment.""}; {'HISTORIC VALUES': ""The study aims to reconstruct the lost Sycamore Gap tree using crowdsourced images and videos, emphasizing geometric and colorimetric accuracy. This reconstruction serves to document the tree's historical form and appearance, providing knowledge about the past for future generations.""}; {'AESTHETICAL VALUES': ""The study aims to create a 3D reconstruction of the Sycamore Gap tree, focusing on its geometric and colorimetric accuracy. This suggests an appreciation for the tree's artistic and notable qualities, as well as its conceptual materialization as a landmark.""}",digital preservation (1); 3D reconstruction (3),Sycamore Gap tree; Hadrian’s Wall; Housesteads Fort; Once Brewed; Northumberland National Park; England,England (1),Roman (1),the ca 150 year-old tree was felled on the evening of 27th September 2023,The orientation of crowdsourced and multi-temporal image datasets presents a challenging task for traditional photogrammetry.,"to orient all available datasets using photogrammetric AI methods; • to derive a 3D reconstruction the lost tree, emphasizing geometric and colorimetric accuracy.",Wikimedia Commons (1); Flickr (1); Unsplash (1),images (11); videos (7); UAV videos (2); terre