7 and 2021,Lithuanian coast,We developed a script in the Python environment with the Flickr Application Programming Interface (API) to facilitate repeatable requests to the Flickr API.,Flickr Application Programming Interface (API),,,,objective coding technique based on prior CES research and tailored to the Lithuania coastal environment,,"['Artistic or Cultural Expressions and Appreciation', 'Historical Monuments', 'Landscape Appreciation', 'Nature Appreciation', 'Religious, Spiritual, or Ceremonial Activities and Monuments', 'Social Recreation', 'Infrastructure Appreciation', 'Recreational Fishing', 'Other']",,classification (5),Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) (5),VGG (1); Alex Net (1),trained beforehand with supervised methods (KNN),,,RGB images (170*120*3),,80% of the annotated data was used for training and 20% for testing,categorical cross entropy (1),NADAM algorithm (2),0.001,,29,dropout layer of 0.3 (1),,"{'beta 1': '0.9', 'beta 2': '0.999', 'epsilon': '1e-07'}",,,,,,,"The architecture has two Convolution, Pooling, and Dropout layers followed by a Flatten layer, which is usually used as a connection between the Convolution and the dense layers.","The CNN architecture was trained using loss functions as a supervised metric for the early stopping process in addition to the performance metrics mentioned above. Early Stopping was used as a trigger to stop the training process based on the validation loss metric with a patience of nine, once the chosen performance measure stopped improving. The Model Checkpoint, which monitors training in order to keep the model that has achieved the best performance.",no,[],,,,,,,,,,accuracy (4); AUC (Area under the ROC Curve) (2); precision (3); recall (3),"['accuracy, AUC, precision, and recall (1)']",[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],confusion matrix (2),"['landscape appreciation (3)', 'nature appreciation (2)', 'historical monuments (2)', 'social recreation (3)']",[],[],[],[],[],['management of these protected and natural areas (1)'],[],[],[],[],"['inherent biases associated with capturing certain activities or events, as well as uncontrolled changes in data availability and quality over time (1)']","['data protected by social media users’ rights was not considered (1)', 'public data containing sensitive and personal information (including images with recognizable faces or structures) were treated as confidential or (pseudo-) anonymized (1)', 'Images containing private data were anonymized before being used for scientific presentations or other public events (1)', 'Personal information about the user, such as name, age, emails, was not extracted and/or considered (1)']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],Not applicable.,All the data generated or analyzed during this study are included in this published article.,,,,Python (3),,ecosystem services (ES) (3); natural capital (1); sustainable development (1); Millennium Ecosystem Assessment (MEA) (1); natural support systems (1); social media-based methodology (1); determinate innovation (1); Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) (5); citizen science platforms (1); camera traps (1); deep learning methods (2); supervised learning algorithm (1); K-nearest neighbors (KNN) algorithm (2); Arc GIS 10 for Desktop (1); Principal Components Analysis (PCA) (2); machine learning algorithms (2); Application Programming Interfaces (1),,,
