_Novack et al.-2020-Towards Detecting Building Facad.txt,Towards Detecting Building Facades with Grafﬁti Artwork Based on the Automatic Interpretation of Images from Google Street View,T. Novack; L. Vespe; H. Leukert; A. Zipf,,2020,journal article,,,,,,,,,city’s walls (1); roofs (1); pavements (1); building facades (6),street art (10); tourism (2); artwork (20),,"{'value': 'Aesthetical Values', 'reasoning': ""The paper discusses grafﬁti as a form of street art that brings life and color to the city, contributing to the city's aesthetics. It also mentions the visual pleasantness of urban landscapes.""}; {'value': 'Social Values', 'reasoning': 'The paper mentions that grafﬁti raises questions and protests, and is recognized as a relevant expression of creativity, diversity, and freedom. It also discusses the sense-making dynamic of this type of art and its geographic and economic values.'}; {'value': 'Economic Values', 'reasoning': 'The paper correlates grafﬁti artworks with commercial and social vibrancy and associates them with urban tourism and revitalization dynamics. It also mentions that making grafﬁti artworks more visible and accessible helps to increase grafﬁti’s geographic and economic values.'}",,Greater London Area (2); London (5); Brick Lane (1); Shoreditch (1); Hackney Wick (1),Greater London Area (2); London (5); United Kingdom (2); Paris (1); Berlin (1),,,Grafﬁti enthusiasts and urban planners frequently lack a reliable source of data on the exact location of grafﬁti works in a city.,"In this work, we propose a workﬂow for locating building facades with grafﬁti artwork.",Flickr (10); Open Street Map (OSM) (10),images (10); geo-tagged photographs (2); geo-referenced data (2),geo-tagged photos (6); geo-referenced data (2); geographic coordinates (1),spatial correlations (1); kernel density map (2),,,,"191,234 geo-tagged Flickr photos (2)",,,"36,000 GSV images (1)",,,,between June 1st of 2014 and January 1st of 2018 (1),Greater London Area (1),extracted b