om/le0x99/SA_classiﬁer (2),,,,,Open CV (1); Tensor Flow (1); Py Torch (1); Apache MXNet (1),,folksonomy (3); geo-datasets (1); urban tourism (1); urban revitalization dynamics (1); street-level greenery (3); urban landscapes (2); urban canyons (2); pedestrian routes (2); aesthetically pleasant (1),,,Making the information on the exact locations of grafﬁti works available may help researchers to better understand the associations between grafﬁti and other social-economic variables and built-up aspects.
_Nowacki and Kowalczyk-Aniol-2023-Experiencing islands is sustain.txt,Experiencing islands is sustainability: tourist experiences in Baltic islands,Marek Nowacki; Joanna Kowalczyk-Anioł,"Institute of Applied Sciences, WSB University in Poznań, 61-895 Poznań, Poland",2023,journal article,,,https://doi.org/10.1080/14724049.2022.2041648,https://doi.org/10.1080/14724049.2022.2041648,,59 79,,,Baltic islands (3),sustainability (14); sustainable tourism (7); sustainable experiences (12); sustainable development (7); cultural resources; cultural experiences; authentic (5); authenticity (5),,"{'value': 'Social (Emotional collective)', 'reasoning': 'The paper discusses the importance of tourist experiences in shaping sustainable destinations and mentions the atmosphere and authenticity of Bornholm, the forest and wildlife of Wolin, and the plants and flowers of Gotland as distinguishing features. These elements contribute to a sense of place attachment and communal value.'}; {'value': 'Economic (Use)', 'reasoning': ""The paper mentions that sustainable experiences are becoming an important key to obtaining a competitive advantage while enhancing destinations' sustainability and experience value. This suggests that the function and utility of the asset (the island destinations) are being considered in terms of their economic value.""}; {'value': 'Aesthetical (Artistic)', 'reasoning': 'The paper describes the natural environment of the islands, including forests, plants, and flowers, and mentions the beauty of the landscape. These descriptions suggest an appreciation for the artistic and aesthetic qualities of the natural environment.'}; {'value': 'Ecological (Essential)', 'reasoning': 'The paper discusses the importance of sustainable tourism development for island destinations and mentions the need to balance social, economic, and environmental objectives. This suggests that ecological ideologies are being considered in the design and construction of tourism offerings.'}",,Wolin; Bornholm; Gotland,Baltic Sea region; Baltic countries; Sweden; Denmark; Poland; European,nineteenth century,Covid-19 pandemic,Sustainable experiences are important for consideration in this research.,this article aims to analyse the experiences gained and shared via Trip Advisor by tourists visiting Baltic islands. It is equally important to identify the presence of the sustainability issue in these experiences: Are sustainability-related issues recognized and reﬂected in tourists’ online reviews on Trip Advisor? Are they becoming part of the Baltic island experience?,Trip Advisor (11); Facebook,"text (posts, captions, comments, reviews, hashtags)",,,,,,"1,480 reviews",463 million users monthly,"1,480 reviews",,,,,,"Three islands – the main island holiday destinations in three diﬀerent Baltic countries: Sweden, Denmark and Poland",web scraping technique,Web Scraper Google Chrome extension (webscraper.io),"Reviews for attractions with at least 5 entries were collected: 11 for Wolin, 15 for Bornholm and 17 for Gotland",,,automatic coding,,[],,text mining,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,,[],[],[],non-parametric Pearson chi-square diﬀerence test,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,,,,,,
_Nyelele et al.-2023-Using social media data and mach.txt,Using social media data and machine learning to map recreational ecosystem services,"Nyelele, Charity; Keske, Catherine; Chung, Min Gon; Guo, Han; Egoh, Benis N.","Department of Earth System Science, University of California Irvine, Irvine, CA 92697, USA; Department of Environmental Sciences, University of Virginia, Charlottesville, VA 22904, USA; School of Engineering, University of California-Merced, Merced, CA 95343, USA; Environmental Systems Graduate Group, University of California-Merced, Merced, CA 95343, USA",2023,journal article,Ecological Indicators,Elsevier Ltd,10.1016/j.ecolind.2023.110606,https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/,,,,,,,,,,Tahoe Central Sierra Initiative (TCSI) project area; Lake Tahoe Basin,"California; USA; Sierra Nevada; Europe; North America; Western USA; New England, USA",,COVID-19-related travel restrictions,"There is therefore an urgent need for studies that improve and spatially refine existing mapping approaches to fill in key data and methodological gaps associated with mapping socio-ecological systems, refine indicators for mapping ecosystem services, and improve our understanding, estima­tion, and reporting of model uncertainties.","The main objective of this study is to use newly available techniques and data sources to improve ecosystem service modeling methods and reduce uncertainty in the mapping of cultural services. We specifically use recreational ecosystem services as an example to illustrate how crowdsourced social media data and machine learning can fill in key data and methodological gaps and help improve how we measure, map, and manage ecosystem services on public lands. Secondly, we aim to identify the key pointers and indicators influencing recreational activ­ities that are useful for mapping the recreational potential of landscapes. Lastly, we seek to understand the extent to which California ecosystems, particularly protected areas, provide recreational services.",Flickr; Facebook; Twitter; Instagram,text; videos; geotagged photographs,geotagged posts; latitude; longitude,,,,location; date; time; web address; photographer; unique identifier; origin,"80,500","approximately 5,000",,,,,,between 1 January 2005 and 31 December 2019,non-urban areas of the TCSI area,querying the Flickr Application Programming Interface (API) using Python scripts,Flickr Application Programming Interface (API),bounding box of coordinates defining the boundary of the TCSI to search for all geolocated posts,filtered the resulting Flickr records using a United States Census Bureau (2021) urban area shapefile to discard any photographs taken within an urban area,photographs taken within an urban area,manual content analysis on a random sample of 385 photographs,,"['trees', 'other vegetation types', 'accessibility', 'wildlife', 'rocks, hills, and mountains', 'water', 'recreational activities', 'accommodation', 'general landscape features', 'attractions']",Cohen’s Kappa resulted in a good agreement (93%) between the manual coding and Google Cloud Vision derived labels (Kappa statistic = 0.918),classification; regression,machine learning,Random Forest; Google Cloud Vision,,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,accuracy,['accuracy of 0.99'],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,We used publicly available data,,,,,,,,,
_Németh et al.-2021-Visitation Rate Analysis of Geoh.txt,Article ABSTRACT: tance of abiotic natural features.,B. Németh; K. Németh; J.N. Procter,,2021,journal article,Geosciences,MDPI,https://doi.org/10.3390/geosciences11110480,https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/,,,Cultural Heritage (2),,volcanic cones (5); cultural heritage (2); geosites (2); geomorphological features (3); historic heritage; sacred volcanoes (ancestral mountains),geoheritage (13); geoconservation (10); geoeducation (16); geotourism (6); geoparks (3); geosites; geosystem services (4); Outstanding Natural Features; cultural relations; cultural heritage; historic heritage; sacred volcanoes; ancestral mountains; geological heritage; geological signiﬁcance; geomorphological features; geological sites; geomorphologic feature; geological processes; geomorphology; geological history; geological hazards; geological exposure; geomorphologic feature; geological site; geological features; geomorphological sites; geological heritage; geological processes; geomorphological features; geological sites; geological site; geological information,,"Social: Emotional (collective) – The study mentions community building and involvement of local communities, suggesting a focus on cultural identity and communal value.; Economic: Entertainment – The paper discusses tourism and recreational aspects of geoheritage, indicating the role of these assets in the contemporary market.; Political: Management – The study analyzes policies and strategies for incorporating geoheritage into political strategies and policies.; Aesthetical: Notable – The paper highlights the aesthetic value of the volcanic cones and their green cover, suggesting they are notable for their visual appeal.; Scientific: Conceptual – The study uses landform classification and GIS techniques to analyze and understand geological features, indicating a focus on conceptual understanding.; Ecological: Spiritual – The paper mentions the harmony between the building and its natural environment.",geoconservation (10); heritage conservation (2); heritage protection; heritage planning,Auckland volcanic ﬁeld (12); Auckland (10); Hong Kong Geopark,New Zealand (10); North Island (2); Egypt; Slovakia; Sardinia; Argentina; Greece,Quaternary,COVID19 pandemic,"This paper investigates the use of big data (Flick R), Geopreservation Inventory, and Geographic Information System for identifying geoeducation capacity of tourist attractions.","The answer for our research question was attained through four objectives: (1) To identify strengths and gaps in existing legislations relevant to geoconservation, (2) to identify the degree of grass roots initiatives, (3) to deﬁne what geological or geomorphological features receive visitation, and (4) to derive geoeducational value of the non-visited geological or geomorphological sites to depict current bases of promotion.",Flick R (5); Panoramio; Geograph,metadata; geospatial content; photo,geographic coordinates (3); geographic position systems,spatial distribution; spatial perspective,Temporal data,,metadata,,,,,,,,,"bounding box of speciﬁc latitude, longitude, and accuracy",Crowdsourcing,Flick R API (2),,,,,,[],,landform classiﬁcation (5),,,,,,geographic information,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],['urban planning (6)'],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,Not applicable,,,,Arc GIS (4),,abiotic natural features; geoconservation; geoeducation; landform classiﬁcation; topographic position index; crowdsourcing; Flick R; GIS; urban planning; geomorphology; geosites; geosystem services; geoparks; geotourism; volcanic cones; cultural heritage; historic heritage; sacred volcanoes; ancestral mountains; geological heritage; geological signiﬁcance; geomorphological features; geological sites; geological site; geological processes; geological history; geological hazards; geological exposure; geomorphologic feature; geological information; Li DAR; D