_Oliveira et al.-2021-Unveiling Island Tourism in Cape.txt,Unveiling Island Tourism in Cape Verde through Online Reviews,C. Oliveira; P. Rita; S. Moro,,2021,journal article,Sustainability,MDPI,https://doi.org/10.3390/su13158167,https://doi.org/10.3390/su13158167,,,,,island tourism (5),sustainable tourism (2); sustainable development (4),,,,Islands of the Sun; Boa Vista; Sal; Cape Verde; Atlantic Islands,Cape Verde; Atlantic Ocean; West Africa; Portuguese Madeira; Spanish Canary Islands; UK; Germany; France; Portugal; Benelux; Caribbean; Oceania; Northern Cyprus,15th century,,"Lack of studies was found both in SIDS, including Cape Verde, in regard to analyzing customers perception and satisfaction, and even more so when considering online reviews as a proxy of tourism experience.","This research aims to challenge Cape Verde’s NTO marketing communication approach by directly exploring the real data source of what are the most valued experiences that tourists have, if and how they are presented on the ofﬁcial website.",Trip Advisor; Expedia; Yelp,"text (posts, captions, comments, reviews, hashtags)",,,,,,"almost 38,000 online reviews",more than 884 million user reviews,,,,,,,Boa Vista and Sal islands,Automated data collection used the R statistical tool,R statistical tool,,"cleaning the text of irrelevant words, like articles and adverbs; (2) stemming, i.e., reducing words to a single root word (e.g., “diving” is reduced to “dive”",,,,[],,topic modeling,Topic Models,Latent Dirichlet Allocation (LDA),,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,three-level hierarchical Bayesian modelling process grouping collections of items in topics deﬁned by identiﬁed words/terms and the probability that each of them characterizes the topic,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,The data presented in this study are available on request from the corresponding author.,,,,R,,online reviews; text mining; big data; online reviews; User Generated Content (UGC),,,
_Otero et al.-2022-Building Cultural Heritage Refer.txt,Building Cultural Heritage Reference Collections from Social Media,D. Otero; Javier Parapar; Álvaro Barreiro,,2021,journal article,ACM Journal on Computing and Cultural Heritage,ACM,,,,9:3-9:13,Cultural Heritage (14),,patrimonial entities (7); heritage elements (1); cultural elements (1); heritage entities (2),heritage (16); patrimonialization (4); cultural heritage (6); heritage elements (1); cultural elements (1); heritage entities (2); patrimonial attacks (4); heritage attacks (3); heritage in social conflict (1); social fractures in heritage (1); patrimonial processes (2),,"{'SOCIAL VALUES': ""Emotional (collective) – The study mentions the importance of citizen's motivations and comments, and the different social sensitivities concerning attacks on heritage entities, suggesting a focus on cultural identity and communal value.""}; {'POLITICAL VALUES': 'Educational – The study aims to create a reference collection that will allow future researchers to have real information about citizen’s motivations and comments, the different social sensitivities concerning these attacks on heritage entities, as well as references to places or heritage entities under attack throughout the protests.'}",preservation (2),,Spain (1); United States (2); America (1),2020 (10),death of George Floyd (2),"However, and as will be seen throughout this article, retrieval and archiving techniques used in social networks within heritage studies have some problems: (i) they are still carried out manually or, (ii) carried out using computer techniques not adapted to the informational domain or the final purpose of the information, which is ultimately the creation of archives or collections as a reflection, preservation, and source for the study of social processes.","With the transdisciplinary perspective offered by Computational Archival Science [38], and after a review of the intersection between Information Retrieval (IR) and the creation of archives from social networks, we present a platform for the application of IR strategies (combined with the judgment of experts) for the creation of reference collections (as born-digital archives) in cultural heritage from social networks in a customisable, reproducible, documented, and shareable way.",social networks (14); Reddit (10); Facebook (1),comments (2); posts (10); textual format (1); multimedia (1); photos (1); videos (1); links (1),,,temporal criteria (1),,username (2),"260,578 (1)","90,000 (1)",,,,,,"between 25th May, 2020 (date of death of George Floyd) and 31st October, 2020 (1)",different areas of the world (1),download posts (2),Reddit API (2),"sampled 1,400 of them (1)",anonymised them by substituting their original Reddit username with a randomly generated identifier (1),,automatic retrieval but with a second annotation phase in which experts have to annotate the entire collection (1),experts (3),[],,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['anonymisation processes (1)', 'ensure their anonymity (1)']",['implicit bias (2)'],[],[],[],[],[],[],,"The resultant reference collection is available at this link,1 constituting the first reference collection, as far as we know, that preserve and give access for the study of the recent attacks on patrimonial entities motivated by anti-racist protests.",,https://www.dc.fi.udc.es/~david/heritage,,,,born-digital archives (11); social processes (4); social network (5); social networks (10); reference collections (14); information retrieval (13); Computational Archival Science (8); anti-racist protests (4); racial tensions (3); heritage entities (2); patrimonial entities (7),,,
_Palt et al.-2025-Automated photo content classifi.txt,"Automated photo content classification of Instagram posts to identify patterns of human uses in peri-urban protected areas: A case study from Vienna, Austria",Martin Palt; Michael Binder; Anna Huber; Christa Hainz-Renetzeder; Alice Wanner; Lena Ortega Menjivar; Nur Banu ¨Ozcelik; Friedrich Leisch; Florian Borgwardt; Nina N. Kaiser; Stefan Stoll; Rafaela Schinegger,"University of Applied Sciences Trier, Environmental Campus Birkenfeld, Hoppst¨adten-Weiersbach, Germany; BOKU University, Department of Landscape, Water and Infrastructure, Institute of Landscape Development, Recreation and Conservation Planning, Vienna, Austria; LANIUS - Research Association for Regional Nature Conservation, Theiß, Austria; BOKU University, LAWI (Departement of Landscape, Water and Infrastructure), Institute of Statistics, Vienna, Austria; BOKU University, Department of Ecosystem Management, Climate and Biodiversity, Institute of Hydrobiology and Aquatic Ecosystem Management, Vienna, Austria; Hessian Agency for Nature Conservation, Environment and Geology, Wiesbaden, Germany; University of Duisburg-Essen, Faculty of Biology, Essen, Germany",2025,journal article,Urban Forestry & Urban Greening,Elsevier Gmb H,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ufug.2025.129029,www.elsevier.com/locate/ufug,,,,,peri-urban protected areas (2); peri-urban ecosystems; urban recreation areas; urban and peri-urban blue and green spaces (3); historical monuments,Nature protection areas; Nature conservation (2); conservation objectives; conservation strategies; protected areas (7); national parks; biosphere reserves; local conservation areas; Natura 2000 sites (3); Ramsar Convention sites; national park; natural monuments,,"{'Aesthetical': 'The paper discusses landscape preferences and scenic views, indicating an appreciation for the artistic and notable qualities of the environment. The study identifies that users are attracted by distinct natural characteristics which is reflected in the type of photos they post online.'}; {'Social': 'The study highlights the importance of green spaces for recreation and well-being, especially during the COVID-19 pandemic, indicating a focus on emotional and collective values. The paper mentions that blue and green spaces significantly contribute to mental and physical well-being by offering non-material services such as recreation.'}; {'Ecological': 'The paper emphasizes the ecological sensitivity of protected areas and the need to balance visitor interests with conservation objectives, reflecting essential and existential values. The paper mentions that urban ecosystems are threatened by degradation and pollution, but also by other activities, including recreation.'}",visitor management (3); conservation (4); management planning; management plans (2); ecological preservation; adaptive management strategies,Vienna; Lainzer Tiergarten (6); Lobau (9); Nussberg (8); Leopoldsberg (3); Danube,Austria (3); Europe; EU,,COVID-19 pandemic (10),"This creates a conflict between the high importance and value of ES, particularly CES derived from experiencing nature, and the negative impacts of human use on the ecological integrity of urban and periurban blue and green spaces.","First, we investigate which types of human uses and interests can be identified through a comprehensive clustering of social media photos taken in three study sites in Vienna. Second, we analyse differences in frequency and spatial distribution of human uses and interest between three specific case study sites of urban and peri-urban blue and green nature-protection areas. Third, we address how external factors - such as seasonality and the dynamics of the COVID-19 pandemic - affect the observed patterns teractions of people with peri-urban protected areas and the related ES they offer.",Instagram (16); Flickr (4),photos (15); visual content; metadata (3); text; captions,geotagged photos,spatial distribution; spatial patterns (2); hotspot areas,temporal patterns (2); seasonal variations (3); monthly patterns,,upload time; username; caption; location; hashtags (4),"54,751","11,540",,"54,751",,,,2018–2022,Vienna,"extraction of all publicly posted photos in a given time frame for a search term, which can be a location or hashtag",4 K Stogram (4),,"Duplicate posts with the exact location and hashtag were deleted, and data for the lo cations Nussberg and Leopoldsberg were merged.",,automated,,[],,classification; clustering (4),,,,,,labels,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,"Labeling Instagram photo content enabled the clustering of photos into groups of shared motives with commonalities regarding user ac tivity and interest (Kaiser et al., 2021). To do so, we considered labels’ presence/absence instead of the continuous reliability measure, which describes the likelihood of occurrence of a label, not its importance to the overall photo motive.",no,[],,,,,,,,,,,[],[],[],Chi-squared test of independence; one-sample binomial proportion tests; global one-way analysis of variance (ANOVA); pairwise Wilcoxon rank sum tests,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,R,,Social media data; Photo content analysis; Human uses; Recreational activity; Nature perception; ecosystem services; cultural ecosystem services; social media posts; Instagram locations; Instagram posts; computer vision analysis; Google’s Cloud Vision API,,,
_Paolanti et al.-2019-DEEP CONVOLUTIONAL NEURAL NETWOR.txt,DEEP CONVOLUTIONAL NEURAL NETWORKS FOR SENTIMENT ANALYSIS OF,,,,other,,,,,,,Cultural Heritage (CH) (11),tangible (1); intangible (1),archaeological sites (2); cultural sites (1); artistic sites (1); architectural sites (2); ancient monument (1); historical buildings (2); archaeological sites (2); museum objects (1),Cultural Heritage (CH) (11); UNESCO (2); World Heritage properties (1); monuments (7); historical buildings (2); archaeological sites (2); museum objects (1); preserve (1); protect (1); maintain security (1); manage (1); enhance (1); digital documentation (2); Sentiment Analysis (SA) (3); geotag (1),,"{'SOCIAL VALUES': ""Emotional (collective) – The study aims to understand users' opinions and sentiments towards cultural heritage sites, which directly relates to cultural identity, pride, and a sense of place attachment.""}; {'ECONOMIC VALUES': 'Entertainment – The paper discusses the promotion of cultural heritage goods through tourism, indicating the entertainment value of these sites in attracting visitors and contributing to economic development.'}; {'POLITICAL VALUES': 'Educational – The paper mentions the role of monuments in education, suggesting their use in formal and informal learning, which aligns with the educational role of heritage assets for political purposes like nation-building.'}; {'HISTORIC VALUES': 'Historic-Artistic – The paper focuses on sentiment analysis of images related to monuments and historical buildings, which are rare examples of historical, stylistic, or artistic movements.'}; {'AESTHETICAL VALUES': 'Artistic – The study analyzes images of cultural heritage sites, which are original products of creativity and imagination.'}",preserve (1); protect (1); maintain security (1); manage (1); enhance (1),Tour Eiffel (1); Colosseum (1); tower of Pisa (1); Victorian (1),Italy (2); Indian (1),,,"In Italy, the Cultural Heritage (CH) is huge and there is an urgent need to preserve, protect, maintain security, manage without waste and above all enhance this heritage, for Italians, foreigners and future generations.",This work introduces an approach to estimate the sentiment of Social Media pictures CH related.,Social Media (2); Instagram (8); social networks (1),pictures (10); images (21); captions (4); hashtags (5); visual information (1),geotag (1); locations (2),,daily (1),,locations (2); hashtags (5),8472 (1),,,8477 (1),,,,daily (1),,"downloading from proﬁles, hashtags and locations (1)",keywordtool1 online tool (1),,ﬁltered only from those examples that had a multiframe structure (1),,manually estimated by human annotators (2),human annotators (2),"['positive (10)', 'neutral (13)', 'negative (15)']",inter-annotatoragreement (1),sentiment analysis (7); image classiﬁcation (3); classiﬁcation (6); sentiment recognition (1),Deep Convolutional Neural Network (DCNN) (3); Convolutional Neural Networks (CNN) (10); neural network models (1); residual networks (Res Net) (4); Inception network (4),VGG16 (7); Res Net (10); Inception Res Net (3); Caffe Net CNN (1); Alexnet (2); Google Net (1); VGGNet (1); RESNet (1); Inception-Res Net-v2 network (1),trained by ﬁne-tuning a model pretrained using the Image Net dataset (1),,manual feature extraction (1),visual features (1); visual information (1); images (1),,80% training and 20% test images (1),binary cross entropy (BCE) (1),stochastic gradient descent (SGD) (1),10−5 (1),5 (1),100 (1),,,{},,,,,,,"The VGG-16 network consists of 5 convolutional blocks where corresponding output ﬁlter have [54, 128, 256, 512] dimensions and a fully-connected classiﬁer. (1)",The sentiment of a picture is identiﬁed by a machine learning classiﬁer based on visual features extracted from especially trained DCNNs. (1),no,[],,,,,,,,,,Accuracy (4); Recall (3); Precision (3); F1-score (5); Support (1); confusion matrix (5),[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],['the experiment of introducing a dropout layer into the architecture did not bring any noteworthy results. (1)'],The dataset is split into 80% training and 20% test images. (1),,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],"['a system that ensures the management of data with a multimedia and multidisciplinary approach through sentiment analysis techniques, to allow a CH analysis ﬁnalized to planning and distribution needs. (1)']",[],"['a demonstration that Deep Learning architectures can be applied for sentiment analysis evaluation of Social Media Pictures CH related (1)', 'performance comparison of different DCNNs for image classiﬁcation (1)']","['a challenging new dataset of images collected by Instagram of CH goods in the List of UNESCO, hand-labelled with ground truth (1)']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,"developed the VGG16 model in Keras, a high-level neural networks library and written in Python (1)",Keras (2); Tensor Flow (1); Python (1),,embedded scenes (1),,,
_Paolanti et al.-2021-Tourism destination management u.txt,ORIGINAL RESEARCH ABSTRACT:,Marina Paolanti,"Università Politecnica delle Marche, Ancona, Marche, Italy",,other,,,,,,,,,,sustainable tourism (1); sentiment (21),,,,Cilento,Southern Italy (2); Italy (2); Marche; Campania region,,,"Sentiment analysis on social media such as Twitter is a challenging task given the data characteristics such as the length, spelling errors, abbreviations, and special characters.","We aim at demonstrating and testing a deep learning social geodata framework to characterize spatial, temporal and demographic tour- ist flows across the vast of territory this rural touristic region and along its coasts.",Twitter (13),text (10); geotagged information (2),geotag (1); geotagged (4); latitude (2); longitude (2),,,,username (1); user id (1),3200 tweets with positive sentiment; •	4720 tweets with neutral sentiment; •	4842 tweets with negative sentiment.,,,,,,,from May 2017 to May 2019,Cliento’s area,custom Python script that relies on the tweepy library,Twitter streaming API,spatial filter based on the bounding box that retrieves only tweets in a well-known area exploiting the geographical feature of Twitter API,"subsampling procedure, keeping all the classes balanced (1/3, 1/3, 1/3)",,manually assessed by human annotators,Two different reviewers (annotators) with a Master’s Degree in Computer Science,"['Positive', 'Neutral', 'Negative']",Conflicts or disagreements between the annotators happened only for few revised tweets. A joint agreement was always found after a further mutual confrontation.,sentiment analysis (10); classification (10),Deep Neural Networks (DNNs) (7); Convolutional Neural Networks (CNN) (3); recurrent neural networks (1),Word-CNN; Word-LSTM; Char-CNN; Conv Nets; word2vec,pretrained “word2vec” vectors,word embedding (2),,,,80% training and 20% validation,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,The networks have been trained from scratch on our dataset.,no,[],,,,,,,,,,accuracy (10); precision (