_Runge et al.-2020-Pan-Arctic analysis of cultural.txt,PAPER • OPEN ACCESS,Claire A Runge,,2020,journal article,People Nat.,,https://doi.org/10.1002/pan3.10149,,,,,,,cultural ecosystem services (4); nature appreciation (2),,,protected areas management (1),Arctic,Arctic; Alaska; Canada; Iceland; Greenland; Norway; Sweden; Finland; Svalbard; Russia; marine areas; Russian Federation,,,"Despite their value to a large number of people, cultural ecosystem services remain challenging to quantify, differ among users, and can change over time [3, 4]. As a result, such beneﬁts have often been neglected in assessments and decision-making around management and use of natural areas [5].",In this paper we examined a comprehensive suite of Flickr photographs from across the Arctic to uncover what types of nature experiences are important to people inside and outside protected areas in eight countries.,Flickr (8),photographs (13); metadata (2),,,,,,805 684 photos,538,,805 684,,,,2004 and 2017,Arctic,We extracted photos taken in the Arctic between 2004 and 2017 that were posted to Flickr,Google Cloud Vision API (V1),,,We limited our analysis to any labels with score of 0.6 or higher up to a maximum of 20 labels for each photo (median number of labels per photo=17).,manual (5),four independent people,"['abiotic nature', 'biotic nature', 'wildlife', 'bird', 'plant', 'non- service (pet, non-nature)']",iota=0.612,content analysis (8); image recognition (2); image classiﬁcation (1),machine learning (3),Google Cloud Vision (7),,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,iota coefﬁcient (2); percent agreement (3); Fleiss’s kappa (1); Cohen’s kappa (1),[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],['ecotourism (2)'],[],[],[],[],['Flickr data is limited in arctic areas of the Russian Federation and it is likely that our dataset substantially underestimates cultural ecosystem services in this region.'],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],The R code associated with the project is available at doi:10.1