_Scarrone-2021-Discovering Latent Information f.txt,Discovering Latent Information from,,,2021,thesis,,Springer Nature Switzerland AG,,,,,cultural heritage domain (7),,,,,,,,,,,"Given the above context, in this thesis, I focus on developing novel algorithms, techniques, and tools for leveraging multi-modal, sparse, and noisy data available from multiple public sources to integrate and enrich useful information available to the public in the cultural heritage domain.",research aims to develop novel models that take advantage of multi-modal features extracted by deep neural models to improve the performance for various underlying tasks.,Twitter (4),social media; text; images (7); visuals,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,"Using the Twitter API, we are building a Cultural Heritage dataset collecting related tweets with their associated images.",Twitter API,,,,manually labeled by Mechanical Turkers,Mechanical Turkers,['BIO tagging scheme'],,named entity recognition; entity type recognition; multi-classiﬁcation,deep-learning based approaches; transformers; convolutional model,BERT (4); VGG16,Trained on a large corpus of unlabelled text including the entire Wikipedia and Book Corpus.,Latent embeddings; Bert generates context related embedding at sub-word level.,,text messages; images embeddings; visual features,cross-attention mechanisms,"75% training, 15% validation, and 10% testing",,Adam W optimizer,,32,600,Decoupled Weight Decay Regularization,,{},,,,,,,Model (A) uses only the text messages and applies a linear layer after the Bert model in order to classify the tokens in the available classes. Model (B) uses text messages and images embeddings – Bert embeddings and visual features are combined in the attention module and the result goes through a linear model for classiﬁcation.,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,F1 score (4),[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['novel algorithms', 'novel techniques', 'novel multi-modal, cross-attention mechanism']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,W