_Sedmak et al.-2023-Data Mining of Visitors’ Spatial.txt,Data Mining of Visitors’ Spatial Movement Patterns,,,,other,,,,,,,World Heritage (4),architectural heritage (4),architectural attractions (4); iconic architecture (2); architectural heritage (3); historic sites (1); Old Town (1),unesco (7); World Heritage Site (2); architectural heritage (4); cultural (4); unesco World Heritage Committee (1); unesco List of World Heritage Sites (1); public spaces (2); public institutions (1); cultural context (1); urban landscape design (1); heritage tourism (1); World Heritage cities (1); unesco World Heritage assets (1); thematic itineraries (1); cultural value (1); exceptional world heritage (1); cultural tourists (2),,"{'Aesthetical Values': 'The paper discusses the aesthetic qualities of architecture, particularly in relation to tourism, suggesting an artistic value. The built environment design and its consumption affect the tourist experience.'}; {'Historic Values': 'The paper mentions historical sites and the tendency of tourists to visit them, indicating an educational value. Urban cultural tourists tend to visit as many historical sites as possible.'}; {'Social Values': 'The paper discusses the role of architecture in creating a sense of place and drawing tourists into an area, suggesting an emotional (collective) value. Architecture aestheticises spaces with recognisable markers that create a particular sense of place.'}; {'Economic Values': 'The paper discusses the importance of architectural attractions for tourism and city marketing, suggesting an entertainment value. Understanding the function and relative importance of specific architectural attractions is vital for their sensible inclusion into the overall tourism product and city marketing activities.'}",sustainable management (2); destination management (3); promotion (3); mobility measures (1),"Ljubljana (20); Akka, Israel (1); Hong Kong (1); Bilbao (1); Hamburg (1); Nanjing City (1); Shanghai (1); Nordic countries of Europe (1); Melaka World Heritage Site (1); Austria (1); South Korea (1); China (4); Queensland (1); Madrid, Spain (1); South Anhui (1); Beijing (1); Slovenia (2); Sydney (1); Danube region (2)",Slovenia (2); Europe (1); China (4); Hong Kong (1); Israel (1); Spain (1); Austria (1); South Korea (1); Queensland (1); Nordic countries of Europe (1); South Anhui (1); Beijing (1); Sydney (1); Danube region (2),Roman Period (2),unesco inscription (2),"Understanding inter-destination and especially intradestination tourists’ movement patterns is important for strategic policy-making decisions, organisation of public transport, planning of road networks and public spaces, safety issues, and management and marketing of the tourist destination, which includes product development and visitor use policies","The aim of this study was to analyse the spatial movement patterns of visitors in the newly declared World Heritage city of Ljubljana, focusing on the spatially dispersed attractions of Jože Plečnik’s architectural heritage.",Flickr (12); Instagram (1); Panoramio (1); Facebook (1); Trip Advisor (1),photos (13); metadata (5); images (3); videos (2); geotagged content (2); location loggers (1); cell phone satellite position records (1); textual tags (1); photo timestamp (1); upload date (1); owner name (1); owner id (2),geocode (longitude and latitude) (1); geotagging service (1); geographical positions (1),spatial distribution (5); spatial movement (10); spatial behaviour (11); spatial dispersion (1); spatial flows (3); spatial structure (3); spatial syntax (1); spatial relationship (1); spatial distribution (5); spatial concentration (1),timestamp (1); upload date (1); temporal sequence (3); temporal complexity (1); spatiotemporal changes (2); temporal heterogeneity (1); spatio-temporal behaviour (2),,photo id (1); photo title (1); geocode (longitude and latitude) (1); textual tags (1); photo timestamp (1); upload date (1); owner name (1); owner id (2); user’s name (1); location (1),"65,210 (1)","4,735 (1)",,"68,520 (1)",,,,January 2007 and December 2018 (1),administrative area of the city (1),"To crawl the data, we used a Python code for recursive Flickr Application Programme Interfaces (api) calls.",Flickr Application Programme Interfaces (api) (2),A boundary box containing the administrative area of the city was used to limit a query response.,"Occasionally, the Flickr apis returned duplicate photos, errors, spatial outliers and incomplete records. These records were deleted from the dataset during the data cleansing process.","Specifically, all Flickr users who indicated a foreign home country or a hometown outside Slovenia and for whom the time span of a sequence of their uploaded photos (within one year) was less than one month were classified as tourists.",,,[],,clustering (3),,dbscan (2),,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,yes,"['weighted directed network (2)', 'tourist flow network (1)', 'attraction network (1)']",aois (clusters) (2),the edges between each pair of i and j nodes represent the movements (1),559 (1),"8,537 (1)",node degree centrality (2); node weighted degree centrality (2); betweenness centrality (2); node degree (2); weighted degree (3); in-degree (2); out-degree (2); in-centrality (1); out-centrality (1),"In this way, we constructed a weighted directed network where the aois (clusters) represent nodes, the edges between each pair of i and j nodes represent the movements, and the weight wij of the edges equals the count of user trajectories (tourist flow) between i and j nodes.",,,The constructed weighted directed network of tourist movements provides an opportunity to quantitatively analyse structural properties of the tourist attractions and the relations between them.,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],"['The organic embedding of Plečnik architecture in the city, defined in the unesco charter as the central value of its exceptional world heritage, is indeed reflected in the tourist ‘consumption’ of Ljubljana, which allows for an authentic and sustainable communication of its exceptionality with relatively little intervention.']",[],[],"['A clearly visible concentration of movements was identified in the relatively limited area with a high agglomeration of attractions, including the banks of the\nLjubljanica River and the bridges, Vegova Street with the National and University Library and Congress\nSquare with Zvezda Park.']",[],"['As Plečnik’s scattered attractions were added to the unesco list only last year, the destination management can better prepare for development, promotion and mobility measures related to Plečnik’s attractions based on our analyses.', 'We suggest that the destination be promoted as a ‘new unesco World Heritage City,’\nas Plečnik’s attractions are already a key component of tourist tours.']",[],[],[],"['One of the main limitations of this study is that it examines the movement patterns of tourists in a newly designated unesco whs.', 'The small number of photos by domestic visitors and deficiency and inconsistency of the personal information disclosed by Flickr users did not allow us to make comparisons that would show the differences in movements between segments of domestic and foreign tourists.', 'Moreover, the information source itself is likely to be biased – it is virtually impossible to verify how representative the sample of Flickr users is in relation to the population of visitors to Ljubljana.']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,Python,,cumulative attraction (3); gravitational pull (2); attraction city (1); city of attractions (1); friction of distance (1),,,
_Seitsonen-2017-Crowdsourcing cultural heritage.txt,Crowdsourcing cultural heritage: public participation and motivations in conflict site mapping,Oula Seitsonen,"University of Helsinki, Finland",2017,journal article,Journal homepage: www.tandfonline.com/journals/ycah20,Taylor & Francis Group,,www.openstreetmap.org,,,conflict heritage (3),tangible; intangible; material,twentieth century conflict heritage (2); Ancient monuments; First World War (WWI) sites; WWII sites; Nationally important built cultural environments; other cultural heritage site/fortifications/trenches; German military installations; Prehistoric sites; Russian fortification,authorised heritage discourse (2); Ancient monuments; Nationally important built cultural environments; other cultural heritage sites,,"{'SOCIAL VALUES': 'The study discusses the importance of local perspectives and pride of place, suggesting a connection to emotional (collective) values related to cultural identity and sense of place attachment.'}; {'POLITICAL VALUES': 'The study mentions the educational role of heritage assets in nation-building myths, suggesting a connection to educational values used for political purposes.'}; {'HISTORIC VALUES': 'The study discusses the potential of heritage assets to provide knowledge about the past, suggesting a connection to educational values related to historical knowledge.'}",heritage management policy,Finland; Porkkala; Lapland; Lappeenranta Huhtiniemi; Vyborg,Finland; Norway; Russian territory; Eastern Karelia; Lapland; Helsinki; Ostrobothian region,twentieth century,Second World War (WWII),"My analysis contributes to ongoing discussions on public participatory behaviour and incentives, especially in cultural heritage.","I will offer methods and recommendations for organizing analogous community initiatives online, which is nowadays technically relatively straightforward.",Open Street Map®; YLE website,geo-spatial information; photographs; text,,spatial analyses; spatial distribution