_Seok et al.-2020-An Analysis of the Sustainable T.txt,Article ABSTRACT:,H.S.; Y.J.; Y.N.,Kyung Hee University,2020,journal article,,MDPI,,http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/,,,,,graﬃti tours (6),socio-cultural sustainability (7); cultural heritage; traditional values,,"{'SOCIAL VALUES': ""The paper discusses the social and political issues facing Bogota, the artists' political views, and the history of the native Colombians and their struggle to keep their identity, which aligns with the definition of collective emotional values.""}; {'HISTORIC VALUES': 'The paper mentions the history of the native Colombians and their struggle to keep their identity, which aligns with the definition of educational historic values.'}",conservation of cultural heritage (1),Bogota (7),Colombia (3); Spain (4); UK (4); The Netherlands (1),,,,The purpose of this study was to analyze the value of graﬃti tours from the perspective of sustainable tourism by examining actual reviews by social media users using text mining and social network analysis.,,text (1),,,,,,,,,,,,,2013–2016 and 2017–2019 (2),Bogota (2),,,,,,,,[],,topic modeling,,,,,,text tokens,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,yes,"['social network (2)', 'word co-occurrence network (2)']",words,mutually connected,,,,co-occurrence extraction,,,analyze the value of graﬃti tours from the perspective of sustainable tourism,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,,,graﬃti (13); street art (3); reviews (7); keywords (3); online review (1),,,
_Sequeira-2020-Simplified Crowd Simulation in V.txt,Simpliﬁed Crowd Simulation in Virtual Heritage Sites,Luís Miguel Sequeira,Polytechnic Institute of Santarém; Ph D student at University Trás-os-Montes and Alto Douro (UTAD),2020,book chapter,Chapter,,10.1093/oso/9780190498900.003.0007,https://www.researchgate.net/publication/340036085,,,Cultural Heritage (2),,heritage sites (6); virtual heritage sites (3); Ancient Rome (2); historical site (10); historical European theatres; baroque city of Lisbon; Ancient Rome,virtual heritage (3); heritage sites (6); historical accuracy (5); virtual archaeology (10); heritage exhibits; heritage site (10); virtual museum; London Charter (4); Seville Charter (5); virtual archaeology projects (5); virtual agent (7); virtual agents (12); virtual worlds (15); virtual laboratory of archaeology (4); historical sites (2); historical site; heritage (4); heritage sites; historical re-enactment societies; heritage site; virtual agents; historical catastrophes; historical site; historical site; heritage sites,,"{'SOCIAL VALUES': 'The paper discusses the importance of virtual heritage sites in providing a sense of place and cultural identity, which aligns with collective emotional values. The sites allow people to connect with the past and share experiences, fostering a sense of community and belonging.'}; {'HISTORIC VALUES': 'The paper emphasizes the educational role of heritage assets in providing knowledge about the past. Virtual archaeology projects aim to create historically accurate models of heritage sites, allowing independent researchers to evaluate their historical accuracy.'}; {'AESTHETICAL VALUES': 'The paper mentions the artistic and conceptual aspects of virtual heritage sites, highlighting the creativity and imagination involved in recreating historical environments. The models are compared to existing paintings and engravings, suggesting an appreciation for artistic representation.'}",heritage sites; reconstructions; conservation support,Rome; Lisbon; Uruk,Europe; Greece; Portugal,the 1990s,1755 earthquake,"Early research focused merely on displaying models of the architecture or of archaeological artefacts, but, with the emergence of virtual worlds, researchers and the public could ‘immerse’ themselves in the reconstructed environment and experience the equivalent of a guided tour.","In this chapter, an alternative solution is offered, whereby historians are able to manipulate the parameters of the crowd simulation itself — using the virtual worlds platform Open Simulator — without the need of learning conventional computer programming.",,,,,,,,,"Second Life, now entering its 13th year of operation, still boasts about a million regular users.",,,,,,,,,,,,,,,[],,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,,[],,,,,,,,,,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,,,3D models (4); virtual reality (3); computer graphics (3); crowd simulation (11); virtual agents (12); artificial intelligence (AI) (7); virtual worlds (15); Open Simulator (10); Second Life (8); NPCs (6); avatars (6); genetic algorithms (2); PHP,,,
_Shabani et al.-2017-City-stories A multimedia hybri.txt,City-Stories: A Multimedia Hybrid Content and Entity Retrieval,S. Shabani; L. Rosseto; I. Giangreco; K. Stockinger; H. Schuldt,,2017,other,"Histo Informatics 2017, November 2017, Singapore",,,,,,cultural heritage (6),,,,,,,city center of Berlin (1); Brandenburg Gate (4); Berlin (2); Singapore (1); New York (1); Lower Manhatan (1),Dublin (1); Berlin (3); Singapore (1); New York (1); European (1),1920’s (1),fall of the iron curtain in 1989 (1),"Users are not only interested in the current appearance of landscapes, monuments, or buildings, but also in the evolution of these places over time.","Te contribution of the paper is threefold. First, we show how multi-feature content-based similarity search providing a plethora of query types can be enriched by entity recognition and entity linking, thereby allowing for cross-media retrieval based on semantic concepts.",,photos (3); videos (1); user ratings (1),,,,user ratings (1),,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,[],,entity recognition (4); entity linking (6),deep neural network (1); convolutional network (1),AlexNet (1),,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,yes,[],media items (2),an edge is present between two items if they contain the same entity and are thus related (1),,,,,,,,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,,,,,,
_Shabani et al.-2020-Hybrid Human-Machine Classificat.txt,Hybrid Human-Machine Classification System for,Shaban Shabani; Maria Sokhn,,2020,conference paper,"SUMAC'20, October 12, 2020, Seattle, WA, USA",IEEE,,https://www.notrehistoire.ch,,,cultural heritage (4),,historical data (3); historical digital collections (1); historical content (1); historical images (2); historical data classification (1); historical information (1); historical content (1),digital preservation (1); metadata (10); digital management platforms (1); spatio-temporal properties (1); provenance properties (1); cultural_interest (2); Creative Commons license (1),,"{'Social': 'Emotional (collective) – The study aims to enrich metadata of historical images, contributing to cultural identity and a sense of place attachment by categorizing images with cultural interest.'}; {'Historic': 'Educational – The study focuses on classifying historical images, which can provide knowledge about the past and contribute to the educational role of heritage assets.'}; {'Aesthetical': 'Artistic – The study involves categorizing images with historical content, which can be considered original products of creativity and imagination.'}",data curation (1),,Switzerland (1); Australia (1),,,Incomplete cultural data lose their relevance in search engines and consequently their historical value when they cannot be found.,"In this paper, we address the issue of completing the metadata of historical digital collections. For this, we introduce a new hybrid human-machine model. This model jointly integrates predictions of a deep multi-input model and inferred labels from multiple crowd judgements.",Wikipedia (1); Amazon Mechanical Turk (MTurk) (1); Micro Workers (2); Figure Eight (1),images (12); text (6); videos (2); audios (1); documents (2); metadata information (2),,,,,title (3); description (3); location (2); year (1); tags (4); author information (1),"5,015","thousands of registered users, and several hundred active participants",,"5,015",,,,,different regions of Switzerland,participatory platform,,filtering only images that had a “by-nc-nd” Creative Commons license,,,manual,10 participants from the region,"['place', 'object', 'person', 'event', 'tradition']",𝜅= 0.55,image classification (4); object detection (2); sentiment annotation (1); multi-label classification (5),deep learning (7); deep neural network (2); transfer learning (4); machine learning (5); CNN models (1),VGG19 (1); Mobile Net (5); Res Ne (1); VGG16 (1),pre-trained models (4),Glo Ve (2); word embeddings (1),"term frequency, inverse document frequency (tf-idf) (1)",visual features (4); text features (4); image features (1),weighted aggregation (2),"60% of the data for training, 20% for validating the models, and 20% for the test set",binary cross entropy loss (1),,1e-5,,30,,,{},Logistic Regression (Log) (2); Random Forest (RF) (3); Support Vector Machines (SVM) (4),,,,,8 hours effective time,The customized implementation has a logistic regression final layer with sigmoid activation function and uses the binary cross entropy loss [26].,"The new custom classification head was trained with images of our dataset (training set), so that the model addresses the multi-label classification task. A learning rate of 1e-5 on the training process was used, and the performance on the validation set was measured on 30 epochs.",no,[],,,,,,,,,,precision (1); recall (1); F1 score (1); exact match accuracy (subset accuracy) (1); Hamming-loss (4),"['SVM model achieved the highest accuracy of 58% on the testing set.', 'After 30 epochs, our model achieved an accuracy of 63% and Hamming-loss of 10% on the validation set.', 'Finally, we evaluated the model with data from the testing set and the accuracy achieved was 62% with a 10% Hamming-loss.', 'Incorporating the human judgments in the final output showed to improve the accuracy by 3%.', 'the weights of 0.7 for deep learning and 0.3 for crowd outputs achieved the highest strict accuracy of 65% and hamming-loss of 10%']",[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['We implement and evaluate a deep learning multi-input approach by combining pre-trained models that leverage the image visual features that explores the text features available in the metadata.', 'We design a crowdsourcing task that leverages the human cognitive skills of online crowd workers to categorize historical images. We implement a customized aggregation model that considers the crowd users’ profiles for the answer selection.', 'We implement and evaluate two hybrid human-machine approaches for image classification. The hybrid approaches perform better than automatic classification and crowdsourcing schemes.']",[],[],['The size of the dataset is a possible limitation that especially affects the deep learning approach.'],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,"The data selection process included further inspection of licenses of shared data, filtering only images that had a “by-nc-nd” Creative Commons license2. This is important in order to reproduce the experiments and validate the results we obtained.",,,,,,crowd judgements (1); crowdsourcing (7); crowd users (6); online crowd workers (3); domain experts (3); GLAMs (3); citizen science (1); DBpedia (6); HITs (Human Intelligence Tasks) (2); Notre Histoire (4),,,
