_Shi et al.-2022-Adaptive Renewal of Mountainous.txt,Adaptive Renewal of Mountainous,Yulin Shi; Ying Huang; Ying Zhang; Jianming Jiang; Lin Zhang,,2022,journal article,Frontiers in Environmental Science,Frontiers Media SA,,,,,Cultural Heritage,cultural; historical,historical towns (24); historical and cultural heritage; historical and cultural resources; historic district; historical buildings (2); cultural relics (2); historic streets,"Conservation of Cultural Relics; historical value; commemorative signiﬁcance; traditional features; local ethnic characteristics; core conservation; conservation and management; historical and cultural elements; conservation of historical cities, towns and villages; natural landscapes; cultural environments; livelihood environments; historical authenticity; intangible cultural heritage; conservation planning; conservation and restoration measures; guarantee mechanism; adaptive renewal (2); conservation assessment; social network conservation; social network structure (5); social ties (14); value characteristics; conservation measures; conservation grades (3); conservation zone (3); historical buildings/sites",,"{'SOCIAL VALUES': 'The study emphasizes the importance of social ties (kinship, neighborhood, job relationships) in historical towns, indicating a focus on collective emotional values and cultural identity. The research aims to guide the adaptive renewal of built environments and social networks, reflecting a concern for maintaining community bonds.'}; {'HISTORIC VALUES': 'The research focuses on historical towns and their conservation, indicating a strong emphasis on the educational and symbolic values associated with these sites. The study aims to analyze the influencing factors of social network structure in historical towns, reflecting an interest in understanding the historical context and evolution of these communities.'}; {'AESTHETICAL VALUES': 'The study considers the style integrity and spatial layout of core conservation areas, suggesting an appreciation for the artistic and conceptual aspects of the built environment. The research aims to guide the adaptive renewal of built environments, reflecting a concern for preserving the aesthetic qualities of historical towns.'}; {'ECONOMIC VALUES': 'The introduction mentions that urban renewal can improve property value and economic development, indicating a consideration of the use and entertainment values of heritage assets. The study also discusses the commercialization of historical towns, reflecting an awareness of the economic forces shaping these areas.'}",Conservation (13); management (2); restoration measures; conservation planning (2),Chongqing (10); Yunshan Town; Nuodeng Town; Shuhe; Shuangjiang; Lijiang town; Hongyadong Block; Ningchang town; Zhongshan (ZS); Baisha (BS); Wenquan (WQ); Pianyan (PT); Qingyang (QY); Ningchang (NC); Xituo (XT),"China (8); Chongqing (10); southwest China; Ontario, Canada; Hong Kong; George Town, Penang; Norway; Japan; Hubei Province, Central China; Nova Scotia; Botswana; Northern Norway; Guangdong Province, China; south carolina",,,"Previous studies have indicated that both of built environments and social networks are important in conservation and adaptive renewal of historical towns (8). However, in view of these practical issues, existing studies have focused on the perspective of built environments and neglected social networks in historical towns.","Therefore, this article aims to analyze the inﬂuencing factor of SSNS in historical towns of Chongqing, and guide the adaptive renewal of built environments and social networks for other historical towns in China.",,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,data on households and social ties were collected by informant interviews and semi-structured interviews with residents of the studied samples.,,,,,,,[],,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,yes,['social networks (10)'],“Node” means one household in the CCA of the historical town.,"“Line” means social ties among households in the CCA of the town, which consists of three categories in terms of kinship, geographic, or job relationship.","123, 116, 79, 50, 70, 99, 98, and 116","1,764, 1,080, 886, 318, 512, 914, 592, and 854",network density; lambda set; degree centrality; clustering feature; k-core (11),the collected data on households and social ties in the seven studied samples were converted into an adjacency matrix consisting of “0” and “1.”,k-core model of SNA,,"This article explored the SSNS and the conservation strategy of historical towns based on the construction of social network models and analysis of the k-core indicators of seven historical towns in Chongqing, China.",k-core indicator (2),[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['this study also has limitations, particularly regarding small sample size and limited social ties.']",[],[],[],[],[],[],['Creative Commons Attribution License (CC BY)'],[],,"The original contributions presented in the study are included in the article/supplementary material, further inquiries can be directed to the corresponding authors.",,,,,,SSNS (14); spatial layout (7); function of households (5); informant interviews; semi-structured interviews; kinship; geographic; job relationship; UCINET,,,
_Shimada et al.-2011-Analyzing tourism information on.txt,Analyzing Tourism Information on Twitter for a Local City,Kazutaka Shimada; Ryosuke Tadano; Tsutomu Endo,,2011,other,"Journal of the Japanese Society for Artiﬁcial Intelligence, 26(3):234–240, 2011",,,,,,,,,tourism informatics (2); tourism events (1); tourism properties (1); tourism development (2); tourism locations (1); tourism information (4); sightseeing areas (1),,"{'Economic': 'Entertainment: The study focuses on analyzing tourism information on Twitter to detect good or weak points of facilities or events, which can be used to improve the tourism market.'}",,Iizuka City (2); Ito residence (2); Iizuka historical museum (2),Tenjin (1),,fireworks event at Iizuka (1),"The Web contains much information for the tourism, such as impressions and sentiments about sightseeing areas. Analyzing the information is a signiﬁcant task for tourism informatics.","In this paper, we propose a tourism information analysis system for a local city. The target resource for the analysis is information on Twitter. First, we discuss a method to extract tweets (posted sentences) relating to the target locations and tourism events. Then, we analyze the polarity of the extracted tweets; positive or negative opinions.",Twitter (2),text (1),,,,,,116 tweets,,,,,,,,local city,extract tweets containing the seed words by an exact match approach,,,,,,,"['positive', 'negative']",,classification,naive bayes classiﬁer (2),,,vector space (2),,seed words (4),,,,,,,,,,{},scoring method based on polarity dictionaries (2),,,,,,,"pseudo training data acquisition and the P/N classiﬁcation method using it. First, our method extracts tweets containing the seed words by an exact match approach. We regard the extracted tweets as the training data for a classiﬁer, and construct the vector space from the data. The naive bayes classiﬁer generates the model from the vector space.",no,[],,,,,,,,,,accuracy rate (2),"['Our method 0.89', 'Scoring 0.76']",[],[],,The reason was that the dictionary-based method could not handle tweets with informal expressions in the test data appropriately. This result shows the effectiveness of our method with the naive bayes classiﬁer using the pseudo training data.,[],[],,[],[],[],,dictionary-based method,['The accuracy of our method was 13% higher than that of the dictionary-based method.'],,[],[],[],[],[],[],['tourism information analysis system (3)'],[],[],[],[],"['The number of extracted sentences was, however, small in amount and not sufﬁcient.', 'However, the size of our test set was small; approximately 100 tweets.', 'Moreover, we dealt with only positive/negative classiﬁcation. Naturally, there is 3rd class, i.e., neutral sentences, which do not contain sentiment information. Three-class problem, namely positive, neutral and negative, is unavoidable work in the future.']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,,,P/N classiﬁcation (4); pseudo training data (4); seed words (5); polarity (2); sentiment (4); Okapi-BM25 (1),,,This work was supported by a research grant from Iizuka City.
