_Shivottam and Mishra-2023-Tirtha - An Automated Platform t.txt,Tirtha - An Automated Platform to Crowdsource Images and,Jyotirmaya Shivottam; Subhankar Mishra,,2023,conference paper,"The 28th International ACM Conference on 3D Web Technology (Web3D ’23), October 09–11, 2023, San Sebastian, Spain",ACM,https://doi.org/10.1145/3611314.3615904,https://tirtha.niser.ac.in,,15 pages,Cultural Heritage (CH) (7); World Heritage (2); digital heritage (DH) (3),tangible cultural heritage (TCH) (2); intangible cultural heritage (ICH) (2); cultural; natural,artefacts; monuments (4); a group of buildings and sites; museums; TCH or CH sites; historical sites (2); temples (2); forts; palaces; State Protected Monuments (2); Somanatha and Gopinatha temples (2),"values including symbolic, historic, artistic, aesthetic, ethnological or anthropological, scientific and social significance; UNESCO (4); World Heritage Committee; digital technologies to record, preserve, and disseminate knowledge from cultural heritage (CH) sites; digital documentation of CH sites (3); heritage objects; museum assets; digital documentation for CH sites; site preservation; Creative Commons Attribution-Non CommercialShare Alike 4.0 International (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0); Creative Commons Attribution-Non CommercialNo Derivatives 4.0 International (CC BY-NC-ND 4.0); heritage conservation (3); State Protected Monuments; Kalinga architecture; digital heritage; cultural heritage sites (2)",,"Social (Emotional (collective)): The platform aims to involve the general public and experts in documenting CH sites, fostering a sense of cultural identity and communal value by allowing them to share their heritage globally.; Historic (Educational): The platform aims to preserve and disseminate knowledge from cultural heritage sites, providing educational resources about the past.; Aesthetic (Artistic): The remaining carvings showcase intricate patterns and floral motifs.; Economic (Use): The platform aims to provide opportunities for local communities to engage in sustainable tourism and support their livelihoods.",preservation (3); heritage conservation (2); digital preservation (2); digital documentation (3),"Odisha, India; Somanatha and Gopinatha temples; Khurdha district",India (3); Odisha; Spain,13th century AD,,"This work addresses the lack of a cost-effective method to document CH sites, in culturally rich but resource-limited countries like India.","Our work aims to provide a dataset of crowdsourced images and 3D reconstructions for research in computer vision, heritage con- servation, and related domains.",Facebook; Instagram,images; 3D models; metadata,,,,,EXIF data,,,,,,,,,,crowdsourcing,,,"We perform client-side checks on images, such as EXIF data validation, file type validation, and conversion to JPEG for consistency.",,manual,,"['“good”', '“bad”']",,semantic segmentation,,MANIQA,pre-trained model,,,images,,,,,,,,,,{},,Ubuntu 22.04 LTS server,A100,1,512 GB RAM,,,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,Dynamic Range (DR); Contrast-to-Noise (CNR); No Reference Image Quality Assessment,[],[],[],,we assess the quality of the generated mesh based on visual appearance and completeness.,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['the main challenge lies in quantifying the quality of the crowdsourced data and corresponding 3D reconstructions.', 'compressing and delivering the meshes over the web.', 'crowdsourcing remains an ongoing challenge for\nTirtha, particularly in terms of volunteer incentives and continued engagement.']","['This approach minimizes the personal information we store, complying with various privacy laws, while allowing us to identify users for moderation and attribution purposes.']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],the code available on Git Hub,"The resulting models and images are stored as datasets under a non-commercial Creative Commons license, facilitating further use in research and creative disciplines.",,,"Tirtha is currently deployed on-premise in a Docker container on a Ubuntu 2