_Sidor et al.-2025-On the Road Towards Identifying.txt,CASE REPORT ABSTRACT:,Csaba Sidor,"Department of Geo and Mining Tourism, Faculty of Mining, Ecology, Process Control and Geotechnologies, Technical University of Kosice, Letná 9, Kosice 042 00, Slovakia",,other,,,,,,,geoheritage (6),cultural (2); natural (3),Slovak geoheritage (3); significant geological sites (SGS) (11); geosites (17); geological localities (1); protected areas (10); national parks (1); castle ruins (1); castle hills (1),geoheritage (6); geosites (17); protected areas (10); natural values (1); conservation (1); protection (2); geoparks (6); nomination; management (10); tourism resources (12); attraction (3); geotourism (7); scientific value (2); cultural (1); aesthetic (1); emotional (1); heritage (1); digital identities (1),educational; scientific; cultural; aesthetic; emotional,"{'value': 'Educational', 'reasoning': 'The paper discusses the potential of geological sites to be transformed into geosites, primary tourism resources capable of creating main motivations for visiting a destination. The paper also mentions the necessity of identifying tourists’/visitors’ awareness about geosites.'}; {'value': 'Economic', 'reasoning': 'The paper discusses the potential of geological objects to become geosites, a main primary tourism resource capable of supporting or even carrying a destination’s tourism related economy via implementing principles of Geotourism.'}; {'value': 'Social', 'reasoning': 'The paper mentions the necessity of incorporating visitor experiences associated with geosites’ visit into geotourism development processes are considered essential for geoheritage interpretation when targeting general public.'}",conservation (1); protection (2); management (10),Slovakia (10); Slovak Repbulic (1),Slovakia (10); Slovak Repbulic (1); Eastern European subregion (1); Czechia (1); Poland (1); Austria (1); Hungary (1); Ukraine (1); Northen Europe (1); Great Britain (1); Western Asia (1); Israel (1