_Silva et al.-2025-Sentiment Classification Model f.txt,Sentiment Classiﬁcation Model for Landscapes,,,,other,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,"(i) classify sentiments in natural sceneimages(landscapes),(ii)classifythesentimentslinkedwiththetextassociatedwith a landscape, and (iii) combine image and text classiﬁcation, returning the information about its discrepancy.",Instagram; X; Twitter,photos; texts; image; text; multimodal data,,,,,,~ 3.4 M,,"379k unbalanced samples, from which 50k balanced samples",~ 4 M images,,,,2016 and 2017,,,,a sub-dataset of text posts was selected from the B-T4SA.,"(i) the replacement of emojis/emoticons for words (e.g., was replaced by “smiling face with hearts”); (ii) convert all text to lowercase; (iii) remove stop words (e.g., ‘i’, ‘me’, ‘after’, ‘moreover’), proves useful as they do not contribute to sentiment analysis and their exclusion avoids unnecessary computations; (iv) removed HTML tags, images, mentions, links, punctuation etc., because they do not carry sentiments; (v) apply a lemmatizer, which removes inﬂectional endings from a token to turn it into the base word lemma (e.g., the word ‘dancing’ would be lemmatized to ‘dance’); and (vi) apply stemming, which is the process of removing sufﬁces from words to obtain their root form (e.g., the word ‘dancing’ would be stemmed to ‘danc’).","dataset was ﬁltered to include only those cases where a minimum of ﬁve out of the six individuals unanimously agreed on the sentiment classiﬁcation (positive, negative, or neutral).","photos were presented and classiﬁed by a group of 6 persons (3 male, 3 female), with ages between 21 and 55 years, all with Portuguese nationality.","6 persons (3 male, 3 female), with ages between 21 and 55 years, all with Portuguese nationality","['positive', 'negative', 'neutral']","minimum of ﬁve out of the six individuals unanimously agreed on the sentiment classiﬁcation (positive, negative, or neutral).",sentiment analysis; classiﬁcation,deep learning; machine learning,Dense Net121; Xception; Res Net-50,all the backbones were trained using the Image Net dataset.,,Bag of Words (BOW),image; text,,80% of those images were used for training and 20% for testing,,SGD,1e-2,32,20,dropout,,{},,Google Colab (with 12.7GB de RAM and 107.7GB disc space) and Kaggle platform (with 14.8 GB RAM e GPU T4 x2),GPU T4,2,12.7GB,,"three primary models are introduced (predeﬁned), distinguished by the applied backbone architecture. Speciﬁcally, one utilizes the Dense Net121 (121 layers) architecture as the backbone [20], another uses the Xception architecture (71 layers) [21], and the third one uses the Res Net-50 architecture (50 Layers) [22].","the image models were trained with Flickr Col Img, composed of 81.834 images (see Table 1), where 80% of those images were used for training and 20% for testing. As the dataset had images with different scales, (a.1) image pixel values were normalized between 0 and 1 and (a.2) resized to 224 × 224 pixels. The (b) text models were trained with B-T4SAtext, composed of 50.001 text tweets, where 80% of the samples were used for training and 20% for testing. The (c) MSC was trained using B-T4SALand and a stratiﬁed K-fold cross-validation technique, but only using the samples where the image and the text have the same sentiment, resulting in 273 samples.",no,[],,,,,,,,,,accuracy,['accuracy of 78.75%'],[],[],,,[],[],the main error of the model is to assign positive images to neutral images.,[],[],[],Stratiﬁed K-Fold cross-validation technique,,[],confusion matrices,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['the focus should be on improving the sentiment detection model in images and getting more and, also extremely relevant, better datasets of image-text related to landscapes.']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,available at https://www.ee.columbia.edu/ln/dvmm/vso/download/ﬂickr_dataset.html.,,http://www.t4sa.it/#dataset,,,,Human-Centered Artiﬁcial Intelligence (HCAI); Affective Computing (AC); Landscape Sentiment Classiﬁcation model (