_Song et al.-2023-The Cultivation Effect of Archit.txt,Article ABSTRACT:,L. Song; R.Y.M. Li; T. Wareewanich,,2023,journal article,Buildings,MDPI,https://doi.org/10.3390/ buildings13020508,https://doi.org/10.3390/ buildings13020508,,,Cultural Heritage (2),architectural; cultural (2),architectural heritage (14); historical architecture (2); historical relics; cultural architectures; ancient charm of history; Forbidden City (2); architectural heritage sites; traditional architectural heritage,cultural heritage (3); historical assets; historical architecture (2); historical relics; cultural architectures; ancient charm of history; architectural heritage sites; traditional architectural heritage; monuments (3); archaeological sites (2); aesthetic; historical; social; scientiﬁc; technological interest; groups of buildings; technical signiﬁcance; topographic units; sites; artistic; repurposing; protection and conservation of architectural heritage in tourism,,"{'SOCIAL VALUES': ""Emotional (collective) – The study highlights the importance of architectural heritage in shaping a country's image and attracting tourists, which can foster cultural identity, motivation, and pride among its citizens.""}; {'ECONOMIC VALUES': 'Entertainment – The study focuses on the use of YouTube videos to promote architectural heritage, which can enhance tourism and generate revenue for the destination.'}; {'POLITICAL VALUES': ""Educational – The study suggests that architectural heritage can be used to educate the public about a country's history and culture, which can promote national identity and pride.""}; {'HISTORIC VALUES': ""Historic-Artistic – The study emphasizes the importance of architectural heritage as a representation of a nation's history and culture, which can be a source of artistic and historical value.""}; {'AESTHETICAL VALUES': 'Artistic – The study focuses on the visual appeal of architectural heritage and its potential to attract tourists, which can be a source of artistic and aesthetic value.'}",architectural heritage conservation (2); protection and conservation of architectural heritage in tourism,Beijing (12); Forbidden City (2); Great Wall (4); Barcelona,China (7); Chinese; francophone territory; ﬁve continents; France; Slovenia; Greece; Bucharest; Phuket; Thailand; Singapore; Seoul; South Korea; United States,3000 years of history,,The research rarely studies the formation of Beijing’s destination image via architectural heritage on You Tube.,(1) How does Beijing’s architectural heritage in French You Tube videos cultivate Beijing’s destination image? (2) How do You Tube viewers perceive Beijing’s architectural heritage tourism destination image cultivated by these videos? (3) What are the characteristics of You Tube video networks?,You Tube (18); Twitter (3); Sina Weibo; Trip Advisor (3); We Chat,videos (10); comments (13); text; audio; ﬁgure; metadata,,,,likes (3); comments (5),channel ID; channel title; video ID; publication date; video title; video description; tags; video category; duration; dimension; deﬁnition quality; view count; like count; dislike count; favourite count; comments of videos; technical parameters,2237 You Tube videos in French,,"25,234 comments",,2237,,,,Beijing,You Tube API v3,"You Tube API v3, Node XL version 1.0.1.510",,eliminating the videos without descriptions,,sentiment analysis,,"['strong negative', 'negative', 'neutral', 'positive', 'strongly positive']",,sentiment analysis,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,yes,['social network'],"social structure or content, virtual physical location, event, or individual, for instance, an institution, organisation, or country",Link or connection that occurs when two vertices collaborate or exchange information,"22,677","20,867",average geodesic distance; modularity,,Clauset–Newman–Moore algorithm; Harel–Koren fast multiscale layout algorithm,,investigate the relationships among You Tube viewers,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],