_Stewart et al.-2020-A Pilot Study on Remote Sensing.txt,Technical Note,C. Stewart; G. Lombardo; D. L. González,"European Space Agency (ESA), Frascati, Italy; Scifabric (Southampton, UK); Tor Vergata University of Rome",2020,other,,MDPI,,http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/,,,cultural heritage (2),,archaeological structures (5); archaeological sites (2); Roman period (3); ancient Roman city (2); ancient Etruscan city,archaeology (6); archaeological (27); archaeological record; preservation (3); cultural heritage (2); archaeological prospection (10); archaeological survey (3); archaeological residues (6); archaeological interpretation (3); heritage practitioners,,"{'value': 'Educational', 'reasoning': 'The paper discusses the potential of citizen science and remote sensing for archaeological prospection, implying an educational value in understanding and preserving cultural heritage.'}; {'value': 'Historic-Artistic', 'reasoning': 'The study focuses on detecting and interpreting archaeological cropmarks, which are remnants of past human activities and structures, thus relating to the artistic and historical significance of the sites.'}; {'value': 'Economic', 'reasoning': 'The paper mentions the conflict between preservation of the archaeological record and territorial/economic development, indicating an economic value associated with land use and development versus heritage preservation.'}",preservation (3),Rome; Italy; Ferentium; Ostia; Veii,Italy; Rome; Netherlands; North Sinai Desert; Poland; Mediterranean region,Roman period (3),,"Particularly in countries with a rich cultural heritage, the abundance of buried archaeological structures poses a challenge.",It aims to determine to what extent the eﬃciency of using the freely available Bird’s Eye service of Microsoft Bing Maps for archaeological prospection can be improved by addressing the challenges of human interpretation through citizen science.,Microsoft Bing Maps (5); Google Maps; Google Earth (3); Apple