_Sulistyaningsih et al.-2022-Can Combined Marketing and Plann.txt,"Can Combined Marketing and Planning Approaches Transform Slums into Tourism Villages? A Case Study from Malang, Indonesia",Tri Sulistyaningsih; Salahudin Salahudin; Hazel Dapat Jovita; Achmad Nurmandi,,2022,journal article,Journal homepage,,,www.tandfonline.com/journals/wnon20,,,,,slum project (1); slum area (3); tourism village (4); slums (10); informal settlements (1),sustainable development (2); place branding (10); tourism (14); tourist destination (7); cultural (4); environmental (7); economic (7); social (16); preservation (1); planning (11); branding (26); sustainable tourism development (1); quality of life (10),,"{'value': 'Social – Emotional (collective)', 'reasoning': 'The study discusses the transformation of a slum into a tourist village, which enhances cultural identity, motivation, pride, and a sense of place attachment for the local community.'}; {'value': 'Economic – Entertainment', 'reasoning': 'The study focuses on transforming a slum into a tourist destination, which directly relates to the entertainment value of the area and its role in the contemporary tourism market.'}; {'value': 'Political – Management', 'reasoning': 'The study examines how the transformation of the slum is incorporated into political strategies and policies, particularly concerning urban planning and community development.'}; {'value': 'Aesthetical – Artistic', 'reasoning': 'The transformation of the slum into a colorful tourism village involves artistic elements such as painting and murals, enhancing the aesthetic appeal of the area.'}; {'value': 'Ecological – Essential', 'reasoning': 'The study mentions the improvement of environmental sustainability as a result of the transformation, indicating the presence of ecological ideologies in the design and construction of the tourism village.'}",slum upgrading (1); slum structuring (2); place branding (10); sustainable development (1),Jodipan slum area; Malang Ci