_Sun et al.-2015-Road-based travel recommendation.txt,Road-based travel recommendation integrating landmark and routing mined from geo-tagged images,Lei Sun; Esther Ruas; Sabine Lang; Patrick Le Callet,,2015,other,"Computers, Environment and Urban Systems",Science Direct,,http://www.ﬂickr.com/services/api/,,,,,,,,,,,Munich; Germany,,,"The recommended routing is always represented as the average of the historic routings (trajectories) or the one with the highest ranking. Nevertheless, such recommended trip routings sometimes lack convenience and effectiveness for users to position and navigate on the digital map, since they are based on GPS trajectory instead of separate road in the road network.","through leveraging Flickr geotagged images, this paper aims to generate recommended routing from separate roads instead of historic trajectories of users. In other words, the atomic unit of the routing is road segment rather than trajectory segment. Moreover, to recommend the suitable routing, in addition to the popularity of the road, POIs on the road as well as the length of the road are considered in the proposed recommendation system.",Flickr; Trip Advisor; Open Street Map; Gowalla,images; geotagged images; tags; GPS data; user check-in data,geotagged images; GPS traces; longitude; latitude,,,reviews; comments,user ID; longitude; latitude; time; user proﬁle; user location,"45,950 images",2422 users,,"45,950",,,"31,335",year 2010 and 2011,"Munich, Germany",Flickr API,Flickr API,,"discarded 1223 images whose tags are not indicating the popularity of any POI or road but reﬂecting some persons, persons’ gestures and other contents unrelated to tourism.",the image whose tag has only one user,,,[],,classiﬁcation; clustering,machine learning methods,Binary Logistic Regression; Support Vector Machines; DBSCAN,,,,distances of image to the 1st and 2nd nearest roads; number of POIs,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,,[],,,,,,,,,,accuracy,['The total validation accuracies of BLR and SVM are 78.5% and 80.4% respectively.'],[],[],Wilcoxon test,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['Duo to the data quality (e.g., incompleteness, tagging error, etc.) of the Flick data, to enhance the travel recommendation, there are some aspects should be taken into account in the future research.']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,,,,,,
_Sun et al.-2019-Building a model-based personali.txt,Building a model-based personalised recommendation system with geotagged photos,Zhou Huang; Yiran Chen; Yu Liu,,2019,journal article,Journal of Spatial Information Science,Taylor & Francis,https://doi.org/10.1080/17538947.2018.1471104,https://doi.org/10.1080/17538947.2018.1471104,,661 678,,,attractions; tourist attractions,,,,,Beijing; Forbidden City; National Art Museum of China; Purple Bamboo Park; Prince Gong’s Mansion; Sanlitun Village; Factory 798; Tiananmen Square,China; Beijing; San Diego; CA; Melbourne; Australia,,,"In travel recommendation systems, a simple assumption is that users have specific interests and thus visit attractions matching their preferences.","Therefore, using these geotagged photos, we built a personalised recommendation system to provide attraction recommendations that match a user’s preferences.",social media websites; Flickr; Foursquare; Trip Advisor; Twitter; Facebook; Instagram; You Tube,photos; geotagged photos; multisource information; weather; transportation; textual information; text; pictures; videos; geographic location information; comments; geotag,geographic location information; geographic location; geotagged photos; latitude; longitude,spatial distributions,timestamp; time sequence; spatio-temporal contexts,,photo ID; user ID; tags; date Taken; latitude; longitude,"213,938 geotagged photos","11,173 users",,,,,"213,938",from 1 January 2005 to 1 January 2016,Beijing,We used Flickr’s public API to retrieve geotagged photos taken in Beijing from 1 January 2005 to 1 January 2016.,Flickr’s public API,,"After removing incomplete data, we harvested a total of 213,938 geotagged photos.",removing incomplete data,,,[],,classification; regression,Bayesian classifiers; neural networks; ensemble learning models,support vector machine (SVM); gradient boosting regression tree (GBRT); Ada Boost; latent Dirichlet allocation (LDA),,one-shot encoding,,travel history data; weather context; t