_Tenerelli et al.-2017-Spatial assessment of aesthetic.txt,Spatial assessment of aesthetic service provision in mountain landscapes using crowdsourced geographic information,P. Tenerelli; S. Luque; C. Pu¨ffel,"UR EMGR Mountain Ecosystems Unit, IRSTEA - National Research Institute of Science and Technology for Environment and Agriculture, 2 rue de la Papeterie, 38402 Saint Martin d’He`res, France; Institute of Geography, Humboldt University, Unter den Linden 6, 10099 Berlin, Germany; IRSTEA – UMR TETIS Territoires, Environnement, Te´le´de´tection et Information Spatiale, 500 rue JF Breton, 34000 Montpellier, France",2017,journal article,Ambio,Royal Swedish Academy of Sciences,https://doi.org/10.1007/s13280-017-0919-z,,,,,,,Cultural Ecosystem Services (CES) (6); aesthetic value (3); scenic beauty (6); cultural capital stock (2); cultural landscapes (2); landscape information functions (2); Integral Biological Reserves (IBRs) (1); Vercors Natural Regional Park (VNRP) (1); Long Term Ecological Research sites (LTER) (1); Natura 2000 areas (1),,"{'value': 'Aesthetical Values', 'reasoning': 'The study focuses on assessing the aesthetic value of landscapes, particularly scenic beauty, using visual indicators and crowdsourced geographic information. The research aims to map the scenic beauty of complex mountain landscapes from the perspective of observers.'}; {'value': 'Social Values', 'reasoning': 'The study considers the human perception of landscapes and how they contribute to human well-being. It analyzes how different landscape characters attract different types of users (foreign, domestic, local), indicating a connection to cultural identity and sense of place.'}; {'value': 'Ecological Values', 'reasoning': 'The study uses indicators such as naturalness, habitat variety, and the presence of water to assess the aesthetic service provision. These indicators reflect the ecological characteristics of the landscape and their contribution to the overall aesthetic experience.'}",landscape planning (3); landscape monitoring (1); landscape management (1),‘Quatre Montagnes’; French Alps; Vercors massif,France; Europe,,,"Despite the increasing research in ES, there is currently a lack of focus on demonstrating the relation between human well-being, landscape character and its associated cultural services.","(i) spatially assess biophysical and built-up characteristics of the landscape through visual indicators over a range of view points where photos were shared by visiting users; (ii) on the base of these visual indicators and the actual presence of beneﬁciaries, map the aesthetic service provision and identify geographic patterns of landscape characters; (iii) last, analyse the correspondence of visiting users’ provenance—i.e. arrivals by place of origin—with speciﬁc landscapes characters and preferences.",Flickr; Panoramio; Open Street Map (OSM),images / photos; geotagged posts or GPS coordinates; spatial maps,geotags or GPS coordinates,geographic distributions; spatial clustering,,,username or account ID; location tags,2167,170,,270,,,,2012 to 2014,‘Quatre Montagnes’,API,Flickr Application Programming Interface (API),,"Expert knowledge and multi-media data—such as background satellite photo, virtual globes and land use/land cover data—were used to exclude photos with incorrect location.",highest geotag accuracy (street level),manual,expert,['panoramic view'],,clustering,,K Means,,,,visual indicators,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,R2 value; Calinski–Harabasz (CH) index,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['support landscape monitoring', 'support landscape management']",[],[],[],['lack of representativeness of the Flickr community in relation to speciﬁc groups'],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,Arc GIS 10.3,,geo-tagged photos; panoramic views; visual indicators; crowdsourced geographic information; visual landscape; aesthetic service provision; landscape characters; visiting users’ preferences; visual scale; naturalness