or heritage, are not fully captured in this analysis, mainly due to the fact that there are no data that can be used for a wall-to-wall European assessment.']",,,,,,Python,,cultural ecosystem services; aesthetic appreciation; cultural identity; sense of place; farmland biodiversity; traditional landscapes; low-intensity farmland; social-ecological linkages; management intensity; landscape structure; value and meaning; aesthetic enjoyment; outdoor recreation; traditional food products; Protected Designation of Origin; geotagged landscape pictures; visual; sense of place; social media data; crowd-sourced information; landscape preference; landscape valuation; anthropogenic inﬂuences; afforestation; nature conservation; farmland abandonment; traditional forest; modern forest; silvo-pastoral landscape system; non-timber forest products; meat production; European Landscape Convention,,,
_Tikunov et al.-2019-Evaluation of tourist activities.txt,Evaluation of Tourist Activities and,Vladimir Sergeevich TIKUNOV; Vitalii Semenovich BELOZEROV; Stanislav Olegovich ANTIPOV,"Faculty of Geography, Lomonosov Moscow State University; Department of Socio-Economic Geography, Geoinformatics and Tourism, North-Caucasus Federal University",2010,other,,,,,,,,,tourist destination (2); tourist sites,tourist destination (3); tourist attraction (2); recreational areas; recreational activities (4); tourist objects; tourist activity (2); tourist flows (3); tourist attractions; tourist facilities; urban spa area; places of interest,,"{'value': 'Entertainment', 'reasoning': 'The paper discusses the attractiveness of tourist destinations and sites, which directly relates to the entertainment value these places offer to tourists. The analysis of tourist flows and preferences also indicates the importance of entertainment in tourism.'}; {'value': 'Economic', 'reasoning': 'The study evaluates the attractiveness of tourist destinations, which has direct implications for the economic value generated by tourism in the Caucasian Mineral Waters area. The analysis of tourist flows and preferences can inform tourism planning and management strategies to maximize economic benefits.'}; {'value': 'Social', 'reasoning': 'The paper analyzes the gender and age structure of tourists, their seasonal preferences, and geographic origins, which are all aspects of social value. The identification of recreational areas used by both locals and tourists also highlights the social value of these spaces.'}",,Caucasian Mineral Waters (5); Pyatigorsk (7); Budapest,Caucasian Mineral Waters (5); Moscow (2); St. Petersburg (2); Rostov-on-Don (2); Krasnodar (2); Russia (3); South Korea; Vienna; China,,,"Since these methods of attractiveness evaluation are costly and time-consuming when it comes to global research, there is obviously a need for alternative approaches.","The purpose of this study was to evalu