_Tyner and Graham-2022-Tweeting the Laurentian Great La.txt,Tweeting the Laurentian Great Lakes: A community opinion analysis,E.H. Tyner; J. Graham,"University of Wisconsin-Green Bay, 2420 Nicolet Drive, Green Bay, WI 54311, United States",2022,journal article,Journal of Great Lakes Research,Elsevier,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jglr.2022.03.013,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jglr.2022.03.013,,,,,Great Lakes Areas of Concern (AOCs) (6); National Park Service (NPS) locations in the Great Lakes (4); Great Lakes (17); Great Lakes Basin (1),restoration (10); revitalization (3); conservation (4); remediation (1); habitat restoration (1),,"{'SOCIAL VALUES': 'Cultural identity, motivation and pride, sense of “place attachment,” and communal value. The study explores community opinions of ecosystem services, indicating a focus on cultural identity and place attachment related to the Great Lakes.'}; {'ECONOMIC VALUES': 'The function and utility of the asset, original or attributed. The study mentions economic benefits as features of interest related to restoration and conservation activities, indicating a discussion of the utility of the restored sites.'}; {'POLITICAL VALUES': 'The educational role of heritage assets, often used for political purposes (e.g., nation-building myths, glorification of leaders). The study aims to evaluate online discussions around Great Lakes Areas of Concern (AOCs) and National Park Service (NPS) locations, suggesting an interest in the educational role of these sites.'}; {'AESTHETICAL VALUES': 'Original product of creativity and imagination. The study mentions landscape aesthetics as an ecosystem service, indicating a discussion of the artistic value of the Great Lakes region.'}",restoration (6); conservation (3),"Great Lakes Areas of Concern (AOCs) (3); National Park Service (NPS) (6); Flint, Michigan (2); Detroit River (3); St. Lawrence River (3); Cuyahoga River (4); Indiana Dunes (4); Isle Royale (4); Eighteen Mile Creek AOC (1); Grand Portage Natio