_Vila-López and Küster-2024-Data mining to reposition a reli.txt,Data mining to reposition a religious tourist,Natalia Vila-Lopez; Ines Kuster-Boluda,"Department of Marketing, Faculty of Economics, University of València, València, Spain; Department of Marketing, Faculty of Economics, University of València, València, Spain",2024,journal article,International Journal of Contemporary Hospitality Management,Emerald Group Publishing Ltd.,https://doi.org/10.1108/IJCHM-03-20220390,https://doi.org/10.1108/IJCHM-03-20220390,,pp. 457-477,Cultural Heritage (1),cultural (1),religious tourism destination (5); religious destination (7); urban city (1); urban religious tourism destinations (1); city tourism (3); sacred sites (1); sacred places (2); holy places (2); holy monuments (1),religious tourism (10); religious pilgrimage (1); religious motivations (2); religious passion (1); city branding (1); spiritual essence (1); Urban Planning Theory (1); religious destinations (5); religious spaces (1); religious festivals (2); spiritual support (1); spiritual consolation (1); spiritual issues (1); spiritual comfort (1); spiritual calm (1); renaissance (culture) (3); spiritual (3),,"{'SOCIAL VALUES': 'The study discusses the importance of religious sites for spiritual comfort and emotional connection, especially during crises like the pandemic. It highlights the role of faith and the psychological impact of closing religious places, indicating a strong spiritual and emotional (collective) value associated with these sites.'}; {'ECONOMIC VALUES': 'The study explores how religious tourism destinations can be repositioned to attract visitors, focusing on the function and utility of these sites for tourism. It also touches on the potential for entertainment through religious festivals and events, indicating a use and entertainment value.'}; {'POLITICAL VALUES': 'The study implicitly discusses the management of religious sites and their incorporation into tourism strategies. It also mentions the educational role of these sites in promoting cultural awareness, suggesting a management and educational value.'}; {'HISTORIC VALUES': 'The study emphasizes the historical and cultural variety of religious sites, particularly in the context of Italy. It highlights the importance of history, art, and culture in attracting tourists, indicating a historic-artistic value.'}; {'AESTHETICAL VALUES': ""The study mentions the beauty and architecture of religious sites, such as St. Peter's Basilica and the Sistine Chapel. It also refers to the artistic and cultural interest of these sites, suggesting an artistic value.""}",repositioning (14); repositioning strategy (10); repositioning plan (1); repositioning research (1); repositioning strategy of (1); repositioning strategy for (1),Vatican City (29); Rome (10); New Orleans (1); Sarajevo (1); Barcelona (1); Shanghai (1); Konya Museum (1); Guanajuato (1); Beijing (1); Shanghai (1); India (3); Japan (3); West Nusa Tenggara (1),Spain (2); Italy (3); Europe (2); Baltics (1); Mexico (2); USA (1); Canada (1); Japan (1); Colombia (1); France (1); Brazil (1); Costa Rica (1); Spain (1); Australia (1); England (1); Germany (1); China (2); India (2),18th century (1),Covid-19 (13),"The main problem is that markets are dynamic and heterogeneous, and the positioning of a tourism destination can easily change, and this represents a significant challenge for Destination Marketing Organizations (DMOs) (Pike and Ryan, 2004).","Two main specific objectives guide our work: (i) first, to investigate the main topics associated with a religious tourism destination (Vatican City) globally and since the pandemic crisis, and, (ii) second, to identify potential topics that could be highlighted to reposition this tourism destination more favorably.",Trip Advisor (11); Airbnb (1),text (1); online travel reviews (OTRs) (6); user-generated content (UGC) (3),,,,,,7152,,,,,,,since the beginning of Covid-19,Vatican City,web data extraction,Cyotek Web