_Vincent and Coughenour-2016-Crowdsourcing the Reconstruction.txt,REKREI: RECREATING THE PAST SECTION: Body Crowdsourcing the Reconstruction of Lost Heritage,Matthew Vincent; Chance Coughenor,"University of Murcia, Spain; Institute for Photogrammetry at the University of Stuttgart, Germany",2015,other,"2015 Digital Heritage, vol. 1, pp. 171172. IEEE, 2015",IEEE,,,,,Cultural heritage (7),,artefacts in the Cultural Museum of Mosul (2); Bamiyan Buddhas; sites of Hatra; Nimrud; Nineveh; Assyrian Empire’s city of Nineveh,preservation (2); artefacts (3); reconstruction (3); architectural drawings; archaeological reports; cultural heritage preservation (2); 3D model (2); lost heritage (4); international exhibition on the Assyrian; digital applications; new methodologies for archaeology; digital techniques in field work; archaeological investigation; cultural heritage preservation,,"{'value': 'Social (Collective)', 'reasoning': 'The paper discusses the importance of cultural heritage as a testament to how we perceive the past, implying a collective cultural identity and a sense of place attachment.'}; {'value': 'Historic (Educational)', 'reasoning': 'The paper focuses on the reconstruction of lost heritage, which has the potential to provide knowledge about the past in the future.'}; {'value': 'Aesthetic (Artistic)', 'reasoning': 'The paper describes the 3D reconstruction of artifacts, which can be considered original products of creativity and imagination.'}",preservation (2); reconstruction (3); recreating; recovery of lost heritage,Cultural Museum of Mosul; Bamiyan Buddhas; Hatra; Nimrud; Nineveh; Syria; Egypt; Yemen; Nepal; Amsterdam; The Netherlands; Dutch National Museum of Antiquities; Assyrian Empire’s city of Nineveh; Lisbon; Portugal,"Mosul, Iraq; Afghanistan; Northern Iraq; Syria; Egypt; Yemen; Nepal; Amsterdam; The Netherlands; Dutch; Assyrian; Lisbon, Portugal",Assyrian Empire,"destruction of artefacts in the Cultural Museum of Mosul, Iraq","Cultural heritage s