_Viñán-Ludeña and de Campos-2022-Analyzing tourist data on Twitte.txt,Analyzing tourist data on Twitter: a case study in the province,,,,journal article,Journal of Hospitality and Tourism Insights,,10.1108/JHTI-11-2020-0209,,,,Cultural Heritage (1); World Heritage (1),,city (1); province of Granada (3); tourist destination (6); tourist service (1),World Heritage Site (1),,,,city and the province of Granada (1); Granada (17); Spain (6),Spain (7); United States (1); Japan (1); Europe (1); Asia (1); Andalusia (2),,,"when users search for information about tourist destinations on social media, they may become confused by the amount of information available and consequently make poor decisions because this type of search usually contains a lot of noise and might be unreliable.","The main aim of this paper is to analyze the tourist content posted on social media, this provides to practitioners how to draw business insights and to travelers, relevant information of the tourist destination.",Twitter (21); Facebook (5); Instagram (7); Tripadvisor (4); Yelp (4),text (1); photos (4); videos (3); geo-location (1),geo-location (1),,,likes (3); retweets (7); comments (5); followers (4),username (1); hashtag (1),"262,859 (6)","66,409 (3)",,"123,809 (1)","123,809 (1)",,432 (1),2008 to July 2020 (1),city of Granada in Spain (2),crawler (2),"API (6), Twint (7)",,"text cleaning (4), tokenization (2), stop-word removal (2) and stemming (3)",searching for the word tourism in the text of the English tweets and turismo in the Spanish tweets (1),,,[],,topic modeling (5); sentiment analysis (8); emotion detection (2),artificial neural network (1); Bayesian network model (1),latent Dirichlet allocation (LDA) (7),pre-trained classifier (1),,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,three-level hierarchical (1),,,[],,,,,,,,,,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,Python 3.7 (1),Gensim (2); Natural Language Toolkit (NLTK) (3),,,,,
_Vonitsanos et al.-2019-A NoSQL Approach for Aspect Mini.txt,A No SQL Approach for Aspect Mining of,,,2019,conference paper,,IEEE,,,,,cultural heritage (3); Cultural Heritage Management (1),,historical sites (2); monuments (2),preservation (1); Topic Modeling (1); cultural content (3); historical sites (2); monuments (2); cultural inheritance (1),,,,Greece (2),Greece (2); countries (1),,,"The excessively increasing abundance of data leads the researchers in its processing as well as its analysis, which will enable the extraction of important knowledge.","In this paper, a No SQL database method for aspect mining of a cultural heritage scenario by taking advantage of Apache Spark streaming architecture is presented.",Twitter (4); Facebook (1); Google (1),text (1); images/videos (1),,,,likes (1),tweet language (1); location where the account was opened (1); place from which the tweet was sent (1),"5, 000",3 million monthly active users,,,,,,from 01/03/2019 to 30/03/2019,Greece,crawl the tweets from Twitter utilizing Apache Spark Streaming,Twitter platform,"captured posts with keywords that are relevant to Cultural Heritage in the domain of Greece are ﬁltered. These keywords are related to different heritages, activities and speciﬁc tourist destinations.",,,manual,10 students associated with the University of Patras,[],,topic modeling (3); clustering (2); topic detection (1); text categorization (1); aspect mining (3); Aspect Extraction (1),,LDA (4),,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,"cluster with 20 nodes, where each node is equipped with quad-core Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-2400 CPU@3.10 GHz with 4GB RAM",,,4GB RAM,,,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,accuracy (1),['65% of aspects are correctly identiﬁed'],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,,,streaming technologies (1); Big data analytics (2); streaming engines (2); batch (2); streaming (5); real-time analysis (1); real-time data analytics platform (1); online aspect mining procedure (1); cross langua