_Vu et al.-2021-Improving the resident-tourist r.txt,Improving the resident-tourist relationship in urban tourism hotspots: A data analytics approach,Huy Quan Vu; Birgit Muskat; Gang Li; Rob Law,"Business school of Deakin University; Research School of Management, Australian National University; school of information technology, Deakin University; school of hotel & tourism management, the Hong Kong Polytechnic University",2021,journal article,,,https://doi.org/10.1080/09669582.2020.1818087,https://doi.org/10.1080/09669582.2020.1818087,,595–615,,urban,urban tourism hotspots (2); popular urban destinations,sustainable tourism (7); destination attractiveness (2),,,sustainable tourism planning (3),Paris,Paris; France; Europe,,global COVID-19 pandemic,"High volumes of tourists often pose a threat to tourism and decrease the quality of life for local residents, particularly in attractive urban tour- ism places.","This study aims to present potential solu- tions, based on data analytics.",Trip Advisor; Expedia; Yelp; Foursquare; Twitter,social media data; venue check-ins; geotagged photos,GPS coordinates,spatial activity patterns,temporal activity patterns; local date and time,,"venue name; venue category; local check-in date and time; location in the form of GPS coordinate; user profiles, including the location of origin","52,782","3,715",,,,,,from 2017 to 2018,Paris,data collection via the Twitter Application Programming Interface (API),Twitter API,"Free access to the Twitter streaming API has a quota limit, in which only a small proportion of tweets are returned.",,Users without information on the location of origin are excluded from the dataset.,,,[],,topic modelling,,LDA,,,,,,10-fold cross validation approach,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,"The overall framework of our process consists of three major steps: (1) VR-SMD extraction, (2) activity topic modelling of activities and (3) comparative analysis.",no,[],,,,,,,,,,perplexity value; topic concentration; t-test,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],10-fold cross validation approach,,[],word cloud; heat map,[],[],[],[],[],[],"['planning how to best get insights from an analysis of activity', 'preparing for check-in data retrieval at the individual venue level at the exact time of day, owing to the availability of local time data to obtain visit patterns at popular hotspots from both residents and tourists when demand grows again', 'strategizing for communication practices on how to best share this up-to-date information on crowded hot spots and when to avoid the hotspots for both tourists and residents', 'developing mobile applications that support social distancing for safe travel during and after a pandemic based on the introduced approach owing to their capability of pinpointing users’ locations and urban hotspots']",[],"['extend the sustainable tourism literature with an analytics-based approach, using innovative geo-tagged data']",[],[],"['we focused on the analysis from the spatial and temporal aspects, while resident’s attitudes and sentiments about tourists at the hotpots have not been examined', 'this study only provides a short-term solution for residents', 'data were collected from a single VR-SMD source, namely, Foursquare, representing behaviours of a specific groups of users, such as young people who use the Twitter and Foursquare platforms', 'Tourists from major markets, such as China, were not well represented in the collected dataset as Foursquare is not common in use amongst Chinese users']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,"The final dataset contains 52,782 venue check-ins generated by 3,715 users at 11,008 unique venues throughout Paris.",,,,,,venue-referenced social media data (VR-SMD); venue check-ins,,,
_Väisänen et al.-2021-Exploring human-nature interacti.txt,Exploring human–nature interactions in national,,,,other,,,,,,,,,national parks (18),nature conservation (2); protected areas (7); conservation (14); conservation goals (1); conservation strategies (2); national park management (1); national park use (1); landscape values (1),,"{'value': 'Aesthetical Values', 'reasoning': 'The paper discusses the use of computer vision to quantify the beauty of outdoor places, which aligns with the definition of aesthetic values.'}; {'value': 'Economic Values', 'reasoning': 'The paper mentions that recreational use of conservation areas may help fund conservation on-site and gain political support for conservation, which aligns with the definition of economic values.'}; {'value': 'Social Values', 'reasoning': 'The paper discusses understanding the human dimensions of environmental issues supports nature conservation, which aligns with the definition of social values.'}",conservation (3); national park management (1),Finnish national parks (6); Lapland Fells (4); Eastern Hills (3); Forests and Lakes (5); Archipelago (3),Finland (8); Europe (1); United States (1); Japan (1); Lapland (2),,COVID-19 crisis (1),"Although it is acknowledged that understanding the human dimensions of environmental issues supports nature conservation (Bennett et al. 2017; Sutherland et al. 2018), traditional on-site approaches for collecting information are time-consuming and costly.",We aimed to contribute to the application of computer-vision methods to visual content analysis in protected-area visitor monitoring.,Flickr (14); Twitter (2); Instagram (2),photographs (16); images (11); video (2); textual (1),geotagged (6),,,,user profile (4); gender (5),"14,585 (1)",969 (1),,"13,363 (1)",,,,2002 to 2019 (1),Finnish national parks (1),Flickr API (4),Flickr API (4),searched the Flickr API for all geotagged Flickr posts located within 500 m of all Finnish national parks (n = 40) in January 2019 (1),"Images were resized to 224×224 pixels for feature extraction and scene classification, and to 512×512 pixels for instance-level object detection. (1)","We selected 20 parks with the highest Flickr post counts (>100) as our final data set for content analysis: 12,759 images uploaded by 824 unique users. (1)",manual (2),We manually classified the 824 unique users in the data set as national (from Finland) or international and by gender based on the information available in public profiles. (1),"['national', 'international', 'gender']",,semantic clustering (6); scene classification (7); object detection (5),deep neural networks (3); neural network architectures (2),Res Ne Xt101 (4); VGG16 (4); Mask R-CNN (4); NASNet (1); Xception (1); Res Net50 (1),pretrained (2),UMAP (4),,pixels (1),,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,"Semantic clustering involves using a pretrained neural network to extract a high-dimensional feature vector that represents the semantic content of the photograph, whose dimensionality is then reduced to enable plotting lowdimensional representations to explore similarities and differences between photographs and their contents. (1)",no,[],,,,,,,,,,,[],[],[],"A permutational analysis of variance (PERMANOVA) test with 999 permutations revealed a statistically significant difference (p < 0.001) in the semantic clustering of photographs taken by international and national visitors (1); Mann–Whitney U test revealed statistically significant (p < 0.001) differences between nationals and internationals for 3 object categories: dog, backpack, and dining table (1); Mann–Whitney U test revealed statistically significant (p < 0.05) (1)",,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['Because the most photographed object on social media platforms is often people, both analysis and reporting of results must follow appropriate ethical practices (1)']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],The scripts used in this article are available at https://github.com/Digital Geography Lab/someparkbaskets. (1),"Other social media platforms, such as Instagram, may capture a broader variety of human activities (Hausmann et al. 2018), but are not available for download or allowing computer-vision analysis (Toivonen et al. 2019). (1)",,,,,,,,,
_Walter et al.-2023-Social media analysis reveals en.txt,Social media analysis reveals SECTION: Results Perceived park quality reveals distributive injustice.,M.W.; P.M.; B.B; I.A.,,2023,journal article,Scientific Reports,Nature,https:// doi. org/ 10. 1038/ s41598- 023- 39579-4,https:// doi. org/ 10. 1038/ s41598- 023- 39579-4,,,,,urban parks (1); urban park (1),,,,park planning (1),Philadelphia (4); Wissahickon Valley Park (2); Love Park (1); Rittenhouse Square (1); Logan Square (1); Washington Square (1); Franklin Square (1); Pennypack Park (1); Center City (1); North Philadelphia (1); West Philadelphia (1); Hope Park (1); Barrett Playground (1); Mc Pherson Square (1); Hissey Playground (1); Morris Estate Recreation Center (1); Norman Ellis Playground (1); Ziehler Playground (1); Scanlon Playground (1); Conestoga Park (1); Baker Playground (1); Nelson Playground (1); Olney Recreation Center (1); Houseman Playground (1); Mc Veigh Recreation Center (1); Harrowgate Park (1); Mullin Playground (1); Deni Playground (1),Philadelphia (3); Northwest Philadelphia (1); Central Philadelphia (1); North Philadelphia (1); West Philadelphia (1); River Wards (1); North Delaware (1); Lower Northeast (2),,opioid epidemic which led to 1046 fatal overdoses in 2021 in ­Philadelphia,"Philadelphia has an extensive park system serving its diverse neighborhoods. Yet the public perception of parks based on Google Maps reviews is significantly lower in areas with higher populations of Black and Hispanic residents, disadvantaged SES groups, children, and people with disabilities.",Our study offers empirical evidence for undoing legacies of inequality in park quality by centering the voices and experiences of underserved communities and their lack of access to highly-rated parks and their benefits.,Google Maps (10),text (1); aerial/satellite imagery (2),,,,reviews (10); user scores (2),park name (1); number of reviews for the park (1); average park score of all the user scores for a park (1); the individual’s user score (1),"143,913",,"69,686",,,,,2011 and 2022,Philadelphia,scraped,Python (2),,"(i) autocorrected words, (ii) removed numbers, capitalization, special characters, and common stop words, and (iii) lemmatized words to return them to their base forms",reviews with three letters or less,semi-supervised,,"['safety', 'built amenities', 'accessibility', 'recreation', 'natural amenities', 'condition', 'size', 'aesthetics']",,topic modeling (6); classification (2),random forest (RF) classifier (3),Latent Dirichlet Allocation (LDA) (3); Anchored Correlation Explanation (Cor Ex) (3),,,,text (1); aerial images (2); satellite imagery (2),,70/30,,,,,,,,{},,cloud-based platform,,,,,,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,Spearman’s Rank Correlation (2); Spearman’s correlation coefficients (3); p-values (3); accuracy (2),[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],bivariate mapping (1); heat maps (2); correlation matrix (1),[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['park planners must go beyond boosting aesthetics and natural amenities in parks within White and higher educated tracts, by refocusing attention on diverse user concerns and their pressing needs for improved and quality park systems that can enhance health, safety, and overall wellbeing especially in marginalized and underserved neighborhoods.']","['Our classification of park-based land cover via high-resolution remote sensed data is novel, but aligns well with past studies classifying similar urban \xadspaces71.']",[],[],"['Google Maps does not provide a user’s demographic information.', 'One limitation of Google Maps text-based reviews is its open-ended nature, only prompting users to “Share details of your own experience with this place”.', 'This means that users leave reviews with varying amounts of information and relevance to the conditions of the park they are reviewing, leading to some reviews that provide a lot of useful information about park conditions and many that do not, introducing noise to the \xaddataset43.']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"code is available at https:// code. earth engine. google. com/ 32d3a 77e70 955a6 279ec 22233 778bd 8f. Topic modeling, data analysis and plots were run in Python and data is available at https:// github. com/ matts walter/ Phila delph ia_ Park_ Scores/ tree/ main.","The land cover classified ­datasets73 for Philadelphia are available at https:// zenodo. org/ record/ 76041 04. The GIS data used to delineate park boundaries (https:// www. opend ataph illy. org/ datas et/ ppr- prope rties), streets (https:// www. opend ataph illy. org/ datas et/ street- cente rlines), residential areas (https:// www. opend ataph illy. org/ datas et/ zoning- base- distr icts), incidence of crimes (https:// www. opend ataph illy. org/ datas et/ crime- incid ents), and park facilities (https:// www. opend ataph illy. org/ datas et/ city- facil ities- master- facil ities- datab ase) are publicly available at Open Data Philly.org.",,https:// zenodo. org/ record/ 76041 04,Python (2),,,"distributive injustice (2); environmental justice (2); green gentrification (1); environmental racism (1); SDG 11.7 target (1); interactional, distributive and spatial justice (1)",,,
_Wang and Wang-2021-Understanding tourists' urban im.txt,Understanding tourists’ urban images from Big Data using,Wang; Wang,,2021,conference paper,International Conference on Environmental Remote Sensing and Big Data (ERSBD 2021),,,http://www.2bulu.com/,,,,,historical and cultural city (1); Terracotta Warriors and Horses of Qin Shihuang Mausoleum (1); Big Wild Goose Pagoda (2); Small Wild Goose Pagoda (2); Daming Palace Ruins of Chang’an City in Tang Dynasty (1); ancient architecture (1); ancient buildings (1); towers (1); Bell Tower (2); Xi’an City Wall (1); Datang Furong Garden (1); Qinling Mountain Scenic Area (2); Jingye Temple Longtan Water Play Scenic Area (2); Jiawutai Scenic Area (2); Shaanxi Cuihua Mountain National Geological Park (2); Xingqing Palace Park (1); Wangshun Mountain National Forest Park (1); Taiping Wanhua Mountain Scenic Area (1); Xi’an Banpo Museum (2),historical and cultural city (1); cultural heritage (1); ancient capital (2); history (2); culture (2),,"{'SOCIAL VALUES': 'Emotional (collective) – The study mentions that a good destination image enhances tourists’ satisfaction with the destination, which can be interpreted as contributing to cultural identity and a sense of place attachment.'}; {'ECONOMIC VALUES': ""Entertainment – The study focuses on analyzing tourist photos to understand the tourism image of Xi'an, indicating the role of the city's image in attracting tourists and contributing to the tourism market.""}; {'HISTORIC VALUES': ""Educational – The study mentions that tourists' perception of architecture and interpretation is focused on traditional attractions and cultural heritage, which contain the long history and culture of the ancient capital Xi'an.""}; {'AESTHETICAL VALUES': 'Artistic – The study mentions that the colorful lights attract many tourists to take pictures, which fully demonstrate the elegance of the Tang Dynasty.'}",,Xi’an,Russia; China,Tang Dynasty (2),,"In the existing destination image studies, scholars 