_Wang et al.-2024-How to perceive tourism destinat.txt,How to perceive tourism destination image? A visual content analysis based on inbound tourists’ photos,Xiaoyu Wang; Naixia Mou; Shaodong Zhu; Tengfei Yang; Xiuchun Zhang; Yameng Zhang,"College of Geodesy and Geomatics, Shandong University of Science and Technology, Qingdao, 266590, China; The Fourth Prospecting of Shandong Coal Geology Bureau, Weifang, 261200, China; Aerospace Information Research Institute, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Beijing, 100094, China",2024,journal article,Journal of Destination Marketing & Management,Elsevier Ltd,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jdmm.2024.100923,https://www.elsevier.com/locate/jdmm,,,,,historical sites,,,,,Beijing; Forbidden City; Great Wall; Yuanmingyuan Garden; Summer Palace; Olympic Park,"China; Beijing (115.7◦E~117.4◦E, 39.4◦˜N41.6◦N); Shanghai; Tokyo; Spain; Peru; Poland",,,Constructing a complete destination image analysis framework for effective planning of tourism resource distribution is both challenging and meaningful.,"this paper aims to propose a framework for analyzing the tourism destination image that integrates picture scenes, visual aesthetics, and emotional experience.",Flickr (5); Twitter; Facebook; Instagram; Weibo; WeChat,photos (13); geotagged photo data; photo content data; metadata,geotagged; longitude; latitude,spatial distribution; kernel density analysis; hotspot analysis; spatial heterogeneity; spatial autocorrelation analysis; spatial distribution pattern,shooting time; time of uploading,,image address (Url); shooting time (P_date); longitude; latitude; photo unique identification (P_id),"53,491",,,,,,,"January 1, 2014 to December 31, 2019","Beijing (115.7◦E~117.4◦E, 39.4◦˜N41.6◦N)",acquired through the Flickr API interface,Flickr API interface,,"(1) It is inevitable to obtain data outside of Beijing when obtaining data through the API interface because the maximum radius of the area is 32 km. As a result, it is necessary to clean up the data from an area whose attribute is are screened. If nationality information is not available, this paper used the 30-day stay threshold set by Girardin et al. (2008) as a criterion for determining foreign tourists, a method that has been widely applied. (3) To avoid misinterpretation of user behavior due to time bias, this paper remove data where the time of shooting does not coincide with the time of uploading to ensure the rigor of this research. (4) To make sure that a visitor is associated with a single record at the same time and location, the de-duplication operation is carried out using various combinations of user identification, latitude, longitude, and shooting time.",,,,[],,image scene recognition and classification; aesthetic evaluation; image emotion extraction,Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) (3); deep learning,Inception-v4 model (4); NIMA (Neural Image Assessment) model (4); VGGNet model,,,,images; semantic features of images,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,"The Inception-v4 model is able to accurately identify multiple key scenarios in Beijing tourism. For example, the model can recognize buildings and landmarks of historical significance such as the Forbidden City, which is a reflection of Beijing’s rich cultural heritage and archi­ tecture. At the same time, the model is also able to recognize nightlife scenes such as bars and restaurants, which is in line with the vibrant and open image of Beijing as a cosmopolitan city.",,no,[],,,,,,,,,,accuracy,[],[],[],"Moran I = 0.180, p = 0.007, and z = 2.683",,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['The framework proposed in this study is useful for planning, man\xad\naging, and allocating resources for tourism destinations.']",[],[],"['Firstly, the user base limits the amount of data available on\nFlickr. Age, gender, educational attainment, and other demographics of users are not disclosed.', 'Secondly, the tourism destination image goes beyond the visual dimension and in\xad\nvolves all senses.']",[],[],[],[],[],[