"_Xi et al.-2022-Spatial patterns, causes and cha.txt","Spatial patterns, causes and cha",Xi Xuesong; Xu Anqi; Guo Zihan; Sun Lei,"College of Water Resources and Civil Engineering, China Agricultural University, Beijing, China; College of Architecture and Engineering, Zhejiang Industry Polytechnic College, Shaoxing, China; College of Horticulture, China Agricultural University, Beijing, China",2022,journal article,Heritage Science,Springer Nature,,,,20,Cultural Heritage (1),,cultural landscape (5); cultural routes (6); historical and cultural landscapes (2),heritage protection (2); cultural integration (1); cultural belt (3); cultural landscape resources (1); cultural landscape (12); cultural tourism belts (1); cultural heritage (1); cultural relic protection units (2),,"{'SOCIAL VALUES': 'Cultural identity, motivation and pride, sense of “place attachment,” and communal value: The Road of Tang Poetry in Eastern Zhejiang is presented as a unique cultural phenomenon, a road of landscape tourism and residence, poetry creation, the spread of ideas and cultural integration.'}; {'HISTORIC VALUES': 'Educational – Potential of the asset to provide knowledge about the past in the future: The paper discusses the historical evolution of the Road of Tang Poetry and its significance in Chinese cultural history, highlighting its role as the birthplace of Chinese pastoral landscape poetry and other cultural centers.'}; {'AESTHETICAL VALUES': 'Artistic – Original product of creativity and imagination: The Road of Tang Poetry is described as a cluster of cultural landscapes where nature and humanity blend together under the narrative of Tang poetry, emphasizing the artistic and aesthetic qualities of the landscape.'}",heritage protection (1); heritage preservation (1),Eastern Zhejiang (23),Eastern Zhejiang (13); Zhejiang Province (3); Shaoxing (5); Ningbo (3); Zhoushan (3); Taizhou (4); Hangzhou (2); China (6),Tang Dynasty (14),Southern Crossing of Yongjia (307–311 A.D) (1),"However, the basic research based on the information mining of poetry texts and the analysis of the characteristics of related cultural landscape resources is still relatively lacking, and it is difficult to provide effective support for the construction of cultural routes linked by poetry such as the Road of Tang Poetry in Eastern Zhejiang.","This paper summarizes the spatial distribution characteristics of the cultural landscape of the poetry road and the poets’ social network relationship of “person-place-landscape” based on the text information of1593 poems of 451 poets of the Tang Dynasty, and explains the causes and characteristics of the Road of Tang Poetry in Eastern Zhejiang with quantitative data.",,text (11),,spatial distribution (5); spatial location (2); spatial distribution pattern (6),,,,1593 poems (6),451 poets (4),1593 poems written by 451 poets (1),,,,,Tang Dynasty (4),Eastern Zhejiang (4),OCR tool (CS Cam Scanner software) for text recognition (1),OCR tool (CS Cam Scanner software) (1),,carry out comprehensive manual inspection and error correction to ensure the accuracy of the information of each ancient poem (1),,manual interpretation (2),,"['“places of writing”', '“places of description”', '“name of person”', '“name of landscape”']",,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,yes,['social network (5)'],action subjects in the real society (1),mutual relationships or roles between social subjects (1),948 (2),1072 (1),average degree (3); graph density (3); degree central potential (2); degree (3); intensity (3),,,Gephi tools (3),The network characteristics are analyzed from the two aspects of the overall network structure and the node importance (1),,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],['tourism industry development (2)'],[],[],[],[],"['there are still some limitations in the interpretation method of artificially discriminating the content of poems from the three levels of “person,place and landscape”, and it does not go deep into the word class and syll