_Yang et al.-2022-What constitutes a favorable des.txt,What constitutes a favorable destination brand portfolio? Through the lens of coherence,Fiona X. Yang; Xiangping Li; Yeongbae Choe,"Faculty of Business Administration, University of Macau, Avenida da Universidade, Taipa, Macau, China; School of Tourism Management, Macao Institute for Tourism Studies, Colina de Mong-H´a, Macau, China; Department of Tourism Management, College of Social Science, Gachon University, 1342 Seongnamdaero, Sujeong-gu, Seongnam-si, Gyeonggi-do, Republic of Korea",2021,journal article,Tourism Management,Elsevier Ltd,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tourman.2021.104480,www.elsevier.com/locate/tourman,,,Cultural Heritage (6),cultural (4),cultural heritage (10); Historic Center of Macao (1),cultural heritage (10); UNESCO World Heritage Site (1); World Heritage Sites (WHSs) (1); World Heritage Site (1),,"{'SOCIAL VALUES': ""Emotional (collective) - The study discusses the cultural identity and sense of place associated with Macao's heritage, indicating a collective emotional value.""}; {'HISTORIC VALUES': ""Educational - The paper mentions the potential of Macao's heritage to provide knowledge about the past, aligning with the educational aspect of historic values.""}; {'AESTHETICAL VALUES': ""Artistic - The paper refers to the artistic elements of Macao's cultural heritage, suggesting an aesthetic value related to creativity and imagination.""}",,Macao (16); Las Vegas (4),China (2); Hong Kong (2); Taiwan (1); Asia (1); Republic of Korea (1),,UNESCO inscription (1),"no tourism study to date has empirically investigated how the dynamics within a destination brand portfolio (i.e., brand portfolio coherence) affect tourists’ beliefs and attitudes toward the destination.","Using the case of Macao, the current research aims to fill this void through a mixed-method approach incorporating two empirical studies.",Mafengwo (3),text (1); photos (1); audios (1); videos (1),,,,,,2098 reviews (1),10.04 million active users (1),2098 reviews (1),,,,,up to August 2020 (1),Macao (1),crawled (2),"R 4.0.5 software and packages including RSelenium, rvest, and tm (1)",Reviews containing keywords from both cultural heritage and gaming categories were crawled (1),two researchers manually cleaned the data and separated cultural heritage from gaming-related experiences (1),A review was excluded from further analyses if no such experiences were identified (1),manual (1),two researchers (1),[],,sentiment analysis (3),,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],word clouds (4),[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,LIWC2015 (1),,,,,
_Yang et al.-2025-Qiantang River (Hangzhou section.txt,Urban imagery research based on ancient poetry and social media: A case study of the Qiantang River (Hangzhou section),Shuai Yang; Jingzhao Feng; Yile Chen; Liang Zheng; Yuqing Feng,"Faculty of Humanities and Arts, Macau University of Science and Technology, Avenida Wai Long, Taipa, Macau 999078, China; Zhejiang History Research Center, Hangzhou City University, No. 51 Huzhou Street, Gongshu District, Hangzhou 310015, China",2025,journal article,Journal homepage: www.tandfonline.com/journals/tabe20,Th A th ( ) P bli h d b I f UK Li it d t di T l & F i G b h lf f th A hit t l I tit t f J A hit t l I tit t f K,,,,,Cultural Heritage,,urban imagery; urban landscape; traditional Chinese poetry; Qiantang Poetry Road Cultural Belt; Qiantang River tourist area; leisure tourism area; Poetry Road Cultural Belt; ancient city; Hangzhou section of the Qiantang River; Fuchun River; Baiyunyuan Scenic Area; Yaoling Cave; Yan Ziling Stool; West Lake (Xi Hu); Baiyunxi Rafting; Northern Peak; Leifeng Pagoda; Lingyin Temple; Thousand Islands National Park; traditional settlements; cultural landscapes,poetry landscape; historical and cultural value; literary and aesthetic value; poetry road culture; protection; inheritance; utilization; heritage; ecological protection; recreation; leisure; protection; cultural heritage; cultural connotations,,"{'value': 'Aesthetical Values', 'reasoning': 'The paper discusses the natural beauty of the Qiantang River and its surrounding areas, as well as the artistic conceptions described in ancient Chinese poetry. This suggests an appreciation for the artistic and notable aspects of the landscape.'}; {'value': 'Historic Values', 'reasoning': 'The paper explores the historical and cultural background of the Qiantang River, including its association with ancient poetry and historical figures. This indicates a discussion of the potential of the asset to provide knowledge about the past.'}; {'value': 'Social Values', 'reasoning': 'The paper mentions the importance of cultural identity and the emotional connection people have with the Qiantang River. This suggests a discussion of the collective emotional value associated with the place.'}",protection (2),Qiantang River (Hangzhou section); Zhejiang; China; Hangzhou; Fuchun River; Baiyunyuan Scenic Area; Yaoling Cave; Yan Ziling Stool; West Lake (Xi Hu); Baiyunxi Rafting; Northern Peak; Leifeng Pagoda; Lingyin Temple; Thousand Islands National Park; Shilu Ancient Town; Ancient Village Tour in Hangzhou; Dream-seeking Tang Poetry Study Tour in Shaoxing; Poetry and Painting Qianjiang Source Tour in Quzhou; Fairyland Tang Poetry Tour in Taizhou,Zhejiang; China; Hangzhou; Yangtze River Delta; East China,Tang and Song dynasties,COVID-19,"As people’s demand for spiritual culture and tourism continues to increase, the tradi­tional tourism and leisure model has been unable to meet people’s diverse needs.","(1) Taking the Hangzhou section of the Qiantang River as an example, what is the traditional urban image reflected in the text in ancient Chinese poetry? (2) Combined with modern social media users’ comments, what is the result of the feedback on the modern urban image? (3) If we want to plan a leisure tourism area in the Hangzhou section of the Qiantang River, what role can these ancient poetry images provide for the construction of leisure tourism?",Xiaohongshu; Sina Weibo; Trip Advisor; Dianping.com (DZDP); Facebook; Twitter; Instagram,text; pictures; videos,,,,,,"30,597",,,,,,,"1 January 2020, to 31 October 2023",Qiantang River Basin,crawl online text data,Python software,"core attractions in the Qiantang River Basin, such as the Fuchun River, Hangzhou West Lake, and Tianzhu Temple, were used as keywords","challenges include filtering out ads, duplicate content, irrelevant comments, and incorrectly formatted data such as web page tags, emoticons, and links when Python crawler technology is used",,,,[],,sentiment analysis; text mining,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,yes,['semantic network'],words and concepts in text,relationships between them,,,node degree,,,,reveal the complex interac­tions of concepts within a text and how they come together to form a broader semantic and intellec­tual framework,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],element matrix diagram; tourism sentiment distribution map,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['the number of ancient poetry texts is relatively small, and relevant works need to be excavated and further analyzed', 'the currently captured social platform data focus only on Xiaohongshu, Sina Weibo, and Trip Advisor', 'Several challenges and limitations remain with respect to the accuracy of natural language processing (NLP) software when proces\xadsing ancient and modern Chinese texts', 'the time span of this study is nearly 3 years, and in the past 3 years, cities in the Chinese mainland have experi\xadenced multiple lockdown policies related to COVID-19, which has greatly affected the number of tourist arrivals']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],The original code of the program cannot be released yet because our program is being used in other research.,The datasets used and analyzed during the current study are available from the corresponding author on reasonable request.,,,,,,netnographic; natural language processing; ROST CM 6.0,,,
_Yannacopoulou and Kallinikos-2025-Measuring Destination Image Usin.txt,Measuring Destination Image Using AI and Big Data: Kastoria’s Image on Trip Advisor,A. Yannacopoulou; K. Kallinikos,,2025,journal article,Societies,MDPI,https://doi.org/10.3390/soc15010005,https://,,,,,"attractions (such as monuments, museums, lakes, rivers, parks, etc.) (1)",,,,,Kastoria,Greece; European Union,,COVID-19 pandemic (1),"This research introduces a big data-driven approach to analyzing and measuring the perceived and conveyed TDI in OTRs concerning the reflected perceptive, spatial, and affective dimensions of search results.","our main objective is to measure and analyze the TDI promoted by Trip Advisor for the attractions of the city of Kastoria, Greece.",Trip Advisor; Google Maps,text; images / photos,,spatio-temporal distribution,temporal distribution,votes; ratings,,2577,1631,2577,2598,,,,between 2012 and 2024,Kastoria,data extraction,apify.com,,"removed a total of 7 entries (three cafes, one internet cafe, and three fur shops), as they did not belong to the category. In addition, for two entries there was no review.",,manual,,[],,object recognition; sentiment analysis,Convolutional Neural Network,,,,,images; text,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,"output contains only a single probability score vector, which is organized along the depth dimension.",,no,[],,,,,,,,,,,[],[],[],chi-square test,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],word clouds,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,Data are contained within the article.,,,,PIL; tqdm; Num Py; sklearn.cluster; pandas; webcolors; collections; Text Blob; langdetect; googletrans,,Tourist Destination Image (TDI); electronic Word of Mouth (e Wo M); Online Travel Reviews (OTRs); user-generated content (UGC); Destination Management Organizations (DMOs),,,
_Ye and Liu-2023-Indicator System and Constructio.txt,Article ABSTRACT:,"Ye, P.; Liu, Y.",,2023,journal article,Sustainability,MDPI,10.3390/su15097441,https://doi.org/ 10.3390/su15097441,,,historical and cultural city (1),,tourist attractions (17); historical and cultural cities (1),,,,,Yangzhou (11); Yangzhou City (6); Slender West Lake (3),China (7); Yangtze River (1); Beijing-Hangzhou Grand Canal (1); Jiangsu Province (1); East Asian (1); Guangdong province (1),,,"However, despite to the vigorous development of mobile information technology practices, there is not sufﬁcient academic attention in the ﬁeld regarding the new advances in mobile information technology which are represented by new media [9].","(1) In the context of how the mobile Internet is reshaping tourism, what online service functions are provided for tourists by the new media platforms of tourist attractions? (2) What are the differences in online service functions for different types of new media platforms, and what is the evaluation indicator system for the construction level of tourism new media platforms? (3) What is the current construction level of NMPOSFs for A-grade tourist attractions in Yangzhou City?",We Chat (5); We Chat public account (8); Dianping (8); Sina Weibo (7); Amap (9); Tik Tok (7),,,,,,,,1262 million monthly active accounts in the third quarter of 2021 (WeChat) more than 599 million monthly active users (Amap) monthly active users have exceeded 800 million (Tik Tok),,,,,,third quarter of 2021 (WeChat),"China (WeChat, Dianping, Sina Weibo, Amap, Tik Tok)",investigating the types of online services provided by A-grade tourist attractions in Yangzhou on different new media platforms,,,,,,,[],,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['this paper focuses on the tourism online service functions provided by ﬁve different types of new media platforms, composing the online service function system on new media platforms of 