_Yoo and Kang-2025-Visual Narratives and Digital En.txt,Academic Editor: Lewis Ting ABSTRACT: Social media platforms like Instagram significantly shape destination images and influence tourist behavior.,S.C.Y.; S.M.K.,,2025,other,,MDPI,,https://zenodo.org/records/3946761,,,,,,,,,,Seoul; Tokyo; Seoul Metropolitan City; Tokyo Metropolis,South Korea; Japan; Asia; East Asian,,,Understanding how different cities are represented and perceived on these platforms is crucial for effective tourism marketing.,"This study provides a comparative analysis of Instagram content and engagement patterns in Seoul and Tokyo, two major Asian metropolises, to derive actionable marketing insights.",Instagram; Facebook; X,images; videos; text; geotagged posts; location tags,geotags; latitude and longitude coordinates,spatial patterns; Kernel Density Estimation [KDE]; hotspots; coldspots; Spatial Autocorrelation; Global Moran’s I,timestamp; posting time; weekend days,likes; comments,post ID; timestamp; user ID; image/video content (via URL); caption text; number of likes; number of comments; location tag (if available); geotag coordinates (if available),"59,944",,,,,,,March 2018 and November 2019,Seoul and Tokyo,collected Instagram photos with the hashtag “#Seoul” and “#Tokyo”,Instaloader (version 4.9.6),"stratified approach during collection, monitoring the distribution of posts across different administrative districts (Gu in Seoul, Ku in Tokyo)",validated against administrative boundary shapefiles for Seoul and Tokyo,"Posts were selected based on location criteria: either precise geotags (latitude and longitude coordinates) within Seoul Metropolitan City or Tokyo Metropolis administrative boundaries, or location tags explicitly mentioning Seoul, Tokyo, or their well-known districts and landmarks.",manual,two independent coders,"['Food', 'Person', 'Animal', 'Landmark/Architecture', 'Urban Objects/Scenes']",0.86,classification; topic modeling; sentiment analysis; predictive modeling,Convolutional Neural Networks (CNN); Topic Models (LDA); Gradient Boosting Machines,Res Net-50; VADER,"fine-tuned on a manually labeled dataset of 5000 Instagram posts from various Asian cities, including Seoul and Tokyo, to improve its accuracy for the specific context",,,"content category; posting time (hour, day of week); caption length; hashtag count; flags indicating the presence of people or food",,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,,[],,,,,,,,,,accuracy; precision; recall; Cohen’s Kappa; R2,[],[],[],Chi-square test; t-tests; Mann–Whitney U tests; Cramer’s V; Cohen’s d; rank–biserial correlation; Benjamini–Hochberg procedure,"Sentiment analysis using VADER revealed that comments on Seoul posts had a slightly, but statistically significantly, higher average sentiment score (Mean = 0.28, SD = 0.35) compared to comments on Tokyo posts (Mean = 0.25, SD = 0.33; Mann–Whitney U = 7,654,321, p < 0.001, r = 0.04).",[],"Seoul comments more frequently contained emotional language (37% vs. 24% for Tokyo), questions seeking information (28% vs. 19%), and personal narratives (25% vs. 16%). Tokyo comments more frequently contained brief appreciative phrases (45% vs. 32% for Seoul) and technical observations about photography or aesthetics (22% vs. 14%).",,[],[],[],,,[],heatmaps,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['The data collection window of March 2018 to November 2019 captures a specific temporal context in the evolution of social media tourism, reflecting particular platform dynamics and user behaviors characteristic of this period.', 'Instagram content and engagement likely shift with seasonal events and tourism patterns throughout the year.', 'We also acknowledge that our content categorization system, while refined to address the previously ambiguous ‘Other’ category, still paints with relatively broad strokes.', 'The geotagging disparity between Seoul (40.00%) and Tokyo (7.00%) users reflects deeper cultural differences in privacy preferences and social media usage patterns, aligning with research on East Asian cultural variations in self-disclosure behavior (H. Kim & Papacharissi, 2003).']",['All data was anonymized at the source or during processing to protect user privacy.'],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,The data presented in this study are available on request from the corresponding author due to privacy considerations related to social media platform policies.,,,,Geo Pandas library in Python; Py SAL library; Matplotlib; Contextily,,destination image; social media analytics; tourism marketing; comparative analysis; content analysis; engagement; geospatial analysis; sentiment analysis; predictive modeling; user-generated content (UGC); destination marketing organizations (DMOs); platform affordances; competitive identity; Kernel Density Estimation (KDE); SHAP (SHapley Additive ex Planations) values,,,"During the preparation of this manuscript, the authors used Chat GPT (Open AI, GPT-4, May 2025 version) for the purpose of language editing and improving the clarity and readability of the text."
