_Zhang and He-2021-Understanding the visual image o.txt,Understanding the visual image of Kailash Sacred Landscape through geo-tagged landscape photos mapping,Yucheng Zhang; Jie He,"School of Architecture, Tianjin University, No.92 Weijin Road, Nankai District, Tianjin, 300072, PR China; School of Architecture, Harbin Institute of Technology (Shenzhen), University Town of Shenzhen, Nanshan District, Shenzhen, Guangdong, 518055, PR China",2021,journal article,Environmental Challenges,Elsevier,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.envc.2021.100360,,,,Cultural Heritage,,Kailash Sacred Landscape; sacred site; sacred mountain,Kailash Sacred Landscape; sacred site; sacred mountain; cultural landscape; historical and cultural heritage,,spiritual; emotional; cultural identity; symbolic; historic; artistic; aesthetic,,Kailash; Darchen of Burang County; Ngari Prefecture of Tibet Autonomous Region of China,Trans-Himalayan region; China; India; Nepal; Tibet Autonomous Region of China; Burang County; Ngari Prefecture,17th centuries,,"This paper focuses on the visual construction of Kailash Sacred Landscape in a web-based context, supposing that the generation of Kailash image is through people’s selection of symbolic elements from the landscape and then reconstructed through visual media.","(1) to explore the relationship between the visualscape of Kailash and spatial distribution of photos, and (2) to ﬁnd the most representative elements of the landscape and the paradigms within the photos.",Flickr; Pinterest; Instagram,images; photos; geo-tagged photos; texts,geo-tags; GPS; latitude; longitude,spatial distribution,,,EXIF (Exchangeable Image File Format); latitude; longitude,"8,092",,,,,,,,core research area (10 * 10km square around the peak of Kailash),Web crawler technology,,,manually ﬁlter those photos following three rules. (1) We removed all photos that were taken outside our research area. (2) We identiﬁed and removed duplicate photos all attributes of which are the same. (3) We ﬁlter those photos the theme of which is unrelated to landscape.,,semantic segmentation,,[],,semantic segmentation; clustering,deep learning,Deep Labv3 +,pretrained on ADE20k dataset,,,image pixels,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,Xception as network backbone,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,pixel-wise accuracy,['pixel-wise accuracy of this model is 82.52% on the validation set'],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],dendrogram,[],[],[],[],[],[],"['Using social media to publicize the image of Kailash Sacred Landscape can be a feasible and eﬃcient way.', 'digital management of cultural heritage providing people’s real time cognition and feedback']","['On the premise of maintaining the historical and cultural characteristics of the landscape, the image diversity of Kailash Sacred Landscape should also be enriched.', 'it is necessary to develop some distinctive and representative paradigms and eliminate images that are inconsistent with the landscape character.', 'it is also necessary to open for multi-expression of landscape image so as to avoid only stereotypical image.']","['The AI technology facilitates the data analyzing of huge amounts of photos in a time-saving and standardized way, which provides great ﬂexibility for visual content analysis.', 'Computer vision technology including semantic segmentation not only enables us to recognize the 150 common items from photos, but also the speciﬁc proportion of elements which can hardly be calculated manually.']",[],[],"['The 150 categories of items are still too rough to identify those with religious elements like “sutra streamers ” and “prayer stone ” from the photos, little in their amounts but signiﬁcant in the meanings.', 'content analysis mainly based on the proportion of visual elements cannot distinguish the background and subject in the photo so clearly, which partly lose sight of the meaning of a photo.', 'lack of the consideration of other factors like color and composition of a photo, the identiﬁcation of paradigms through clustering is still a rather generalized one, and some more symbolized images of Kailash still need to be ﬁltered out in the further study.']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,,,,,Sci Py in Python,,geo-tagged photos; visualscape; viewshed analysis; visual content analysis; computer vision; semantic segmentation; Deep Labv3 + model; hierarchical clustering; GIS; AI technology; cultural landscape; UGC (user-generated content),,,
