_Zhang and Xiao-2025-Digitalising cultural heritage t.txt,This study investigates the transformative impact of digital technologies on sentimental engagement within cultural heritage tourism through a comprehensive analysis of online reviews.,Aojia Zhang; Honggen Xiao,,2025,journal article,Current Issues in Tourism,,https://doi.org/10.1080/13683500.2025.2566861,www.tandfonline.com/journals/rcit20,,,Cultural Heritage (12); World Cultural Heritage (1),cultural (10),places of cultural heritage (1); cultural heritage sites (4); heritage settings (1); World Cultural Heritage site Yungang Grottoes (1); culture artefacts (1); heritage locations (1); cultural heritage tourism (6); heritage site (2); Yungang Grottoes (5); Buddhist carvings (1); historical narratives (1); Chinese cultural assets (1),culture transmission (1); culture experiences (1); culture heritage (5); UNESCO World Heritage site (2); digital heritage (2); heritage interpretation (1); heritage tourism (3); heritage destinations (1); heritage destination marketing (1); heritage destination management (1); heritage sites (1); heritage site’s relevance (1); cultural integrity (2); cultural depth (1); cultural context (3); cultural significance (1); cultural stories (1); cultural institutions (1); cultural immersion (3); cultural content (2); cultural attributes (1); cultural identity formation (1); cultural heritage sites (1); cultural heritage sector (1); cultural heritage tourism (1); cultural heritage digitalisation (1); cultural heritage experience (1); cultural learning (1); cultural heritage managers (1); cultural heritage destinations (1); cultural heritage experiences (1); cultural heritage (1),,"{'value': 'Social Values', 'reasoning': ""The study explores how digital technologies impact tourists' cultural appreciation and engagement, influencing their cultural identity formation and sense of belonging through shared cultural experiences.""}; {'value': 'Historic Values', 'reasoning': 'The research examines the emotional and sentimental experiences occasioned by digital technologies in places of cultural heritage, focusing on how these technologies affect the understanding and appreciation of historical culture.'}; {'value': 'Aesthetical Values', 'reasoning': ""The study investigates how digital tools enhance tourists' cultural appreciation and engagement levels, particularly through the aesthetic appeal and historical significance of sites like the Yungang Grottoes.""}; {'value': 'Educational', 'reasoning': 'The study highlights the educational benefits of digital tools in cultural heritage settings, emphasizing how they improve accessibility and interpretation in history storytelling, making culture more engaging and inviting to various participants.'}",conservations (1); preservation (1); heritage interpretation (1),Yungang Grottoes (5),China (3); Shanxi Province (1),,,"Accordingly, the question is not just whether digital tools enhance engagement, but how they evoke specific emotional responses and influence tourists’ overall sentiment toward the experience.",The research seeks to learn how digital engagement affects tourists’ emotions and to construct an extensible framework to be applied in other heritage settings with immersive technologies and mixed-reality content provision.,Chinese social media platforms (2); Weibo (3); Douyin (3); Xiaohongshu (5); Trip Advisor (1); Yelp (1),online reviews (6); user-generated content (3); text (1),,,,,,"22,920",,,,,,,,,,,,"The raw data went through preprocessing to exclude non-text elements like emojis, URLs, and unwanted characters, and stop words were excluded to enhance the efficiency of the model.",,manual annotation,two independent expert annotators with backgrounds in sentiment and computational linguistics,"['joy', 'trust', 'fear', 'surprise', 'sadness', 'disgust', 'anger', 'anticipation']",0.82,sentiment analysis (8); sentiment classification (3),BERT models (2),BERT (4); BERT-base-Chinese model (2),pre-trained BE