_Zhang et al.-2019-Discovering place-informative sc.txt,Discovering place-informative scenes and objects from social media images,Fan Zhang; Bo Zhou; Li Liu; Yu Liu; Hung-Hsiang Fung; Haishan Lin; Carlo Ratti,,2019,other,R. Soc. open sci.,the Royal Society,,https://royalsocietypublishing.org/,,,,cultural; natural,landmarks (2); historical architecture (2); religious sites (2); unique urban scenes (2); unusual natural landscapes (2),,,,,,China; United States,,,"Understanding the visual discrepancy and heterogeneity of differentplacesisofgreatinteresttoarchitecturaldesign,urban design and tourism planning. However, previous studies have beenlimitedbythelackofadequatedataandefficientmethods to quantify thevisualaspects ofaplace.",This work proposesa data-driven framework to explore the place-informative scenes and objects by employing deep convolutional neural network tolearnandmeasurethevisualknowledgeofplaceappearance automatically from a massive dataset of photos and imagery.,,images; photos; imagery; geo-tagged photos,geotags,spatial distribution,,,,more than 2 million social media photos,,,,,,,,18 cities worldwide,collecting the image data,,,,,,,[],,classification,Convolutional Neural Networks (CNN),DCNN (3),,,,image pixels,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],['Crowd-sourced data are always biased towards a group of people that generates the data.'],[],[],[],[],[],['The performance of the proposed framework depends largely on the representativeness of the data source used.'],,,,,,,,,,,
_Zhang et al.-2022-CollabLearn An Uncertainty-Awar.txt,Collab Learn: An Uncertainty-Aware Crowd-AI,Yang Zhang; Ruohan Zong; Ziyi Kou; Lanyu Shang; Dong Wang,"Department of Computer Sci- ence and Engineering, University of Notre Dame, Notre Dame, IN 46556 USA; School of Information Sciences, University of Illinois at Urbana–Champaign, Champaign, IL 61820 USA",2021,journal article,,IEEE,10.1109/TCSS.2021.3109143,,,,Cultural Heritage (4),,cultural heritage sites (11); historical buildings; monuments; archeological sites; landscapes; tower; stone lions; castle; stair ﬂight; stone wall,cultural heritage damage assessment (CHDA) (8); cultural heritage site (3); cultural heritage damages (3); conservation (2); recovery actions; cultural and artistic design; long-term aging effects,,"{'value': 'Social – Emotional (collective)', 'reasoning': 'The paper discusses the importance of cultural heritage sites to society and their historical, aesthetic, and social values, indicating a sense of cultural identity, motivation, and pride associated with these sites.'}; {'value': 'Historic – Historic-Artistic', 'reasoning': 'The paper mentions historical buildings and monuments as cultural heritage sites, which are rare or unique examples of historical, stylistic, or artistic movements.'}; {'value': 'Aesthetic – Artistic', 'reasoning': 'The paper explicitly mentions the aesthetic values of cultural heritage sites, which are original products of creativity and imagination.'}",protect (2); conserve (2); conservation (2),,Syria,,natural and man-made disasters,Our work is motivated by the limitation of current AI solutions that fail to accurately model the complex cultural heritage damage due to the lack of essential human cultural knowledge to differentiate various damage types and identify the actual causes of the damage.,"In this article, we develop an integrated crowd-AI collaboration system to solve the CHDA problem by exploring the collective strength of both AI and human intelligence. In particular, our goal is to achieve a win–win objective between AI and human intelligence by effectively leveraging the high detection efﬁciency of AI solutions to automatically process the vast amount of cultural heritage site images and explicitly exploring the human intelligence to identify and ﬁx the failure cases of AI in CHDA applications.",social media (7); Twitter,imagery data; images (10),,,,,,,,,,,,,,seven different recently damaged cultural heritage sites,cultural heritage imagery data crawler tool,,randomly sample the training and testing data from the dataset by setting the ratio of training to testing data as 1:1,,,manually annotated by domain experts using the image polygonal annotation tool Labelme,domain experts,[],,damage assessment (10); object detection,deep learning (5); deep convolutional network; convolutional neural networks,UNet; FCN; DFANet,Image Net pretrained convolutional layers,,,image pixels,,1:1,cross-entropy loss,RMSprop optimizer,10−4,10,300,,,{},UNet; FCN; Attention UNet; DFANet; Hybrid Para; Deep Active; Crowd Learn,NVIDIA Quadro RTX 6000 GPUs,NVIDIA Quadro RTX 6000,,,,UDDA network architecture design consists of two network components: an encoder network (EN) and an assessment network (AN).,The training dataset is used to train all compared AI models for CHDA.,no,[],,,,,,,,,,intersection over union (Io U); dice similarity coefﬁcient (DSC),[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,UNet; FCN; Attention UNet; DFANet; Hybrid Para; Deep Active; Crowd Learn,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['Collab Learn addresses two key challenges: the identiﬁcation of AI failures cases without ground truth labels and the imperfect CI fusion.', 'We develop an uncertaintyaware crowd-AI collaboration system to explicitly model the uncertainty of both AI models and crowd responses in a principled estimation framework and explore their complementary strengths to improve the overall performance of the CHDA applications.']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,The ground truth damage area in each cultural heritage image is manually annotated by domain experts using the image polygonal annotation tool Labelme.,,https://crisisnlp.qcri.org/heritage,Py Torch 1.1.0 libraries,PyTorch,,crowdsourcing (7); crowd intelligence (CI) (12); AMT; social sensing (3),,,
_Zhang et al.-2022-Research on Landscape Perception.txt,Research on Landscape Perception and Visual Attributes Based on Social Media Data—A Case Study on Wuhan University,"Zhang, X.; Xu, D.; Zhang, N.",,2022,journal article,Appl. Sci.,MDPI,https://doi.org/10.3390/ app12168346,https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/ 4.0/,,,Cultural Landscape (2),cultural (1),core cultural landscape area (4); palatial historical buildings (1); historic designed landscapes (1); traditional villages (1),landscape management (1); landscape planning (1); visual landscape quality (5); cultural hotspot (1),,,,Wuhan University (9); Wuhan University Library (6); the Old Dormitory (10); Neo-confucianism Building (6); Yifu Building (8); College of Engineering (7); Wanlin Art Museum (2); Songqing Gymnasium (6),"Europe (1); Dutch (1); China (5); Hubei province (2); Spain (2); Scotland (2); USA (4); Turkey (1); South Wales, UK (1)",,Cherry Blossom Festival (5),"From this overview, it appears that the photo analysis of landscape visual indicators based on geotagged social data needs more evidence to understand the mapping of the observer’s perception of the landscape.","This study aims to analyze user-generated digital photographs uploaded on a famous Chinese social platform Sina Weibo (hereinafter referred to as Weibo), to select the most popular scenic spot in a cultural landscape and characterize the content itself in terms of its landscape visual indicators.",Sina Weibo (2); Weibo (15); We Chat (2); Douyin (2); Flickr (4); Panoramio (4); Instagram (1); Ctrip (1),photographs (20); photos (20); trajectory data (3); text (2); short videos (1); meta-data (1); geo-tag (1),geographical location (1); geo-tag (1),spatial locations (1),upload date and time (1),likes (4); comments (2); forwards (1); search volume (2),user name (1),600,385 personal users and 215 ofﬁcial accounts,,600,,,,23 March 2019,Wuhan University,automated API requests with Python,API,,"Only landscape photographs were preserved through manual recognition, while photographs of people, other buildings, or vehicles were excluded.","photographs of people, other buildings, or vehicles were excluded",manual recognition,,"['6 groups, which represented 6 scenic spots']",,clustering (1); scene recognition (1),deep learning (2),,,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],"['manage cultural landscape (1)', 'enhance the attractiveness of tourism destinations (1)']",[],['methodology demonstrated in this paper adds to a growing body of evidence for visual indicator application based on content analysis of social media photographs (1)'],[],[],"['the ﬁndings might not be suitable for extrapolation to cultural landscapes at a large scale (1)', 'the potential for rigorous quality control and generalizability is required to be clariﬁed (1)']",[],"['Considering sex has no signiﬁcant inﬂuence on landscape preference in prior studies, this paper did not explore the gender differences on landscape evaluation.']",[],[],[],[],[],[],,Not applicable.,,,,MATLAB,,landscape visual characters (4); landscape perception (4); computer vision technology (3); photographic behavior (2); scenic spot (14); patch richness density PRD (3); HSV color model (1),,,
_Zhang et al.-2022-The International City Image of.txt,The International City Image of Beijing: A Quantitative Analysis Based on Twitter Texts from 2017–2021,"Zhang, Z.; Luo, M.; Luo, Z.; Niu, H.",,2022,journal article,Sustainability,MDPI,https://doi.org/10.3390/ su141710675,https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/ 4.0/,,,,cultural,ancient capital,cultural preservation (1); intangible cultural heritage (1),,,,Beijing; Peking,China; Beijing; Peking; German; Hong Kong; North Korea; New York; Barcelona; Moscow; London; Shanghai; Washington; Germany; USA; EU,,2022 Beijing Winter Olympic Games,"This research aims to tap into the international image of Beijing presented on Twitter, and provide data support for the relevant Chinese and Beijing authorities to develop communication strategies, as well as providing a reference for other cities aiming to manage their international image.","This paper selects the international city image of Beijing as the research object, and uses web-crawler technology to obtain tweets containing “Beijing” (“Peking”) from 2017 to 2021.",Twitter,text,,,timepoint; trends in sentiment values from January to December 2017–2021; monthly changes,,,"129,260",,"129,260",,,,,2017–2021,Beijing,web-crawler technology,web-crawler technology,,"language recognition, language transcription, word separation",,,,[],,topic mining; sentiment analysis,Topic Models,LDA; VADER,,,TF-IDF,text,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,coherence; perplexity,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,"['ancient capital charm', 'cultural atmosphere', 'traditional culture', 'campus culture']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],['social media platform text-mining framework was formed for city-image research.'],[],[],"['The research in this paper mainly uses text data, and the original data types could be further expanded in the future to include pictures, videos, audios, etc.', 'Due to the limitation of the languages learned by the authors, it was not possible to proofread the English results obtained by the machine translation of tweets in other languages.', 'In addition, the authors believe that the prediction of keyword statistics, LDA topics, and sentimental analysis value based on machine learning methods can be further explored in the future, and the Empirical Mode Decomposition (EMD) could be applied to reduce noise in non-stationary and non-linear data.', 'Finally, the international image of Beijing as presented on a wider range of social media platforms should be a future research direction.']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,The data in this study can be obtained by contacting the author: bfsuniuhy@163.com.,,,,NLTK,,,,,
_Zhang et al.-2023-A Deep Transfer Learning Toponym.txt,A Deep Transfer Learning Toponym Extraction and Geospatial Clustering Framework for Investigating Scenic Spots as Cognitive Regions,Chengkun Zhang; Yiran Zhang; Jiajun Zhang; Junwei Yao; Hongjiu Liu; Tao He; Xinyu Zheng; Xingyu Xue; Liuchang Xu; Liang Xu; Yuanyuan Wang; Jing Yang,,2023,journal article,ISPRS Int. J. Geo‑Inf.,MDPI,doi.org/10.3390/ijgi12050196,https:// doi.org/10.3390/ijgi12050196,,,,,scenic spots (4); tourist attractions (10); West Lake Scenic Region (5); Xixi Wetland Scenic Region (3); Baima Lake Scenic Region (4); Xiang Lake Scenic Region (6),scenic regions (7); scenic spots (4); tourist attractions (10); scenic area (2),,,spatial planning (2),Hangzhou; West Lake; Xixi National Wetland Park; Baima Lake; Xiang Lake,China,,,Extracting the names of tourist attractions from social media data and exploring their spatial distribution patterns is the basis for research on the cognitive region of tourist attractions.,"This study takes Hangzhou, a well‑known tourist city in China, as a case study to explore the human cognitive region of its popular scenic spots.",Xiaohongshu,text; spatial coordinates,,spatial clustering,,,,,,,,,,,,Hangzhou,,,,,,,,[],,classification; name entity extraction,Transformer models; Recurrent Neural Networks (RNN/LSTM/GRU),Ro BERTa; BERT; Bi LSTM; CRF; Softmax,pretrained,,,,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,three‑stage framework,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,precision; recall; F1,"['precision = 0.7371', 'recall = 0.6926', 'F1 = 0.7141']",[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],"['spatial planning of scenic areas', 'optimal layout of tourism facilities and commercial layouts', 'optimization of the transportation network and building distribution', 'planning the scenic area’s scope and land use']",[],['new method for generating vague perception regions of tourist attractions based on the tourism attraction name data uploaded by travelers on social media'],[],[],"['relatively singular source of data', 