n UGC(User Gener- ated Content) data and deep learning models.,"how to construct a comprehensive evaluation model of WHK aesthetic value and quantify its aesthetic value will be the focus of future heritage research [29], and an important component of achieving ecological protection and sustainable development.",Ctrip; Two Steps Road; Six Feet,images; texts,POI; longitude and latitude,spatial distribution patterns,,,user ID; upload time information,"73,200",,,,,,,the maximum range searchable on these websites,"Jiuzhaigou Valley Scenic and Historic Interest Area, Yunnan Stone Forest, Libo Karst, and Guilin Karst, the marine karst at Vietnam’s Xialong Bay WHs",crawling,automation and API excuses,,"duplicates, marketing advertisements, and garbled text are filtered out",,self-labeled,,"['mountain', 'water', 'forest', 'cave', 'people']",,semantic segmentation,Transformer models,Seg Former,pre trained Transformer models,,,images,,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,lightweight MLP decoder and the Transformer structure,,no,[],,,,,,,,,,,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],['These data are anonymous and we have not collected any personal information.'],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],yes,All relevant data are within the manuscript and its Supporting Information files.,,,,,,naturalness; diversity; physiological perception; psychological perception; uniqueness; natural Language Processing; NLP; GIS; Kriging interpolation method; semiotics; structuralism; linguistics analysis methods; Word Frequency Analysis; ROST CM6 software; We Chat Cloud Snow NLP sentiment analysis software; Arc GIS; Visual Sensitivity Analysis; VSA; Story Map; Augmented Reality; AR; Virtual Reality; VR; Unmanned Aerial Vehicles; UAV,,,
_Zhao et al.-2025-Rural Image Perception and Spati.txt,Article ABSTRACT:,"Zhao, B.; Gao, Z.; Jiao, M.; Weng, R.; Jia, T.; Xu, C.; Wang, X.; Jiang, Y.",,2025,journal article,Land,MDPI,,,,,Rural Heritage (1); Cultural Landscape (2),cultural (1); natural (1),traditional villages (5); traditional village (4); cultural landscape (3); architectural heritage value (2); raw earth architecture (2); historic streetscape; historical districts; historical and cultural towns; ancient towns; ethnic villages,cultural landscape (3); cultural–natural (1); living museum (1); heritage conservation value (1); red culture (1); heritage attributes (1); living conservation (2); cultural heritage (3); red revolutionary heritage (1); traditional residential function (1); conservation (6); preservation (2); spatial governance (2); spatial protection (1); revitalization (7); living cultural landscape (1); cultural connotation (1); cultural journey (1); cultural heritage DNA (1); cultural nodes (1); cultural value (2); cultural relics (1); cultural exhibition (1); cultural label (1); cultural activities (1); cultural identity (1); cultural ecosystem services (2); cultural genes (1); cultural landscape experience destination (1); cultural sensitivity (1); cultural interpretation (1); cultural groups (1); cultural themes (1); cultural journey (1),,"Social (Emotional (collective)): The study mentions the importance of architectural heritage and unique environmental experiences, suggesting a sense of cultural identity and pride associated with Baishe Village.; Historic (Educational): The study highlights the historical depth and conservation status of the Yaodong architecture, indicating the potential for learning about the past.; Aesthetical (Artistic): The study focuses on the unique spatial feeling and architectural forms of the Yaodong architecture, suggesting an appreciation for its artistic qualities.; Economic (Use): The study discusses the tourism service facilities and their impact on the overall attractiveness of the destination, indicating the importance of the asset's function and utility.",conservation (1); spatial optimization (3); spatial planning (3); spatial governance (2); spatial protection (1),"Baishe Village (16); Guanzhong region of Shaanxi Province (1); Yongqing Fang in Guangzhou (1); Tongguan Kiln Ancient Town (1); Jinggang Ancient Town (2); Longmen Ancient Town (1); Wuzhen (1); Guoliang Village (1); Yuanjia Village (1); villages in Southern Fujian (1); Jixi, Anhui Province, China (1); Nanxun Ancient Town (1); Beishan Village, Zhuhai City, Guangdong Province, China (1)",China (4); Shanghai (1); Beijing (1); Europe (1); Poland (1); Israeli (1); Austrian (1),,,The sustainable development of traditional villages faces a core challenge stemming from the disconnect between public perception and spatial planning.,"Specifically, this study will address the following core research questions: 1. Based on social media data, what are the core constituent elements of tourists’ perceived rural image of Baishe Village, and what is its internal structure? 2. What is the overall emotional tendency of tourists towards the rural image of Baishe Village, and what specific image elements or experiences are the main sources of positive/negative emotions? 3. What geographical distribution patterns do tourists’ spatial activities and visual focal points in Baishe Village exhibit, and which are the perceived hotspot spaces? 4. What is the relationship between the formation of these spatial hotspots and their intrinsic constituent image elements?",Sina Weibo (2); Xiaohongshu (3); Flickr (2); Google Maps (1); Weibo (1),text (10); images (10); multimodal data (5); survey data (1); questionnaire (2); GPS coordinates (2); geotagged posts (1); reviews (2); photos (10); visual data (3),GPS (Global Positioning System) coordinates (1); landmarks (1),spatial analysis (10); spatial differentiation (1); spatial patterns (4); spatial correlation (1); spatial hotspots (5); spatial utilization (1); spatial indicators (1); spatial governance (2); spatial resource allocation (1); spatial resource investment (1); spatial carrying capacity (1); spatial movement (1); spatial structure (1); spatial attraction (1); spatial distribution (1); spatial experience (1); spatial zones (1); spatialized correlation analysis (1),,,,2378,,978,263,,,,2013 to 2023 (2013 to December 2023),Baishe Village,targeted web crawler,Scrapy framework in a Python 3.10 environment,,rigorous data cleaning and filtering process,"Removal of advertisements, duplicate content, and invalid text (e.g., pure emojis). Exclusion of texts irrelevant to the theme of Baishe Village. Exclusion of images where the geographical scene is unrecognizable or dominated by selfies (human face > 70% of frame). Ensuring image content pertains to landscapes, architecture, or activities within Baishe Village.",Manual,,[],,sentiment analysis (7); text mining (7); visual encoding (2),Naive Bayes classifier (1),BERT-BILSTM (1),trained on a sentiment lexicon (1),,TF-IDF algorithm (2),text (1); images (1),,,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,,yes,"['keyword co-occurrence network (3)', 'social network (1)']",keywords (2),the frequency of their co-occurrence within the same text (1),83,81,community structure (2); Betweenness Centrality (1); centrality value (1); semantic clusters (2),co-occurrence (1),Community Detection (1); Correlation Analysis (2); Centrality Analysis (1); Modularity algorithm (2),,reveal the network’s topological features and semantic structure from multiple dimensions (1),,[],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],"['heritage monitoring (1)', 'tourism planning (1)', 'conservation support (1)', 'risk assessment (1)', 'educational applications (1)']","['policy (1)', 'planning (1)', 'conservation (1)', 'management strategies (1)']","['new algorithms (1)', 'improved pipelines (1)', 'new datasets (1)', 'annotation guidelines (1)', 'fusion methods (1)']","['empirical discoveries (1)', 'dataset-related contributions (1)']",['new conceptual definition of cultural value (1)'],"['dataset limitations (1)', 'representativeness issues (1)', 'methodological constraints (1)']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],"['social media data cannot fully represent all tourist groups and, crucially, lack the essential perspective of local residents (1)', 'the spatial analysis precision of this study was limited by landmark identification rather than exact geographical coordinates (1)', 'this cross-sectional study failed to capture the dynamic evolution of perceptions (1)']",available on request from the corresponding author (1),available on request from the corresponding author (1),,,Python 3.10 environment (1),Jieba library (1); Snow NLP library (1); NVivo 20.0 (1),,Digital Humanities (3); Spatial Analysis (6); Tourism Destination Image (TDI) (1); User-Generated Content (UGC) (1),,,
_Zheng et al.-2024-Research Note Linking sensory p.txt,Research Note: Linking sensory perceptions with landscape elements through a combined approach based on prior knowledge and machine learning,Tianchen Zheng; Quan Pan; Xucai Zhang; Chenxing Wang; Yan Yan; Tim Van De Voorde,"Department of Geography, Ghent University, Ghent 9000, Belgium; Computational and Applied Vegetation Ecology, Department of Environment, Faculty of Bioscience Engineering, Ghent University, Ghent 9000, Belgium; State Key Laboratory of Urban and Regional Ecology, Research Center for Eco-Environmental Sciences, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Beijing 100085, PR China",2023,other,Landscape and Urban Planning,Elsevier B V,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.landurbplan.2023.104928,https://doi.org/10.1016/j.landurbplan.2023.104928,,,,,Belgian greenspaces (2),,,,greenspace management (4),Belgian greenspaces (2); Hong Kong Wetland Park,Belgium (2); Europe,,,Challenges remain when assessing cultural ecosystem services (CES) due to the subjective and intangible fea­ tures.,This study aims to identify and correlate landscape elements and sensory perceptions using social media data.,Trip Advisor (7); Twitter (11),texts (2); tags; pictures; videos,,,,,,"151,356 (Initial data)",,,,,,,"March 1st, 2010 to March 31th, 2022 on Trip Advisor and from March 1st, 2007 to December 31th, 2021 on Twitter",Belgium,,,,"We cleaned the data by deleting web links and duplicate data. Using the Natural Language Toolkit (NLTK), emoticons were replaced as relevant phrases in the Twitter and Trip Advisor data, reviews were tokenized to split long paragraphs into several sentences to translated into English via Google Translate to ensure language consis­ tency and distinguishability.","Here, we only collected reviews written in English, Dutch and French.",manual,three researchers,[],,classification,convolutional neural networks (CNNs),BERT,pre-trained,"word vectors from Glo Ve (Pennington et al., 2014); contextualized vector representation was generated by the pre-trained model of Bidirectional Encoder Representations from Transformers",,,,5 % of the reviews from each category were randomly excluded from the dataset to be used as a test set,,,,,,,,{},,,,,,,,"The framework of Con Wea was introduced to identify the dominant sensory perception in each sentence containing any landscape element (Mekala & Shang, 2020). It supports the weakly supervised classification by lexicons, enabling the retention of ambiguous words through con­ textualization. Three main steps are addressed: contextualizing the re­ views; generating pseudo-labels to train a classification model; expanding and disambiguating keywords to re-train the model.",yes,['perception correlation network'],perceptions and elements,connections,,,modularity; degree,,walktrap algorithm,,to link the sensory perceptions with the landscape elements,confusion matrix; precision; recall; accuracy; F1 score,['all classifiers have successfully predicted the sensory perception with an accuracy of exceeding 80 %'],[],[],,,[],[],,[],[],[],,,[],,[],[],[],[],[],[],['facilitate the greenspace management to effectively respond to the visitors’ direct perceptions.'],['provide directional guidance for Belgian greenspace management'],['proposed a thorough and transferable workflow to understand the vis\xad\nitors’ sensory perception on each landscape element'],"['conducted a comparison using data from two popular Belgian platforms, and the results could provide suggestions for data selection in a subsequent social media-based analysis']","['findings indicated the general association between various sensory perceptions and the landscape elements, offering valuable tools for landscape management']","['long reviews could make the perception extraction challenging', 'there was no clear perceptual inclination in certain sentences or particular used expressions']",[],[],[],[],[],[],[],[],,Data will be made available on request.,,,,Natural Language Toolkit (NLTK),,Cultural 